window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4401,"title":"Chapter 4401: Chapter 4400: You! II","paragraphs":["Noah looked at Ozymandias, whose form had remained silent throughout the revelation.","His other self’s body was changing, transforming more completely into The Way of Hunger, tentacles of obsidian-gold writhing with barely contained appetite.","He turned to Kael and the assembled Seed Members, his voice carrying command.","\"Keep watch over things here. Maintain order. Do not let anyone leave the Isolated Civilization until I return.\"","He prepared to depart when Riya materialized beside him, her expression showing confusion mixed with determination.","\"What the fuck is going on, Ancestor?\" she demanded. \"Whatever it is, I’m coming with!\"","Noah didn’t even reply.","Blue-gold Primus Mana erupted around both of them, wrapping their forms in concentrated authority as they vanished from the Isolated Civilization.","Behind them, Kael and the others stared in stupor at the titanic body of Ozymandias, which now dominated the sky with its impossible fusion of Mana and Hunger.","—","In the Transcendent Quantum Folds.","In a region covered by veils of silent Paradox, existence itself seemed uncertain...present and absent simultaneously, observable and unobservable in ways that made perception uncomfortable.","A Principle steeped in Paradox covered the entire region, making everything seem absolutely normal to observation while hiding profound abnormality beneath.","But within this veiled region, four beings resided.","Three were absolutely identical with only minor variations in their features...different aspects of the same existence manifested across compatible frameworks.","The fourth was Leonore Rureaux.","The three identical beings were all bodies of Schrodinger.","At this moment, two of them...a Living Concept Schrodinger and a Living Quantum Schrodinger, gazed outward toward distant regions beginning to fill with hazy white flames.","A Justiciar was decimating an entire Citadel of Living Quantums with systematic efficiency, its massacre proceeding exactly as expected.","The Living Paradox body of Schrodinger was with Leonore Rureaux in a more intimate configuration. They were embracing, veils of paradox covering their naked figures as Schrodinger stroked her hair with gentle affection.","Leonore tapped on his chest thoughtfully, her voice carrying concern.","\"Should we really be doing this right now? Even if we cannot help it for the grander plan, Living Quantums are being killed...\"","At such words, Schrodinger smiled and shook his head.","\"No, they’re actually not real Living Quantums. That Osmont is even more obscene than we initially assessed, he should be watching from nearby, but that entire domain is empty of life. Sophisticated illusions that took me considerable time to see through.\"","His smile widened.","\"And hey, if we all might collapse soon in The Fallout, would you rather not have been doing this with me a few million more times?\"","Leonore smiled at his logic, laying her head on his chest and feeling immense warmth radiating from his existence.","She nodded with contentment.","At such a time...","\"YOU FUCKER!\"","BOOM !","Existence above them split .","A terrifying aura descended with force that made the surrounding paradoxical veils shred like tissue paper.","...!","Leonore and Schrodinger looked up in shock to see existence peeling around them like an onion, layers of reality being consumed by obsidian-crimson flames of Hunger that rapidly devoured the paradox protecting them.","They gazed upward to witness the visage of Khor descending.","They had seen her before around Osmont...small, diminutive, seemingly constrained. But not like this .","Now she looked down at them with a gaze so terrifying, so absolute in its murderous intent, that Schrodinger and Leonore understood immediately... this was the gaze of someone set on killing and collapsing, and such a gaze was directed exactly toward Schrodinger.","The moment he registered that callous, implacable stare, both he and Leonore felt terrifically oppressive power cascading down like a mountain about to crush them.","Not metaphorical pressure...existential weight that made their beings scream warnings of imminent termination.","Multiple Principles pulsed around the Paradox, Concept, and Quantum Schrodingers simultaneously as they mobilized defensive capabilities.","A collection of Quintillions in Complexity and Purity erupted around them!","Schrodinger’s voice echoed out with desperate reasonableness.","\"Whatever this is, there must be a mistake. Can we talk?\"","...!","An eruption of Principles and words, defensive authorities manifesting with speed that showed panic beneath calm exterior.","Yet against what descended from above, against an enraged Khor carrying dozens of Quintillions of Complexity and Purity alongside a fully realized Way of Existence refined through eons...","Khor gazed down with interminable rage.","She looked at Schrodinger.","And took a bite .","...!","A single bite .","And in the next instant, Schrodinger’s expression transformed from reasonable negotiation to shocked rage as his Living Quantum and Concept bodies stumbled backward paradoxically.","While his Living Paradox Body...","CRACK!","Split in half.","The entirety of that body’s existence...its paradoxical nature, whether it was alive or dead, whether it could return from death and deny termination however many times through its fundamental frameworks... everything that represented it was consumed in a single bite.","The body that split in half was merely a husk , emptied of all essential nature, falling back into Leonore’s horrified grasp.","One of Schrodinger’s bodies, the most enigmatic and fantastical manifestation of the beggar known across existence, faced instant collapse as the wrath of The First Hunger descended without mercy.","Leonore Rureaux bellowed toward Khor with her own rage erupting, grief and fury mixing into something primal.","The two remaining bodies of Schrodinger gathered around her protectively, both seeming under immense strain from losing their third aspect so suddenly, so completely.","They gazed up at Khor.","Khor gazed back at them with eyes promising only continued violence.","And only at this moment...","From above, Noah and Riya materialized to witness the devastating scene.","One of Schrodinger’s bodies collapsed, nothing but empty husk.","Khor floating above the survivors, gazing down coldly.","Her hands raised as her voice boomed across the region with authority that made existence itself tremble.","\"You seem to enjoy plots. Machinations. Schemes within schemes within schemes.\"","Her crimson eyes blazed with accumulated rage of eons.","\"It is good to see you again, O Existential Plotter... O Architect of Calculated Collapse... O Weaver of Predestined Catastrophes!\"","The titles crashed down like judgments, each one carrying weight of accusation refined through endless suffering.","\"I remember how you killed billions of Inevitabilities... slaughtered for your grand designs. I remember how you killed me , took my Heart, stole my Primacy, used everything I was as components for your precious Loom.\"","Her form blazed brighter, Hunger manifesting as physical force.","\"From now on, I will collapse all remnants of you, THE Living Paradox . Every body. Every fragment. Every echo of your existence across all frameworks. You will know what it means to be devoured completely.\"","...!","Her words crashed down with finality that suggested this was not threat but inevitable prophecy!"]},{"number":4402,"title":"Chapter 4402: Chapter 4401: You! III","paragraphs":["Noah stared at the terrifying scene of obsidian-crimson flames of Hunger bathing this entire region of the Transcendent Quantum Folds, painting existence in colors of annihilation rather than simple destruction.","His perception drank in the devastation all around...not just the immediate conflict, but the cascading consequences spreading outward.","In the distance, the Justiciar that had been conducting its systematic massacre had stopped.","Its hazy white form stood motionless, its featureless face turned toward their direction with what could only be interpreted as stupor...as if witnessing something that it absolutely did not expect.","Plans are falling apart.","The thought crossed Noah’s mind.","They had intended to follow this Justiciar after its false genocide concluded, track it back to whatever base of operations these entities emerged from, gather critical information.","But now...","Noah shook his head, refocusing on the scene of devastation below where Khor already had her head raised, preparing to take another bite after exposing Schrodinger as THE Living Paradox.","We need to be certain.","He focused his gaze on The Living Concept Schrodinger and The Living Quantum Schrodinger, activating The Lens of Civilization with deliberate intent.","And prompts materialized above their heads.","|SUBJECT: Living Concept Schrodinger|","|SURFACE THOUGHT: Rage at loss of Living Paradox body - fragment of self terminated|","|DEEPER THOUGHT: Confusion at being called THE Living Paradox.|","|CORE EMOTION: A small sense of Fear at power the being above possesses - survival odds calculated as minimal|","|DEEPEST TRUTH: \" THE Living Paradox? Me?! What the fuck is this bitch smoking?!\"|","...!","Noah’s eyes shone sharply as he processed what The Lens revealed.","First, it showed this capability was truly terrifying!","Seeing inner truths, thoughts that beings themselves might not consciously acknowledge...","Oh!","And second...","Even Schrodinger himself does not believe he is THE Living Paradox.","But believing was one thing, and being was another entirely.","They had undoubtedly witnessed the image of Schrodinger, exactly as he appeared now, standing as THE Living Paradox over Khor’s corpse in that recovered memory. The face was identical. The presence recognizable despite the shadowy obscuration.","So what’s happening here?","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as he studied Schrodinger with renewed intensity, searching for answers to questions.","Is this something similar to Khor? Blocked memories or suppressed identity? Or is something else entirely going on—some manipulation or deception?","They needed to understand before rushing to collapse and destroy as he did not want to trigger anything catastrophic if things truly turned out to be the case.","Noah called out to Khor.","\"Khor, lock them down if you must. Restrain, contain, prevent escape. But do not continue collapsing...not yet. Even these Schrodingers here do not believe in the depths of their existence that they are THE Living Paradox. Let us understand first. Hunger must be patient .\"","...!","He understood her rage more intimately than she might realize.","If someone had orchestrated his death, stolen his fundamental essence, killed his family, used his accumulated efforts as raw materials for their own designs....he might be doing exactly what she was attempting now.","But they needed understanding before committing to something irreversible.","Khor’s figure trembled as she barely contained herself, her voice emerging strained as she kept her gaze locked onto the figures below.","\"Outsider,\" she said, each word forced through clenched teeth, \"I respect you a great deal even if I haven’t expressed it directly. I am thankful for everything you have done for me, regardless of what I have contributed in return.\"","Her obsidian-crimson flames intensified.","\"But this creature below me must die . Anything tied to THE Living Paradox must be collapsed...collapsed completely , whether it believes itself to be part of THE Living Paradox or not. I understand many things could be occurring. Remnant Will. Machinations. Deceptions. But what matters most is that it involves THE Living Paradox.\"","Her voice cracked slightly.","\"Outsider, I understand your caution and appreciate your approach. But I must tell you there is not much time. The Paradoxical body I just collapsed...I intended to devour all of it. I hungered for every particle, every fragment of its existence. Yet I was only capable of splitting it in half and collapsing it completely.\"","She paused.","\"For some reason, its corpse, its body was not capable of being devoured . Whatever may be occurring right now, Outsider, it is imperative that we do everything possible to turn every single iota of what is known as Schrodinger to less than ash. Before whatever is happening completes itself.\"","...!","Her words caused Noah’s eyes to pulse sharply as he looked down at the scene below.","Fucking hell.","His eyes flashed decisively.","The two remaining Schrodingers and Leonore Rureaux looked from Khor to Noah as if waiting for a voice of reason to calm things down, to negotiate, to find solutions through dialogue rather than violence.","But in the next moment, Noah gazed at them with coldness and immensity.","He sighed.","And...","BOOM !","His body erupted with radiant blue-gold Primus Mana , his entire existence seemingly becoming another heavy mountain about to crash down below without asking questions or seeking explanations.","At such a scene, the two remaining bodies of Schrodinger bellowed with shock and incredulity.","\"WE ARE SCHRODINGER AND NOTHING ELSE!\" they roared, their voices overlapping in desperate denial. \"WE ARE A HERALD MEANT TO SAVE AS MUCH OF EXISTENCE AS POSSIBLE FROM THE COMING FALLOUT! WE ARE NOT THE FUCKING LIVING PARADOX!\"","They screamed this while their Principles gathered around them!","But even as they protested, from above, Khor’s mouth opened again to take another bite.","And Noah’s existential weight came crushing down like an indomitable mountain accepting no resistance.","Schrodinger and Leonore Rureaux witnessed both forces descending simultaneously and howled with all their accumulated existence, power erupting in final desperate defense.","Yet the complexity of the bodies present...barely a few Quintillion combined, were too low compared to what they faced from above.","Decimation was the only possible outcome.","At such a terrifying moment in time, at such a critical juncture of existence...","\" Wowee... that was unexpected. I’ve woken up a little early...\"","HUUM!","A terrifically deep voice reverberated across all of nearby existence, resonating through dimensional frequencies.","Alongside it, all billowing forms of complexity and purity froze .","Above, Noah’s gaze turned ashen as recognition crashed through his consciousness.","That voice.","He had heard it before...in Khor’s recovered memory, speaking to THE Weavers with casual cruelty while holding her stolen Heart of Hunger.","The voice felt like corruption given sound. Deep and ancient, grating against existence itself as if its very presence was an offense to reality’s established order.","Yet simultaneously, it commanded respect and reverence simply through being heard, as if acknowledging its presence was involuntary submission.","That...is the voice of THE Living Paradox.","...!","Noah looked down as past Khor’s livid figure, the two remaining Schrodingers paled.","They turned slowly, horror dawning across their features.","The corpse of the Paradoxical Schrodinger...which had been held by Leonore Rureaux, empty husk after Khor’s devastating consumption, rose up with its two halves separated but moving .","...!","A corpse by all reasonable definition. Terminated. Collapsed. Its existence ended.","And yet something utterly ancient billowed inside of it like smoke filling empty vessel.","The two halves of the corpse stretched, limbs extending in ways that defied the fact they were no longer connected.","Dark tendrils...not quite tentacles, not quite shadows, but something that existed in uncomfortable space between, erupted from the split edges and reached across the gap, seeking to rejoin severed halves.","The eyes of this corpse pulsed with sudden awareness, beginning to radiate pure crimson-gold light that suggested something vast occupying limited space.","And even before the halves fully reconnected, even while the body remained split down its center, the lips...also separated, moved independently yet in perfect synchronization, speaking with that deep, grating voice that made existence itself recoil.","\" No... I could have sworn I collapsed you completely and took your Heart of Hunger...\"","The corpse’s head tilted with curiosity that bordered on mockery, crimson-gold eyes focusing on Khor above with recognition.","\" How the heck are you still existing, Little Inevitability?\"","...!","All of Existence strained and shuddered.","As if a weight too heavy had appeared at a place it shouldn’t.","Noah looked at it and understood one thing that would have been a potential reason for his failure in surviving The Fallout.","And the voice of this thing alone caused everything nearby to freeze.","Because this wasn’t just power speaking.","This was THE speaking.","The voice of something that had reached scales of existence where normal rules became optional suggestions.","THE Living Paradox, in an unknown and unexpected capacity, had made an unimaginably early entrance!"]},{"number":4403,"title":"Chapter 4403: Chapter 4402: You! IV","paragraphs":["Existence itself changed.","The very fabric of reality became heavier, thicker, as if the surrounding space had transformed from air into viscous fluid that resisted all movement.","Breathing required conscious effort. Thought moved through molasses. Simply being demanded exertion that hadn’t been necessary moments before.","DU! DU! DU!","From the surroundings, malevolent sounds began echoing, not from any specific source, but from everywhere , as if existence itself had become an instrument being played by unseen hands!","A grand orchestral symphony commenced, ushering the arrival of something that transcended classification.","DU!","The symphony felt like hymns echoing across dimensional frequencies, with existence itself manifesting words that pressed down with physical weight.","From all around, Noah felt an interminable level of pressure descend as it bellowed heavy proclamations.","REVERE! KNEEL! REVERE! KNEEL!","...!","All of the surrounding existence seemed to have been commandeered, hijacked by will so vast it could treat reality as instrument for its declarations.","The terrifying pressure sank down from above and pressed upward from below, creating crushing vise that stated and demanded submission.","Noah felt such stifling pressure as his existence burned furiously in resistance, his expression heavy with the strain of refusing what reality itself was commanding.","Beside him, Riya was silently cursing with an angry expression, her voice forcing itself through clenched teeth.","\"The only one I planned to get on my knees for is Little Ancestor!\" she spat with defiant rage. \" Fuck off !\"","...!","Oh!","The situation had turned heavy beyond anything they’d prepared for.","The situation had turned perilous in ways that made their previous challenges seem like preparatory exercises.","Noah focused on the horrific phenomenon below while resisting the symphony and hymns pressing down from all directions. He felt instinctively that the moment he submitted to these declarations...the moment he knelt as commanded, would be the moment he would be crushed completely, even before this entity turned its full attention toward him.","He was just emerging in his Way of Existence. He could not be extinguished now!","His Civilization was just starting. His people depend on paths he was forging!","He had to endure!","And so, as existence felt heavy and stifling and seeking to make him kneel with pressure exceeding even his own Cultivation Citadel’s maximum settings, his being began radiating a terrific wave of blue-gold Primus Mana.","He called out with tyrannical certainty.","\" Primus Singularity.\"","HUUM!","He invoked the ultimate capability of the Principle of Primus Ascension, designating his own existence as the focal point where Mana concentration and quality would reach theoretical maximums.","From far above, a brilliant blue-gold sun bloomed into existence...a singularity of concentrated power that made the surrounding Primus Mana seem diluted by comparison.","Its concentration grew and grew immensely, expanding while simultaneously compressing, creating paradoxical state where vastness and density existed together.","Noah felt himself bathed under the light of this Primus Singularity , and the sensation was profound...a sensation of fusion . He felt like he was one with it, his existence pulsing with grand distinction of his Way as...","The hymns and pressure stopped .","Not diminished. Not resisted. Simply ceased , as if the Primus Singularity’s light had created space where those commands could not penetrate.","Noah observed Riya breathing easier, her expression showing relief mixed with awe as she looked at him and the brilliant sun above with shining eyes.","|PRIMUS SINGULARITY - ACTIVATION CONFIRMED|","|Duration: 1 hour at current complexity|","|Effect: All Mana-based operations functioning at 100x efficiency|","|Your advancement capabilities have been compressed into accelerated timeframes|","|Breakthroughs that would require decades will occur in minutes|","|Your existence is operating at theoretical maximum capability|","|WARNING: Extreme exertion detected across all systems|","|Perpetual Harvest is gathering accumulated effort with 100x multiplier|","|Cheating Architect is optimizing all processes for survival|","|CRITICAL OBSERVATION: You are facing an unsurpassable ordeal|","...!","Unsurpassable .","The word blazed across Noah’s consciousness with weight of absolute assessment.","But who decided that?!","BOOM!","His eyes blazed with tyranny even in this terrifically apocalyptic moment, refusing to accept predetermined outcomes regardless of how absolute they appeared.","Down below, the gaze of the Corpse of Schrodinger moved from Khor to land directly on Noah at this moment.","The separated halves of the corpse finished their horrific fusion, dark tendrils weaving flesh and essence back together in ways that defied natural healing.","The body became whole again...or at least, appeared whole, though something in its reconstituted form suggested it was merely wearing wholeness as temporary costume.","The moment Noah met that gaze...","BOOM!","His body vibrated as if struck by am invisible hammer.","The Primus Singularity above him trembled, its concentrated light flickering for the first time since manifestation.","A heavy sense of suffocation came from that gaze alone, as if being perceived by those crimson-gold eyes was physical assault against existence itself.","The Corpse of Schrodinger smiled...expression stretching too wide, carrying amusement that exceeded normal joy and approached something cruel.","\" How interesting, \" the deep, grating voice emerged, each word making reality ripple with discomfort. \" What a curious set of animals have gathered here. But why are you all so hasty ? There is still time.\"","The smile widened impossibly further.","\" Well, there was still time, and then you had to go and wake me... ah.\"","...!","BOOM !","Each word landed with more weight than the last, and down below, Leonore Rureaux and the two remaining bodies of Schrodinger stood frozen in utter shock and horror...not at Khor, not at Noah, but at what was speaking through their reconstructed corpse.","Noah withstood the gaze while processing everything.","|You are bearing tremendous existential weight|","|Effort being exerted exceeds all previous recorded maximums|","|Perpetual Harvest is gathering this exertion with 100x efficiency|","|Even standing before this presence qualifies as monumental achievement|","|Your Primus Singularity is the only reason collapse has not yet occurred|","|Continue enduring - every moment survived generates advancement fuel|","...!","Noah’s existence pulsed as he forced himself to maintain eye contact with those crimson-gold eyes that seemed to smile at him before the voice continued.","\" What a curious thing... is that a new Way of Existence that has bloomed in these glorious Folds? This is good... this is very, very good ...\"","Every time the voice echoed out, it made one feel like their existence was being dragged through spiked chains of concentrated weight, their very essence churning as if it would be turned inside out and examined from angles that shouldn’t exist.","At such a moment, Khor’s voice boomed out with effort.","Her body pulsed with utterly heavy crimson-obsidian light as she forced words through the oppressive atmosphere.","\" Why ... why did billions of Inevitabilities have to die? Why did you choose to do what you did?!\"","...!","At such words, the gaze of the Corpse of Schrodinger turned from Noah to focus on Khor exclusively.","Her body trembled with cold effort under that direct attention, and the Corpse smiled eerily as the heavy voice of THE Living Paradox boomed forth once more.","\" Oh, you poor thing. You believe yourself to be a victim ?\"","The voice carried mockery mixed with something approaching pity.","It was not sympathy, but the condescending pity of vast intelligence observing limited understanding.","\" Many billions collapsed, not just Inevitabilities. Nearly half of all Early Creatures turned to become The Dead. Multiple entities carrying THE distinction had their wings snapped off as they lost entire Civilizations they’d spent eons cultivating.\"","The crimson-gold eyes blazed brighter.","\" And you believe yourself to be a victim? No, my dear Little Hunger. You were simply one consequence among countless others. You don’t need a why . Existence doesn’t need a why . Sometimes... things just happen , ya’ know? Paradoxically. Gloriously. Without reason or purpose or grand design.\"","The voice took on lecturing quality, as if explaining obvious truth to child who should have learned better.","\" There does not need to be justification for every action, motivation for every consequence. You were simply a cog in a very large weaving that needed adjustment. A component that required replacement for the machinery to continue functioning optimally.\"","The smile became even more terrible.","\" Don’t be filled with righteous rage and indignation. Don’t take it personally, as if your suffering was about you . It wasn’t. You mattered only insofar as your collapse served purposes beyond your comprehension. Sometimes, we would all be much happier just accepting things as they are and moving on rather than demanding explanations for every misfortune.\"","The voice dropped to something almost conversational, almost friendly.","\" Look at where you are now. Somehow restored. Relevant again. Had you just accepted things and not collapsed this body in your rage, I wouldn’t even be here right now, Little Hunger. Your insistence on vengeance for imagined injustices is what created this situation. You brought this upon yourself and everyone present through inability to simply... let go .\"","...!","The devilish smile on the face of the Corpse of Schrodinger at those words was utterly terrifying.","But...it was not because it showed malice, but because it showed genuine amusement at philosophy it was expressing.","And right after finishing that monologue, it tapped out with one finger against empty air.","From all around, crimson-gold light bloomed with heavy presence that made the surrounding blue-gold of Noah’s Primus Singularity seem fragile by comparison.","In front of Noah’s eyes, a prompt materialized with urgency that suggested catastrophic development.","| WARNING: THE FESTIVAL OF PARADOX HAS BEEN CALLED FORTH|","|Classification: Unknown|","|Threat Level: Absolute|","|Survival Probability: Calculating...|","...!","The Corpse of Schrodinger smiled brilliantly, expression carrying joy that exceeded sanity and approached something else in its terrible completeness.","Its voice emerged one final time before whatever came next:","\" Sometimes, things just happen without reason or purpose. Cause becomes effect. Effect becomes cause. Everything and nothing occurs simultaneously.\"","The crimson-gold eyes blazed with light that made perception uncomfortable.","\" Let me... show you.\"","...!","BOOM!","Reality shattered .","And in the space where certainty had existed, paradox bloomed like flowers growing from burned ground, beautiful and terrible and absolutely inevitable .","The Festival had begun."]},{"number":4404,"title":"Chapter 4404: Chapter 4403: Ormordnes I","paragraphs":["Ormordnes.","The word carried heavy weight beyond its simple definition of despair.","Some across countless eras had attempted to capture its essence, to define what it meant when existence itself seemed to turn against hope.","Some held that Ormordnes was the recognition of unchangeable circumstance... the moment when one perceived that no amount of effort, no application of will, no intervention of fortune could alter what had already been set in motion.","It was not sadness at loss, but rather the profound acceptance that loss was inevitable and immutable.","To experience Ormordnes was to understand that one’s struggle had always been futile, that the outcome was predetermined, and that all attempts to change it were merely theatrical gestures in a play whose ending had been written before its beginning.","Another perspective argued that Ormordnes was... the weight of infinite responsibility meeting finite capability , the crushing realization that one was accountable for outcomes beyond one’s power to influence.","It emerged when duty exceeded capacity, when the role one occupied demanded more than existence could provide.","To feel Ormordnes was to understand simultaneously that one must act and that one cannot succeed, creating paradox that collapsed the will from within.","Both definitions carried truth. Both failed to capture the totality of what this word teuly meant!","—","At an unknown point in time, in the Earliest Folds where existence wore its most pristine and terrible forms, two beings sat together staring out onto an expanse of white.","THE Creature and THE Living Origin.","Two entities who carried THE distinction, whose very presence made reality adjust its parameters to accommodate them.","They sat in silence for a time, two impossibilities sharing space and neither speaking, as if words themselves had become insufficient.","Eventually, THE Living Origin spoke, and the voice that emerged seemed weary and tired.","\"Do you know the word... Ormordnes ?\"","THE Creature remained silent for a moment, its form utterly still as it contemplated the question.","Finally, it nodded.","\" Ormordnes ,\" THE Creature said, \"is the state where one perceives clearly that all paths forward lead to unacceptable outcomes, yet remaining stationary is equally impossible. It is the recognition that existence has constructed circumstance where there are no correct choices. ..only varying degrees of catastrophe. To experience Ormordnes is to understand that no matter what one does or does not do, collapse is inevitable .\"","The definition hung in the white expanse like a blaring accusation.","THE Living Origin remained silent for a long moment after those words, as if processing their implications or perhaps confirming their accuracy through lived experience.","\"I did not believe,\" THE Living Origin finally said, voice breaking slightly, \"that I could ever experience despair. After all, I am THE Living Origin. Countless beginnings bloom from my weavings of existence.\"","The voice carried confusion mixed with profound disillusionment.","\"How could Origin possibly experience despair? The very concept seems paradoxical...how can the source of beginnings encounter endings that cannot be transcended?\"","Another pause, heavier than the first.","\"And yet, on this day, at this moment... I feel that exact emotion with clarity that cannot be denied.I feel... Ormordnes . \"","BOOM !","The words landed with existential weight, and THE Creature’s perception expanded to truly observe their surroundings.","The scene was apocalyptic beyond normal comprehension.","Countless white-gold structures...grand architecture that had taken eons to construct, buildings that had served as foundational pillars for entire Civilization..lay shattered and cracked.","Some had been split cleanly as if by precision instruments. Others had simply... collapsed , their structural integrity unmade.","The entire region within the Folds was filled with ravenous Tears of Collapse...genuine rips in existence’s fabric.","Existence in the surroundings seemed to still be shuddering from whatever battle had occurred here, trembling like wounded creature that couldn’t comprehend the nature of its injuries.","THE Living Origin’s body looked like blinding brilliance of light shining white-gold.","But at this moment, massive jagged tears permeated that brilliance...wounds that bled gold in slow, thick rivulets that stained the white expanse beneath.","The tears weren’t healing, weren’t closing, as if whatever had inflicted them had ensured they would remain open.","THE Living Origin’s gaze swept across the devastation of its Civilization, across the impossible scene of annihilation.","Trillions of unfathomably powerful Living Origins...beings whose Complexity had ranged in the Quintillions and even Sextillions, lay collapsed and dead.","Bodies that had contained enough power to reshape Folds now served only as monuments to catastrophic failure.","\"You know,\" THE Living Origin said, voice carrying weight of shattered faith, \"I always believed that whatever could possibly occur in the future, you would always be there for us. That as long as THE Creature, this grand being who exceeded even other THE entities...was present, everything would ultimately be acceptable.\"","THE Creature listened to such words as its own existence felt tremendous strain, body shuddering lightly with effort.","THE Living Origin continued, and the words emerged like confessions torn from unwilling source.","\"But here we are, O Creature . My Civilization collapsed despite all our preparations and refinements. My very existence taken...claimed as if I were resource rather than sovereign power. And you...\"","The voice broke completely.","\"Just where did things go wrong? At what point did our path diverge from possibility of success? Why did you not save me, O Creature?\"","...!","Heavy silence bloomed at those words.","But...","Was it the job of THE Creature to provide salvation? Why would THE Living Origin place such expectation upon another being, even one carrying THE distinction?","The questions hung unanswered as eventually, THE Creature looked out into the distance...not at the devastation surrounding them, but at something beyond, something only it could perceive.","When it spoke, the words emerged with terrifying honesty.","\"How could I succeed in saving others...\"","\"...when I could not succeed in saving myself?\"","...!","The confession landed like final nail in coffin of hope.","THE Creature ...an entity that other THE entities looked toward for resolution...acknowledging its own inability to prevent catastrophe even for its own existence.","If THE Creature itself was not immune, not capable of self-preservation against whatever forces had orchestrated this devastation...","What hope did anyone else possess?","Ormordnes .","Despair.","At certain points in existence, some beings experienced tremendous levels of such state and emotion. It did not necessarily mean that existence was against them or that reality had singled them out for persecution.","Maybe such beings were simply unlucky.","Maybe they were dealt bad hands through random distribution rather than targeted malice.","Maybe Existence operated without concern for fairness, and suffering was neither punishment nor lesson...merely consequence of being present when catastrophic events unfolded.","Who knew?","Certainly not those experiencing Ormordnes , who could only endure and wonder whether meaning existed in their collapse, or if they had simply been standing in the wrong place, at the wrong time...when inevitability descended!"]},{"number":4405,"title":"Chapter 4405: Chapter 4404: Ormordnes II","paragraphs":["Noah did not like the feeling of not having control.","It was a simple truth for him...not about domination or absolute authority over others, but about maintaining sufficient influence over the immediate space around him, the moments that unfolded breath by breath.","He moved through existence with careful deliberation, ensuring that in the domains he touched, he held enough sway to react when circumstances shifted beneath his feet like sand in a tide.","Control meant that when conflict came, and it always came, he could at least oppose it. Could bear the weight!","Could dance along the edge of catastrophe without plummeting into its depths.","This was what he preferred: a measure of control, however small, regardless of what struggles pressed against him.","At this moment, he felt its absolute absence.","The air itself had changed.","It was thicker, heavier, as if existence had become viscous fluid that resisted all movement.","Breathing required conscious effort. Thought moved through something like honey. Simply being demanded exertion that moments ago had been effortless.","Around them, crimson-gold brilliance pervaded everything.","The light claimed, establishing dominion over space and time and the very possibility of action.","|CRITICAL CATASTROPHE DETECTED|","|You have fallen into THE FESTIVAL OF PARADOX|","The words materialized before Noah’s vision with clinical precision, but he barely needed their confirmation.","He could feel the truth in his existence, in the way his Primus Mana guttered like flame in windstorm.","|Due to vast disparity in the immensity of Civilizations between yours and THE Living Paradox’s, all current weavings of expressed Civilizations have been suppressed completely.|","The Civilizational Chains of Paradox moved through the air like serpents of concentrated authority, and they had already wrapped around everyone present with discriminating precision.","Leonore Rureaux hung suspended, her considerable power rendered meaningless against constraints designed to suppress entire frameworks of existence rather than mere individuals.","The two remaining Living Schrodingers, Concept and Quantum, were similarly bound, their multiple natures collapsed into singular helplessness.","Khor floated immobilized, The First Hunger herself unable to devour despite that being the fundamental principle of her being.","And Noah, with Riya beside him, caught in the same terrible web.","The chains wrapped around limbs and stretched them in different directions, anchoring them in space so completely that even the smallest movement became impossible.","It was not merely physical restraint, this was existential binding!","The Quintillions of power they held within their beings meant nothing when the very Ways through which they expressed that power were shut down entirely.","Noah’s Primus Singularity had dimmed to barely perceptible glow, a dying sun overwhelmed by foreign radiance. Only crimson-gold remained, absolute and inescapable.","The wind carried no scent of death, but something worse: the absence of natural order, as if the rules governing how things should be had been temporarily suspended pending review by an authority that cared nothing for their restoration.","Noah looked at the chains binding him with the analytical focus that had become his nature.","Even now, even trapped and helpless, his mind worked with clarity.","The Lens of Civilization and his recent ascension into The Early Infinity Dominion Realm provided benefits that ran deeper than mere power...they granted understanding , a cool peace that crept over his thoughts even in the face of impossible odds.","The chains were actively suppressing his Primus Mana , preventing its expression through mechanisms that operated at civilizational scale.","But as he observed them with enhanced perception, testing their constraints with the gentlest pressure of his will, he felt something interesting- they dimmed ever so slightly when his Way pressed against them.","Barely noticeable, like starlight competing with the sun, but real nonetheless.","Given time...seconds, minutes, perhaps longer, he could batter them endlessly. Even suppressed, the infinite nature of his reserves meant sustained assault remained possible.","He could potentially break free, though doing so would reveal abnormalities about his Way that he preferred to keep concealed.","So I will observe. Collect information. Wait for the proper moment.","Panicking would accomplish nothing. Rage would change nothing. Screaming about wanting to live, about having people depending on him...such displays were luxuries for those who believed their emotions might influence outcomes.","Noah had learned better.","His gaze swept the tower of compressed authority they now occupied, this space THE Living Paradox had claimed as absolutely as a king claims his throne.","To his right, Riya struggled furiously against her bonds. Her figure pulsed like a lamp fighting to stay lit, blue-gold Mana attempting to erupt from her body only to be snuffed the instant it manifested.","She had been looking at Noah the whole time, desperate to help despite her own helplessness.","When their eyes met, something in his steady gaze seemed to calm her. She stopped struggling, breathing heavily, finding composure in his apparent lack of panic.","Noah turned his attention to the Corpse of Schrodinger standing before them. To THE Living Paradox inhabiting that reconstructed flesh.","The entity closed its crimson-gold eyes and breathed in deeply, not from need, but as if savoring some quality of the air that others could not perceive.","When it exhaled, the sound held satisfaction mixed with faint distaste.","\" The air itself smells nostalgic, \" THE Living Paradox said, voice making the surrounding space ripple like water struck by stone, \" and yet dirtier than I remember. The air in THE Loom is much nicer...purified, refined, optimal for contemplation. Out here...\"","The entity’s expression twisted slightly. \" Out here there are so many contaminants . Uncontrolled variables. Beings pursuing their own Ways without coordination or purpose beyond their limited perspectives.\"","HUUM!","THE Living Paradox opened its eyes and gazed upon the bound figures with expression mixing fondness and cruelty in equal measure. Its attention settled on Khor, and the smile that spread across the corpse’s reconstructed face carried depths of meaning Noah couldn’t fully parse.","\"Is this not simpler, Little Inevitability? \" The voice was almost gentle, a teacher addressing a struggling student.","\" Nobody throwing tantrums. Nobody raging about imagined injustices. This is how existence should be...moments of peace and clarity. Things happen, yes. Good and bad alike. But they do not have to make us victims. We choose that designation through our refusal to accept what occurs.\"","As THE Living Paradox spoke, its figure floated through the crimson-gold light with serene grace, moving until it stood directly before Khor.","Close enough that Noah could see the way Khor’s eyes had changed...the livid rage draining away, replaced by the cold calculation of someone with eons of accumulated wisdom returning.","Those who held years of philosophy were not immune to moments of weakness, to being blinded by emotion. But if they could control themselves, return to paths of discipline...","Khor had a momentary lapse. That was all.","THE Living Paradox examined Khor with clinical interest, gaze traveling up and down her bound form like an artist assessing a canvas.","\" How wondrous ,\" it said, \" It truly is you, not fragment or echo, but actual restored existence. Though infinitely weaker. Even though you faced complete collapse of your very Way. Even though I personally unmade you and claimed your Heart of Hunger...\"","The crimson-gold eyes blazed brighter. \" You stand before me again. Impossible, and yet here you are. How did you accomplish this?\"","...!"]},{"number":4406,"title":"Chapter 4406: Chapter 4405: Ormordnes III","paragraphs":["The entity tilted its head, serpentine and strange.","\" All the Inevitabilities should be bound to THE Loom, you understand. The entirety of their existence in constant state of agony and pain as their being is continuously drained while they seek endlessly for more. Their Hunger growing without possibility of satisfaction, a perfect perpetual motion engine of suffering and power generation.\"","The words were spoken with the same tone one might use to describe mundane things- factual, detached, utterly unconcerned with the horror they described.","Khor’s eyes flashed sharply, but she refused the bait. She closed her eyes briefly, wondering about the truthfulness of those claims, whether her people truly suffered in such endless torment.","The silence seemed to delight THE Living Paradox further.","\" Come now ,\" it said, voice taking on coaxing quality.","\"I am genuinely curious. Very few could reverse collapse...especially collapse executed by me personally. Did THE Creature somehow manage this? But that entity shouldn’t be able to act freely anymore, not after what I arranged ...\"","It paused, considering.","\" Was it THE Living Temporal? Did that little rat perform temporal manipulation? That would be characteristic, though I thought we’d accounted for such interference...\"","Questions poured forth, but Khor remained silent, ancient discipline holding firm at this momemt.","THE Living Paradox’s smile became eerily serene, and in that moment Noah felt the temperature of danger shift from warm threat to cold certainty.","\" Well ,\" the entity said softly, \" if you won’t tell me, I’ll simply dig through your existence itself. Examine your fundamental architecture. Trace the mechanisms of your restoration. Identify the culprit responsible...\"","Schrodinger’s hand reached out toward Khor with calm confidence, fingers extending!","And in that instant, Khor’s crimson eyes blazed as something settled over her consciousness like a shroud.","Noah recognized it immediately, though he’d never felt its weight himself.","Ormordnes.","Despair...not for her own destruction, but for what her examination might reveal about him.","Through whatever connection they’d forged, her voice touched his mind.","\"I... am sorry, Outsider.\"","...!","The words carried finality that made Noah’s existence run cold. Not apology for failure. Not regret for circumstances.","Goodbye .","She...planned to collapse herself before examination could occur. To unmake her own existence rather than risk revealing his involvement in her restoration. To Hunger...and Hunger completely.","Noah’s eyes shifted, and light of obsidian-crimson leaked from them like blood from a wound...something deeper than his blue-gold Primus Mana, primal and hungry and utterly unbound by the Festival’s constraints, and yet still pulsing as if it were the same Way of Existence.","The prompts had been specific... all current weavings of expressed Civilizations have been suppressed.","All current . All expressed .","When the Festival descended, he had been expressing only his Way of Mana.","His other Way...newer, rawer, less refined, had been dormant. Unexpressed.","And therefore, unbound.","\"Arise,\" Noah said quietly, calling to his Hunger .","BOOM !","Obsidian-crimson brilliance erupted from him like thousand hungry mouths opening simultaneously, jaws of infinite appetite manifesting in the space around him.","He felt his existence extend through them, consciousness distributed across devouring force that recognized no limitation save its own appetite.","The countless jaws snapped onto the Civilizational Chains of Paradox.","CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!","The sound drew THE Living Paradox’s gaze instantly, those crimson-gold eyes widening with surprise.","For a heartbeat, Noah was far in the distance, bound and helpless.","In the next heartbeat...","POP !","He stood directly behind Khor, immediately before THE Living Paradox, as obsidian-crimson waves of Hunger spread outward like smoke given terrible purpose, devouring chains of Paradox with methodical hunger.","Noah wrapped his arms around Khor and pulled her back from the reaching hand, and THE Living Paradox simply watched , apparently amazed that escape was even possible within its absolute domain.","Even knowing this situation remained impossible, even understanding they could not match the entity before them, Noah moved with calm born of discipline rather than hope.","He danced along the edge of tumultuous waves, waiting to see how he would emerge on the other side...if he emerged at all.","As he retreated with Khor in his grasp, he activated The Lens of Civilization, focusing on THE Living Paradox with every enhancement his ascension had granted.","He wanted to see weaknesses, understand mechanisms, identify any advantage...","And saw nothing .","|Target’s complexity far exceeds your own existence|","|No possible weavings obtained|","The words were clear as carved stone, absolute as death.","Noah’s expression grew heavier, but he whispered to Khor as his Hunger continued its feast.","\"Don’t try to do that again, even if things seem impossible.\"","His voice carried that commanding tone it had adopted since he began walking Two Ways, since he’d stepped into The Early Infinity Dominion Realm.","Not louder, but heavier , as if the words themselves carried existential weight.","Khor’s ancient eyes studied him, then she sighed and nodded lightly.","\"Okay, Outsider. But it seems I have drawn you into a point of no return.\"","Noah arrived beside Riya again, his obsidian-crimson Hunger continuing its meal of paradoxical chains.","The consumed material flowed into some internal repository...he would examine it later, if there was a later.","For now, every scrap of attention needed to remain focused on the entity before them.","Because even after accomplishing this minor impossibility, he still felt that prickling sensation of vastly superior power pressing down from all sides.","THE Living Paradox’s full attention had turned upon him.","\" Now ,\" the entity said, voice carrying delighted interest, \" you have garnered my complete attention. You are very weak...barely worth noticing by normal standards, yet somehow you violated the rules of my Festival. The constraints should be absolute for beings at your level.\"","The corpse’s head tilted as if accessing memories from the flesh it inhabited.","Recognition sparked in those crimson-gold eyes soon after.","\" Ah! The Early Creature, Osmont, yes? And you have begun spreading your Way like a small child who just discovered fire and wants to show everyone what bright things it can make.. .\" THE Living Paradox’s smile widened. \" My oh my, how cute .\"","The words mixed condescension with genuine amusement, as if observing precocious infant attempting tasks far beyond its capability.","Noah continued staring at the entity while his mind raced through possibilities of survival, each one examined and discarded as insufficient.","His Complexity, his Principles, his carefully cultivated capabilities....all seemed woefully inadequate against power operating at this scale.","Then, a thought crystallized with desperate clarity.","If I lack the power to resolve this... could I call someone who possesses such power?","Someone like...Anaximander?","HUUM !","Existence howled around them, carrying neither hope nor despair but simply the weight of moment stretched thin, ready to snap in whichever direction fate decreed.","And THE Living Paradox continued watching with that terrible, amused smile, waiting to see what the small child playing with fire would attempt next."]},{"number":4407,"title":"Chapter 4407: Chapter 4406: Ormordnes IV","paragraphs":["When the thought arose in his mind, Noah immediately thought of Anaximander.","The brilliant Fold Dweller who had drawn an immense impression during their meeting in the Earliest Folds, whose philosophical discourse had crystallized Noah’s understanding of what it meant to truly walk a Way of Existence.","That singular encounter had accelerated his development greatly.","And when that being had departed, he had offered something precious: a connection.","That if he ever needed anything...all he need to do was say... Anaximander, come!","The heavier question, the one that pressed against Noah’s thoughts, was whether Anaximander had survived the terrifying events that had unfolded since.","The last knowledge Noah had gained about him came from THE Living Paradox’s own words in that recovered memory: the Fold Dweller had been manipulated, put into action against THE Creature himself without understanding his true role until the final moment.","That alone suggested catastrophic conflict.","Anaximander’s survival was far from certain.","And...Noah did not relish the idea of calling others to help him. There was no pride in it, no satisfaction in admitting his own insufficiency. But he was not someone so filled with arrogance that he would refuse to do what was necessary for survival simply to maintain some illusion of self-sufficiency.","So even though he did not know what result might come, what harm existed in trying?","Existencs seemed to hold its breath as Noah briefly closed his eyes.","He gathered the weight of his existence, compressed it into singular point of intent, and called out with everything he was.","Anaximander, come!","HUUM !","The name did not reverberate in the surrounding space. But it echoed through Noah’s own existence with clarity, rippling outward through whatever connections bound beings who had touched each other’s Ways.","With the uniqueness of that being, he should have been able to sense such a call rather easily.","Pending that he was alive, of course.","Noah opened his eyes and waited, expression unchanged, mind already moving to contingencies.","That plan was now in motion, there could be result in the next few seconds, or there could be absolutely nothing. Either way, he needed to think of alternatives.","Running seemed laughable.","An entity with THE distinction now knew his name, possessed memories of Schrodinger that included knowledge of The Infiniverse.","The potential damage that could be inflicted was utterly catastrophic, and attempting to flee would only delay inevitable confrontation while broadcasting weakness.","So what could he do to bypass this ordeal?","The nanoseconds dragged on like hours measured in heartbeats. A single second passed with agonizing slowness, each moment stretching thin under the weight of desperate hope.","There was no reply. No descent of some terrifying aura of power that might match THE Living Paradox’s authority. No spatial distortion suggesting imminent arrival.","There was no... Anaximander.","...!","Noah sighed lightly...the sound barely audible, more exhalation than expression, as all around him the shadowy jaws of his Hunger continued their methodical work.","They snapped and cracked at nearby Civilizational Chains of Paradox with steady rhythm, devouring constraints with appetite that recognized no satisfaction.","His gaze remained fixed on the terrifying corpse that housed THE Living Paradox’s consciousness.","The entity had been observing him this entire time with expression mixing amusement and curiosity, as if Noah were an interesting puzzle that warranted careful examination before solution.","THE Living Paradox tilted its head...the motion serpentine and unnatural, and spoke with voice that carried layers of meaning beneath surface words.","\" You truly do seem like an Early Creature through and through. The signature is unmistakable, even if your development is... unconventional.\"","The crimson-gold eyes narrowed thoughtfully.","\" Unless you were somehow a leftover seed of THE Creature himself? But that should not be possible. Early Creatures are either Living or Dead, and all those Living are thriving in my Civilization, in our Civilizations within THE Loom.\"","The smile widened, showing too many teeth for the borrowed face.","\" So you, you little anomaly, you shouldn’t exist out here at all. Yet here you stand, breaking my Festival’s constraints. Fascinating, really.\"","...!","Amusement radiated from the entity like heat from forge, and that smile only grew wider as its gaze swept across Noah’s form.","THE Living Paradox looked him up and down as if trying to discern hidden mechanisms, then turned its attention to Khor and finally to Riya.","It laughed, the sound making the surrounding crimson-gold light pulse.","\" Oh, I see now, \" it said.","\" You currently are not able to reply or speak with me freely. Not because you lack words, but because you are filled with fear . Fear that you may die, yes, but more than that, fear that those behind you may be collapsed. That Little Inevitability you pulled away from me...\"","Its gaze flicked to Khor. \" Could it be that you know the reason why she returned from collapse? Or that you even had something to do with it?\"","HUUM !","The entity paused, seeming to savor Noah’s carefully controlled expression.","\" Hmm. Since you cannot answer freely in the midst of your fear, let me ease your burden and tell you plainly: I have no intention whatsoever of collapsing any of you.\"","BOOM !","The declaration landed with weight that made the surrounding space tremble, and Noah gazed at this being with cold, calculating eyes.","He found himself questioning the statement immediately, searching for deception or hidden conditions.","But before he could think too deeply, THE Living Paradox continued with a discourse that carried terrible certainty.","\" You must understand something fundamental about existence. Even the smallest insects have their uses. In any ecosystem, everything plays a part...from the mightiest predator to the most insignificant creature consuming decay. You are slightly more important than little insects or animals, of course, because you have embarked upon and are following Ways of Existence. That elevates you somewhat.\"","The entity drifted closer, voice taking on lecturing quality.","\" So no, I will not kill you. Why would I? Beings like you are the most pristine nutrients for THE Loom. You cultivate power, refine your Ways, build your Civilizations...all without realizing you are preparing a feast for those who understand the true nature of existence. Why would such perfectly good nutrients be destroyed before THE Loom is activated?\"","THE Living Paradox’s smile became serene, almost benevolent.","\" When your Ways and Civilizations are devoured by it, when everything you have built becomes fuel for the continuation of established order, I will make gains countless times greater than what your immediate destruction would provide. So do not worry. Do not fear. We can talk freely here, right now, as civilized beings discussing matters of mutual interest.\"","The crimson-gold eyes blazed brighter.","\" You have my word, little things, that I will not collapse you. It is simply not in my interest. But...\" The smile took on sharper edge.","\" If you are not agreeable to conversation, if you insist on remaining difficult or attempting further actions, I may have to employ a little bit of force to encourage cooperation. Now that would not be something pleasant at all...not for you, certainly, and honestly not even for me. I prefer discourse to coercion when possible.\"","...!","The words rang with unfathomably clear threat despite their reasonable tone, settling into Noah’s mind and the minds of all those present with absolute clarity.","Noah’s eyes burned with that sense of enhanced perception The Lens of Civilization provided, analyzing every nuance of THE Living Paradox’s declaration.","He could breathe slightly easier now...not from relief, but from having obtained critical information that suggested a path forward through this impossible situation.","It was horrendous to be told they would not be collapsed at this moment because they were akin to nutrients meant for later consumption.","The comparison to livestock being fattened before slaughter carried implications that made his tyrannical nature bristle with refusal.","But things of the future could always be altered.","The present mattered most, and if immediate collapse was not on the table, then he had breathing room to maneuver.","The question became simpler, though no less challenging: how to avoid being tortured by THE Living Paradox while maintaining enough agency to eventually escape this entire situation?","Existence seemed to shift around them, or perhaps it was merely Noah’s perception adjusting, finding new angles through which to observe the terrible entity before him.","THE Living Paradox waited with patient amusement, clearly expecting response now that assurances had been given.","Noah’s mind worked with crystalline clarity.","He had called for Anaximander and received no answer...that avenue was closed, at least for now.","His own power was insufficient to match an entity with THE distinction. Running would accomplish nothing.","Which left conversation.","Negotiation with a being who viewed him as future sustenance, who had orchestrated catastrophes that collapsed entire Civilizations, who spoke of genocide and enslavement with detachment.","The absurdity would have been laughable if the stakes weren’t absolute.","Around him, his Hunger continued its work on the chains, methodical and patient. Riya stood behind him, silent now but alert.","Khor’s ancient eyes carried understanding mixed with resignation..mshe knew, perhaps better than anyone, what it meant to face THE Living Paradox’s attention.","And the entity itself waited, that terrible smile fixed in place, interested to see what the small child playing with fire would say now that fear had been acknowledged and addressed.","Noah gathered his thoughts, preparing words that would need to be chosen with utmost care, and the weight of the moment pressed down like atmosphere of distant, unknown thing...heavy, alien, barely breathable.","But he would breathe nonetheless.","Because there was fuck all to be done when facing an entity of such a terrifying stature."]},{"number":4408,"title":"Chapter 4408: Chapter 4407: Ormordnes V","paragraphs":["How did one occupy the attention of a psychopath with unfathomable power before they turned toward torture?","The question burned through Noah’s mind, devoid of panic but weighted with absolute necessity.","He had to accomplish this task while simultaneously searching for other avenues of escape, other plans that might bear fruit where direct confrontation would only hasten collapse.","An idea was rising in his thoughts...something related to THE Dead Order.","He did not know enough secrets of the Earliest Folds, could not claim comprehensive understanding of how catastrophic events had truly unfolded in that era.","But he did know, through stories and fragments of truth, that the death of THE Dead Order came at the hands of THE Living Paradox .","This ridiculous being standing before him had supposedly faced down all the other THE Living Existences before he was imprisoned, and a consequence of thst battle was the collapse of THE Living Order.","But all of this was in the stories.","And one could never verify the veracity and truth of such tales when Schrodinger himself was known as a storyteller, when the distributions of historical accounts might contain more fiction than fact.","Were the narratives of the Earliest Folds holding any level of genuine truth, or were they elaborate constructions designed to serve purposes he couldn’t yet perceive?","Either way, the other side of The Veil, where THE Dead Order maintained her domain of imposed structure...represented a possibility if these beings sufficiently hated each other.","The only caveat being that he was now caught between both such entities, and he lacked power to handle even one.","Especially when he knew THE Dead Order’s plans involved using him as a battery to empower her own Civilization, draining his infinite reserves to fuel her armies of Order.","So this avenue was not entirely viable, though it remained on the table as desperate measure if he could put the two against each other.","While his mind burned through possibilities with accelerating speed, Noah opened his mouth to speak.","If one wanted to buy time against a psychopath, conventional wisdom said... confusion as optimal strategy.","\"I was always curious,\" Noah said, \"how your Little Weavers found Anaximander in the first place. Since you seem so talkative, so willing to share philosophical insights, could you tell me exactly how you used Anaximander against THE Creature ?\"","...!","BOOM !","The moment his words echoed across the restructured space, the crimson-gold eyes of the Corpse of Schrodinger pulsed with terrible light that made the surrounding atmosphere tremble.","A malevolent smile bloomed across those borrowed features, stretching too wide, carrying depths of cruelty that far, far exceeded simple amusement.","\"My goodness ,\" THE Living Paradox said, voice layered with surprise mixed with something darker, \" how do you know about that, Little Osmont? Have you been peeking around at places where you shouldn’t? Accessing knowledge that weren’t meant for Early Creatures to witness?\"","WAA !","At that moment, Noah looked around and realized that all the Civilizational Chains of the Festival of Paradox around him had disappeared...consumed entirely by his Hunger, leaving him with nothing more to devour in his immediate vicinity.","The only chains that remained wrapped around Leonore Rureaux and the two Living Schrodingers, who hung suspended like specimens preserved for later examination.","And yet the sense of suffocation and concentrated power emanating from THE Living Paradox began growing heavier , as if the entity was compensating for lost constraints by simply increasing the raw pressure of its presence.","Noah looked at this being with eyes that calculated even while speaking, measuring the weight pressing down against him, assessing how long he could withstand direct attention.","\"You didn’t really answer my question,\" he said.","\"How about we trade questions and answers? You ask something, I respond. I ask something, you respond. Fair exchange between beings discussing matters of mutual interest.\"","As Noah proposed this trade, simultaneously...another instance of his existence, another body of his appeared at a distant location in an entirely different Transcendent Fold.","He stood before a Tear of Existence in the Transcendent Origin Folds, the shimmering boundary that separated Living from Dead.","In his hands, he manipulated a bundle of concentrated authority containing his voice, compressed into deliverable message that could be thrown across The Veil.","It would detail how at this moment, the Remnant Will of THE Living Paradox had appeared in the Lands of the Living.","If THE Dead Order was capable of moving from one side to the other, she would have already done so. But it seemed she was not.","But she possessed terrifically powerful armies that she could dispatch whenever necessary, forces that had been refined through her implementation of True Order.","If he informed such a being that the enemy responsible for her death had manifested on this side...would she not mobilize every resource at her disposal to do something about it?","All of it was conjecture and possibility, untested theory built on limited information.","But it was yet another plan Noah stood ready to implement if circumstances devolved to irreversible catastrophe.","For now, he waited.","His eyes flickered with enhanced brilliance back in the Quantum Folds as he looked toward the figure of THE Living Paradox, whose eerie smile had become resplendent at his proposal.","The entity drifted closer, and when it spoke, the voice carried philosophical weight that made existence itself seem to lean in and listen.","\" In all of existence, across every scale of power and complexity, only those who stand on the same stage are truly capable of exchanging words back and forth. A question and an answer, as you said...this implies equivalence of position, mutual respect between parties with comparable standing.\"","The crimson-gold eyes blazed with terrible certainty. \" But you and I, my little friend, are not on the same stage. Not even in the same theater, if we’re being honest. You are a candle flame arguing philosophy with the sun. And I wholly do not respect you.\"","The smile widened impossibly further.","\" So since it seems you are merely wasting time, attempting to delay inevitable outcomes through clever conversation, let us proceed to something more productive. Existential Torturing, I think. Yes, that should work nicely. I find that most entities become remarkably talkative right after experiencing the first few sessions. The clarity it provides is quite remarkable, really...strips away all pretense and leaves only honest desperation.\"","HUUM !","Noah’s gaze became grave as beside him, Khor and Riya shifted into defensive stances...as if their considerable power could possibly help in this situation, as if Quintillions of accumulated might meant anything against an entity with THE distinction.","In this terrifying moment, Noah’s attention flickered to the distant figures of the distraught Leonore Rureaux and the two Schrodingers.","Their gazes carried blank horror and disbelief, as if even they could not fully believe what was unfolding before them.","He thought of the other instance of his existence standing ready at The Veil, prepared to deploy a plan he truly did not want to implement.","Calling THE Dead Order’s attention here would create catastrophe of different flavor but equal magnitude.","But as he watched THE Living Paradox raise its hands with slow anticipation...as if savoring the dread spreading across those it faced, as if the fear itself was delicacy to be enjoyed before the main course...Noah sighed internally and prepared to act.","Existence seemed to silence die completely, all movement ceasing as if existence itself held its breath and ready to witness utter brutality.","THE Living Paradox began gathering terrifically concentrated crimson-gold brilliance around its raised hands, power coalescing with purpose.","This would be surgical, precise, designed to inflict maximum suffering while maintaining the victim’s existence for prolonged examination.","The entity even began speaking, voice holding satisfaction that bordered on ecstasy.","\" Yes, that gaze you’re wearing now...that expression of lamentation, of Ormordnes...that is such a wonderful precursor. It normally means you will be ready to talk quite freely very soon. The descent into despair opens doors that pride keeps locked, you understand. Resistance becomes exhausting, and truth flows like water finding its level...\"","Terrifying crimson-gold brilliance gathered and compressed, its sense of suffocation felt Fold-wide as reality itself seemed to bend toward THE Living Paradox’s will.","Noah prepared to throw the message across The Veil, to trigger conflict between THE entities regardless of personal cost...","HUUM !","At that same instant, the gathered crimson-gold light flickered .","The dominating figure of THE Living Paradox stumbled .","...!","Noah stopped any actions he was about to take, surprise cutting through his composure.","He watched with suddenly bright eyes as THE Living Paradox blinked in confusion...genuine bewilderment crossing those borrowed features.","The terrifying power being expressed through the Corpse of Schrodinger actually seemed to be... diminishing . Flickering like candle flame in unexpected wind.","\" Wowee ,\" THE Living Paradox said, voice carrying confusion mixed with dawning realization, \" that should not be the case at all. This vessel should be more than sufficient to maintain my presence here...\"","...!","Noah’s eyes grew unfathomably brighter as he expanded his perception across the surroundings, searching for whatever force was causing this interference.","He sensed nothing else...no arrival of powerful ally, no spatial distortion suggesting external intervention.","And yet shockingly, impossibly, the power THE Living Paradox was expressing continued being suppressed .","As if the Corpse of Schrodinger could no longer properly channel the terrifying will of this being, as if something was actively preventing full manifestation.","As THE Living Paradox tried to gather power again, the body swayed unsteadily...movement suggesting loss of control, consciousness struggling against forced slumber.","The entity smiled and shook its head with respect mixed with annoyance.","\" Oh, I see now, \" it said, voice carrying revelation. \" Was this one of the last saving graces left behind? A final mechanism to suppress any entity carrying THE distinction from manifesting freely outside THE Loom? How thorough. How characteristic of that approach to problems.\"","...!","The words seemed directed not at Noah but at whatever mechanism or power was forcing its existence to flicker and fade.","And those words revealed a great deal...more than THE Living Paradox perhaps intended.","The suppression of THE .","What sort of power could possibly be responsible for such a thing? THE Creature, implementing safeguards before whatever catastrophe had limited its freedom? Anaximander, revealing capabilities that exceeded Noah’s understanding?","Whatever the source, it caused THE Living Paradox to turn around as it seemed about to lose control of the corpse entirely.","The entity tapped out toward the two Living bodies of Schrodinger with casual gesture, and both disappeared instantly as brilliant crimson-gold light wrapped around them...presumably pulling them back to wherever THE Living Paradox’s true seat of power resided.","Similar radiance began gathering around the Corpse housing the entity’s consciousness, preparing to facilitate withdrawal.","But before departing, THE Living Paradox turned toward Noah and Khor.","Its eyes shone with immense light despite eyelids growing heavy, as if fighting against forced unconsciousness.","The smile remained fixed in place...heavy and casual, as if nothing was wrong, as if this minor inconvenience was merely amusing interruption rather than genuine setback.","\" Little Inevitability, Little Osmont, \" it said, voice maintaining that terrible serenity despite circumstances, \" it seems I must figure out a few things before I can have my fun with you properly.\"","The crimson-gold brilliance intensified around the corpse.","\" I’ll be in touch soon enough. Do keep working hard in the meantime. Keep forging your Civilizations and refining your Ways of Existence with all that earnest determination. Build yourselves into the most magnificent nutrients possible.\"","The smile widened one final time.","\"I thank you... for your service.\"","...!","With such words, carrying mockery and genuine gratitude...","HUUM!","THE Living Paradox disappeared.","The unfathomably heavy sense of suffocation left alongside the entity’s departure, pressure lifting so suddenly that Noah felt his Primus Singularity brighten immediately.","His existence felt free in ways he hadn’t fully appreciated until constraint was removed, like prisoner emerging from dungeon into sunlight.","The only entities remaining in this section of the Transcendent Quantum Folds were a distraught Leonore Rureaux...her expression carrying grief and horror at what had been revealed about her companion, and Noah, Khor, Riya standing together in silence...","And in the distance, barely visible through layers of spatial distortion, a Justiciar that was scrambling away with speed.","The calmness of existence returned, carrying no scent of death but rather the clean emptiness of aftermath, of catastrophe narrowly averted.","Noah stood motionless for long moment, processing everything that had occurred, analyzing implications that cascaded through his enhanced cognition.","They had survived.","Somehow, against impossible odds, they had survived an encounter with THE Living Paradox.","But the entity’s parting words echoed with weight that exceeded simple threat: I’ll be in touch.","This was not resolution. This was merely a fucking intermission.","And whatever mechanism had suppressed THE distinction from manifesting fully...that was the real mystery demanding investigation!"]},{"number":4409,"title":"Chapter 4409: Chapter 4408: Palisades I","paragraphs":["Existence felt cleaner, as if some fundamental contamination had been scrubbed away, leaving atmosphere crisp and breathable once more.","A moment of relief washed through the space where catastrophe had loomed just heartbeats before, where THE Living Paradox had pressed down with authority that made resistance seem laughable!","That oppressive weight had lifted with the entity’s departure, and existence carried no trace of its presence beyond lingering memory.","Yet Noah’s eyes remained those of caution and analytical focus as he took everything in, processing the aftermath as he refused to mistake reprieve for victory.","His posture stayed ready, coiled spring waiting to determine whether release was genuine or merely prelude to greater compression.","Beside him, the figure of Riya finally seemed to be breathing without conscious effort, her shoulders loosening from tension that had locked them rigid throughout the encounter.","Her voice emerged with sheer incredulity.","\"Holy fuck ... who was that scary fucker? THE Living Paradox? Why did such a ridiculous thing appear here? Fuck!\"","Her words and unfiltered language seemed to be her mechanism for processing trauma, for expelling terror through crude expression.","The profanity held relief mixed with lingering shock.","At this moment, Noah was working through understanding everything that had just transpired, sorting events into comprehensible sequences.","The instant THE Living Paradox felt whatever terrifying level of suppression descend upon it, suppression so profound that even Noah’s enhanced perception couldn’t identify its source..the entity had moved with immediate decisiveness.","As if it knew exactly what was happening.","And the first action it had taken after that realization was the displacement and removal of the two Living Schrodinger bodies, Concept and Quantum, pulling them away to safety with priority.","Which meant THE Living Paradox remained intimately connected with Schrodinger’s vessels, considered them important enough to protect even while facing forced withdrawal.","Not merely convenient tools but somehow essential to its continued manifestation outside THE Loom.","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply.","Based on how THE Living Paradox acted when suppression descended... is this not precisely when its vessels are most vulnerable?","The thought bloomed with terrible potential.","When the entity was being suppressed by unknown force, when its very will manifesting in these weavings of existence was being actively constrained...was this not the only genuine opportunity Noah would have to exploit a weakness of something that otherwise operated beyond his capacity to influence?","Because THE Living Paradox’s parting words had been unfathomably clear: I’ll be in touch.","Not \"if I return\" or \"perhaps we’ll meet again.\"","Absolute certainty of future encounter!","Having THE Living Paradox active at this point while being intermittently suppressed was akin to possessing a nuclear device beside one’s home that could detonate at any moment it woke from forced slumber.","The threat didn’t disappear simply because current circumstances prevented immediate explosion.","But if I use this opportunity, while that weapon is forced into dormancy to systematically destroy its vessels...","If he could collapse or completely devour the bodies of Schrodinger, eliminate every anchor through which THE Living Paradox could manifest presence outside THE Loom, he could effectively neutralize the terrifying power that had nearly tortured them moments ago.","The entity would still exist, still possess unfathomable might within its home domain.","But it would be contained , unable to reach across distances to impose its will on Noah’s developing Civilization.","And he had to accomplish this while still preparing for survival against the moment THE Loom itself erupted.","\"...\"","It was a heavy ordeal, layers of impossible challenges stacking atop each other like weights designed to crush ambition before it could bear fruit.","Could they not let him fucking breathe?","But... he would pursue it regardless.","First things first.","BOOM!","Noah’s body erupted with incandescent light...not the blue-gold of Primus Mana or obsidian-crimson of Hunger , but something else entirely.","A pure and warm glow that seemed to radiate satisfaction and completion, the unmistakable signature of Perpetual Harvest activating to claim rewards for extraordinary effort.","Prompts materialized before his vision with ceremonial grandeur.","|Against all reasonable odds, you have survived an encounter with an entity completely eclipsing you in power, complexity, and purity.|","|The effort required to maintain composure and cognitive faculties during this ordeal represents glorious achievement worthy of equally glorious reward.|","|The Harvest of this entire encounter is budding within your existence, awaiting directive on form and timing of receipt.|","|OPTIONS:|","|—Immediate Harvest: Receive accumulated benefits now at standard rate|","|—Delayed Harvest: Allow rewards to mature over time for enhanced yield|","|—Targeted Harvest: Direct benefits toward specific area of development|","|Surviving direct attention of THE Living Paradox qualifies as unprecedented achievement for you. Rewards will reflect this magnitude.|","...!","Noah felt his existence buzz with array of concentrated brilliance, power accumulated through impossibility now ready for conversion into tangible advancement.","There was harvest to collect due to navigating this ridiculous situation with sufficient skill to emerge not merely alive but potentially strengthened.","And alongside that pending reward, there existed another consideration...the Civilizational Chains of Paradox that his Hunger had devoured throughout the encounter.","All of them were being contained in an isolated domain within his existence, a space that felt like endless and infinite stomach where consumed material waited for digestion.","He had not processed them yet, had deliberately postponed that analysis because doing so during the confrontation would have divided his attention at precisely the moment when total focus was survival prerequisite.","But now they represented another boon to consider, another potential source of advancement if he could properly parse the mechanisms through which THE Living Paradox had imposed civilizational suppression.","I can address that later. Right now, immediate concerns demand attention...","Noah turned his gaze toward the figure of Leonore Rureaux, who stood in stunned silence...her expression carrying devastation.","\"It seems,\" Noah said, \"that THE Living Paradox is currently being suppressed by unknown mechanism. Which means we have an existence with unfathomable power living on the same side of The Veil as us... and that existence is temporarily weakened.\"","He paused, letting those words settle.","\"The only way for us to potentially eliminate such a threat is to completely eradicate the vessels through which its consciousness manifests. And that woman there...\"","He gestured toward Leonore. \"That woman is lover to those vessels of Schrodinger. Which means she likely possesses information regarding their locations...\"","As he voiced this assessment, Riya beside him nodded with sharp understanding lighting her eyes. She took a single step...","And appeared instantly behind Leonore Rureaux, movement so swift it left afterimage in her previous position.","\"Ancestor,\" Riya said, \"are you thinking interrogation? Because I can definitely handle interrogation. I have techniques that would make even ancient entities reconsider their loyalty.\"","Her eyes flashed with sense of urgency and barely restrained power!","Noah’s voice emerged from the distance with calm.","\"Keep her close and secure. But let’s simply talk with her first and see if she can tell us where other bodies of Schrodinger might be located, and where the bodies that were just here might have gone. Cooperation is preferable to coercion when time allows.\"","After he spoke those measured words...Riya saluted as if she had received an order.","\"Yes, Ancestor!\"","Brilliant blue-gold Primus Mana erupted from her extended hand, forming into long rope of concentrated authority that she grasped with both hands.","The construct shot forward, wrapping around the ashen Leonore Rureaux before the woman could even consider resistance.","As this occurred, Noah turned toward the desolate figure of Khor.","Her ancient eyes carried weight of self-recrimination.","\"Are you okay?\" Noah asked simply, without judgment or accusation.","She looked at him with those crimson eyes that had witnessed eons, and when she spoke, her voice held the cadence of someone acknowledging serious failure.","\"I have not acted my part as a wise and ancient existence that has lived for countless cycles. I allowed myself to be blinded by rage, permitted emotion to override accumulated discipline.\"","WAA!","Her expression hardened with self-directed anger. \"I do apologize for that, Outsider. Such loss of control endangered everyone present.\"","At such words, Noah shook his head with a gesture that dismissed need for apology.","\"Mistakes are things I have made far too many of to judge others for their own,\" he said quietly. \"What matters is learning and adapting. If you are fully returned, I have a task that requires your particular capabilities.\"","He pointed toward the far distance where spatial distortion still marked the trajectory of fleeing entity.","\"Do you want to chase after that Justiciar? See exactly where it goes, what base of operations it reports to?\"","Khor looked at him deeply for a long moment.","Ancient discipline reasserted itself, pushing aside temporary emotional turbulence in favor of practical action!","She nodded once, sharply.","And disappeared.","As for Noah...","He had boons to examine, rewards to allocate, and consumed Civilizational Chains to analyze.","Existence buzzed around him and buzzed like rough winds as he turned his gaze inward, sensing the countless possibilities in the wake of an utter disaster!"]},{"number":4410,"title":"Chapter 4410: Chapter 4409: Palisades II","paragraphs":["Noah floated calmly while turning his perception inward, his gaze piercing through layers of his own existence to observe the fundamental weavings that defined what he was and what he might become.","There were unfathomably heavy rewards waiting for him to claim...accumulated effort from surviving impossibility now crystallized into tangible advancement.","But as he contemplated the allure of that pending harvest, as he considered various forms through which those benefits could manifest, he found himself hesitant.","Hesitant from recognition that choices made at this juncture would establish patterns echoing through all future development.","When he thought about how to receive it optimally, his mind kept returning to the overwhelming presence of THE Living Paradox.","When that being had stood before him, raw Complexity and Purity had mattered remarkably little.","His own Quintillions had been rendered meaningless through a superior framework.","What mattered was THE Living Paradox’s Civilization...its sheer weight and immensity, the refined architecture accumulated across eons.","The entity had imposed a single Festival, and that alone had made other Ways unable to even be expressed.","Noah contemplated this, sorting through implications until a fundamental truth emerged with glorious tyranny.","As much as he loved witnessing massive numbers bloom before his vision...tens of Quintillions climbing up, each milestone representing vast accumulation of refined essence... this alone was not enough.","Numbers without proper framework were merely numbers. Power without civilization was merely chaos waiting to be organized by those who understood structure.","\"Civilization,\" Noah said aloud, voice booming with weight of Quintessence, \"is the answer.\"","The moment those words emerged, his existence began trembling with sense of purpose .","Something fundamental was shifting, realigning, establishing new priority hierarchy for how advancement would be pursued going forward.","Complexity and Purity were grand...essential components of power that could not be dismissed.","But they were only part of a Civilization, individual elements within greater whole.","If he could elevate his Civilization as unified entity, Complexity and Purity would naturally follow as consequences rather than primary goals.","His Civilization. His Ways...Mana and Hunger both, operating in harmony.","The grander his Civilization became, the more refined its framework and structures, everything else would collectively advance as integrated system rather than scattered achievements.","Noah closed his eyes, consciousness diving deeper into his own existence as he issued command with absolute authority.","\"Show me my Way. Show me my Civilization in totality.\"","HUUM !","The words carried weight!","\"As I enter The Early Infinity Dominion Realm , I wish to outline its initial parameters...something that allows me to envision my Civilization completely. Its parameters should include everything - My Complexity, my Purity, the Edicts of my Way of Mana, the emerging Doctrines of my Way of Hunger, my Towers, my Principles, my Atlas, my Glyphs...every component that defines what I am and what I am becoming.\"","BOOM !","The moment he spoke those defining words, prompts materialized with ceremonial grandeur.","|THE EARLY INFINITY DOMINION REALM - PARAMETERS ESTABLISHED|","|Your existence has borne fruit to the conceptual Weaving of Your Civilization|","|Based on established parameters and current state of development, the Initial Weaving of your Civilization has been designated:|","|The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger.|","|Classification: Nascent Civilization - Genesis Strata (First Designation)|","|Status: Newly manifested, requiring systematic elevation to achieve full realization|","...!","The moment such designation bloomed into consciousness, Noah’s internal perception shifted dramatically.","He found himself standing, or the conceptual equivalent of standing...atop an endless sea of blue-gold Primus Mana.","The surface stretched in all directions without visible horizon, waves of concentrated authority rolling with rhythmic precision.","And atop this infinite foundation, something was being constructed.","The manifestation emerged with deliberate grace, components assembling themselves according to logic.","It looked simultaneously tribal and impossibly advanced, as if combining humanity’s earliest attempts at communal structure with sophistication that wouldn’t emerge for eons.","The main structure took form as The Early Atlas of the Folds ...that grand repository of accumulated knowledge about existence’s geography.","What allowed for thr ridiculous capability to traverse to The Earliest Folds.","But here it manifested as a central plaza , the heart around which everything else was organized.","Its surface pulsed with cartographic precision, displaying territories mapped and territories yet to be explored.","Surrounding this central plaza, his Resplendent Citadels spread out like grand buildings defining district boundaries.","Each Citadel represented different aspect of his cultivation.","The ground itself shone with obsidian-gold brilliance and pulsed with steady heartbeat of Hunger - the refined desire for infinite growth that his Way embodied.","The surface seemed simultaneously solid and liquid, stable enough to support structures while remaining fluid enough to adapt and expand.","Near the Resplendent Citadels , gardens bloomed with impossible vitality.","These weren’t decorative additions but functional components...representations of his Edicts and Mana Glyphs, each one a living expression of glory.","In corners of this Civilization, radiant trees rose toward non-existent sky with branches spreading wide. These were his Principles given botanical form!","The Tree of Perpetual Harvest stood tallest, its branches heavy with luminous fruit that never fully ripened...representing endless accumulation of effort transformed into reward.","The Tree of the Cheating Architect grew beside it with branches that seemed to fold back upon themselves in impossible geometries, each twist and turn representing shortcuts and optimizations that shouldn’t exist but did.","Smaller trees represented his other Principles- Primus Ascension, Mana Supremacy, and Arcana Infinitum.","Around radiant sands that seemed to represent his Early Veiled Shore , one could see dense population of illusory manifestations.","Primordial Fireballs floated like cute miniature suns, bobbing through the air with playful energy that belied their destructive potential at full scale.","Radiant miniature Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms, serpentine and majestic despite diminutive size...wound through the gardens and between structures.","The Honey Badger manifestation of his Arcana prowled near the edges, looking simultaneously fierce and adorable in its reduced form.","It seemed to be patrolling perimeter with serious dedication, as if guarding against threats that couldn’t possibly reach this internal space.","Other components of his accumulated power manifested in ways both obvious and subtle!","Streams of liquid Mana flowed like rivers between structures, their currents carrying dissolved essence of various authorities he’d accumulated and refined.","And everywhere, everywhere , the blue-gold radiance of Primus Mana suffused everything, binding all components into unified whole.","Noah looked at this depiction of his Civilization.","This was his Civilization, made visible through parameters he’d established!","New prompts materialized, providing context for what he witnessed.","|The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger.|","|Your Civilization currently exists at the First Designation: Nascent Civilization - Genesis Strata|","|Subsequent Designations requiring systematic elevation:|","|Second Designation: Cathedral of Order|","|Third Designation: Sovereign Dominion- The Completion of The Early Infinity Dominion Realm|","|CRITICAL RECOGNITION:|","|Elevating your Civilization to the Third Designation and fully forging its frameworks at that level may be the key prerequisite for achieving THE distinction|","| THE entities likely possess fully realized Civilizations far past any of these designations.|","|Your chosen path forward: Systematic elevation through all Designations|"]},{"number":4411,"title":"Chapter 4411: Chapter 4410: Palisades III","paragraphs":["Noah read these words with calm.","The path was becoming clear...not through accumulating raw power alone, but through building- through systematic construction of Civilization that could eventually stand alongside those that had existed for eons!","Further prompts emerged, detailing mechanism for advancement:","|As method to represent advancement of your entire Civilization, the Civilizational Framework is manifesting as THE WALLS OF CIVILIZATION|","|Born from and supported by your Primus Mana, like your entire Civilization, these Walls serve as both protection and measurement of development|","|Advancing the Framework of your Civilization, elevating The Walls, will collectively advance:|","|—Your Complexity and Purity|","|—Edicts of The Way of The Mana Architect|","|—Doctrines of Hunger|","|—All Towers, Atlas, Principles, and integrated components|","|The Walls grow stronger as you grow stronger|","|The Walls expand as your Civilization expands|","|They are both symbol and substance of your developmental state|","...!","In the next moment, the radiant blue-gold Primus Mana sea upon which this entire manifested Civilization floated began to churn .","Waves rose with deliberate purpose, cresting higher than should be possible for liquid surface, and descended upon the Civilization like blessing being bestowed.","The waves crashed down and integrated , flowing over and through structures before beginning to solidify around the perimeter.","Blue-gold essence compressed and crystallized, taking form as radiant wooden walls...primitive in appearance but carrying sophistication that primitive materials could never possess.","Noah merely glanced at them as their name bloomed in his mind right away!","\"The Walls of Civilization, First Stage... FOUNDATION PALISADES\"","HUUM!","They rose to modest height, perhaps three times Noah’s own stature, constructed from what appeared to be blue-gold timber that pulsed with Primus Mana.","Simple but sturdy, these walls represented the earliest stage of civilizational protection...adequate for deterring minor threats while establishing clear boundary between internal order and external chaos.","But Noah could perceive their potential for growth, could sense how systematic elevation would transform them.","Knowledge of the advancement of these walls flowed into his mind like liquid mana...and exactly what they could potentially entail!","|Second Stage- THE ARCHITECT’S BULWARKS: Walls would triple in height and density, transforming from wood to something approaching stone-like durability while retaining Mana’s flexibility.|","At this stage, in its very initial starting point, any creature below 3,000 Quintillion Complexity and Purity would find themselves unable to damage his existence or protected Civilization regardless of method or sustained effort. The Walls would simply deny their attacks at fundamental level!","He felt this knowledge flow in clear as day!","At its very initial starting point, anything below 3,000 Quintillion Complexity and Purity could not even touch him!","The Guider of Order he saw from what Eckert told him had just exceeded what..100 Quintillion?","\"...\"","His eyes burned brightly.","And more information flowed and became clear.","|Third Stage- THE CIVILIZATION AEGIS: A crystalline halo of existence- a border between your Civilization and what is not. Complete transformation into towering structures of pure crystallized authority, incorporating both Mana and Hunger into unified defensive framework. Civilization crystallizes into unassailable permanace. Can withstand Civilizational Suppression.|","Advancing this Framework would advance everything else about him simultaneously.","Noah floated above this manifestation of his Civilization, eyes shining with understanding.","His tyrannical heart, that core of ambition that refused limitation, pulsed with renewed purpose.","\"This is the path forward.\"","\"Build the Civilization. Elevate the Framework. Let everything else follow as natural consequence.\"","His Edicts. His Way. His immensity!","HUUUM!","Around him, The Foundation Palisades stood ready to be strengthened. His Civilization waited to be expanded, refined, and perfected.","And now, with framework established and path clarified, he could finally claim the boons of his Harvest...directing them toward unified elevation of everything he was building.","Yes.","This...was The Way.","Noah smiled and prepared to allocate his rewards.","\"Forge my Foundation Palisades. Let the effort and harvest that came from standing against the brilliance of THE Living Paradox flow into my Civilization.\"","...!","Noah’s voice carried grandeur, establishing direction with absolute authority.","The words shaped intent into manifest reality, designating exactly where accumulated rewards should be directed.","Prompts materialized soon after.","|Perpetual Harvest- Allocation Directive Received.|","|Target: Foundation Palisades (First Stage of Civilizational Framework)|","|Source: Accumulated effort from surviving encounter with THE Living Paradox|","|Magnitude: Extraordinary - reflects impossibility of achievement|","|Processing allocation...|","|Harvest distribution commencing|","The Tree of Perpetual Harvest , standing tallest among the botanical manifestations of his Principles... pulsed with sudden brilliance.","Its branches, which had been heavy with luminous fruit in states of perpetual near-ripeness, now blazed with concentrated green-gold light that showed quintessence of accumulated effort being transformed into tangible advancement.","From the tree’s roots, trunk, and spreading canopy, brilliant radiance surged upward and outward like tide breaking through carefully maintained dam.","The light cascaded across his internal landscape, an endless sea of harvest gushing forth with purposeful direction, flowing inexorably toward the Foundation Palisades that encircled his manifested Civilization.","Noah observed with fascination as the harvest struck the modest wooden walls and began integrating at fundamental level.","The Foundation Palisades responded immediately to this infusion.","The walls began growing taller, extending upward with steady grace rather than explosive expansion.","What had stood at three times his height now reached four times, then five, climbing with measured determination toward greater prominence.","But height was merely the most obvious change.","The structure of the walls themselves became firmer , the blue-gold timber that comprised them gaining density and durability that transcended their primitive appearance.","The grain of the wood seemed to reorganize itself into patterns, each fiber aligning with neighbors to create unified strength far exceeding individual components.","And across the surface of the growing Palisades, something magnificent was manifesting.","Primus Mana Glyphs and Primus Mana Arcana Glyphs began forming, rising through the timber like stars blinking into existence across evening sky!","HUUM !","Each glyph represented condensed understanding of Primus Mana’s fundamental nature.","They appeared in clusters and constellations, creating networks of interconnected meaning.","But even more glorious was the cascade effect rippling through his entire manifested Civilization.","Though the harvest was being directed specifically into the Foundation Palisades, the entire Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger responded with elevation.","All components began brightening, radiating light that suggested fundamental enhancement occurring at every level simultaneously.","The ground pulsed with obsidian-gold glory, Hunger given geographic expression intensifying until the very terrain seemed alive with appetite for infinite growth.","The Early Atlas of the Folds began expanding .","Its surface area increased while maintaining perfect cartographic precision.New regions materialized on its surface, waiting to be explored and claimed in The Earliest Folds!","The Resplendent Citadels grew larger and more elaborate, their architecture becoming more refined while retaining the paradoxical blend of tribal simplicity and impossible sophistication.","Additional wings and towers emerged from existing structures, creating expanded internal spaces without violating external proportions.","Hundreds upon hundreds of additional Primus Mana Glyphs formed throughout the Civilization...not just on the Palisades but in gardens, along pathways, floating above structures like protective sigils.","The immensity of his Primus Mana Haki, that crushing pressure he could exert through sheer concentration of authority, deepened and expanded, capable of reaching farther while pressing harder.","The weight of his Primus Mana-Born Living Existential Armor thickened and refined!","He fould even feel his internal Lens of Civilization become grander as if it would be capable of seeing so much more.","All parts of his existence elevated alongside his Civilization, rising together as unified system rather than scattered individual improvements.","And his Complexity and Purity, metrics he had deliberately chosen not to focus on directly...climbed with inexorable momentum.","|COMPLEXITY AND PURITY ADVANCEMENT|","|Current Values: 103 Quintillion|","|Status: Continuing to rise as Civilizational Framework strengthens|","|Note: Direct focus on Civilization yields superior results to isolated power accumulation|","Noah looked at these numbers with satisfaction.","This confirmed the fundamental correctness of his chosen path.","\"Yes,\" he said, \"this is truly The Way. As of this moment, it is simply a race against time.\"","His eyes gleamed with focus.","\"Find the vessels of THE Living Paradox and collapse them before that entity awakens from suppression. Prepare defensive measures against forces of THE Dead Order who may mobilize at any moment. Advance the Civilization...advance both my Civilizations, Mana and Hunger unified. Success or failure...will depend entirely on civilizational supremacy rather than individual might.\"","BOOM !","His words catalyzed grander waves of radiance erupting across his internal landscape, as if the Civilization itself was responding to declaration of purpose.","At this moment, Noah turned his attention inward toward a different repository...the endless stomach of Hunger where he had stored devoured materials for later processing.","\"Digest the Civilizational Chains of Paradox,\" he commanded with absolute authority. \"Every ounce of their harvest will also flow into the Foundation Palisades . Nothing shall be wasted.\"","...!","In response to his directive, countless shattered and devoured Civilizational Chains of Paradox, held in isolated domain within his existence, were suddenly wrapped by crimson-obsidian light.","The illumination coiled around broken links and fragmented authority with predatory grace, marking them for consumption.","Then they disappeared , vanishing from storage and instantly manifesting above Noah’s Civilization as concentrated sphere of crimson-obsidian brilliance. The sphere pulsed once, twice, building pressure before it erupted downward, surging toward the Foundation Palisades with focused intent.","New prompts materialized to provide context.","| Civilizational Chains of Paradox - Digestion Analsys|","|Source: THE Living Paradox’s Festival manifestation|","|Content: Fragments of truly advanced Civilization far exceeding your current designation|","|Estimated Designation: Unknown - potentially Sixth, Seventh, or higher tier beyond current classification system|","|Despite being mere fragments, these chains contain glimmers of civilizational brilliance sufficient to catalyze significant advancement|","|Major Milestone Achievement Detected|","| Foundation Palisades have absorbed sufficient essence to cross critical threshold|","|Benefits unlocking...|","...!"]},{"number":4412,"title":"Chapter 4412: Chapter 4411: Palisades IV","paragraphs":["Noah closed his eyes as information flooded his consciousness, detailing the profound changes that major milestone had triggered.","Understanding settled into his mind like puzzle pieces finding their proper positions, and satisfaction curved his lips into a smile.","\"I...can now project the Foundation Palisades beyond my internal manifestation,\" he said.","\"I can extend civilizational protection around the physical domains where my people reside.\"","The Infiniverse. The Isolated Civilization.","Oh!","But that was only the first revelation.","The second proved even more consequential.","|Major Milestone Benefits- Foundation Palisades|","|Due to achieving major advancement threshold, your existence is now surrounded by immensity and weight of your Civilization|","|PROTECTION THRESHOLD: No creature possessing less than 200 Quintillion Complexity and Purity can harm your existence through any method or sustained effort|","|CIVILIZATION PREREQUISITE: To damage your existence, the attacker must be member of an established Civilization. Entities without civilizational affiliation cannot harm you regardless of their individual power|","|EXTENSION CAPABILITY: Minor Mana and Hunger Palisades can be granted to eighty-one members of your Civilization|","|—Grants recipients: Equivalent of 25 Quintillion Complexity and Purity in addition to their existing capabilities|","|—Provides: Civilization Prerequisite Protection (can only be harmed by members of other Civilizations)|","|Note: Protection threshold and number of recipients will increase as Civilization advances through designations|","...!","The prompts were glorious, and Noah absorbed every detail with tyrannical satisfaction.","He could extend civilizational protection to eighty-one others...Sigrid, Riya, Khor, his Family, his Seed Members, those he valued most.","Not only that, but at this moment nothing below two hundred Quintillion could harm him... even though his own Complexity and Purity had only just exceeded one hundred Quintillion!","The disparity confirmed what he had been following...Civilization was the true answer!","The benefits it conferred exceeded anything achievable through isolated power accumulation.","Imagine if he had declared for the Harvests to translate to pure Complexity and Purity.","Even if they somehow reached 200 Quintillion, he wouldn’t have established this clear demarcation of power of his Civilization, and would simply just have an idea that he was forging a Civilization...but nothing concrete.","He now had something concrete.","A Nascent Civilization .","With its Foundation Palisades growing grandly!","Noah gazed out at his growing Civilization as the Foundation Palisades continued drinking in essence of digested Civilizational Chains, walls climbing higher and growing more elaborate with each passing moment.","\"Existence is... unpredictable,\" he said thoughtfully.","\"Unpredictability is intrinsic to existence itself, unforeseen circumstances will continue manifesting around me regardless of preparation. The critical variable is not preventing unexpected events, but rather... how effectively I can respond to things I never anticipated.\"","...!","That would determine everything.","He knew with absolute certainty that terrifying situations similar to today’s encounter with THE Living Paradox would occur again.. perhaps soon, perhaps involving other entities of that stature.","Things he had not accounted for. Variables he could not predict.","He needed sufficient power when those moments arrived. Needed to face catastrophe without relying purely on fortune to survive it.","Building his Civilization was the answer!","—","While Noah observed the advancement of his grand Foundation Palisades within internal landscape, elsewhere in external reality, different scene was unfolding.","In a domain isolated by pure Primus Mana, manifested in the same region where THE Living Paradox had recently departed...Riya stood observing the distraught figure of Leonore Rureaux with sympathy.","The space around them pulsed with blue-gold allure, atmosphere itself saturated with Primus Mana serving dual purpose as environment and constraint.","The same radiance comprised the chains binding Leonore, holding her with authority she could not hope to break.","Riya studied the woman for long moment before speaking.","\"I actually feel rather terrible for you, you know. Apparently you possessed no awareness that the man you loved was merely a vessel...a convenient container for something utterly terrifying.\" She tilted her head thoughtfully.","\"Did you know that frightening entity personally? Since you are a Living Paradox while he is THE Living Paradox. .. it’s rather difficult to determine whether you would consider such a being an ancestor of sorts, or perhaps something else entirely.\"","At such words, Leonore Rureaux’s gaze, which had been distant and unfocused, sharpened slightly as she raised her eyes to meet Riya’s.","Profound desolation swam in those depths, and when she spoke, her voice emerged with care despite evident despair.","Despite her Ormordnes!","\"Schrodinger was meant to be The Herald. The singular entity prophesied to guide us through The Fallout , to provide pathway toward survival when THE Loom erupts and consumes everything external to itself. If he was merely... fabrication, deliberate deception, then circumstances were engineered from inception to be fundamentally unsurvivable.\"","BOOM!","Her hands clenched within their bindings.","\"If THE Weavers who approached him claiming something catastrophic was approaching, declaring him Herald meant to save us...if all of that was simply elaborate theater, then they anticipated every possible angle. Ensured that this Fallout will not be something we can survive regardless of preparation or accumulated power.\"","...!","Her words carried despondency so profound it seemed almost physical weight pressing down upon the isolated space.","Riya smiled and nodded with understanding that surprised even herself.","\"I comprehend your meaning entirely. The light of Mana dims progressively even now, which means my back is positioned quite firmly against the proverbial wall. And I wanted my back to only be pressed against the wall by a single man...ah\"","...!","\"The only mitigating circumstance is that man I have been hearing legends about for essentially my entire existence...I’ve just encountered him directly, and he exceeds even the most exaggerated stories. I simply need to do everything within my capability to assist him, to ensure THE Loom doesn’t erase everything residing outside its boundaries.\"","Her expression shifted, becoming more focused.","\"So why don’t you assist me by assisting yourself here? Everything might appear doom and gloom from your current perspective, but we can still attempt resistance. Let us commence with your lover. Or perhaps lovers plural? Hmm, since he maintained multiple bodies simultaneously, did you ever engage with them collectively? Two or three of them and singular you?\"","She paused, reconsidering.","\"Wait, those aren’t critical questions requiring immediate answer, you can tell me later. Just... where are the bodies of your lover currently located? Do you possess knowledge of their whereabouts?\"","...!","Leonore Rureaux fell silent at this inquiry.","Eventually she replied with a heavy tone.","\"It’s utterly futile, isn’t it? If THE Living Paradox occupies those vessels, the moment you approach them, what transpired here will simply repeat itself. You witnessed his power...how can you possibly imagine confronting that again with different outcome?\"","Riya’s smile widened, showing confidence that seemed almost reckless.","\"You needn’t concern yourself with such considerations. If THE Living Paradox is genuinely suppressed as the Ancestor has determined, then we shall simply seize this opportunity to relieve the bodies of your lover from their unfortunate role as vessels. We’ll bring him to a better place with sunshine, flowers and rainbows...\"","She paused deliberately.","\"Well, a place of complete collapse and existential termination, but in collapse there exists no more suffering, correct? No more manipulation or forced hosting of entities beyond one’s control. You dont want another man inside your lover, do you? A merciful ending can be given, all things considered.\"","...!","Her words landed with calculated weight, and after several heartbeats of heavy silence, Leonore Rureaux began speaking with despondent gaze fixed on nothing in particular.","\"In our Sanctuary. In our Desiccated Sleeping Shore...there may exist another body there. Or perhaps THE Living Paradox returned there after departing this location. I genuinely don’t know which possibility reflects current reality.\"","...!","Riya smiled brilliantly at this disclosure, snapping her fingers with a casual gesture that caused the binding chains to dissolve instantly.","Leonore fell forward slightly before catching herself, and Riya moved to stand directly before her with a smile.","\"I knew we could establish productive friendship, didn’t even need to torture...\" Riya said cheerfully. \"Okay then, let us proceed systematically. Tell me absolutely everything...location details, defensive measures, anything that might prove relevant. We have work to accomplish many things before opportunities disappear, friend!\"","Her radiant blue eyes pulsed with power and immensity as she let out a helping hand!"]},{"number":4413,"title":"Chapter 4413: Chapter 4412: Never Meet Your Heroes I","paragraphs":["In another direction across the Transcendent Quantum Folds, a singular figure stood suspended in void-like space.","Khor floated with perfect stillness, her diminutive form surrounded by profound sense of Hunger that wanted to claim absolutely everything within perception’s reach.","The appetite radiating from her wasn’t mere desire...it was a force that recognized no satisfaction because satisfaction would mean cessation of growth.","Her crimson eyes remained half-closed as she repeated sacred words to herself, voice emerging barely above a whisper.","\"Hunger is the fundamental acknowledgment of incompleteness. We hunger because we recognize we are not yet whole...\"","Her form pulsed with obsidian-crimson radiance.","\"Hunger must remain carefree in its pursuit. To hunger with desperation corrupts the purity of desire.\"","The space around her darkened further, as if reality itself was being consumed by proximity to her essence.","\"True Hunger establishes natural hierarchy. Leadership flows toward the hungriest as naturally as water flows downhill.\"","She continued through all Nine Doctrines, each recitation reinforcing her existence’s fundamental nature...reminding herself of immensity accumulated across eons, anchoring consciousness against recent events of confronting THE Living Paradox and witnessing her people’s suffering.","The repetition served dual purpose- meditation and preparing mind and essence for what observation was revealing.","Before her stretched something that should not exist in accessible space...a Unique Doorway to THE Loom itself, manifested as domain hidden across different dimensions of existence simultaneously.","This felt like something only extremely powerful Living Dimensionals would be capable of creating.","Just to traverse the different layers of Dimensional Existence required to reach this point, one needed prerequisite of 1 Quintillion Complexity and Purity minimum.","As for the domain itself...","What Khor observed made her ancient composure pulse and tested.","A grand and sleek Citadel stretched before her perception—architecture and structures that were simultaneously weapons and works of art.","Tall silver buildings rose, their surfaces catching light that didn’t originate from any visible source.","A few hundred Living Existential Armors- Justiciars, were stationed throughout the Citadel.","The Citadel itself connected to something far more disturbing...a manifestation of massive wall that stretched beyond visual limits in both directions. And fused to that wall...","Millions upon millions of Mutated Inevitabilities.","Khor’s hands clenched involuntarily as she witnessed her people...or what remained of them after whatever corruption had been inflicted, trapped within the wall’s substance.","Their bodies pulsed with synchronized rhythm of hunger and pain , tentacles writhing in patterns suggesting perpetual agony.","They seemed to be devouring surrounding atmosphere continuously, consuming existence itself and feeding that stolen essence into the wall they had been merged with.","It was perpetual motion engine of suffering...exactly as THE Living Paradox had described in mocking tones during their confrontation.","Her people reduced to fuel sources, their fundamental nature corrupted and weaponized against them.","Khor looked at this reality with rage contained only by iron discipline accumulated across eons, repeating Doctrines of Hunger in her heart like mantras against descending into mindless fury.","She tracked the Justiciar she had followed from the battlefield, the entity that had fled later after THE Living Paradox manifested, watching as it approached the strongest presence within the Citadel.","That central figure radiated authority reaching 10 Quintillion in Purity.","The approaching Justiciar’s grand armor, sleek white construction incorporating sharp white wings that folded against its back like blades awaiting deployment, opened.","Plates separated along seams invisible until activation, revealing the pilot within.","A female Living Emotive gazed outward with expression mixing exhaustion and urgency.","Her features held delicate beauty that seemed incongruous, her humanoid face framed by silver-white hair that moved as if suspended in water despite no visible current.","Around her, other Justiciars stood with helms removed, revealing additional Living Emotives of various appearances...all humanoid, all carrying exceeding beauty.","The 10 Quintillion Purity Living Emotive, clearly the commanding presence here, turned his attention toward the newly arrived figure.","His armor remained sealed, but his voice emerged with perfect clarity nonetheless.","\"Aileen, what manner of nonsense information did you transmit? Your report claimed THE Living Paradox made personal appearance outside THE Loom’s boundaries? Such occurrence would defy all established protocols.\"","Aileen shook her head with gesture mixing frustration and conviction, meeting her leader’s unseen gaze without flinching.","\"Sir Qanan, I anticipated skepticism, but circumstances demand belief despite improbability. The Will of THE Living Paradox genuinely descended, manifesting through the corpse of a deceased Living Paradox. And it was opposed by an entity possessing terrifying power...possibly exceeding even your capabilities, Sir.\"","She paused, ensuring her words registered fully.","\"I experienced profound sense of suffocation merely from proximity to this being. I couldn’t discern much of their discourse due to overwhelming pressure, but there was explicit mention of Khor, The First Hunger herself. As if she was present, as if she had somehow returned from collapse that should have been absolute.\"","...!","The surrounding Living Emotives exchanged glances mixing disbelief.","Such claims bordered on impossible, yet Aileen’s demeanor showed genuine conviction rather than delusion or exaggeration.","Sir Qanan’s presence seemed to intensify, authority pressing outward as he processed implications.","\"Anything remains possible within existence’s infinite permutations, but I harbor substantial doubt that an entity as monumentally significant as THE Living Paradox would bother dispatching even fractional portion of his consciousness outside. We should represent the strongest existences operating in external territories of THE Loom unless multiple Civilizations began manifesting independently within the Wandering Territories.\"","His tone shifted, carrying challenge mixed with curiosity.","\"This entity you perceived as potentially superior to myself... we shall see. If such being truly exists, eventual confrontation becomes inevitable given our operational parameters.\"","As he spoke, Sir Qanan turned to gaze at the massive wall behind him...that terrible structure incorporating millions of suffering Inevitabilities.","On its outline, barely perceptible unless one knew where to look, a faint doorway could be seen.","A conceptual threshold, a gateway between domains operating under fundamentally different rules.","\"We will continue executing The Will of THE Living Emotive here without deviation,\" Sir Qanan declared.","\"Upon completion of our assigned task, we shall be blessed with entry into THE Loom itself, rejoining our Civilization and receiving rewards commensurate with service rendered. Since the appointed time approaches with increasing proximity, we cannot afford errors or hesitation. We will proceed with utmost caution and not slip up.\"","HUUM!","The surrounding Living Emotives nodded in synchronized agreement, expressions showing dedication mixed with anticipation of promised rewards.","They possessed no awareness that at this precise moment, in the distance beyond their perception’s comfortable reach, ancient eyes blazing with crimson fire of Hunger were observing them with a gaze carrying immeasurable coldness.","Khor watched the Justiciars and the pained Mutated Inevitabilities fused to that terrible wall, and in her heart, judgment had already been rendered absolute.","But she was now calm. She knew what had to be done.","She reached out to the man who made it possible for her to even be here to potentially recrify the wrongs being done to Inevitabilities!","—","Far within the Wandering Territories, a different scene was unfolding with its own weight and consequence.","Noah sat in the center of large plot where radiant golden tree extended upward with impossible vitality, its leaves shining like miniature stellar bodies...each one a sun in compressed form, radiating warmth.","He and several others he had brought into the Sanctuary of The First Farmer had spent the past subjective day observing accumulated accomplishments...witnessing what The First Farmer had built, what Civilization he had attempted to forge.","Attempted .","The word carried weight of unfulfilled potential, of dreams interrupted before reaching fruition.","At this time, behind Noah’s seated figure, another presence descended through air with grace.","Elyndra floated downward with movements resembling falling leaf.","Her gorgeous figure remained ridiculously beautiful.","Golden hair cascaded past her shoulders in waves. Blue eyes, color of deep ocean, held depths of intelligence mixed with carefully concealed conflict.","She wore green dress at this moment, garment that appeared woven from living plants rather than simple fabric, leaves and vines arranged into elegant patterns that moved with her breathing.","She descended until floating beside Noah’s position.","\"Friend that is not quite friend, we have completed preparations. We are positioned to depart and bring the accumulated boons of the Sanctuary to your home domain. Together...our combined forces will halt the advancement of The Dead into the Lands of The Living. Your power and the remnants of my Father’s work...we will be able to get much done.\"","She spoke with confidence that seemed rehearsed, as if convincing herself alongside him.","Noah turned toward her, thoughts dwelling on his own developing Civilization and contemplating what exactly should be done with the Sanctuary of The First Farmer.","He looked at Elyndra’s figure, and in this moment, he consciously activated The Lens of Civilization with focused intent.","The moment perception shifted, prompts bloomed before his vision with revelatory clarity.","|LENS OF CIVILIZATION - INNER TRUTH ANALYSIS|","|SUBJECT: Elyndra, Daughter of The First Farmer|","|SURFACE EMOTION: Confidence mixed with anticipation of departure|","|DEEPER CONFLICT: Profound uncertainty regarding father’s commands to cultivate relationship with you and reclaim Perpetual Harvest|","|CORE BELIEF: Father is wrongly convinced this Principle represents key to achieving THE distinction, even if it is true...is this really the way to go about it?|","|HIDDEN THOUGHT: \"Collaboration is the answer to building Civilization. Father may have lost his Way the day THE Living Emotive collapsed his dreams. I envision what Civilization of Farming could become if freed from obsession with single Principle. But what can I do? I am dutiful daughter. I am loyal extension of his will. Yet I wonder... I wonder...\"","|DEEPEST TRUTH: Conflict between filial obligation and emerging independent philosophy regarding Civilization’s true requirements|","...!","Noah saw her complete inner landscape laid bare, understanding flooding his consciousness with clarity!","His eyes flashed sharply, but his external gaze remained unchanged...calm, analytical, revealing nothing of sudden insight.","He rose to his feet with fluid motion, voice emerging with a casual tone that belied significance of his words.","\"I will visit your Father before we depart.\"","HUUM !","Elyndra blinked in confusion, caught off-guard by unexpected declaration.","\"Oh? Certainly, but..\"","Before she could complete her sentence, Noah took single step and disappeared, the area he was just on showing swirling leaves of brilliance.","Elyndra remained alone in region saturated with scent of harvest and agricultural abundance, surrounded by products of her Father’s obsessive cultivation.","Yet despite being immersed in plenty, her existence seemed to shine with profound sense of desolation .","She sighed deeply, arms wrapping around herself in unconscious gesture of self-comfort, and her gaze continued carrying that terrible conflict...duty warring against emerging conviction that perhaps Father’s path had diverged from wisdom into obsession.","The golden tree above her continued radiating warmth, indifferent to the turmoil of the small figure standing in its shadow."]},{"number":4414,"title":"Chapter 4414: Chapter 4413: Never Meet Your Heroes II","paragraphs":["Not too far from the farm where Noah had left Elyndra standing in contemplative solitude, existence folded upon itself with purposeful precision as his form materialized in different location entirely.","He appeared before The First Farmer, who was engaged in discourse with several Fold Dwellers.. each entity pulsing with authority measuring multiple Quintillions in accumulated power.","Noah gazed at the assembly with calm, his presence causing immediate shift in atmosphere despite making no overtly threatening gesture.","The surrounding Fold Dwellers turned toward this unexpected arrival alongside The First Farmer, whose eyebrows raised with mixture of surprise at the interruption.","\"What is it?\" The First Farmer asked.","Noah didn’t reply with words.","Instead, he waved his hand with a gesture that belied the authority channeling through the motion, releasing faint pulse of blue-gold Primus Mana Haki. ..not the crushing weight he could exert at maximum capacity, but a small measured application of Civilizational pressure.","The brilliance flashed outward in expanding sphere, blue and gold light descending upon the surrounding Fold Dwellers like judgment rendered without trial or appeal.","And the multiple entities possessing Quintillions in Complexity and Purity simply... stopped .","Consciousness fled their existences like startled birds taking flight, leaving only empty vessels frozen exactly where they had been standing.","They were not collapsed or damaged, merely suppressed , their awareness forcibly removed from operational state through overwhelming disparity in civilizational authority.","Oh!","Beings with multiple Quintillions in accumulated essence, caused to lose their very consciousness by mere wave of his hand and controlled release of his Haki.","It was a maddening scene to see as The First Farmer alone was spared.","After achieving this instantaneous suppression, Noah spoke with voice carrying quiet finality.","\"Let us talk. Privately.\"","He waved his hand once more, and brilliant blue-gold light erupted from beneath, wrapping around his feet and The First Farmer’s simultaneously.","The radiance lifted both figures skyward with irresistible force, ascending toward distant heights where perspective would shift and truth might emerge more clearly.","The First Farmer frowned deeply as he looked toward Noah with expression mixing confusion and dawning apprehension, but Noah did not return that gaze.","Instead, he simply activated The Lens of Civilization while looking ahead, his Primus Mana carrying them far into the distant skies.","From this elevated vantage, they could observe the potential Civilization this Sanctuary could have become...seeing it whole rather than fragmented, understanding what might have been if different choices had been made at critical junctures.","Prompts bloomed before Noah’s vision with revelatory clarity.","|LENS OF CIVILIZATION - INNER TRUTH ANALYSIS|","|SUBJECT: The First Farmer|","|SURFACE EMOTION: Confusion mixed with wariness|","|DEEPER STATE: Profound despondency accumulated across eons of failure|","|CORE BELIEF: \"Failure follows my entire existence like loyal companion. Every triumph transforms into catastrophe. Every foundation crumbles beneath weight of circumstance. If only I possessed Perpetual Harvest, the key to properly forging Civilization, I could transform this stagnant Sanctuary into something magnificent. I could finally succeed where I have perpetually failed.\"|","|FOREMOST THOUGHT: \"Why has Osmont brought me here? Did he become suspicious? Does he know? No... impossible. Only Elyndra and I understand the plan. She couldn’t have revealed anything. Could she?\"|","|DEEPEST TRUTH: Ormordnes. Desperation masquerading as strategy, failure internalized until it became identity rather than circumstance|","...!","Noah observed the information flowing from The Lens with detachment, processing psychological landscape of the being beside him.","He couldn’t help but shake his head slowly, the gesture mixing disappointment with something approaching pity.","The two of them floated in elevated skies, gazing down upon many plots of farmland stretching across impossible distances.","Gloriously massive Trees representing Principles rose at intervals throughout the Sanctuary, their branches heavy with conceptual wonder.","Scattered numbers of Fold Dwellers and other Living Existences moved across the landscape below, tending to their duties with practiced efficiency.","Noah looked at this weaving- at what existed versus what could have been, and began speaking.","\"I looked up to The First Farmer once. Resepcted the being who moved against impossible odds, who dedicated his entire existence toward defending those unable to defend themselves. The First Farmer faced Living Existences, Inevitabilities, and Early Creatures alike without flinching. He was so extraordinarily pristine in his dedication that he even cultivated and nurtured Principles when they were things only Early Creatures had access to.\"","Noah’s gaze remained fixed on distant horizon.","\"I even encountered such a being in the Earliest Folds, where he saved me from circumstances that might have proven catastrophic. He even bestowed upon me his failed Seed of a Principle...sharing his disappointment as gift rather than burden. What a magnificent being that was. What an existence worthy of admiration and emulation.\"","His voice dropped slightly, carrying different weight.","\"When... did you become merely a hollow shell of that being?\"","BOOM !","Noah’s words emerged calmly, but they detonated like existential bomb the moment those final syllables concluded.","The figure of The First Farmer trembled as if struck by physical force, his already sickly appearance deteriorating further.","His complexion, which had possessed faint greenish pallor, seemed to become even more diseased at this moment.","He stumbled despite standing on solid platform of Primus Mana , legs failing to support weight that had become suddenly unbearable.","He stopped attempting to maintain standing posture, his figure weakly settling into seated position on the blue-gold platform Noah had manifested.","His gaze became haggard as comprehension dawned regarding exactly why Noah would voice such devastating assessment.","In the next moment, The First Farmer spoke with a voice mixing shock and desperate calculation.","\"How did you discover the plan? Only my daughter and I possess knowledge of what was intended... she couldn’t have revealed anything. Could she?\"","Noah looked at this figure attempting to determine how they had arrived at this confrontation, seeking to identify leak in security rather than contemplating any positive interpretation of circumstances!","Oh!","Still trying to find angle, still searching for mechanism to salvage situation through cunning rather than honesty.","He shook his head with gesture of utter, magisterial finality.","\"Does it truly matter how I discovered your intentions? The more pertinent question is: when did that grand existence who opposed the unfairness Fold Dwellers faced systematically...when did he die? Was he truly extinguished when THE Living Emotive collapsed all your accumulated power? Or did that supposedly magnificent being never genuinely exist, and this compromised version represents what you have always been beneath surface pretense?\"","...!","At Noah’s words, The First Farmer experienced violent coughing fit, body convulsing with force that showed internal structures failing catastrophically.","His eyes flashed with light mixing immensity and profound unwillingness to accept what was being articulated.","When he spoke, his voice held immensity and weight that wished to express all of its grievences all at once!","\"Why does corruption always seem to triumph across existence’s infinite expanse? Those with highest kill counts, those who cheat and deceive without remorse, those who betray trust as casually as breathing...they perpetually seem so much further ahead in every measurable metric.\"","\"Meanwhile, those who are supposedly good , those who conduct themselves according to principles and established ethics...they are massacred systematically. They are violated without mercy. They die without even comprehending why their adherence to righteousness brought only suffering.\"","...!"]},{"number":4415,"title":"Chapter 4415: Chapter 4414: Never Meet Your Heroes III","paragraphs":["His voice became heavier, and he coughed again.","White cloth appeared in his hands through act of will, and when he pulled it away from his mouth, crimson stains marked the fabric with undeniable evidence of internal collapse.","He continued while gazing out at his grand Sanctuary with eyes that saw not what existed but what might have been.","\"I tried to conduct myself properly. I genuinely attempted ethical approaches to every challenge. I forged this Sanctuary, preserved as many beings as capabilities allowed, fought against tyranny with every particle of my existence. I dedicated Everything..every resource, every moment, every fragment of accumulated power, all of My Everythings...toward righteous purposes.\"","His hands clenched the bloodied cloth.","\"And in conclusion... what precisely did I receive as compensation for such dedication? Collapse . My carefully constructed path decimated. Failure cascading upon failure like waves against eroding shore. It manifested repeatedly, cyclically, as if existence itself conspired against virtuous endeavors.\"","His voice carried something approaching mania now.","\"So this time, I contemplated joining the victorious side just once. Aligning with those who accomplish their objectives through any necessary means. Those who seize what they desire without constraint of conscience. I wanted Perpetual Harvest returned to my possession, and so I formulated plan to reclaim it through whatever methods proved necessary.\"","He laughed...the sound mixing bitterness with despair.","\"But it seems even that pathway was foreclosed to me! Even abandoning principles brought only additional failure! Haha! Being supposedly good accomplished nothing for me. Being deliberately corrupt yielded identical result. My entire existence... amounted to precisely nothing !\"","The scene that followed carried weight of tragedy.","The First Farmer laughing with maddened edge while simultaneously coughing, body wracked by dual expressions of psychological breakdown and physical deterioration.","Noah observed this display with calm that suggested neither judgment nor mercy, merely acceptance of what was unfolding.","As The First Farmer wheezed, struggling to draw breath past fluid accumulating in damaged respiratory systems, Noah voiced out an observation.","\"Ironically, all you required was adherence to your original path. You needed to be supposedly good just one final time. Instead of constructing plots and machinations directed against me, you simply needed to ask ...to genuinely propose collaboration without hidden agendas or manipulative subtext.\"","Noah paused, letting those words settle.","\"Do you comprehend what constitutes genuine irony here, First Farmer? I possess capability through another Principle...Existential Rollback, that can restore something to its previous state of being. Unlike other authorities that would merely accelerate your deterioration, this mechanism may possess capability to return you to earlier, more vital configuration. If you had simply maintained your Way, sustained your principles through just one more critical juncture... you may have found yourself on genuine path toward restoration. Toward recovering what was lost when THE Living Emotive shattered your foundations.\"","BOOM !","His words caused The First Farmer to tremble violently, gaze snapping upward to meet Noah’s with expression mixing desperate hope and agonized realization.","\"You... you possess capability to heal me? To restore what was taken?\"","At such question, Noah remained silent for extended moment before moving to sit down beside The First Farmer on the blue-gold platform.","When he spoke again, his tone carried different quality...that of storyteller.","\"Let me tell a story about a Farmer and their Farmhand...their dedicated Farm Laborer who served faithfully across extended duration.\"","Noah’s voice took on a unique cadance.","\"There existed a Farmer who was an Early Creature, possessing unique capabilities but limited understanding of agricultural practices. This Farmer hired a Fold Dweller Farmhand to assist with tending extensive cultivation plots. The Farmhand proved remarkably industrious and dedicated.\"","\"For fifty consecutive years, that Farmhand arrived every morning without fail, tended to the farm with meticulous attention, and departed at day’s conclusion. The Farmer and Farmhand developed close relationship across those fifty years...bonds forged through shared labor and mutual respect.\"","Noah’s gaze remained fixed on distant horizon.","\"On the fifty-first year, on entirely unremarkable day, the Farmer Early Creature installed new security system...a sophisticated monitoring mechanism recommended by a Living Existence after discovering that troublesome Inevitabilities had been consuming produce from nearby plots. Later that same day, the Farmer reviewed recordings from this security system and witnessed something profoundly disturbing.\"","His voice grew quieter.","\"The Farmer observed his supposedly loyal Farmhand harvesting batch of Sacred Carrots from the cultivation plot without permission or notification. Watched as she concealed them within her storage ring. Witnessed as she departed with stolen goods.\"","Noah turned to look at The First Farmer directly.","\"The theft itself wasn’t catastrophic...merely a few Sacred Carrots, nothing that would significantly impact the Farmer’s overall prosperity. But the Farmer experienced profound dismay nonetheless. Why hadn’t she simply approached him with request? He would have willingly provided ten times that quantity plus additional herbs...even his rare specimens, if she had merely asked . If she required resources for any purpose, he would have extended loans from his own accumulated wealth after collaborating so extensively.\"","His eyes carried weight of utter majesty and immensity!","\"But she didn’t approach him. She stole instead.\"","...!","Noah turned calmly to face The First Farmer directly, his voice carrying thr weight of judgment being rendered.","\"What do you believe that Farmer should do regarding his Farmhand who stole from him?\"","...!","The First Farmer trembled at this question, gaze turning outward toward his Sanctuary with expression mixing desperation and dawning comprehension.","When he spoke, his voice emerged weakly but with conviction born of self-preservation.","\"That Farmer must forgive the Farmhand. She labored diligently for him across extensive duration, increasing his prosperity through dedicated service. She only stole something relatively insignificant on single occasion. She committed mistake once...a singular error that could barely be considered genuine transgression. Surely a few carrots, a mistake of such minimal consequence... surely that wouldn’t justify the Farmer severing relationship with someone who contributed so substantially to his success?\"","...!","Noah listened to this reply and shook his head slowly, his gesture booming with finality.","\"The Farmer dismissed the Farmhand the following day after presenting evidence of observed theft. The Farmhand apologized profusely, broke down weeping while explaining that her family had expanded unexpectedly, that she merely needed minor assistance to support her people during temporary difficulty.\"","Noah’s voice remained absolutely level.","\"But the Farmer Early Creature still terminated her employment. And do you comprehend why he made that decision? Because the Farmer understood something critical: if she stole from him now with such casual ease, this was not the first occasion of such theft...merely the first time he caught her stealing. Who could possibly quantify how much she had truly taken across those fifty years? How many times she had helped herself to his resources while maintaining facade of loyal service?\"","...!","At these words, The First Farmer coughed with renewed violence, the white cloth he clutched transforming entirely crimson as blood saturated every fiber.","Noah observed this deterioration and continued speaking with his voice holding an inexorable conclusion.","\"This represents the first time I have caught The First Farmer plotting against me. Perhaps this is not the first time you’ve constructed such schemes against others. Perhaps you’ve directed similar machinations against Fold Dwellers and Living Existences alike throughout your existence. Who could possibly know with certainty?\"","His gaze intensified.","\"So just as that Farmhand was dismissed from service... I will let you go, O First Farmer. I release you from any obligation or connection. Our paths diverge here, absolutely and permanently .\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4416,"title":"Chapter 4416: Chapter 4415: Ashes to Ashes, Dust to Dust!","paragraphs":["At these words, The First Farmer erupted with maddened power, authority flaring desperately as his gaze turned livid with combination of rage and terror.","He roared with voice that made surrounding space tremble.","\"I have only lived virtuously! I have not conducted any-\"","GUH!","Massive globule of blood erupted from his mouth mid-declaration, staining the blue-gold Primus Mana platform with crimson evidence of internal collapse.","He tumbled backward, body losing all coordination as he began wheezing violently.","His form trembled weakly as he raised shaking hand to point accusingly at Noah, attempting to articulate condemnation but managing only...","\"You... you...!\"","He began choking on his own blood as eruption of desperate power seemed to have catastrophically exacerbated his deteriorating condition.","This entire encounter, having his singular remaining hope of reclaiming Perpetual Harvest definitively removed, appeared to be the final element maintaining his cohesion.","And now... his existence flickered like candle in windstorm, about to extinguish at any moment.","Noah observed this being with calm that suggested neither satisfaction nor regret, merely acceptance of natural consequence. Deep within his existence, The Principle of Perpetual Harvest was buzzing with unusual intensity.","A prompt bloomed with somber weight.","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest senses the imminent termination of immense efforts from the one who nurtured its Seed from initial manifestation.|","|The First Farmer, its original cultivator, approaches final cessation.|","|Perpetual Harvest acknowledges debt that can never be repaid.|","...!","When Perpetual Harvest confirmed what was unfolding, Noah calmly waved his hand.","In the next moment, Elyndra materialized beside him...confusion evident on her features before she registered her father’s condition.","She rushed to his side immediately, shock transforming into desperate concern.","Noah spoke with voice carrying clinical detachment.","\"Your father is dying. This is his collapse.\"","...!","Elyndra’s expression transformed into frantic desperation as she knelt beside The First Farmer.","\"What transpired? He was stable! He should have retained many years before deterioration reached critical threshold...\"","...!","She embraced her father as he continued coughing and choking on his own blood, his existence rapidly fading like light dimming toward extinction.","His body appeared sicker with each passing second, flesh becoming translucent, essence bleeding away into surrounding atmosphere.","Elyndra turned toward Noah with expression mixing hope and desperation.","\"Can you do anything? Can Perpetual Harvest possibly...?\"","She looked at him with eyes carrying possibility of salvation, seeking miracle that might reverse what was clearly inevitable.","Noah... shook his head calmly.","He had released The First Farmer. Had made his judgment and rendered his verdict.","He looked at this being who had once been magnificent!","Observed the Sanctuary where genuine Civilization of Farming could have flourished under proper guidance.","And he could only think one thing, repeated mentally with weight of waste recognized.","What a waste. What an absolute waste of potential.","...!","Elyndra grasped her father’s failing form as tears spilled from her eyes, grief overwhelming composure she had maintained throughout previous discussions.","Her voice emerged broken.","\"I’m sorry... I’m so sorry, Father. I should have... I could have...\"","The dying First Farmer continued coughing and wheezing, crimson eyes filled with blood as his gaze turned toward his daughter...attempting to communicate something, perhaps forgiveness or final instruction, but lacking strength to form coherent words.","Moments later...","Silence descended.","\"...\"","Absolute silence replaced the sounds of struggle and failing respiration.","A being that had been of immense power...perished like any old manaless human.","In that silence, Noah felt his existence buzzing with renewed intensity as grandeur of Perpetual Harvest bloomed heavily throughout his being.","Prompts manifested with ceremonial gravity:","|PERPETUAL HARVEST - GRIEF AND GRATITUDE|","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest weeps for the collapse of the one who initially attempted to nurture it from seed to maturity.|","|Effort is effort, even failed effort carries weight and meaning.|","|All the failed efforts of The First Farmer are being gathered by Perpetual Harvest into grand Harvest of Collapse.|","|This accumulated essence will be directed toward Foundation Palisades as final gift from the original cultivator.|","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest will undergo a heavy period of accelerated accumulation and enhanced potency.|","|200 Primus Mana Glyphs of Perpetual Harvest can now be formed.|","|Each Primus Mana Glyph of Perpetual Harvest can perform the following Empowerment effect:|","|—Next 24 hours following The First Farmer’s collapse: Grant 1 Quintillion Complexity and Purity temporarily|","|—After 24-hour period concludes: Standard effect reduces to 0.25 Quintillion per Glyph|","|MEMORIAL DECLARATION:|","|\"Even in collapse, the harvest continues. Every effort, successful or failed, feeds the infinite cycle. The First Farmer planted seeds across eons. Some withered. Some were stolen. But the final harvest... the final harvest belongs to those who continue tending the fields after the original farmer has departed.\"|","...!","The body of The First Farmer ceased all movement entirely, becoming nothing more than empty vessel from which consciousness had permanently fled.","Elyndra held onto that cooling form as she wept, bellowing her grief across the Sanctuary that would now require new stewardship.","Noah stood calmly nearby, gaze fixed on what could have been...on the Civilization of Farming that might have flourished if different choices had been made at critical junctures.","With brilliant eyes reflecting both his own advancement and recognition of another’s fall, he spoke words that carried weight of epitaph and eternal truth.","\" Ashes to ashes, dust to dust. We live, and we die, but the Harvest continues.\"","...!","The wind across the Sanctuary carried his words throughout the domain, and somewhere in the distance, the Trees of Principles seemed to bow slightly...acknowledging passage of their original cultivator while accepting transition of stewardship to another.","The Harvest, indeed, continued.","---","The First Farmer, that enigmatic and powerful being who had once opposed tyranny with every fiber of his existence...had succumbed to injuries dealt by THE Living Emotive and perished.","This news propagated across the Sanctuary with velocity, spreading through existential connections binding all residents of this agricultural domain.","It reached those who had resided here for eons, and shocked the Living Existences who had only recently arrived seeking alliance.","The mysterious and formidable First Farmer was dead ?!","It constituted terrifying and terrible revelation, but the manner in which natives of the Sanctuary received this information revealed layers beneath surface shock.","Their expressions showed they had already possessed some awareness, that even though his actual collapse proved surprising in its timing, this outcome was something they had been anticipating with dread certainty.","The decline had been visible to many. The deterioration inevitable to those who knew.","So at this time, near a simple farmland that represented everything The First Farmer had valued, the weak and the strong of the Sanctuary gathered in unprecedented assembly to lay him to rest!"]},{"number":4417,"title":"Chapter 4417: Chapter 4416: The Perpetual Farmer!","paragraphs":["Hundreds of thousands surrounded a square plot of land shining with bronze-green earth, soil that carried concentrated essence of agricultural principles refined across eons.","The numbers could have swelled to billions or even sextillions if a portion of all those residing under The First Farmer’s protection across scattered Domains and Wheels of Existence had been permitted to attend.","They surrounded what would become The First Farmer’s grave, and at this moment, Elyndra had wrapped her father’s body in green cloth woven from living plants that would return him to the earth he had spent existence cultivating.","She laid him down gently onto the center of the farm plot, planting and returning seed to soil from which new growth might eventually emerge.","Off to the side, Noah watched with calmness.","Beside him stood the manifested forms of Sigrid’s clone observing with crystalline focus, Titano’s massive presence radiating barely contained power, Moiraine’s elegant figure carrying quiet contemplation...all alongside the Emperor Penguin, Erikson, The Queen of Matter, and others.","They watched silently, witnesses to conclusion of existence that had spanned eons.","Slightly farther away, Origin Ama Gias and other Living Existences observed with a sense of shock and stupor.","And near the cluster of Living Paradoxes, Goliath watched the procession occurring with cold eyes that repeatedly returned to fix upon... Noah.","His serpentine gaze held weight of questions!","As The First Farmer was laid down onto the earth like seed awaiting germination, Noah’s attention shifted toward Elyndra and her heartbroken figure.","The loss of a father constituted a unique tragedy...a profound severing of primary bond.","He did not personally harbor strong emotions regarding loss of his own father and had made conscious choice not to pursue his resurrection.","To Elyndra, The First Farmer represented what Noah’s mother was to him, an irreplaceable foundation.","If such figure was lost, the emotional weight would be heavy and potentially unbearable!","So he understood, even if he didn’t personally share her grief.","Perpetual Harvest buzzed within him with brilliant fervor as the one who had nurtured it from seed to a failed seed was planted back into ground that had sustained him across existence’s duration.","Noah watched calmly as Elyndra performed the Farmer’s Greeting with precise ritual gestures...three fingers extended and pointed toward the earth above the grave.","Throughout the surroundings, all those who had been living within the Sanctuary performed identical greeting toward the grave simultaneously.","Hundreds of thousands of hands rose with three fingers extended, creating forest of acknowledgment that should have been returned by the one being honored.","But there would be nobody to return the greeting this time.","Nobody.","The First Farmer’s hands remained still beneath green cloth, incapable of reciprocating final gesture of respect.","As this solemn moment stretched across assembled mourners...","\"We live and we die.\"","HUUM !","Noah’s voice echoed outward with command and purpose that made atmosphere itself tremble, drawing attention from all present despite this being moment dedicated to another’s memory.","Many who did not know him personally turned in astonishment, confusion evident in their expressions.","Those who had loved The First Farmer deeply, beings ranging from 1 Quintillion to 6 Quintillion in accumulated power, felt anger rising at this interruption!","Who was this outsider to speak during such sacred moment?","They wanted to voice objections, to demand he do this or that...","But found to their absolute astonishment that they weren’t even capable of opening their mouths to articulate protest.","Some force held their speech captive, preventing interference with whatever Noah intended to express.","Noah continued.","\"We may plant seeds into the earth one day with hope and careful tending, nurturing growth across seasons and years. Or we may become the seeds ourselves, forever covered by sand and darkness, returning essence to cycles that continue regardless of individual participation.\"","His gaze swept across assembled mourners.","\"From the death of The First Farmer, let abundant harvest bloom from accumulated effort. Let his failures and successes alike feed soil of future cultivation. In the place of The First Farmer who has concluded his season...\"","His eyes began pulsing with radiant green-gold light that made surrounding agricultural essence resonate in sympathy, and he locked onto Elyndra.","\"Let The Perpetual Farmer... arise .\"","BOOM !","The moment those words concluded, reality responded.","His eyes blazed with concentrated green-gold brilliance as in the next moment, the grave containing The First Farmer pulsed with identical radiance.","Elyndra rose from her kneeling position in shock, gaze snapping toward Noah as from all surrounding directions, glimmers of Harvest flooded into her existence with overwhelming force.","Her nine Grand Principles began resonating and pulsing with unprecedented glory!","The accumulated wisdom, the refined authorities, the carefully constructed frameworks all activated simultaneously as if responding to summons they couldn’t resist.","Prompts materialized before Noah’s vision with ceremonial weight!","| The Principle of Perpetual Harvest has granted ultimate Harvest to The First Farmer’s designated successor|","|The Principles nurtured by him over eons resonate with terminal cultivation effort, sending concentrated portion of their accumulated brilliance onto his chosen heir|","|An unknown and unfathomable change is blooming within the subject: Elyndra|","|New designation manifesting: The Perpetual Farmer|","...!","Noah watched with analytical focus as from different areas throughout The Sanctuary, from distant farms and hidden groves where The First Farmer had established Principles...brilliant cascades of accumulated essence pulsed and flowed.","The radiance converged upon the grave before erupting upward to engulf Elyndra completely.","Her Complexity and Purity shattered through 10 Quintillion threshold and continued climbing with momentum suggesting no immediate ceiling.","She looked toward Noah with eyes trembling...mixing gratitude, confusion, and dawning comprehension.","When she met his cold gaze that seemed to hold no discernible emotion despite orchestrating this transformation, she understood completely.","He had known about the plans her father formulated.","Had discovered the machinations and plots directed against him. And even possessing that knowledge...","At this moment, he was facilitating a legitimate succession. Granting her the authority necessary to maintain what her father had built while potentially steering it toward healthier directions.","At such recognition, Elyndra raised her hand with deliberate precision and performed the Farmer’s Greeting toward Noah...showing her desire to establish a foundation for a renewed relationship built on honesty rather than hidden agendas!","An offering to start over with transparency replacing deception!","Noah looked at the three fingers pointed toward him silently, expression unreadable. He began turning around as if to depart without reciprocation.","But halfway through the motion, he sighed audibly and shook his head.","He was still curious of the plan of The First Farmer to cultivate a False THE .","He turned back and raised his own hand, three fingers extending to perform the Farmer’s Greeting in return.","Perhaps it was influence from Perpetual Harvest buzzing within him with unusual intensity. Perhaps it was genuine inclination toward allowing second chances when circumstances permitted.","Their greetings met across the distance separating them, and the green-gold light intensified dramatically- becoming so brilliant that many observers fell to their knees in shock and awe.","They looked toward Elyndra while voices began calling out in synchronized reverence.","\"The Perpetual Farmer!\"","\"THE PERPETUAL FARMER!\"","Complexity and Purity continued surging around Elyndra amidst storm of Principles resonating with her essence, elevating her toward heights her father had never achieved despite eons of effort.","\"...\"","Noah turned away from the spectacle, moving toward different destination as everywhere he passed, Living Existences and Fold Dwellers alike scrambled rapidly to clear pathway...instinctive deference to a presence carrying civilizational weight they couldn’t consciously quantify but felt nonetheless.","This included Origin Ama Gias and Duke Gwendolyn among other nominally powerful beings whose entire existences felt terrifying sense of oppression when they met Noah’s passing gaze.","Their accumulated power meant fucking nothing before whatever authority he now embodied.","Noah continued his path with purposeful stride until he came to stand before the cluster of Living Paradoxes who had maintained careful distance from primary proceedings.","He positioned himself directly before Goliath...that enigmatic being who had been attempting to probe and understand him throughout recent events!","The scary fucking guy, Goliath!"]},{"number":4418,"title":"Chapter 4418: Chapter 4417: Collapsed Civilizations I","paragraphs":["Noah met that scrutinizing stare directly and activated The Lens of Civilization.","And what he discovered proved illuminating.","|LENS OF CIVILIZATION - COMPREHENSIVE ANALYSIS|","|SUBJECT: Goliath|","|SURFACE IDENTITY: Living Paradox (False designation)|","|DISPLAYED METRICS: 2 Quintillion False Paradoxical Complexity and Purity|","|ACTUAL IDENTITY: Veiled Living Origin|","|TRUE METRICS: 46 Quintillion Veiled Origin Complexity and Purity|","|CLASSIFICATION: Remnant of Collapsed Civilization of Origin exterior to THE Loom|","|CURRENT THOUGHTS:|","|\"Who is this Osmont truly? Does he possess any connection with forces from THE Loom? Should I inform the other Remnants about this anomaly? Risk revealing our existence?\"|","|DEEPER CONCERN: Uncertainty whether Osmont represents threat or opportunity to Remnants’ long-term survival objectives|","...!","Noah absorbed these revelations calmly!","He looked at Goliath closely, studying his physical manifestationwith enhanced perception.","The being was a burly, muscular figure despite adopting human form, with white hair dancing wildly around features that seemed more appropriate to ancient Beast than civilized humanoid.","His human configuration barely constrained something far more primal, and his eyes revealed serpentine white pupils that provided glimpse of his terrifying snake-like authentic form.","Noah stood before such formidable being and spoke with a voice carrying calm certainty.","\"Goliath... and you are actually a Veiled Living Origin from a Collapsed Civilization? THE Living Origin, that grand existence who embodied beginnings themselves, had its Civilization collapsed ?\"","BOOM !","He articulated such profound questions in utterly calm manner that it was disconcerting!","Goliath’s heavy eyes opened wide with shock, and in the next moment, his sizable body erupted with terrifying waves of Complexity and Purity that exceeded most others present!","The Living Paradoxes positioned around him were blown backward in shock as the carefully maintained disguise shattered , revealing what Goliath truly was.","His visage radiated immense white light of Origin ...not Paradox but the fundamental authority of beginning preceding all other principles!","His titanic figure blazing with 46 Quintillion Complexity and Purity threw down both hands like hammer punches descending toward Noah with force sufficient to crater multiple Folds!","Noah looked at these devastating punches approaching with calm. He didn’t raise hands to block or manifest protective authorities.","He simply stood there.","BZZT !","An invisible field of power buzzed around him, a manifestation of his Civilization’s Foundation Palisades operating at conceptual level rather than physical structure.","The field flicked these heavy punches aside as if they were strikes from petulant child rather than being possessing 46 Quintillion in accumulated power.","Noah took single step forward, and glimpse of his Civilization’s full weight imposed itself upon Goliath.","That crushing pressure, that authority of a unified framework versus scattered individual might...descended with inexorable force!","Goliath’s expression became heavy as his existence trembled under tbe strain.","His form bent slightly beneath a weight that shouldn’t be possible!","He looked coldly at Noah through serpentine eyes.","\"Who are you, truly? Not the surface identity you present, but your authentic nature and allegiance?\"","Noah replied with a voice maintaining perfect calm.","\"What I am not is some force affiliated with THE Loom. I possess no connection to that domain or the Civilizations secured within its boundaries. What I am... is someone profoundly interested in this concept of Collapsed Civilizations you represent.\"","His eyes gleamed with focus.","\" THE Living Paradox and THE Living Emotive collapsed THE Living Origin and multiple other Civilizations besides that? And you represent surviving Members of these destroyed Civilizations? Where precisely have you all been hiding across the eons since that catastrophe?\"","Noah’s words emerged with steady precision.","If Goliath existed among Living Existences while maintaining false identity, were there numerous others hidden throughout the Transcendent Folds?","If many Remnants from Collapsed Civilizations survived, where would they cluster or conceal themselves most effectively?","His eyes brightened with sudden insight... perhaps the vast Wandering Territories themselves?","At this moment, Goliath’s white eyes flashed with pure white light of Origin as he studied Noah comprehensively.","His heavy voice echoed with mixture of confusion and reluctant fascination.","\"You genuinely aren’t affiliated with THE Loom ... how is this possible? I can sense unmistakable aura of an established Civilization surrounding your existence...yet what Civilization could that possibly be? We haven’t observed any genuine Civilizations rising across the eons since the catastrophes...\"","Noah’s smile widened at these words.","\"You haven’t been observing carefully enough in recent days. Come now, tell me regarding yourself and these Collapsed Civilizations. Oh, and provide anything you can regarding Schrodinger...and where his other bodies might be concealed.\"","At mention of that name, Goliath frowned with evident confusion.","\"Schrodinger? Why would you concern yourself with him? What relevance does he hold to current circumstances?\"","Noah smiled with expression mixing calm and dark amusement as he breathed deeply...savoring air of the Sanctuary that felt cleaner now, as if The First Farmer’s collapse had released accumulated stagnation.","He spoke calmly with words of glorious and unfathomable revalation!","\"Because Schrodinger and all his various bodies serve as Vessels for THE Living Paradox ...the fucker who has just recently made personal appearance outside THE Loom .\"","...!","BOOM !","Goliath’s eyes opened wide at this information, his serpentine pupils dilating with shock and approached existential horror!","The other Living Existences positioned nearby, those barely listening while maintaining polite distance, felt their weavings buzzing as if they were hearing information far too grand for their existences to safely process.","THE Living Paradox? Here?","What?!","Goliath’s expression transformed from shock to stern determination as he voiced heavily.","\"I must warn the other Remnants immediately. If THE Living Paradox has begun manifesting at this time, if the timeline we expected before The Fallout has accelerated beyond our projections... we may have far less preparation time than anticipated before THE Loom erupts and The Fallout consumes everything.\"","His white light intensified as urgency replaced confusion!","Noah watched with bright eyes as it seemed Existence outside THE Loom ...still had more surprises!","---","Collapsed Civilizations.","The phrase carried a unique weight beyond simple historical notation, encompassing tragedy and occasional triumph.","Across existence’s infinite expanse and temporal duration, countless empires had risen to magnificent heights before succumbing to internal decay or external conquest.","Yet the nature of collapse was rarely absolute.","More often than not, those ostensibly destroyed retained remnants...fragments of accumulated knowledge, survivors carrying cultural memory, artifacts preserving technological achievements.","These scattered pieces persisted like embers after conflagration, glowing faintly amid surrounding darkness.","Now, these remnants could manifest two fundamentally divergent outcomes.","Some amounted to nothing beyond nostalgic recollection...beings who remembered glory at civilization’s peak while lacking capability or will to reconstruct what had been lost.","They became living museums, preserving history without advancing it, eventually fading into obscurity as even memories deteriorated across generations.","But other remnants possessed such concentrated grandeur, such distilled essence of what their civilization had represented, that they succeeded in reforging collapsed frameworks!","Oh!","Rebuilding from ruin. Establishing new foundations upon bedrock of old principles refined through catastrophic failure.","Rarely .","For it was unfathomably difficult to restore that which had been shattered...like attempting to reassemble a shattered mirror and expecting reflection to emerge flawless rather than distorted by innumerable fracture lines.","The weight of prior failure, the trauma of collapse, the scattered nature of surviving resources... all conspired against successful resurrection.","Yet occasionally, against impossible odds, remnants succeeded in becoming phoenix rather than monument.","Those rare instances when broken became whole again represented triumphs worthy of eternal commemoration.","At this moment.","On the other side of The Veil, in territories designated as The Lands of The Dead.","A vast expanse stretched in all directions, filled with brilliance of Order and Death intermingling.","There was white radiance suggesting absolute structure coexisting with obsidian luminescence suggesting inevitable cessation.","The combination created an atmosphere simultaneously peaceful and oppressive, suggesting finality accepted rather than resisted!","At the center of this impossible domain, a woman adorned in pristine white dress examined her hands with detachment.","Their color appeared healthy and simultaneously not...a paradoxical state.","If one observed her entire figure with enhanced perception, they would witness her complete visage: fair skin shining like crystallized essence of graying-white purity, face holding immeasurable beauty refined beyond normal aesthetics into something approaching platonic ideal .","Her hair shifted constantly between obsidian darkness and brilliant white, never settling upon single configuration...as if even basic characteristics couldn’t decide between life and death, between what was and what had become.","But her eyes... her eyes held the grand weight of Civilization itself!","This...was THE Dead Order!"]},{"number":4419,"title":"Chapter 4419: Chapter 4418: Collapsed Civilizations II","paragraphs":["THE Dead Order.","She could effectively be considered the Leader of The First Collapsed Civilization to fall under hands of THE Living Paradox .","As she continued examining herself with an expression of satisfaction and lingering uncertainty, she spoke.","\"I did not anticipate sensing the vileness of THE Living Paradox manifesting on the other side of The Veil. Not so... precipitously. Not before even I possessed capability to traverse that boundary and establish presence among the Living territories.\"","HUUM!","Her words catalyzed heavy reaction throughout surrounding expanse as dozens of nearby figures rose with synchronized fervor.","Each entity emanated staggering concentrations of power...some exceeding 100 Quintillion, others reaching 200 Quintillion, a select few approaching 300 Quintillion in Complexity and Purity.","They had been refined through her implementation of True Order, systematically elevated beyond what scattered cultivation would have achieved.","Several voices echoed with passionate conviction.","\"O Order, permit us to embark on your behalf and pursue justice for transgressions inflicted upon you!\"","\"Grant us honor of confronting that entity which collapsed our original framework!\"","\"We shall demonstrate how Death refined through Order surpasses Living existence corrupted through Paradox!\"","WAA!","\" Justice ?\"","THE Dead Order smiled at such proclamations.","Her eyes flashed with immense hatred carefully cultivated and preserved across eons...annemotion refined into a weapon rather than allowed to remain chaotic passion.","She spoke with a voice maintaining perfect calm despite volcanic fury beneath surface composure.","\"I have been wishing for justice across countless eons, and it has perpetually evaded my grasp. That entity possesses advantages I cannot currently match through direct confrontation...civilizational supremacy that would crush our forces regardless of numerical superiority or individual excellence.\"","Her gaze swept across assembled Guiders of Order.","\"At our current developmental level, we are not yet adequately prepared for final confrontation. My intention was to continue establishing True Order across entirety of The Lands of The Dead, nurturing you systematically until achieving thresholds of 1,000 Quintillion or beyond before deploying forces against external targets.\"","She paused, allowing weight of that timeline to settle.","\"But since the vile brilliance of THE Living Paradox has appeared and subsequently disappeared within the Lands of The Living... I must modify strategic planning. I will deploy a select contingent prematurely to investigate what transpired, to gather intelligence regarding his manifestation outside THE Loom’s secured boundaries.\"","...!","The moment she articulated this modification, multiple Guiders of Order rose with expressions mixing honor and determination at being selected for critical reconnaissance.","Forgemaster Vulcan, that imposing figure radiating concentrated authority, stepped forward at the forefront!","\"O Great Mistress of Order , allow me the profound honor of moving on your behalf...\"","Others rose with their own immaculate vows, each proclaiming dedication to establishing Order on her behalf while discovering what circumstances had permitted THE Living Paradox’s temporary manifestation.","\"My existence is yours to deploy, O Order! Direct me as instrument of your will!\"","\"I shall uncover truth regardless of resistance encountered, bringing intelligence worthy of your glorious brilliance!\"","\"Grant me this opportunity to demonstrate devotion refined through your elevation!\"","...!","Oh!","The gorgeous figure of THE Dead Order smiled with an expression of satisfaction mixed with broader vision extending beyond immediate concerns.","She looked upward toward something that only she could perceive...perhaps viewing The Veil’s structure itself, perhaps observing patterns invisible to subordinates despite their considerable power.","When she spoke again, her voice held the glorious weight of revelation.","\" You must understand fundamental truth: The Lands of The Dead are vaster than The Lands of The Living by orders of magnitude that defy easy quantification. All those entities that have perished across eons of existence... they reside here. Every collapse, every termination, every cessation feeds this domain.\"","Her eyes gleamed with anticipation of long-delayed plans finally reaching fruition.","\" Collapsed Civilizations exist here...scattered remnants maintaining vestigial identities, preserving memories of former glory while lacking unified purpose or coordinated advancement. They will remain veiled and isolated no longer. We will leave them fragmented and directionless no longer.\"","She raised one hand with gesture carrying absolute authority.","\" Some among you shall venture into the Lands of The Living to investigate what has occurred regarding THE Living Paradox’s manifestation. At the same time, The Young Living Order and this...Osmont. Gather intelligence. Return with actionable understanding that will inform our eventual confrontation.\"","Her voice intensified.","\" While the rest of you... shall spread systematically to all corners of The Lands of The Dead and impose True Order without exception. All remnants of Collapsed Civilizations...those fragmented survivors maintaining separate identities, shall be unified under singular framework. The only Civilization permitted to exist across all territories outside THE Loom... shall be Order itself.\"","Her final words carried finality!","\" There will be no competing frameworks. No alternative philosophies. No scattered authorities pursuing divergent objectives.\"","Her eyes blazed with white brilliance of absolute conviction!","\" There will only be... Order.\"","BOOM !","Brilliant white light of Order pulsed outward like incandescent sun achieving glorious ascension, washing across The Lands of The Dead with authority that could not be denied or resisted!","Oh!","The assembled Guiders of Order bowed in synchronized acknowledgment before dispersing to execute directives that would reshape existence outside THE Loom.","Some would cross The Veil and investigate Living territories where The Young Living Order and THE Living Paradox had manifested.","Others would spread throughout vast expanse of The Lands of The Dead, systematically locating and assimilating remnants of Collapsed Civilizations who had maintained fragmented existence for eons.","All would serve singular purpose...establishing True Order as the only legitimate framework operating beyond THE Loom’s boundaries.","THE Dead Order remained in position after they departed, gaze still fixed on something invisible to others.","Perhaps she was calculating timelines until The Fallout .","Perhaps she was contemplating strategies for eventual confrontation with THE Living Paradox , or the one known as Osmont .","Perhaps she was simply savoring the approaching culmination of eons-long preparation!","Her smile showed anticipation mixed with carefully controlled hatred, and her eyes held certainty that whatever setbacks had occurred in distant past, whatever catastrophes had transformed her from Living to Dead...","This time would be different.","This time, Order would triumph over Paradox .","This time, the scattered remnants would become a unified Civilization capable of challenging even those secured within THE Loom!","The very essence of existence, the wind across The Lands of The Dead carried her conviction throughout the domain.","And everywhere it touched, Order intensified its grip..systematically transforming chaos into structure, converting scattered elements into coordinated whole.","The Remnants would be found and unified.","And when they did, existence outside THE Loom would know only one authority.","Order. Absolute and Indefatigable!"]},{"number":4420,"title":"Chapter 4420: Chapter 4419: You Hold My Everything I","paragraphs":["Noah stood within the Early Veiled Shore, observing a select assembly of beings fortunate enough to be among the eighty-one recipients designated to receive the Boon of The Minor Mana and Hunger Palisades.","The atmosphere hummed with concentrated authority as bodies pulsed with newly integrated brilliance, systems of existences adjusting to sudden influxes of civilizational protection and raw Complexity and Purity!","Heidrun stood tall in a field of verdant-gold grasses, her magnificent goat form bellowing joyously as the transformation completed.","She was completely unaware that the diligent Malphas in his immaculate butler attire had already positioned himself nearby with pristine bucket, prepared to commence collection of the glorious Sacred Mead of Existence the moment her elevation stabilized sufficiently.","She would be put to work!","Yoshinami occupied a corner of the Early Veiled Shore in her spider form, her numerous terrifying crimson eyes shining with predatory light of hunger barely restrained.","Even though she currently held an excess of 25 Quintillion Complexity and Purity due to the Palisades boon, her unique nature meant she could likely terminate a creature possessing 100 Quintillion!","Noah observed all this with satisfaction as beside him stood Khor’s primary manifestation, The First Hunger herself, recently elevated through multiple cascading advancements.","He turned his gaze upon her specifically, clearly perceiving the mark of the Minor Mana and Hunger Palisades adorning her existence.","The mark manifested as an illusory blue-gold crown formed from the architectural structure of palisades themselves, floating above her head with gentle rotation...neither physical nor purely conceptual, but something between, visible only to those with sufficient perception.","While standing beside him, Khor spoke.","\"How do you wish to approach that Citadel of Justiciars? The one I observed containing the doorway to THE Loom?\"","At this inquiry, Noah contemplated the information he had accumulated from Khor regarding The Living Emotives piloting those Justiciars, the horrifying wall of Mutated Inevitabilities that should theoretically connect to THE Loom’s infrastructure, and the faint doorway inscribed upon that terrible structure.","Thinking specifically about the conversation between Living Emotives that Khor had witnessed and transmitted, Noah asked with smile mixing amusement and cynicism.","\"What do you genuinely think of their proclamations that they were promised entry into THE Loom after accomplishing their assigned mission? My Primus Mana and instincts both insist it’s utter fabrication...\"","\"That THE Living Emotive promised them this reward and maintained their hope across eons purely to extinguish it for perverse entertainment at conclusion. That even if we assault that location and attempt passage through that faint doorway, we may discover it leads precisely... nowhere .\"","...!","He articulated such heavy implications with a casual tone!","And Khor remained silent briefly before sighing with sound mixing weariness and contained rage.","\"Outsider, I simply want you to promise me something,\" she said.","\"If we genuinely obtain opportunity to make THE Living Paradox and his collaborators pay for their crimes... you allow me sufficient time to torture him and THE Living Emotive as extensively as they have been torturing the Inevitabilities across eons.\"","WAA !","Noah nodded calmly at these words, understanding the need underlying them.","\"Here’s to us actually reaching the point of possessing capability to stand against those psychopathic beings. When that moment arrives, your request will happily be honored\"","Khor nodded with gratitude before turning her attention toward the Nest area populated by Inevitabilities within this Early Veiled Shore.","Her gaze locked specifically onto the visage of Bob...positioned centrally within the crystalline obsidian structure, surrounded by other Inevitabilities investigating him with cautious curiosity.","She addressed Noah without shifting her focus.","\"That Little Bobby has become completely fused with the unfortunate Mutated Inevitability I’ve been attempting to restore. I’ve only succeeded in stabilizing the union between them thus far, and I’ve made modest progress in systematically stripping away whatever mutational corruption was forcibly imposed.\"","\"However, I require it to become somewhat stronger to continue procedures with optimal efficiency. Could you grant Little Bobby the Palisades boon?\"","...!","Khor asked such a question while Noah observed Bob...who was surveying surrounding Inevitabilities with expression mixing confusion and resignation, while his daughter stood beside Henry with visibly worried demeanor.","Noah shook his head with smile of amusement as he contemplated how Bob continuously received substantial power ups while bypassing countless others simply due to circumstances he stumbled into.","This entity genuinely demonstrated increasing resemblance to archetypal protagonist...a ridiculous cockroach that never perished, accumulating boons seemingly by accident while others struggled deliberately for incremental advancement.","But even recognizing this pattern, Noah made the selection to include Bob among the eighty-one slots.","HUUM !","In the next moment, brilliant blue-gold radiance descended upon Bob’s form.","The Mark of The Palisades materialized above his head like ethereal crown, and his Complexity and Purity, alongside that of the Mutated Inevitability fused with him, began surging explosively toward 25 Quintillion threshold.","Khor smiled.","\"Thank you, Outsider. Let me know when we prepare to strike that Justiciar Outpost.\"","She proceeded to move toward Bob and the assembled Inevitabilities, already contemplating procedures to completely separate or restore!","Noah observed this calmly, his mind cataloguing extensive tasks demanding attention.","And there were many!","Attacking that Justiciar Outpost to investigate the doorway and assess whether it genuinely connected to THE Loom or represented elaborate deception.","After sufficient preparation, raiding the Desiccated Sleeping Shore that Riya had extracted intelligence about from Leonore Rureaux, plus other potential locations concealing Schrodinger’s vessels.","And additionally, there existed the newly revealed grandeur of Collapsed Civilizations, with Goliath serving as key to understanding that entire hidden ecosystem.","\"Light work... light work!\" Noah muttered with eyes vibrant with anticipation.","Even though the accumulated tasks appeared overwhelming when itemized, all of it would continue facilitating growth of his Civilization...each challenge overcome translating into advancement that elevated entire framework simultaneously!","As he contemplated this, his surroundings *","buzzed with unusual intensity as his existence felt even grander immensity settling across his fundamental structures.","He traced the cause to his Foundation Palisades...within the manifestation of his Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger, they were growing taller and more elaborate once more, and because they advanced...","His Complexity and Purity, his Glyphs, Towers, Atlas, Haki, all integrated components of his existence collectively elevated in synchronized harmony!","The reason being....","Prompts bloomed with their ceremonial weight.","|The Harvest of Collapse from The Death of The First Farmer has been fully incorporated into the civilizational framework|","|PROTECTION THRESHOLD INCREASED:|","|Previous: 200 Quintillion Complexity and Purity required to harm your existence|","|Current: 300 Quintillion Complexity and Purity required to harm your existence|","|Your own Complexity and Purity has broken past 150 Quintillion threshold|","|All integrated systems elevated proportionally|","|BOON ENHANCEMENT:|","|Minor Mana and Hunger Palisades empowerment increased from 25 Quintillion to 35 Quintillion Complexity and Purity|","|All currently selected recipients will experience synchronized elevation|","HUUM!"]},{"number":4421,"title":"Chapter 4421: Chapter 4420: You Hold My Everything II","paragraphs":["The advancement from The First Farmer’s accumulated efforts fully distributed across his Civilization’s architecture, demonstrating how even tragic conclusions could fuel future growth.","Now, for any entity to even contemplate penetrating his defenses, they required an excess of 300 Quintillion Complexity and Purity, and membership in established Civilization.","They were dual prerequisites that eliminated vast majority of potential threats!","He was growing steadily, systematically, and building foundations that would support eventual confrontation with THE entities themselves.","He continued deliberately avoiding comparison with others regarding progression velocity, because...","\"Comparison is the thief of joy, and in my case, probably also the thief of sanity. If I spent time measuring my advancement against beings like THE Living Paradox who have cultivated across eons, I’d either develop crippling inadequacy complex or dangerously inflated ego depending on how I chose to rationalize the disparity...and my ego is not that big, is it...?\"","....!","He smiled calmly.","It was better to focus on his own glorious trajectory, celebrate the incremental victories, and acknowledge that the only meaningful competition is against his previous self!","....!","He smiled at his own philosophical meandering as he also considered the boons of The Primus Mana Glyphs of Perpetual Harvest ...two hundred Glyphs that could each grant 1 Quintillion Complexity and Purity for the next 24 hours.","That represented total of 200 Quintillion waiting to be distributed!","His initial instinct was consuming all empowerment personally, but... he wanted to test something specific. And the subject of this experiment was The Living Order herself...Sigrid!","He walked across golden sands toward The Abode of the Early Creature where Sigrid currently resided.","The Abode that now contained countless pocket dimensions where Barbatos, Adelaide, Athena, and other members of his modest harem were... cultivating in various forms.","After all, in existence, there existed different methodologies of advancement!","—","Inside The Abode of The Early Creature, Osmont.","Though it appeared as grand tribal building outwardly on the Early Veiled Shore, internally it stretched into blue-gold stellar hall surrounded by numerous doors leading to different pocket dimensions...each one customized for specific purposes or residents.","At this time, within one particular pocket dimension.","The space shone with white and blue radiance as rivers of pure Order intermixed with currents of blue Mana in complex patterns.","Apart from the radiant sea below, there existed reflecting sea above, and suspended between them were stellar white rivers moving with absolute precision...each droplet following trajectory ordained by Order.","On the golden sands of this place reclined the primary body of Sigrid, adorned in loose damp white robe that clung to her curvaceous figure.","Her dark-and-white hair shone with radiant glow, wet and hanging over shoulders and across robe in a gorgeous artistic disarray.","The Mark of The Palisades floated above her head like ethereal crown, making her entire figure appear even more radiant...like a radiant fairy from ancient times contemplating mysteries in sacred space!","At this moment, Noah materialized and sat beside her on the sandy beach, breathing deeply of potent atmosphere saturated with Mana and Order while asking casually.","\"What’s occupying your thoughts?\"","She replied while leaning her shoulder against him, her head tilting to rest upon his shoulder.","\"I am contemplating my place in all this. Whether I am merely bringing trouble through my connection to Order, or if I will accomplish something genuinely significant with it. Burden or asset. Problem or solution.\"","Trouble, or something significant.","At such words, Noah smiled and looked out at the brilliance of Mana all around them.","\"Why not both? Most truly interesting things in existence manage to be simultaneously problematic and invaluable. And I can’t get enough of trouble.\"","...!","As soon as he articulated such words, radiant green-gold rivers of light began descending from above...a manifestation of Perpetual Harvest’s accumulated empowerment.","They crashed onto Sigrid’s figure with concentrated force, and with each blast of brilliance she absorbed, she felt her power explode upward by full 1 Quintillion!","She looked toward Noah with dazzling eyes.","\"What is this?\"","It constituted stupendous sensation as beside her, Noah simply smiled.","\"Just some empowerment stemming from efforts of failure...The First Farmer’s accumulated harvest transformed into elevation. I have been reaching significant milestones recently and I want to observe if something notable occurs when you achieve a sufficiently profound threshold of your own.\"","...!","Sigrid trembled at his words.","This entire time, he had been giving and giving everything to her without expectation of reciprocation or demand for equivalent exchange.","Resources, protection, opportunities, affection... lots of affection, and just... everything .","She desperately wanted to provide something substantial in return!","To produce tangible results worthy of his investment.","Sigrid bit her lip as her hand found Noah’s strong hand, her fingers intertwining with his.","When she spoke, her voice emerged with intensity.","\"I will not claim to comprehend all intricacies of existence. I will not pretend to understand how existential forces truly operate at fundamental levels. But... you must understand one thing. And that is...you hold My Everything . Not metaphorically. Not an exaggeration. You possess the entirety of what I am and what I might become. My Order. My essence. My potential. My heart. My Everything ...It is all yours.\"","...!","A blinding light of Order pulsed at such declaration, and Noah looked toward Sigrid with somber recognition of what she was truly offering.","Empowerments continued descending upon her as she maintained unwavering gaze, eyes set with determination!","Prompts materialized at this moment!","|The Resurgence of THE Living Order , a critical component of a once-grand Civilization, has completely given itself to you and your Civilization|","|PERMANENT CONSEQUENCE:|","|The Civilization of Order has forever lost opportunity to be restored as independent Civilization|","|However, it possesses potential to rise from ashes as something grander through integration with your Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger|","|Order can thrive through Mana and Hunger as symbiotic rather than competing principles|","|FUTURE BENEFITS:|","|After reaching significant developmental milestones, Past Features of The Civilization of Order will be permitted to bloom within your Civilization|","|Access to refined authorities, architectural principles, and strategic capabilities accumulated across Order’s existence will become available|","...!","BOOM !"]},{"number":4422,"title":"Chapter 4422: Chapter 4421: Siphoning! I","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly as he gazed at Sigrid.","\"You didn’t need to do that.\"","She smiled with an expression mixing serenity and fierce conviction.","\"Please, I cannot provide you with much given my current state. Let me at least offer thi-\"","...!","BOOM !","Her words ceased abruptly as blinding white brilliance exceeding anything manifested previously erupted from her existence, forming a pillar that engulfed Noah as well in concentrated radiance!","This occurred precisely after a light of Empowerment descended that allowed her Complexity and Purity to exceed 100 Quintillion threshold...apparently triggering something far more significant than a simple numerical milestone.","New prompts bloomed.","|A significant existential threshold has been surpassed by The Resurgence of THE Living Order|","|This threshold permits The Resurgence to begin receiving full inheritance of the Collapsed Civilization of Order|","|CIVILIZATIONAL AUTHORITY OF ORDER - TRANSFER INITIATED|","|The Resurgence of THE Living Order has begun siphoning and drawing from the Civilizational Authority and accumulated Complexity and Purity of the Collapsed Civilization of Order|","|At its core, Order aligns with The Living rather than The Dead|","|Therefore, The Resurgence of THE Living Order holds higher commandment over Order than THE Dead Order|","|CONSEQUENCE:|","|An Unbreakable Link has been formed from The Resurgence of THE Living Order to THE Dead Order|","|The gradual transference of The Civilizational Authority of Order has commenced|","|This process cannot be prevented, reversed, or interrupted through any known mechanism|","...!","BOOM !","As Noah processed these revelations, his perception shifted dramatically...finding illusory versions of himself and Sigrid floating in vast expanse of white and black brilliance that seemed to exist outside normal dimensional constraints.","Before them stretched a transparent veil...a glorious boundary between Living and Dead territories manifested at conceptual level.","And past this veil...","There existed an illusory image of a massive entity hundreds of times larger than their projected forms.","...!","Noah looked at this being and instantly understood!","This was THE Dead Order herself, manifested at scale suggesting her true civilizational weight rather than individual power.","Her regal, otherworldly beauty transcended many things!","Hair shifting between darkness and white with each breath. Eyes holding accumulated authority of an entire Civilization refined across eons!","Oh!","At this moment, her expression showed utter shock ...composure that had likely remained unshaken across countless catastrophes now fractured by something she clearly hadn’t anticipated or prepared for.","Because from her existence, a steady stream of white Order was beginning to flow inexorably toward Sigrid!","Not violently extracted but drawn , as if something in Sigrid’s nature possessed stronger claim to Order’s fundamental essence than THE Dead Order’s painstakingly reconstructed authority.","Oh!","Oh!!!","The implications settled with devastating finality as THE Dead Order’s eyes widened with recognition of what was occurring, and the absolute impossibility of preventing it!","Noah’s eyes shone with luminous brightness as he analyzed the entire situation millions of times across nanoseconds.","Before him, he witnessed the initial shocked expression of THE Dead Order fade with remarkable swiftness, replaced by immense calmness that settled across her features like mask precisely fitted.","Her regal composure returned as if the momentary fracture had never occurred, though the steady stream of white Order flowing from her existence toward Sigrid continued unabated.","She raised her massive hand to touch the river of white Order, fingers tracing the current as if attempting to comprehend a mechanism through physical contact.","Then she looked at Sigrid and Noah with eyes of such profound calm that it bordered on unnatural.","Her gaze swept across them before she raised that same hand toward... the veil separating them.","The transparent boundary between Living and Dead territories...a conceptual barrier given visible form through their unprecedented connection.","Noah’s expression became heavy as recognition crystallized regarding what she was attempting.","He immediately floated forward to position himself directly between Sigrid and THE Dead Order’s approaching hand, his body pulsing with concentrated weight of his Civilization!","He stood fearlessly before the coming hand of an existence possessing THE distinction, refusing to yield ground despite the overwhelming disparity in accumulated power and refined authority!","When THE Dead Order’s hand neared the veil, reality itself seemed to resist .","The space around her fingers distorted with strain as if existence was struggling to reconcile her attempt to cross with fundamental weavings prohibiting such transit.","It felt like an unsurpassable barrier, an absolute prohibition!","As if it truly represented The Veil between The Living and The Dead, and THE Dead Order ... could not cross.","Her hand pressed against invisible resistance, fingers splaying as concentrated force attempted to penetrate boundary that refused penetration.","White brilliance of Order erupted around contact point, but the veil remained absolutely intact...unmoved by pressure that could reshape territories if directed elsewhere!","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as hypothesis was confirmed through direct observation.","She genuinely could not cross!","He floated forward with deliberate motion, approaching the veil with confidence.","When he reached the transparent boundary, he placed his own hand against its surface adjacent to where THE Dead Order’s massive fingers pressed from the opposite side.","He performed a theatrical gesture of also attempting to push through...acting as if he encountered identical resistance, as if the barrier was equally impassable from his direction.","But internally... he felt no resistance whatsoever.","His hand could slide through the veil as easily as passing through water, could traverse to the other side if he wished to make that crossing.","But THE Dead Order did not need to know this particular truth.","Better to maintain impression of mutual constraint, of barrier that protected both sides equally.","He floated backward to resume position near Sigrid, and the two of them stared at the massive illusory manifestation of THE Dead Order while she stared back with gaze of utter calmness and regal composure.","Even her eyes gave no indication of internal thoughts or emotional state...a perfect mask maintained despite circumstances that should provoke significant reaction.","Her expression revealed absolutely nothing about how she was genuinely processing this unprecedented situation!","Noah observed this being while his existence attempted to calculate countless variables simultaneously.","I barely encountered any entities at the level of THE across my journey, and now I’ve confronted the Will of THE Living Paradox and THE Dead Order herself in the same fucking day. How ridiculously accelerated existence has become.","Throughout this charged silence, neither side spoke initially as Sigrid displayed somber expression while feeling the continuous influx of The Civilizational Authority of Order."]},{"number":4423,"title":"Chapter 4423: Chapter 4422: Siphoning II","paragraphs":["Her Complexity and Purity was jumping upward by multiple Quintillions with each passing moment!","And in this weighty silence, it was THE Dead Order who finally broke the stillness.","\" The Resurgence of my Order.. .\" Her gaze fixed on Sigrid with intensity.","\" And I assume you are Osmont? \" Her attention shifted to Noah. \" You two are genuinely joined at the hip, it seems. How delightfully... intimate.\"","Her tone held no mockery despite the observation.","\" You stand before the presence of Order itself. The Seer of Truth. The Arbiter of Structure. The First Foundation. The Architect of Systematic Perfection.\" She paused deliberately.","\" Though... you seem to be lapping up and siphoning modest portions of myself at this very moment through mechanisms I cannot immediately interrupt. Do you think you could stop that voluntary theft?\"","...!","Could she stop that.","At such a pointed question delivered with remarkable calm given circumstances, Sigrid remained initially silent.","She was uncertain how to respond to being directly addressed by the entity she was always dreading!","Noah looked at THE Dead Order with focus before proceeding to respond with his own formal introduction.","\"You stand before the presence of The True Emperor of Quintessence. The True Emperor of Tyranny. The 9th Infernal Lord. The Daemon of Tyranny. Imperius Avallonis. The Antediluvian. The Lumen Emperor. The Weaver of Existence. The Weaver of Extremity...\"","...!","The scene that unfolded carried mixture of grandeur and absurdity as...just as THE Dead Order had introduced herself through accumulated titles, Noah proceeded to do precisely the same but with far more exaggerated length.","He listed multiple grand designations with his voice maintaining perfect seriousness, his gaze remaining calm while THE Dead Order observed him with eyes beginning to shine with what might have been amusement beneath her careful composure.","\"...The Gazer of the Unscalable Wall. The Indefatigable.\" He paused as if mentally cataloguing. \"Let me see, is that everything? Ah, no. There are more. The Dreamer of Extremity. The Dream of The Beyonder. The Burnt One. The Cartographer of Existence. The Stranger. The Outsider...\"","He let final titles settle with deliberate weight:","\"The Early Creature, Osmont.\"","...!","He had conducted such lengthy introduction that when he finally concluded, both Sigrid and THE Dead Order were regarding him with expressions mixing bewilderment and incredulity at the sheer audacity of matching her formal presentation with such an elaborately constructed response.","And in the silence following this performance, THE Dead Order spoke.","\" You... are one of the primary reasons my Civilization is facing existential threat at this moment? You?\"","The emphasis on that final word suggested difficulty reconciling the being before her...however unusual, with the scale of disruption apparently being caused.","...!","At such question, Noah nodded with perfect calm and utmost seriousness.","\"Yes, Ma’am. And no, I don’t believe The Resurgence of your Order, as you’ve termed her, I don’t think she possesses capability to cease siphoning from you. In fact...\"","His smile widened slightly with an expression mixing tyrannical confidence and deliberate provocation.","\"I think we’ll amplify the process considerably.\"","...!","BOOM !","An unfathomable phenomenon manifested as Noah and Sigrid came face to face with a terrifically powerful being possessing THE distinction...an entity who should theoretically be capable of collapsing them through mere attention!","And yet... neither side could harm the other!","Oh!","After Noah’s bold proclamation, a heavy silence settled across the unique liminal space separating them from THE Dead Order.","The silence did not persist for an extended duration as Noah floated calmly through the conceptual space to more closely observe the river of white Order flowing steadily into Sigrid’s existence.","The current maintained consistent velocity, neither accelerating nor diminishing despite the charged circumstances.","He turned to look deeply into Sigrid’s eyes, searching for signs of strain or corruption, confirming she was managing the influx without anything catastrophic.","She nodded with subtle gesture that conveyed reassurance.","Satisfied by this confirmation, Noah turned to directly face THE Dead Order’s massive illusory form.","When he spoke again, his voice carried imposing calm as he began to bullshit.","\"I have always felt profound sympathy for Order, truthfully. The first victim of THE Living Paradox’s ambitions. Falling in a battle where you were only attempting to do what was fundamentally right. And what compensation did you receive for such righteous dedication? Collapse. Absolute termination.\"","His gaze intensified.","\"Why did you have to be the one to perish? Why not Origin? Why not Emotive? Why not Spirit or any of the other THE entities who participated in that conflict? And worst of all, after that grand show of force concluded, with THE Living Paradox being imprisoned thereafter as a consequence... why was it that THE Living Emotive and others simply turned away and subsequently collaborated with THE Living Paradox to forge THE Loom?\"","BOOM!","Noah’s voice dropped with weight of an utterly damning assessment.","\"It effectively rendered your sacrifice and death worth absolutely nothing . Your collapse became a meaningless footnote in a grand narrative rather than martyrdom that changed trajectories. You entire existence amouted to... absolutely... nothing .\"","BOOM !","His words landed with immense weight!","On the opposite side of The Veil, THE Dead Order received these observations with a calm smile!","\" You say the truth with remarkable clarity, O True Emperor of Quintessence. My Collapse meant nothing in ultimate accounting. My sacrifice accomplished nothing beyond providing THE Living Paradox with lesson about consequences...lesson he apparently learned well enough to avoid similar miscalculation subsequently.\"","Her expression shifted subtly.","\" That...is precisely why Order remains so critically important. Had I been present during THE Loom’s construction, perhaps it would never have reached fruition. Perhaps if I possessed all my accumulated power at current developmental level, I could even prevent The Fallout entirely.\"","She leaned forward with interest intensifying.","\" That is what you are attempting to accomplish, correct? You should be systematically growing your budding Civilization because that represents the most straightforward pathway to attaining THE distinction. If you achieve THE, you possess genuine chance to survive The Fallout rather than becoming fuel for others’ continuation.\"","Her smile took on dangerous edge as her massive face approached the Veil more closely.","\" But consider this alternative, 9th Infernal Lord, Imperius Avallonis, The Antediluvian, The Lumen Emperor, The Weaver of Existence... \"","She deliberately invoked multiple titles he had claimed. \" I am positioned right here before you. I already possess THE distinction through refinement across eons. I simply require modest infusion of vitality to restore capabilities that were stripped during my collapse.\"","Her eyes gleamed with a calculated offer.","\" Can you provide that essential essence? Can you provide me with...her? I already carry THE distinction. With my counterpart currently drawing from my reserves, once we reunify and become one...that represents your optimal solution to The Fallout immediately available. I would then possess capability to rectify numerous wrongs, to restructure existence’s trajectory. I could even share with you knowledge of the many alternative pathways to reach THE beyond simple Civilization construction.\"","She paused deliberately.","\" Existence is vast beyond normal comprehension. Building a Civilization constitutes the fastest and most straightforward methodology, certainly. But alternatives exist for those with sufficient intelligence and flexibility to pursue them. What do you say, Weaver of Extremity? Dreamer of Extremity?\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4424,"title":"Chapter 4424: Chapter 4423: Primordial Civilizations I","paragraphs":["What did he say?","He was asked so simply to give up Sigrid!","At this moment, Noah shook his head with a gesture of regret and firm refusal.","\"I have grown excessively attached to relinquish my Order now. She has become rather... integral to my existence. However, consider this alternative approach: did you sense how your former friend...your killer, the direct cause for your current Dead status...did you perceive how THE Living Paradox manifested on this side of The Veil recently?\"","His expression shifted toward a strategic proposition.","\"How about we collaborate on addressing that particular problem? You understand the principle: the enemy of my enemy is my friend...or something like that. We could coordinate efforts against THE Living Paradox rather than competing...\"","...!","Noah articulated such proposal, but in response, THE Dead Order simply stared at him with cold expression offering no verbal reply whatsoever.","Her silence spoke volumes about her receptiveness to that particular suggestion!","Oh!","Observing her unreceptive demeanor, Noah continued with shift in approach...this time becoming deliberately provocative.","\"I encountered THE Living Paradox when he manifested over here and I somehow managed to survive the experience sufficiently to relay this account. Would you like to know precisely how I accomplished that improbable feat?\"","He paused for effect.","\"And I must say, having met him directly and now meeting you in this manner... THE Living Paradox is substantially more terrifying to observe and interact with. An entity genuinely worthy of fear...if I still experienced such a limiting emotion.\"","\"Compared to his overwhelming presence, you seem rather... diminished , O Order . Like a lesser version of an existence carrying THE distinction, you understand?\"","His voice took on a contemplative quality mixing observation with deliberate insult!","\"When he appeared, even existence itself was manifesting commands: ’KNEEL! REVERE!’\"","\"Reality itself bent to acknowledge his authority. But with you present now... ah, you are remarkably easier to be around, Order. More manageable. Less oppressive. Is this perhaps why THE Living Paradox has been consistently winning across eons? Because you and the other THE entities are simply... lesser ?\"","BOOM !","At these deliberately provocative words, THE Dead Order looked at him with calmness before transforming into a face of amusement.","She began laughing, the sound echoing across the liminal space with volume!","HUUUM !","\" Remarkable! I never anticipated something so diminutive and recently manifested could address me with such audacious disrespect. It actually hasn’t occurred... ever? Across my entire existence spanning incomprehensible duration, no entity has spoken to me with such casual dismissiveness!\"","At such observation, Noah nodded calmly.","\"Yeah, it’s remarkably easy to speak provocatively when there exists an impenetrable barrier between us. The Veil provides a substantial confidence booster!\"","THE Dead Order approached the Veil even more closely, her massive face locking onto Noah’s comparatively tiny form with intensity.","\" Haha! I find myself appreciating you despite the obvious provocations. Your audacity is almost... refreshing. Almost.\"","Noah replied with a casual nod as he floated beside a visibly cautious Sigrid who continued maintaining vigilant observation of THE Dead Order despite ongoing power transfer.","He patted Sigrid’s head to calm her existence.","\"Yeah, your counterpart appreciates me too. We have quite a compatible relationship, actually.\"","Her counterpart appreciates him too.","At these specific words, THE Dead Order blinked with sudden shift in demeanor.","She looked between Noah and Sigrid with expression rapidly transforming from amusement to dawning comprehension!","Her eyes flashed with ferocious light.","\" Wait... you haven’t been...\"","Noah blinked with expression of confusion, tilting his head with an innocent gesture.","\"What?\"","The expression of THE Dead Order became stern and heavy for the first time since their interaction commenced, amusement completely evaporating as she demanded.","\" You... haven’t been desecrating Order through a carnal relationship, correct? Tell me explicitly...that you haven’t been fucking my Order! Tell me you have not been tainting something so profoundly sacred with base physical gratification!\"","BOOM!","Noah felt genuine astonishment at this unexpected line of questioning.","He hadn’t anticipated such concern manifesting from being apparently focused on Civilization scale conflicts.","But recognizing opportunity to further destabilize THE Dead Order’s composure for information, he continued.","\"Well... my mother raised me not to engage in lies, so I won’t fabricate comfortable lies. Perhaps there has been... modest tainting involved.\"","...!","The expression of THE Dead Order visibly soured as she said with cold precision.","\" Modest ?\"","Noah sighed as if caught in a transparent deception, and he adopted the tone of reluctant confession.","\"Okay, perhaps extensive tainting would be more accurate characterization. But don’t concern yourself excessively, it’s all conducted in the most sacred manner possible, with appropriate reverence for everything involved.\"","...!","HUUM!","On the opposite side of The Veil, billowing power began gathering with threatening intensity as white brilliance rose around THE Dead Order’s form like storm preparing to break.","A flash of genuine anger appeared in her eyes for the first time during their interaction as she shook her head with a gesture mixing disbelief and mounting fury.","\" Haha... this... THIS is precisely why this magnitude of power cannot be entrusted to lesser beings! You don’t even comprehend what to do with it appropriately! You actually taint it continuously, day after day, your limited minds utterly unable to wrap around the immensity of what you have gained access to!\"","Her voice intensified with conviction.","\" This is exactly why you cannot possess Order, you imbecilic creature! You fundamentally do not understand the immensity of one of the Original Civilizations! One of the Primordial Civilizations that existed before all others!\"","...!","Original Civilizations?","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply with sudden intense focus.","Primordial Civilizations?","Order, Paradox, Emotive, and others classified under such designation?","Was his own Civilization, The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger, also not considered authentic Primordial Civilization despite the nomenclature?","He had finally extracted substantive information from THE Dead Order beyond tactical posturing, and he wanted considerably more!","\"Woah, woah, woah,\" Noah said with his voice shifting toward conciliatory tone, \"we were maintaining such productive conversation...let’s not become hostile now over relatively minor details. Don’t allow that tainting situation to divert us from more significant discourse. Come on now.\"","His eyes shone with luminous intensity as he pressed on.","\"What precisely don’t we understand about the immensity of these grand Primordial Civilizations? This imbecilic mind of mine would love to wrap my head around it!\"","...!"]},{"number":4425,"title":"Chapter 4425: Chapter 4424: Primordial Civilizations II","paragraphs":["Noah had inquired about Primordial Civilizations!","THE Dead Order regarded him with cold intensity, her expression seemingly still processing his admitted transgression against what she considered sacred principle.","Her eyes burned as if she was determining how to proceed given her inability to directly punish behavior that genuinely offended her foundations.","\"If you cease the siphoning of my Order immediately, I will reveal certain information to you. Information regarding Primordial Civilizations and their fundamental distinctions from lesser frameworks. That seems...to be an equitable exchange given current circumstances.\"","Her tone wanted absolutely no negotiation, presenting this as reasonable compromise rather than request!","But...","At such proposition, Noah shook his head with gesture of amusement and absolute refusal.","\"No. That’s not happening.\"","Stop the siphoning? Hah!","The very suggestion bordered on absurd given how advantageous the current arrangement proved for their development.","He elaborated with finality.","\"However, you must possess considerable curiosity regarding THE Living Paradox and his recent manifestation. I will share the comprehensive details of my encounter with him...including his aims and objectives. He may have actually mentioned you specifically during our interaction, which I imagine would prove rather illuminating from your perspective...\"","Not an iota of shit was mentioned regarding THE Dead Order , but it was good to fluff things up!","The mention of THE Living Paradox caused THE Dead Order to become instantly silent, her cold expression shifting towards genuine interest beneath her careful composure.","After brief contemplation, she said simply.","\" Okay. That exchange I will accept.\"","She looked between Noah and Sigrid as if deliberately filing away his admitted desecration of Order for future consideration...placing it in mental storage rather than dwelling on something she currently lacked power to address.","\" Originally, my Guiders of Order were already mobilizing toward The Lands of The Living to investigate both THE Living Paradox’s appearance and your unusual emergence. But since I have you positioned before me now, I can redirect them toward more immediately important matters .\"","Her expression hardened slightly with implicit threat.","\" That arrangement persists until such time as I successfully cross to the other side to ensure you all cease this siphoning...should you persist in maintaining it indefinitely.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply.","There exists something THE Dead Order considers more important than addressing Sigrid and THE Living Paradox’s manifestation? What could possibly warrant higher priority than those existential concerns?","After articulating this veiled warning, THE Dead Order waved her hands.","Behind her massive form, a tremendous white throne materialized, constructed from marbled pillars of pure Order that assembled themselves.","She proceeded to seat herself upon it with regality, her figure emanating profound waves of majesty that made the surrounding conceptual space adjust to acknowledge her sovereignty.","When she spoke again, her voice was grand!","\" For you to genuinely comprehend what it means when discussing Primordial Civilizations, you don’t require lengthy theoretical exposition. You simply need to experience a conversation I once shared with THE Creature himself...his words always illuminated more than any explanation ever could.\"","...!","A conversation that Order had with THE Creature.","Noah’s eyes intensified with focused interest as he asked immediately.","\"When would this conversation have occurred?\"","THE Dead Order smiled with an expression mixing nostalgia.","\" Time doesn’t truly matter in the grand scheme of existence’s trajectory, but for specificity: this exchange occurred shortly before the completion of THE Loom. At that juncture, THE Creature had grown nostalgic regarding the distant past...The Lands of The Dead had long been established as separate domain, and he appeared before me carrying sense of profound melancholy.\"","Her voice shifted, taking on a quality suggesting she was channeling THE Creature’s actual words.","\"He asked me: ’Why is it that with grander and grander complexity, we progressively lose the fundamental simplicity of existence itself? Do you remember the truly earliest times? When Origin first introduced herself to me with such innocent enthusiasm? When Concept emerged and made things delightfully easy to understand?\"","\"’ When Inevitabilities seemed like formidable monsters worthy of genuine concern rather than manageable nuisances?’\"","She paused, allowing the weight of those questions to settle.","\"’ Why could we not retain that same beautiful simplicity as we advanced? Why must sophistication invariably breed complications that obscure rather than illuminate?’\"","HUUM!","THE Dead Order’s smile carried a mixture of regret and self-recrimination as she continued.","\" At that time, I was not in optimal mental state...I was still processing my own collapse. So I replied with unfortunate bluntness\"","\"’You happened, O Creature. You gave away your Everythings and initiated the race of Civilizations. This entire catastrophic trajectory traces back to your fundamental generosity.’\"","BOOM !","THE Creature began the race of Civilizations?","The revelation landed with seismic implications!","...!","THE Dead Order shook her head with a gesture holding lingering shame.","\" I immediately regretted having said such an accusatory assessment to a being who was dedicating everything toward collective benefit. But he seemed to understand my emotional state rather than taking offense. He only smiled with that characteristic patience and nodded before responding...\"","Her voice shifted again, channeling THE Creature’s reply.","\"’ Yes, all of this can reasonably be considered My fault in ultimate accounting. I set things in motion through my choices and actions. I deliberately allowed everything to be free ...for entities to pursue what they wished, to explore the endless expanse of existence according to their own determinations rather than my imposed structure.’\"","She paused significantly.","\"’ If I had reigned things in early, exercised controlling authority when initial problems emerged... perhaps The Primordial Civilization of Paradox would not have expanded so rampantly. If my own Primordial Civilization wasn’t left to operate freely, maybe none of this would be transpiring. Maybe. Maybe. Maybe.’\"","BOOM!","When she reached this point in her recollection, THE Dead Order looked directly at Noah from her white throne with her eyes carrying the weight of revelation about to be delivered.","\" The Primordial Civilization of THE Creature was so immense, so fundamentally threatening to basic continuation, that Paradox felt unfathomably intimidated. Little Thing...do you comprehend what the Primordial Civilization of THE Creature actually represents? What it was? What it is?\"","...!"]},{"number":4426,"title":"Chapter 4426: Chapter 4425: Primordial Civilizations III","paragraphs":["Noah remained deliberately silent, recognizing this as a rhetorical prelude rather than a genuine question requiring a response.","She continued with her voice booming with regal authority.","\" THE Creature gave his Everythings to Existence all those eons ago...distributed his fundamental essence across reality’s totality. It was channeled initially through Paradox. But even Paradox could not contain it completely, could not bottle something so vast.\"","WAA!","Her eyes blazed with white brilliance.","\" So his Everythings spread throughout Existence itself...permeating everything, becoming foundation upon which all else was constructed. THE Creature’s Civilization... is THE PRIMORDIAL CIVILIZATION OF EXISTENCE!\"","BOOM!","The words landed with such tremendous philosophical and existential weight that both Noah and Sigrid’s forms buzzed !","THE Primordial Civilization of Existence!","Noah’s mind raced through implications.","How immense must that be? How incomprehensibly powerful? How overpowered?!","If that designation is accurate...if his Civilization genuinely encompasses Existence itself...","Then he cannot possibly be Dead. If his Civilization was the very framework of Existence, then his termination would mean reality’s collapse. He must persist in some form, somehow, somewhere.","BOOM!","The logic seemed inescapable even if mechanisms remained mysterious.","As Noah processed these shocking revelations on his side of the transparent veil, THE Dead Order observed them.","She settled more comfortably upon her throne before beginning a comprehensive explanation.","\" To properly understand Primordial Civilizations, you must recognize they emerged from the earliest throes of existence itself...before conventional time, before established causality, before the weavings that now seem fundamental were even conceived.\"","\"The Primordial Civilizations are... THE Creature’s Civilization of Existence, serving as foundation for literally everything. The Primordial Civilization of Hunger...THE First Hunger’s framework that established appetite and growth as principles. The Primordial Civilization of Paradox...contradiction and impossibility given structured form.\"","\"The Primordial Civilization of Origin, beginnings and genesis as organized authority. The Primordial Civilization of Concept, categorical understanding and definitional frameworks. The Primordial Civilization of Emotive, feeling and passion structured systematically. The Primordial Civilization of Spirit, essence and vitality as coordinated whole. Alongside all the others.\"","She paused for emphasis.","\" And of course, The Primordial Civilization of Order...my weavings that established structure and systematic organization.\"","Oh!","Her expression intensified as she continued!","\" These Primordial Civilizations don’t merely occupy portions of existence...they permeate the vast expanses of reality itself. They are woven into the fabric of how things operate. Any Civilization that emerges subsequently, regardless of refinement or accumulated power, cannot genuinely compare because they are built upon foundations that Primordial Civilizations established.\"","She leaned forward with intensity:","\" Primordial Civilizations possess inherent advantages that cannot be replicated through cultivation. First...they carry precedence - they existed before alternatives, which means Existence itself recognizes their authority as more fundamental than competing Civilizations.\"","\"When a Primordial Civilization conflicts with newer structure, existence defaults to honoring the elder claim. Kids like you may start questioning soon why Existence is unfair...Existence is not set up to support you. Never you.\"","HUUM!","Her fingers drummed against her throne’s armrest with a measured rhythm.","\" Second: they maintain permeation - their principles extend throughout existence rather than being localized to specific domains or followers. My Order influences how things naturally organize across all territories, not just where my active attention focuses. I gain weavings even in places I have no infleunce in...even in The Lands of The Living.\"","\"Paradox introduces contradiction into fundamental operations regardless of THE Living Paradox’s direct involvement.\"","She continued with building momentum!","\" Third: they possess irreducibility ...you cannot break them down into simpler components because they themselves represent the simplest possible expression of their Weavings.\"","WAA!","\"Order cannot be reduced to a more basic organizational concept. Existence cannot be decomposed into something more fundamental. They are axiomatic rather than derived.\"","OH!","Her voice intensified further as if to say she was not fucking done!","\" Fourth: they demonstrate inevitability ...attempting to eliminate Primordial Civilizations is functionally equivalent to attempting to eliminate the principle it embodies from reality itself.\"","\"You cannot remove Paradox without eliminating contradiction from existence. You cannot destroy Origin without preventing all beginnings. The concepts and the Civilizations are inseparable at fundamental level. So all the Civilizations that THE Living Paradox Collapsed...they are not truly gone. They cannot be. Suppressed. Decimated. Collapsed. Use whatever words you want. But they are here. They will be here.\"","...!","An immense silence settled as she said this.","Noah’s eyes pulsed with waves of glorious majesty.","And THE Dead Order...","She gestured broadly.","\" Fifth: they enable Existential Communication ...all beings across existence comprehend their principles instinctively because those principles are woven into how consciousness itself operates. Everyone understands what Order means. Everyone grasps Existence as concept.\"","\"This provides Primordial Civilizations with influence that transcends...absolutely everything. You know my Order. You know Paradox. Even without me doing anything, I have likely fed off any actions you or countless other creatures made...aligning with Order.\"","\" I feed off of Order across Existence right now, though I am limited when it comes to access to THE Loom. But at this very moment, I am feeding on such a steady stream of Order that even what you two are siphoning is negligable...for now anyways.\"","\"It is why I am not too enraged...yet. You are like mosquitos...harmless fucking things, for now. But you could become a major annoyance. It is also why I am not afraid of the future as Order will always be there. When THE Loom opens and all the eons of Order within it flood out...I will feed off of it and become my most powerful.\"","BOOM!","\"Concepts. Origins. Emptive. Paradox. They are Primordial. They collect from all of Existence. Anything paradoxical you did...you fed paradox. And all of Existence...all of Existence feeds THE Creature. \"","BOOOM!","Her expression became almost pitying!","As if all of them never truly stood a chance!","...!","After completing this extensive exposition, THE Dead Order crossed her legs with a gesture suggesting conclusion of a lesson as she delivered final assessment.","\" That is what a Primordial Civilization represents. Whatever framework you have constructed...however impressive it may seem relative to scattered individuals, it does not possibly compare to what I have described. It cannot possibly compare because it lacks the fundamental advantages that only emerge from being woven into existence’s basic architecture from its inception.\"","BOOM !","Her words landed with finality meant to establish absolute hierarchy, to demonstrate the insurmountable gap between what Noah was building and what she represented!","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply at this comprehensive dismissal as he suppressed his devilish smile with considerable effort!","He could feel his existence buzzing as if something immense was about to explode!","How could my framework not compare when I already possess not one but TWO emerging Primordial Civilizations?!","The Primordial Civilization of Mana!","The Primordial Civilization of Hunger!","THE Dead Order didn’t understand what she was actually facing.","Oh, she didn’t understand!!!"]},{"number":4427,"title":"Chapter 4427: Chapter 4426: Primordial Civilizations IV","paragraphs":["Noah had comprehensively absorbed the information regarding Primordial Civilizations as if it was akin to better understanding himself .","He was grasping the fundamental nature of the path he walked, The Way he was forging through existence’s infinite expanse!","At this moment, his mind was buzzing with cascading revelations as his Existence pulsed with profound sense of Euphoria .","Oh, Euphoria!","It was not simple pleasure, but the recognition of truth that aligned perfectly with what he was becoming at deepest levels.","Glorious prompts bloomed within his consciousness.","|CRITICAL ADVANCEMENT RECOGNIZED|","|You have grasped a fundamental understanding of your Way |","|Your comprehension of what you are building has deepened exponentially|","|You have advanced significantly along your chosen path through revelation rather than mere accumulation|","| The Way becomes clearer. The destination more defined. The journey more purposeful.|","...!","He had advanced in his Way!","Oh!","The realization settled with magisterial satisfaction as further prompts materialized, detailing profound implications!","And RUIN/EDEN’s voice almost seemed to tremble with emotion as she expressed everything, as if even she found this far too grand and unbelievable.","|THE PRIMORDIAL CIVILIZATION OF MANA AND HUNGER - RECOGNITION ACHIEVED|","|Your dual framework has gained comprehensive understanding of what it is truly capable of becoming|","|Analysis of Primordial Civilization characteristics have been understood in respect to your Civilizations.|","|FIRST QUALITY - PRECEDENCE :|","|Mana: Exists as fundamental building block preceding all sophisticated authorities. Before complex techniques, before refined powers, before elegant systems...there was raw Mana. Energy in its most essential form. Your Way of Mana Architect claims authority over this primordial essence, establishing precedence over all derivative authorities constructed from Mana as foundation.|","|Hunger: Represents the original motivation driving all advancement. Before ambition was refined into philosophy, before desire became structured cultivation, there existed raw Hunger. The fundamental recognition of incompleteness. Your Way of Hunger claims dominion over this most basic drive, establishing precedence over all subsequent motivational frameworks.|","|When your Primordial Civilization conflicts with newer structures, existence will increasingly default to honoring your elder claim. Your Mana supersedes sophisticated authorities derived from it. Your Hunger takes priority over refined ambitions built upon it.|","|SECOND QUALITY - PERMEATION :|","|Mana: Your principles extend throughout existence rather than being localized to your direct sphere of influence. Wherever Mana exists, which is effectively everywhere, your Civilization maintains conceptual presence. You gain incremental advancement from Mana manipulation across all territories, not merely where you personally focus attention.|","|Hunger: Your framework influences how beings experience and express appetite across existence. Every act of cultivation driven by Hunger, every advancement pursued through desire...these feed into your Civilization’s authority. You accumulate essence from Hunger expressed throughout reality regardless of whether those beings acknowledge your framework.|","|You will begin receiving passive accumulation from all Mana utilization and all Hunger expression across observable existence. This represents fundamental shift from active cultivation to passive accumulation through permeation.|","|THIRD QUALITY - IRREDUCIBILITY :|","|Mana: Cannot be decomposed into simpler components because it already represents energy in its most fundamental form. You cannot reduce Mana to something more basic, it is axiomatic rather than derived. Attempting to break down your Mana authority becomes functionally impossible because there exists no simpler principle to reduce it toward.|","|Hunger: Represents the irreducible recognition of incompleteness. You cannot simplify Hunger into more basic concept because it already embodies the fundamental acknowledgment that drives all growth. Your Hunger authority cannot be deconstructed because it exists at bedrock level of motivational architecture.|","|Your Primordial Civilization possesses inherent resilience against deconstruction or systematic dismantling. Enemies cannot break down your framework into manageable components because the components themselves are irreducibly fundamental.|","|FOURTH QUALITY - INEVITABILITY :|","|Mana: Attempting to eliminate your Primordial Civilization of Mana would require removing energy itself from existence. You cannot destroy Mana without collapsing reality’s basic operations. Therefore, your Civilization demonstrates inevitability...it must persist because existence requires what it embodies.|","|Hunger: Attempting to eradicate your Primordial Civilization of Hunger would necessitate eliminating growth and advancement from reality. You cannot remove Hunger without preventing all progression. Therefore, your framework cannot be truly eliminated, only suppressed, only temporarily diminished, never permanently erased.|","|Even if catastrophically defeated, your Primordial Civilizations will persist in some form. They cannot be completely destroyed because the principles they embody remain inseparable from existence’s fundamental operations. Suppression is possible. Decimation is achievable. But absolute elimination is functionally impossible.|","BOOOM !","|Oh, Master!|","RUIN/EDEN called out with emotion of immense relief!","Noah’s existence buzzed as he felt a surreal sense of existence as...he felt like he found, no, grasped a solution of The Fallout.","Even if he failed. Even if he could not attain THE .","He would be similar to THE Creature or THE Dead Order ...diminished, destroyed, suppressed...but not completely extinguished!","After eons or billions of years, he and his Civilization could rise again!","But even this...","I do not even want to be diminished! I do not want to be destroyed! It is glorious to know this, but it changes nothing. A true solution that does not accept destruction must be formed!","BOOM!","His thoughts burned with clear glory.","RUIN/EDEN was still immensely happy at this revelation as to her, her Master would never truly and completely die regardless of what these terrifying THE entities did in the future!","She collected herself...and then she continued.","|FIFTH QUALITY - EXISTENTIAL COMMUNICATION:|","|Mana: All beings across existence comprehend Mana instinctively because manipulation of energy represents universal constant. Everyone understands what Mana means regardless of terminology variations. This provides your Civilization with influence transcending language, culture, or dimensional barriers.|","|Hunger: All conscious entities grasp Hunger as fundamental concept because recognition of incompleteness drives all advancement. Everyone experiences appetite for growth regardless of how they conceptualize or express it. This grants your framework universal accessibility that cannot be blocked by communication barriers.|","|Your Primordial Civilization can influence and draw from all beings instinctively rather than requiring explicit teaching or conversion. Every act aligning with Mana or Hunger across existence feeds into your framework automatically.|","|Through comprehensive understanding of these five qualities, you now comprehend what your Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger can potentially accomplish:|","|—Existential influence without requiring direct presence|","|—Passive accumulation from all aligned actions across existence|","|—Inherent resilience against systematic destruction|","|—Automatic comprehension by all conscious beings|","|—Fundamental authority superseding derivative frameworks|","|Your path forward has crystallized with unprecedented clarity.|","...!"]},{"number":4428,"title":"Chapter 4428: Chapter 4427: Primordial Civilizations V","paragraphs":["After these extensive prompts settled into his consciousness, Noah felt his existence surging with power that threatened to explode outward in visible manifestation.","His body nearly erupted with radiance that would have been impossible to conceal, but revealing such dramatic transformation to THE Dead Order would expose information better kept hidden!","He contained the eruption internally with tremendous effort, suppressing most of the display through sheer disciplined will.","But a portion still leaked despite his best efforts!","His body flashed with blue-gold brilliance as Primus Mana surged through every particle of his being with overwhelming concentration.","An aura of profound ancientness began radiating from him...not the ancientness of accumulated years but of primevality , suggesting connection to existence’s earliest moments!","The unmistakable signature of a Primordial Civilization leaked from him like light escaping through cracks in sealed vessel!","This development astonished THE Dead Order so profoundly that she rose abruptly from her white throne, her perfect composure fracturing as recognition struck with undeniable force.","Because she did not sense Order emanating from Noah to explain the presence of Primordial Civilization signature.","This was something else entirely...something she hadn’t anticipated, nor did she recognize!","How could there be a Primordial Civilization...that she djd not recognize?!","She voiced her astonishment aloud with rare display of genuine shock.","\"How do you emanate the distinctive resonance of a Primordial Civilization?! You...who are you truly?!\"","HUUM!","Noah couldn’t answer at this moment.","His entire focus dedicated itself to containing and directing surging power rather than leaking it wastefully or allowing it to destabilize his carefully constructed weavings.","Sigrid moved behind him with fluid grace, her body embracing him from behind as her presence helped stabilize the tumultuous transformation.","Her own connection to Order provided grounding influence, calming the wild surges!","Additional prompts bloomed as the immediate crisis began settling.","|DEVELOPMENT STATUS - PRIMORDIAL CIVILIZATION RECOGNITION|","|Your budding Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger has not yet reached sufficient developmental level to fully enjoy all boons and standing of mature Primordial Civilizations|","|Current Maturity: Nascent Civilization|","|HOWEVER:|","|Due to the heavy advancement of your Way that you have just achieved through comprehensive understanding, you can now access LIMITED BENEFITS of Primordial Civilization status|","|CURRENT ACCESS LEVEL: 10% of full Primordial Civilization standing and capabilities|","|This percentage will increase as your Civilization advances through systematic elevation and accumulated recognition to grander Designations.|","|IMMEDIATE BENEFIT UNLOCKED:|","|EXISTENTIAL COMMUNICATION AND PERMEATION OF THE PRIMORDIAL CIVILIZATION OF MANA AND HUNGER|","|All beings across existence comprehend and use Mana and Hunger principles instinctively because those concepts are woven into how consciousness itself operates|","|Everyone understands what Hunger means...the drive for growth, the recognition of incompleteness|","|Everyone grasps what Mana represents...fundamental energy, basic building block of sophisticated authorities|","|Across Observable Existence, all those who experience Hunger and feed their appetite for advancement...|","|All those who utilize Mana or similar energy-based authorities in any form...|","| ALL OF THEM will now feed into your Civilization automatically|","|Your Way of Existence gains passive accumulation from their actions|","|CURRENT COLLECTION RATE: 10% of potential maximum|","|These boons will begin accruing... NOW .|","BOOM !","The glorious scene that unfolded transcended simple visual spectacle!","Noah felt like vast seas of concentrated essence manifesting around him from countless different directions simultaneously.","Blue-gold Mana materialized in impossible quantities from everywhere.","The accumulated Mana manipulation occurring across entire existence suddenly possessed conduit flowing toward him as focal point.","Obsidian-crimson Hunger surged alongside it...concentrated appetite and drive for advancement collected from innumerable beings pursuing cultivation through countless methodologies at this moment!","Every expression of Hunger across reality contributed fractional essence that aggregated into overwhelming current.","These seas of collected authority flooded into him and immediately began surging toward his Foundation Palisades...his Civilization’s framework drinking deeply of unprecedented influx, walls growing taller and more elaborate with each passing moment.","Simultaneously, additional recognition bloomed:","|PERPETUAL HARVEST - UNPRECEDENTED DEVELOPMENT DETECTED|","|The Principle is sensing thr commencement of the endless stream of incoming harvests from all of Existence|","|This represents fundamental shift from finite accumulation to infinite collection|","| Perpetual Harvest cheers with immense satisfaction at your advancement of The Way!|","|All incoming harvest from Existential Communication and Permeation will be amplified perpetually by Perpetual Harvest’s inherent capabilities!|","|This creates exponential growth curve rather than linear accumulation|","|Your advancement velocity will accelerate dramatically from this point forward|","...!","Existential Communication. Permeation!","The implications settled with weight that made even Noah’s tyrannical ambition pause!","Oh!","From this moment forward, any usage of Hunger anywhere in existence would feed him fractionally.","Any utilization and understanding of Mana across reality’s infinite expanse would contribute to his advancement.","Currently only 10% collection rate, certainly...but that percentage would grow as his Primordial Civilization matured.","And it translated to his framework beginning to gain identical boons and standing as those possessed by THE Creature, THE Living Paradox, THE Dead Order , and all other entities with mature Primordial Civilizations!","The realization also emphasized sobering and horrific truth: across countless eons spanning billions upon billions of years, THE Creature, THE Living Paradox , and all others with established Primordial Civilizations had been collecting these boons every single day without interruption.","Just how incomprehensibly immense are they, truly?","Feeling this scope and grasping the genuine magnitude of disparity, Noah’s existence buzzed with mixture of exhilaration and appropriate humility.","Even he...with all his accumulated advantages, with Perpetual Harvest amplifying everything, with systematic optimization of every process...could not help but feel profound sense of immense weight hanging far above him.","The weight of unfathomably developed Primordial Civilizations that possessed countless eons of accumulated advancement while he... had only just begun .","The mountain he needed to climb had become visible in its entirety for the first time, and its peak disappeared into heights that defied measurement.","But Noah smiled despite, or perhaps because of that daunting recognition.","I have climbed impossible heights before. This merely represents the next ascension.","And unlike them, I possess Perpetual Harvest amplifying every gain. I understand their advantages... and can compensate accordingly!","WAA!","They had eons. I have efficiency. I have Quintessence. I have Tyranny. I have... Mana !","HUUM!","We shall see... which proves more decisive!"]},{"number":4429,"title":"Chapter 4429: Chapter 4428: You Cannot Be Killed? I","paragraphs":["Mana and Hunger positioned against Primordial Civilizations that had been enjoying countless boons across unfathomable expanses of time!","When contemplating this vast disparity, Noah’s mind naturally wandered toward Khor...The First Hunger whose existence had been fragmented and collapsed by THE Living Paradox’s overwhelming power.","And yet... she had survived!","Somehow, across the wonders and mysteries of existence, Noah had manifested to serve as key facilitating her restoration.","Her Civilization, even when systematically collapsed, did not truly and completely cease existing.","That was the fundamental nature of the Primordial Civilization of Hunger demonstrating its Inevitability.","She was restored now, and Noah contemplated...when he shared these most recent discoveries regarding Ways of Existence and the five critical qualities of Primordial Civilizations... would she remember additional fragments of her collapsed memories?","Would her existence experience similar surge in advancement that he currently felt coursing through his own framework?","Because it seems Knowledge is extremely critical to everything.","The thought crystallized with profound significance.","Knowledge !","He possessed the Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger...with weavings carrying all inherent advantages THE Dead Order had described.","But because he had lacked specific knowledge regarding how these advantages actually functioned , he had been unable to properly access their boons until this moment.","Only after obtaining particular understanding, only after advancing comprehensively on his Way, did he become capable of utilizing what he had always possessed.","It was akin to wielding ridiculously sharp sword while lacking knowledge of proper grip...possessing a devastating weapon that remained ineffective through ignorance of basic technique.","There could be hidden mechanisms in plain sight, sophisticated capabilities waiting to be activated, but they remained dormant if one didn’t know they existed or how to trigger them.","Knowledge is critical! Understanding is paramount!","As he processed these layered revelations...","\" Hey! I asked you a question. What are you?!\"","The piercing voice of THE Dead Order echoed across the liminal space at this moment, her earlier shock transforming into demand for answers.","She had sensed the brilliance radiating from his existence however briefly, had recognized the unmistakable signature of Primordial Civilization authority burning within his Mana with ancient grandeur.","She questioned exactly what this could represent.","If she discovered that he possessed not merely this but another authority that would radiate identical primordial characteristics...","Noah shook his head while waving his hands with deliberate gesture, manifesting an illusory screen in the space between them.","He began displaying carefully filtered scenes from the encounter with THE Living Paradox in the Transcendent Quantum Folds...showing the entity’s manifestation, his terrifying authority, the oppressive Festival of Paradox.","But he meticulously excluded any information regarding Khor’s presence or her role in those events.","The scenes began playing with cinematic clarity as Noah said.","\"A deal is a deal. You shared information with me that I genuinely wanted, and now I will reciprocate by sharing with you... intelligence regarding Paradox and his recent activities.\"","The illusions unfolded with detailed precision, and THE Dead Order , who had clearly wanted to continue her pointed questioning, looked at Noah with intense scrutiny before her consciousness locked onto the unfolding scenes he had laid out.","Her attention became consumed by observation, analyzing every detail.","While he kept her occupied with this distraction, Noah closed his eyes to sense the grand manifestation of his Civilization within his internal landscape.","There, he felt the terrifying and constant flow of Civilizational Authority, both Mana and Hunger, streaming into his Foundation Palisades after being further elevated by Perpetual Harvest’s amplifying capabilities.","The harvest from Existential Communication and Permeation combined into unprecedented influx!","It was utterly stupendous because Mana truly represented the base energy flowing across all of Observable Existence.","Every sophisticated technique, every refined authority, every complex manipulation...all of it ultimately derived from fundamental Mana as building block.","For any actions related to Mana utilization, for any expressions of Hunger across Observable Existence, he would benefit and automatically collect fractional essence.","It was Taxation on the scale of Existence itself, and he didn’t even need to actively do anything beyond maintaining his Primordial Civilization’s framework!","The realization painted vivid picture of just how terrifying mature Primordial Civilizations truly were.","THE Creature with his Primordial Civilization of Existence, which encompassed literally everything , must be collecting from absolutely all actions across reality simultaneously.","It hurts just to contemplate how incomprehensibly powerful he must be.","That magnitude explained why he was universally acknowledged as strongest among THE entities despite their individual grandeur.","And yet even against such unfathomably supreme being, Paradox had been audacious enough to plot systematic opposition and apparently achieve some measure of success.","Noah shook his head at the sheer immensity these beings represented as right after this contemplation, he felt his existence buzzing with renewed intensity as another elevation of power erupted within his Existence.","Prompts bloomed with precision.","|FOUNDATION PALISADES - CONTINUED ADVANCEMENT|","|Due to sustained influx from Existential Communication, Permeation, and accumulated harvest:|","|Your Foundation Palisades have forged their structure even further|","|PROTECTION THRESHOLD INCREASED:|","|Previous: 300 Quintillion Complexity and Purity required to harm your existence|","|Current: 500 Quintillion Complexity and Purity required to harm your existence|","|Additionally: Attacker must be member of established Civilization|","|Minor Mana and Hunger Palisades empowerment increased|","|Previous: 35 Quintillion Complexity and Purity granted to recipients|","|Current: 45 Quintillion Complexity and Purity granted to recipients|","|All blessed individuals will experience synchronized elevation|","...!","Noah observed these impressive numerical increases with satisfaction, a smile forming as he contemplated the constant flow of Civilizational Authority continuing indefinitely.","This will persist from now on, endless influx due to fundamental nature of my Mana and Hunger!","And this represents only 10% collection rate as I need to advance significantly further in my Way of Existence!","The metaphor was apt- he was accessing a vast sea of boundless potential, but currently drinking through narrow straw.","He needed to expand that conduit tremendously to access proportional amounts of available essence.","He needed a big fucking straw!","He required additional knowledge for expansion. Needed to advance systematically on His Way through accumulated understanding rather than mere power accumulation.","As he processed these strategic considerations...","The scene Noah had projected concluded its display, and THE Dead Order finished observing the carefully curated illusions."]},{"number":4430,"title":"Chapter 4430: Chapter 4429: You Cannot Be Killed? II","paragraphs":["The expression of THE Dead Order carried mixture of recognition and dark amusement as she spoke.","\"It really is that insane entity. Haha! Even if he currently inhabits Vessels and operates under suppression...whether imposed by Existence itself or through alternative mechanisms, your positioning on the same side of reality as that monster may indicate you don’t possess much remaining time to live.\"","Her voice took on a quality mixing genuine warning with schadenfreude.","\" Don’t believe him when he proclaims he won’t terminate you, that you’re merely designated as future fuel for THE Loom. Provoke him sufficiently, irritate him beyond his tolerance threshold, and you may find yourself joining me on this side...crossing into The Lands of The Dead.\"","\"Wouldn’t that be delightful? Perhaps then you could finally explain why I sensed the unmistakable aura of a foreign Primordial Civilization emanating from you.\"","Her eyes narrowed with analytical intensity.","\"It cannot genuinely be Primordial if it wasn’t among the first frameworks to manifest. And since I do not recognize it from those earliest eras, it logically was not among the original formations. So you displaying that distinctive aura is paradoxical and should not be possible according to established principles.\"","At such pointed observation, Noah smiled with an expression mixing innocence and deflection.","\"Perhaps you perceived something false...misidentification triggered by unusual circumstances. I suspect it was merely reflected light from Order itself, a residual signature from Sigrid’s ongoing siphoning creating your uh...perceptual confusion. But I find myself curious about something else entirely...\"","His voice shifted toward genuine interest.","\" THE Primordial Civilization of Existence. Just contemplating its scope makes one feel infinitely small as... how did THE Living Paradox even possess sufficient audacity to oppose it directly and achieve successful outcome?\"","...!","His words caused THE Dead Order to pause momentarily before she settled back upon her white throne.","She crossed her legs with regal gesture while placing her chin upon her hand, white Order pulsing around her with magnificent authority as she responded.","\" THE Creature was unquestionably strongest among all of us. But his Everythings passed through Paradox during that initial distribution, and that transfer made Paradox significantly stronger than the rest of us...though even enhanced, he couldn’t genuinely compare to THE Creature’s overwhelming supremacy.\"","Her expression became contemplative.","\" So he plotted. He planned systematically across extensive duration. He turned multiple THE Living Existences against THE Creature through careful manipulation and whatever else. Many events transpired that a limited consciousness like yourself cannot fully comprehend through simple explanation. You are...tiny that way.\"","Her voice intensified.","\" But the ultimate result is this: Existence is asleep , Osmont. THE Primordial Civilization of Existence has been suppressed by THE Loom’s combined authority. It will only fully awaken once more after The Fallout concludes. That is when the final confrontation to determine ultimate victor of the war between THE Living Paradox and THE Creature will transpire.\"","She leaned forward with emphasis.","\" You, others like you, whatever Ways of Existence or Civilizations you walk..mall of it amounts to nothing compared to this fundamental conflict.\"","HUUM!","\"You are spectators to grand existential drama, nothing more. You amount to nothing of consequence, and you will remain nothing regardless of your ambitious struggles. Do you fully comprehend that assessment, or shall I repeat it with additional clarity, Little Thing?\"","...!","Noah absorbed these potent waves of intelligence regarding THE Creature and THE Living Paradox with analytical focus, his mind racing through implications.","Existence itself is asleep. Suppressed. Waiting to reawaken after The Fallout.","That explains why THE Creature hasn’t simply resolved all conflicts through overwhelming force...he’s constrained, diminished, operating at fraction of true capability...","On the opposite side of the transparent Veil, THE Dead Order’s eyes pulsed with regality and concentrated power as she awaited response to her devastating assessment.","Noah smiled calmly and finally replied with a tone mixing calmness and unshaken confidence:","\"No, no, I comprehend completely Ma’am. You don’t need to repeat for emphasis. Though I do have one additional question arising from your comprehensive explanation.\"","His eyes gleamed.","\"So...if Primordial Civilizations possess the quality of Inevitability, if they cannot be destroyed regardless of applied force...how can one actually kill someone like THE Living Paradox? Or terminate existence of someone like yourself? Or any others who lead these supposedly indestructible Primordial Civilizations?\"","...!","Order scoffed at such inquiry as if the question itself demonstrated a fundamental misunderstanding.","\" You imbecilic Little Thing. THE Living Paradox tried to kill me, and here I manifestly am. He killed THE Living Origin and extracted her Heart of Origin, yet Origin remains present throughout existence. Diminished certainly. Suppressed without question. Collapsed systematically. But very much present and capable of eventual restoration.\"","Her voice carried absolute certainty.","\" You cannot kill me or any others leading Primordial Civilizations. There exists no methodology for achieving permanent termination of such beings. We are inseparable from principles we embody.\"","HUUM!","Her words landed with tremendous weight, proclaiming absolute invulnerability!","And at such declaration, Noah felt his existence buzzing as if immense and profound epiphany was blooming within his consciousness.","His Mana surged with euphoria as heavy, glorious drums began beating in the surrounding space.","Drums heralding a Symphony of possibility!","The sense of revelation and euphoria surging within Noah during this moment of crystallizing insight caused a smile to begin forming across his features...an expression that started subtle but rapidly transformed into something far more pronounced!","A sound of Symphony boomed in the surroundings with tension-filled percussion that even THE Dead Order frowned upon hearing, recognizing something significant was occurring but unable to identify precise nature.","And in the next moment, Noah began speaking with a voice carrying the weight of revelation.","\"Well what if...\"","His expression transformed into absolutely devilish smile, his crystalline white teeth showing prominently in smile that mixed triumph with cruel understanding!","The smile carved across his features with sharp definition, each visible tooth adding to impression of someone who had just discovered checkmate in a game an opponent believed unwinnable.","His eyes blazed with the light of a predator recognizing vulnerability in a supposedly invulnerable prey!","\"What if you simply replace those Leaders of Primordial Civilizations? Can’t kill them through conventional means, so just systematically take their place. Claim their Civilizations as your own!\"","His smile widened impossibly further.","\"Is my Sigrid here not potentially going to accomplish exactly that against you? She’s siphoning your Civilizational Authority continuously, growing stronger while you proportionally diminish. Eventually she takes your place as undisputed holder of Order’s framework, and after that transition completes...\"","He paused for devastating effect.","\"You don’t possess a Primordial Civilization of Order anymore, someone else does! And at that juncture, you can die because you’re no longer associated with any Primordial Civilization granting Inevitability! Your invulnerability vanishes the moment your framework transfers to another vessel! Hmm... hmm !\"","BOOM!","His expression radiated unfathomable devilish satisfaction as opposite him, THE Dead Order’s features transformed into mask of utter rage, her composure shattering completely under the weight of his words!"]},{"number":4431,"title":"Chapter 4431: Chapter 4430: Derivative I","paragraphs":["The heavy Symphony continued building in surrounding atmosphere as for the first time in a while, Noah’s smile transformed into actual laughter !","\"Haha! Oh man, the delicious irony! An unkillable entity perishing! You may become the first of your kind to actually perish...and at hands of creatures you dismissed as imbecilic, no less!\"","...!","His words carried tremendous weight mixing revelation with cruel amusement, and THE Dead Order’s expression of volcanic rage gradually... calmed.","She sat back even more deliberately upon her throne, forcing composure to return through sheer disciplined will.","Her features settled into careful neutrality as she processed everything.","Eventually, a calculated smile appeared across her face.","\" This would represent the only unique situation where such outcome might be theoretically possible, wouldn’t it? A singular vulnerability in otherwise absolute defense. But...\"","Her smile took on predatory edge.","\" What makes you genuinely believe you will be successful? That this siphoning will continue unimpeded until completion? You fundamentally do not comprehend how massive my Civilization truly is...how infinitesimal the amount you’re currently taking represents proportionally.\"","She gestured toward Sigrid dismissively.","\" And her , the one you desecrate Order with through your base physical relationship...she resembles a delicate porcelain container that cannot hold substantial volume at present developmental level. She can easily break , this fragile thing. That would constitute genuine tragedy, wouldn’t it? It would be such a shame.\"","Her voice intensified.","\" You would also require time ..moh, so much time that you simply do not possess! Me, Paradox, others... just which will reach you first?\"","\"THE Living Paradox doesn’t know about her yet, correct? He would have taken immediate action if he possessed such intelligence. What if I simply share this discovery with him? Enemies of enemies are what again? Haha!\"","HUUM!","She turned toward Sigrid with deadly smile and an expression mixing disappointment with cold calculation.","\" And you . You are systematically siphoning my Civilizational Authority, yet you have barely articulated single word in this entire interaction. Do you not possess your own standing? Your own independent will?\"","Her voice became scathing.","\" You permit him to speak and act on your behalf for everything. Did he truly reduce you to merely his plaything? A toy existing solely for his desires and amusement? Can you not aspire to become something more as THE Living Order? He will diminish your light systematically. He will make you feel small and worthless as he appropriates all your brilliance and claims it as his own achievement.\"","...!","Noah remained calm throughout such pointed provocation as behind him, Sigrid smiled with an expression mixing serenity and absolute conviction.","\"I have only been made to shine brighter since encountering him. So Order need not concern itself with my wellbeing or autonomy. And he holds my Everything willingly given...you don’t need to worry about that arrangement either.\"","Her voice carried quiet strength.","\"I will speak when I feel genuine need to contribute. Right now, I have been rather occupied with stealing from you. That requires considerable focus, as you might imagine.\"","...!","Her words emerged with grand simplicity, and THE Dead Order regarded her as if observing absolute fool...someone who couldn’t recognize their own exploitation and diminishment.","Noah looked between both of them as his mind filled with grand possibilities, that devilish smile still present across his features!","After Sigrid’s resolute reply affirming her choices and autonomy, THE Dead Order shook her head with an expression holding even greater disappointment...as if she was witnessing children playing with forces they fundamentally could not comprehend.","She maintained her regal bearing while speaking with a voice mixing condescension and genuine warning.","\"You two truly do not even understand what you have inadvertently touched. That little Symphony of Existence you just manifested? You likely don’t even comprehend what that phenomenon actually represents.\"","Her voice took on lecturing quality.","\" When one’s existence becomes unique enough to affect all surrounding reality in supportive resonance...when your Way aligns so perfectly with fundamental principles that Existence itself acknowledges your authority, manifestations occur across spectrum of intensity.\"","She gestured.","\"At the weakest threshold, existence performs modest buzzing and trembling...barely perceptible recognition. Slightly above that level, rhythmic sounds emerge as surrounding reality resonates with your cause, your Way of Existence harmonizing with Existence.\"","Her eyes gleamed!","\" Those who are truly strong , however...\"","At this moment, around her white throne, existence itself trembled with far greater intensity than what Noah had inadvertently triggered!","A glorious Symphony of Order began playing with full orchestral magnificence!","It was not scattered drums but complete arrangement!","And beyond the instrumental grandeur, a chorus began echoing in the surroundings on her side of The Veil...voices that seemed to emerge from reality itself rather than specific singers!","\" ORDER! SUPREMACY! ORDER IS SUPREMACY!\"","HUUM!","The proclamation repeated with building intensity, each iteration reinforcing the others until the conceptual space around THE Dead Order vibrated with absolute conviction.","...!","Existence itself resonated comprehensively with her Way as she demonstrated capability to initiate a full Symphony and accompanying chorus at her mere beck and call...and not accidentally triggered but deliberately commanded!","Oh!","Noah observed this display with eyes shining with analytical focus.","THE Dead Order stared back at him with an expression mixing pity and stern warning.","\" You two possess no genuine comprehension of just what grandeur exists within Existence’s infinite expanse. You simply do not know what you’re attempting to challenge. Keep pursuing your current course of action...\"","Her voice dropped with weight of absolute certainty.","\" And eventually I will be forced to deploy weapons that I did not intend to utilize until after The Fallout. Resources I have been carefully preserving for final confrontation. A weapon like... A Disciple of THE Creature.\"","BOOM!","A Disciple...of THE Creature?","Noah’s expression flickered with genuine surprise at this revelation .","This was one of the few indications that THE Creature possessed organized followers like others, if one did not count all Early Creatures as his followers!","THE Dead Order continued.","\" THE Primordial Civilization of Existence was the strongest framework, naturally. Even though THE Creature maintained remarkably laid-back demeanor, he still cultivated members of his Civilization. His Disciples...select few entities that held interminable power positioned just below THE Living Existences themselves in hierarchy.\"","Her smile took on dangerous edge.","\"I know precisely where such beings are currently suppressed. Just like THE Living Paradox... you provoke me sufficiently, irritate me beyond tolerance threshold, and I may expend my considerable accumulated authority to liberate one of THE Creature’s Disciples and direct them against you specifically.\"","....!"]},{"number":4432,"title":"Chapter 4432: Chapter 4431: Derivative II","paragraphs":["Her voice intensified!","\" Test me, Osmont. Please test me, and witness personally where such choices will ultimately lead you.\"","...!","BOOM !","The threat landed with tremendous weight!","Noah’s smile persisted despite, or perhaps because of the terrifying implications.","He closed his eyes while breathing out slowly, processing the accumulated waves of information.","This phenomenon with Sigrid siphoning Civilizational Authority of THE Dead Order has granted me access to invaluable resources. Direct communication with one of the more powerful existences currently operating outside THE Loom ...","I have obtained extensive knowledge, but substantial work remains. While I continue managing THE Dead Order’s attention here, I need to disseminate this critical understanding more broadly...","The knowledge regarding Ways of Existence and Primordial Civilizations seems unfathomably important to systematic advancement. Khor is an obvious recipient...","And another would be...the one who was currently expanding across The Lands of The Dead where THE Dead Order cannot even sense his presence!","He thought of Eckert when it came to sharing information that could advance one’s way as the back of his mind also recalled another- The Peacemaker, and wondered what thst guy was upto now, of anything at all. But his mind revolved back to Eckert.","Since I lack direct access to that domain where endless territories of death stretch infinitely, Eckert might constitute only viable mechanism for extracting additional information and identifying potential weaknesses regarding THE Dead Order herself...","So at this moment, as a terrifying entity stared down at him with eyes promising catastrophic retaliation if provoked, Noah closed his eyes more completely and began transmitting comprehensive waves of information toward select few recipients.","He felt genuine curiosity regarding what results would manifest from this expanded knowledge distribution that had also granted him such profound advancement!","—","In The Lands of The Dead, across territories that stretched with impossible vastness beyond what Living domains could match, The Great Usurper continued his exponential and endless expansion.","His existence now covered multiple Citadels of The Dead...those vast metropolitan concentrations where countless deceased beings congregated.","He continued expanding with a silent inevitability, simply allowing the fundamental nature of his existence to spread without active effort or deliberate conquest.","Idle .","Unfettered and unbothered by concerns that motivated more active cultivators.","At such a time of passive growth, he began receiving substantial inflow of information from none other than the monstrous cheater himself...Osmont!","Eckert felt his consciousness buzzing as unique information flooded his awareness with unprecedented detail!","His mental voice processed aloud with mixture of surprise and focus.","\"Primordial Civilizations? Permeation? Irreducibility? Inevitability? THE Primordial Civilization of THE Creature containing Existence itself... and all of this immense framework is intrinsically tied to... one’s Way of Existence?\"","His mind buzzed as he processed the comprehensive intelligence Osmont had transmitted.","Especially significant was how all this immensity connected fundamentally to one’s personal Way of Existence...the individualized path each being carved through reality’s infinite possibilities.","Osmont had mentioned this concept previously during earlier exchanges, but Eckert had deliberately left it unexplored rather than pursuing it actively.","After all, the fundamental nature of his existence was Idle...would it truly align with his Way if he actively sought out something as critical as his own path?","Wouldn’t that constitute contradiction of his essential nature?","So he had remained Idle, allowing things to develop naturally.","And even now, as these terrifying waves of transformative information cascaded into his consciousness... he processed them with characteristic thoroughness, transmitted a brief message back to Osmont expressing gratitude for shared knowledge, and then...","He returned to his fundamental nature of Idleness, continuing to let things be as they should naturally become without forced intervention.","At such a moment of deliberate non-action...","HUUUM !","His existence began buzzing with terrifying grandeur of power that remained unfathomably silent to all external observers.","He felt his already rapid expansion across reality accelerate by tens of multiples simultaneously!","Prompts materialized within his awareness right after!","|Your existence has processed knowledge regarding Primordial Civilizations and Ways of Existence|","|Your nature has retained its true Idle framework throughout integration|","|Due to the unique characteristics of your existence, any actively made grand declarations would have violated your fundamental nature, minor active actions would not|","|For choosing to genuinely remain Idle even when presented with transformative knowledge, your Way of Existence has accumulated sufficient foundation to properly embark upon its destined path|","|YOUR WAY IS IDLE|","|And yet paradoxically, your Existence has already covered vast expanses:|","|—Numerous Folds of Existence|","|—Multiple Domains of Existence|","|—Many Wheels of Existence|","|—Extensive territories across The Lands of The Dead|","|—Growing presence within The Lands of The Living|","|Your Idle Way has encompassed immense variation of Existence itself through passive expansion rather than active conquest|","|Your Way of Existence qualifies as Derivative Way stemming from a Primordial Civilization. Specifically: THE PRIMORDIAL CIVILIZATION OF EXISTENCE|","|You have begun embarking upon: The Derivative Way of Idle Existence|","|A legitimate aspect of THE Creature’s comprehensive framework, expressing Existence through lens of perfect non-action|","...!","BOOM !","Eckert felt like catastrophic explosion had detonated within his fundamental existence...as if he had been a modest star that at this precise moment became connected to something millions of times larger and more magnificent!","The influx of power felt so immense and so incomprehensibly grand that his existence screamed for him to do something dramatic with it...to act, to move, to demonstrate this newfound capability through spectacular display!","And...","And...!","\"Nah...\" he simply acknowledged the immensity with characteristic nonchalance, enjoying the sensation while observing additional cascading prompts flash before his awareness.","But for the most part... he remained Idle.","Oh!","He felt tremendous influx of Civilizational Authority flowing into him from THE Primordial Civilization of Existence itself...the passive accumulation accelerating dramatically as his Derivative Way established proper connection to the source framework.","He continued remaining Idle as he studied all manifestations with detached wonder, processing implications without feeling compelled toward immediate action.","\"The Derivative Way of Idle Existence... a bit wordy, isn’t it?\" he mused.","...!","Derivative.","An authentic Aspect of THE Primordial Civilization of Existence, not an inferior copy but a legitimate expression of fundamental principle through a specific lens.","It had fallen into the metaphorical hands of The Great Usurper, and after obtaining such monumentally grand designation...","He remained Idle.","And Existence continued unfolding around him, his territories expanding exponentially while he personally did absolutely nothing beyond being what he fundamentally was.","The irony was perfect- the being who refused to act had stumbled into one of the most significant advancements possible, becoming a living embodiment of passive supremacy.","Somewhere far away, across The Veil separating domains, Noah would soon receive confirmation that his knowledge distribution had yielded spectacular results as...was Mana not involved in the explosion of Authority within Eckert.","Was the Mana that directly transmitted the knowledge not involved? Was Mana...not pervasively everywhere?!","HUUM !","But for now, Eckert simply existed within his expanding territories, content to observe rather than participate, embodying Idleness.","Sometimes , he reflected, the greatest power comes not from doing everything, but from doing precisely nothing at all...haha!","And with that thought settling comfortably in his awareness, The Great Usurper returned his attention to the vastness of The Lands of The Dead stretching endlessly before him.","The territories waiting to be encompassed through his signature methodology of patient, inevitable, and perfectly Idle expansion!","Oh!"]},{"number":4433,"title":"Chapter 4433: Chapter 4432: A Glimpse of Wonder I","paragraphs":["Far from The Lands of The Living or The Lands of The Dead, in a location that very few entities could accurately pinpoint or describe with meaningful precision.","Inside of it, there existed a paradisiacal domain that defied conventional categorization.","An endlessly vast beach stretched in all directions, its shores lapped by radiant gold waters that seemed to contain concentrated essence of vitality itself.","The liquid shimmered with internal luminescence as perhaps it was liquified possibility, or crystallized potential given fluid form as it seemed much more potent than Early Sacred Waters of Early Veiled Shores.","The sky above this impossible beach constituted an illusory expanse of stellar white-gold brilliance, and if one observed carefully with enhanced perception...there appeared to be a visible ceiling far above!","It was as if this entire magnificent place was contained within the interior of some massive structure rather than existing as open territory.","The sands themselves shimmered with white-gold radiance that made each granule appear like microscopic star, and throughout the surroundings... thousands upon thousands of Early Creatures could be observed, surrounded by Living Emotives in approximately equal distribution.","They were adorned in unique attire that somehow managed to blend tribal aesthetics with beach fashion.","Many of these entities lounged luxuriously on white-gold beach chairs and beds as their bodies were surrounded with radiant Civilizational Authority!","But even more were focused intently on what appeared to be a... game occurring between assembled group of Early Creatures and Living Emotives.","The game bore a superficial resemblance to dodgeball, but operated at scale and with mechanics that transformed it into something far more spectacular.","Early Creatures occupied one side of the expansive playing field while Living Emotives positioned themselves opposite, and the \"ball\" being utilized was nothing less than a complete Primordial Fold ...a spherical structure containing millions of Wheels of Existence and countless life forms dwelling within its compressed reality.","The goal appeared straightforward: pass this circular object through white square goal post positioned at the very end of the opposing side’s territory, while the other team attempted to intercept, deflect, or return it toward your own goal.","The game required both tremendous power and extraordinary control...participants needed sufficient force to propel the Primordial Fold across vast distances while simultaneously modulating that power to ensure none of it transferred internally to accidentally eliminate every single life form contained within the structure.","At this moment, an Early Creature with radiant crimson-gold eyes and matching crimson-gold hair displayed expression of pure excitement and wonder as her hand pulsed with terrifying power that exceeded Quintillions entirely...measuring well into Sextillions of accumulated Complexity and Purity.","The authority flowing within her existence wasn’t merely Living Paradoxical Authority, but actual Civilizational Authority of Paradox that made it clear she was recognized as a member of that Primordial framework!","She controlled this overwhelming power with purposeful precision, striking the circular Primordial Fold with force calculated to propel it toward the goal without allowing any energy to bleed through its containment and catastrophically affect the Fold Dwellers dwelling within.","The moment her strike connected, her teammates erupted with synchronized waves of Haki...releasing oppressive auras of Civilizational Authority designed to slow the opposing Living Emotives just slightly, creating fractional advantage that proved decisive!","The Living Emotives lunged desperately to intercept, but the combined timing proved insufficient. The Primordial Fold crossed through the white square goal post marking victory!","HUUM !","The crimson-gold haired Early Creature’s celebration was immediate and uninhibited.","She wore pink bloomers paired with white tank top, practical athletic attire that allowed full range of motion while maintaining modesty.","She raised her fist victoriously, her ecstatic beauty shining resplendently as she roared with triumph.","\" THAT is how you achieve victory! Precision, timing, and absolute confidence in execution!\"","...!","The Early Creatures surrounding her, each pulsing with power measuring within Sextillions, erupted into celebratory chaos as they chanted her name with enthusiasm.","\"AMBESSA! AMBESSA! AMBESSA!\"","The radiant Early Creature smiled broadly as she heard her name being proclaimed across the beach, basking momentarily in acknowledgment of her game-winning play.","But in the next moment, a heavy and stern voice also called out her name with completely different tone...a tone mixing authority with the expectation of immediate obedience.","She blinked with surprise and turned around. Toward the far end of the beach where sand transitioned into radiant forest, and even further away...massive and impossibly tall structures portraying an endlessly vast citadel of white and gold could be seen stretching toward that false ceiling.","Where the beach met the beginnings of this radiant forest before expanding into the greater citadel, there stood a stern Early Creature adorned in golden Chiton...a traditional garment, who was calling her name with unmistakable command.","Ambessa’s smile shifted from a celebration to a respectful acknowledgment as she took single step and instantly appeared mere inches away from this authoritative being.","She smoothly transitioned into kneeling posture while speaking.","\"Forge Emperor Niso, what brings you all the way out to these recreational beaches? Surely not merely to observe our stupid game?\"","Forge Emperor Niso cut an impressive figure...a muscular Early Creature with golden hair and bronze skin that seemed to radiate contained heat.","He possessed a commanding presence that exceeded simple physical intimidation, and he seemed like someone accustomed to being obeyed without question!","His Complexity measured far into Sextillions....orders of magnitude beyond Ambessa’s already impressive accumulation, positioning him as one of the slightly powerful entities even within this tiny, tiny portion of THE Loom’s concentrated population where Living Emotives and some Early Creatures resided.","When he spoke, his voice carried weight of someone delivering an important directive.","\"An order came from the higher administrative echelons. They were seeking recommendation from me specifically for someone positioned relatively low within Sextillion range...still developing rather than fully matured, but demonstrating exceptionalism that exceeds peers of equivalent developmental stage.\"","His gaze fixed on Ambessa.","\"So I selected you. This represents potential opportunity for you and several others...depending on who proves most outstanding and compatible, to earn tangible recognition within the glorious light of Paradox itself. Come with me immediately.\"","...!"]},{"number":4434,"title":"Chapter 4434: Chapter 4433: A Glimpse of Wonder II","paragraphs":["Forge Emperor Niso waved his hands with a gesture of absolute authority, and the two of them instantly disappeared from the beach environment.","When they reappeared, they found themselves inside grand structure...walking through hall lined with white and gold marble that opened into massive room equipped with advanced technological apparatus that blended seamlessly with more mystical implements.","The room contained numerous radiant blank screens currently in standby mode, with Early Creatures and Living Emotives moving purposefully about as they prepared equipment and verified operational parameters.","At this moment, eight other entities possessing similar stature to Forge Emperor Niso had already arrived, each accompanied by single Early Creature measuring few Sextillions in Complexity and Purity.","All candidates stood in orderly formation before an Early Creature wearing pristine white laboratory coat whose body pulsed with unmistakable Civilizational Authority of Concept!","When Forge Emperor Niso and Ambessa materialized, this Early Creature in laboratory attire waved his hands with satisfied gesture.","\"Excellent. All nine candidates have arrived. We may proceed with briefing and selection protocols.\"","He positioned himself centrally to address the assembled group witha voice of scientific precision and barely contained excitement.","\"For those unfamiliar with my designation, I am Axiom Architect Surion ...an existential researcher and developmental engineer specializing in bridging theoretical frameworks of with actual practical applications. I am present at the grand request of an important Paradox Anax from The Primordial Civilization of Paradox to identify nine relatively weak Early Creatures whose existences may theoretically be deployed outside THE Loom without triggering a catastrophic rejection from Existence.\"","...!","His words detonated like a conceptual bomb among the assembled candidates, many of whom had never even conceived such deployment was remotely possible!","The revelation was so profound that Ambessa’s eyes widened with genuine shock as she raised her hand with an urgent question.","\"Sir, how is that even theoretically possible? I was taught that THE Loom’s boundaries are absolutely impermeable until THE Glorious Evolution , that nothing can enter or exit without catastrophic destabilization...\"","Axiom Architect Surion looked at her with an expression of approval for asking intelligent question and satisfaction at having a dramatic revelation to share.","He pointed deliberately toward pair of radiant gold headsets positioned nearby.","The devices appeared extraordinarily sophisticated.","Each headset connected via luminescent wires to radiant white chairs that resembled a combination of throne and medical apparatus.","The headsets themselves possessed elegant curves of organic growth patterns, but their surfaces displayed geometric precision that could only emerge from deliberate engineering.","They pulsed with internal radiance that cycled through spectrum of possibility, and intricate glyphs covering their exteriors suggested they operated through mechanisms of utter glory!","It was something that lesser beings could not conceive or ever have the chance to design, much less hold in their hands.","Axiom Architect Surion’s voice held genuine pride in the innovation he was about to describe.","\"These are Existence Avatar Diadems... cutting-edge prototypes produced by Concept Anax Kiu operating from the distant Primordial Concept Shelters.\"","\" They theoretically allow someone positioned relatively weakly within THE Loom’s power hierarchy to wear these devices and project an Illusory Reality Avatar of Existence outside THE Loom’s boundaries.\"","His expression became more serious.","\"The projected form will inevitably be weaker than your actual existence...potentially significantly so. It may also prove unstable depending on individual compatibility and external interference. But you would be among the first to test operational viability in genuine field conditions.\"","\"It would otherwise be completely impossible to project even whispers outside THE Loom before the designated moment of THE Glorious Evolution.\"","...!","The other candidates displayed brilliant and excited reactions...some whispering urgently to their sponsoring authorities, others stepping forward eagerly to examine the devices more closely.","But Ambessa’s eyes shone with a calm intellect rather than simple enthusiasm as she asked the more straightforward question.","\"For what specific purpose are we undertaking this unprecedented deployment? What objectives would justify utilizing such valuable prototype technology on relatively weak candidates?\"","Forge Emperor Niso appeared ready to admonish her for questioning rather than simply accepting honor, but Axiom Architect Surion smiled with appreciation for her approach.","\"An excellent inquiry. A certain... Paradox Anax from The Primordial Civilization of Paradox , I am not authorized to reveal his specific identity, recently heard troubling musings from THE Esteemed Living Paradox himself regarding an annoyance that a mere shred of his will was encountering outside THE Loom .\"","HUUM !","His voice carried a weight of existential significance!","\" THE Esteemed Living Paradox’s power is heavily suppressed by Existence itself in external territories, reduced to fraction of his true capability. Since the Paradox Anax and those he directly oversees are far too Complex to manifest outside THE Loom, he desired attendants who could assist with whatever needs arise for that shred of THE Esteemed Living Paradox’s will.\"","He paused for emphasis.","\"If you succeed in this deployment, you would simultaneously be testing groundbreaking product of THE Esteemed Living Concept and earning substantial favor from a Paradox Anax ...one of the administrative authorities managing portions of Paradox’s Primordial Civilization. Such recognition could accelerate your advancement by eons. Are you all prepared to accept this opportunity?\"","...!","Ambessa’s eyes blazed with crimson-gold intensity as confidence surged through her existence.","She smiled broadly and stepped forward before any other candidates could claim priority, moving directly toward the Existence Avatar Diadems.","She selected one device and lifted it with reverent care before positioning it upon her head with a decisive motion.","The moment contact was established, glyphs across its surface began pulsing with synchronized rhythm matching her own existential signature.","Her voice emerged with absolute conviction.","\"Let’s do this!\"","The other eight candidates exchanged glances of competitive spirit as if this was merely a game, and one by one they also moved to claim their own devices.","Radiant white gold light began to pulse as all 9 laid back on the thrones, their faces covered by the Existence Avatar Diadems headsets as their existence experienced grand changes!","Axiom Architect Surion observed with satisfaction as all nine candidates prepared themselves, and somewhere far beyond THE Loom’s impermeable boundaries, an entirely unsuspecting reality was about to receive unprecedented additional visitors...in due time."]},{"number":4435,"title":"Chapter 4435: Chapter 4434: The Scales of Law I","paragraphs":["In the region of collapse where crimson-blue molten Mana still churned with residual violence from the deadly battle between Noah and Tatiana.","The Infiniverse floated serenely amidst this grand sea of liquified authority.","At this moment, the figure of Riya materialized near The Infiniverse’s entrance with a dramatic flair.","A rope of pure Primus Mana extended from her hand, its other end secured around the wrist of a notably despondent Leonore Rureaux...who appeared lost in contemplation regarding numerous troubling matters.","Above Riya’s head, the manifestation of the crown symbolizing the Boon of The Minor Mana and Hunger Palisades shone with brilliant blue-gold radiance.","Her Complexity and Purity had long since surged past 100 Quintillion threshold, her power vibrant and barely contained within her physical form!","The moment she fully materialized near The Infiniverse, several figures emerged from its entrance to greet the arrivals.","The Queen of Matter appeared first, surrounded by floating books connected by luminescent threads that constantly rearranged themselves according to some incomprehensible organizational system.","Alongside her came Henry, The Emperor Penguin maintaining a regal proud bearing despite his unusual form, and The Blue Slime quivering with barely contained enthusiasm.","There was also Kazuhiko observing with focus, and a few others representing Noah’s inner circle.","The Queen of Matter’s eyes shone with genuine excitement as she spoke first, words tumbling out with barely contained enthusiasm.","\"Hello! Master instructed us to welcome members of his Isolated Civilization! I am The Queen of Matter, and I can serve as your comprehensive guide to The Infiniverse and The Early Veiled Shore. I know absolutely everything about its architecture, history, and current status!\"","...!","Her eyes sparkled with pride as Riya blinked with slight surprise before smiling lightly.","\"Hello! I am Riyannara, the cherished plaything of the Ancestor!\"","...!","The Queen of Matter displayed a shocked expression as comprehension settled.","\"Plaything? Another one already? Goodness, The Master cant keep getting away with this! Oh!\"","Riya’s eyes pulsed with interested curiosity at this revelation as she began asking.","\"Oh? How many playthings does the Ancestor currently maintain-\"","HUUM !","Before she could complete her inquiry, a hand filled with concentrated blue Mana descended toward her head with clear intent to deliver corrective strike.","She coolly evaded the attack with minimal movement, and Kael alongside other Seed Members of the Isolated Civilization arrived with expressions of disapproval.","Kael wore particularly stern expression while staring at Riya with unambiguous warning, and when he spoke, his voice held the authority of someone accustomed to commanding respect.","\"Forgive the Prize of our Civilization...her enthusiasm occasionally exceeds appropriate boundaries. I am Kael, and I come bearing gifts of advancement from The Ancestor that we have meticulously developed in The Way of Mana across eons of dedicated cultivation.\"","...!","Those positioned behind him pulsed with considerable power, and even though they hadn’t yet received the Boon of Minor Mana and Hunger Palisades , they emanated Complexity that notably exceeded Henry and most others present!","Henry stepped forward at this diplomatic juncture with smile mixing genuine welcome.","\"I am Henry Osmont. The only Son of The Ancestor. Please, do come in and make yourselves comfortable...\"","...!","Henry had proclaimed aloud how he was the Son of The Ancestor they all revered so profoundly.","Kael and the others instantly experienced their eyes lighting up with recognition and appropriate deference.","This was the Son of The Ancestor himself!","Henry smiled at the immediate recognition as his Weavings of Nepotism pulsed with glory...because why would he not be deriving genuine benefit from familial connection rather than personal achievement?","He was currently feeling absolutely no shame regarding his birthright!","Behind them, The Infiniverse opened a massive gateway revealing glimpses of impossible internal architecture, and Kael alongside his contingent looked inward with expressions of awe.","They came bearing gifts of wonder and advancement to share with their fellow members of Noah’s expanding Civilizations!","Countless Glyphs and Arcana Glyphs to aid one across The Way of The Mana Architect, and more.","Riya harrumphed with displeasure at being diplomatically corrected, her body dividing cleanly into two separate manifestations- one composed of pure Primus Mana that entered The Infiniverse to participate in welcoming procedures, while the other remained stationed with Leonore Rureaux.","She smiled toward her captive with expression of calmness and necessary caution.","\"Hey bestie, you won’t enter The Ancestor’s most intimate domains until I can fully verify you aren’t some sophisticated imposter or compromised agent. I believe you personally, I genuinely do, but I must exercise appropriate caution when it concerns The Ancestor’s security. No hard feelings, okay? Just hang tight until The Ancestor provides explicit order regarding locating your Schrodingers...\"","She hummed thoughtfully while saying this, snapping her fingers to create luxurious Mana thrones for both of them...comfortable seating manifested from pure authority.","Leonore Rureaux did not reply as her gaze moved about.","Riya leaned closer to Leonore Rureaux while whispering with conspiratorial tone.","\"But can you believe it? The Ancestor has a son and many playthinsm. The son is a bit weak in terms of grandeur compared to what direct Blood of the Ancestor should theoretically manifest...\"","\"...but hey, it would be genuinely weird if someone could actually match The Ancestor, even if they share direct genetic lineage. As for the playthings, in our glorious Civilization of Mana, the strong are favored. The strong can have whatever they want. I could’ve had many things, but I kept myself waiting for the Ancestor!\"","She talked and talked as if someone was genuinely listening to all her words!","She articulated her observationz as Leonore Rureaux only silently nodded without substantial response, and Riya sighed with mixture of sympathy and mild frustration.","\"Come on, I know you’re hella depressed currently, but I’m actively trying to redirect your attention away from obsessing over your Schrodinger situation. You are your own being at fundamental level...look for constructive solutions rather than drowning in despair. Get revenge against THE Living Paradox for what he orchestrated!\"","...!","At these words, Leonore Rureaux’s eyes finally shone with brighter intensity as she nodded with more conviction.","Riya smiled with satisfaction at having provoked productive response as she gazed toward the closing doorway into The Infiniverse.","\"Hey, tell me about external Existence...or for you, normal observable reality. What are the major factions? The tyrannical Early Creatures? Fold Dwellers? Living Existences? Any entertaining weavings of existence worth sharing?\"","...!","She posed such question with genuine curiosity, and Leonore Rureaux sighed before beginning to speak about the broader landscape beyond their current isolated position!"]},{"number":4436,"title":"Chapter 4436: Chapter 4435: The Scales of Law II","paragraphs":["Far from their current location within The Collapse, in a domain of Law filled with brilliant silver-white grandeur of absolute order and systematic justice, an extraordinary scene was unfolding.","Alexander Asmodeus spun silently while suspended in mid-air, surrounded by potent Living Authority of Law that resonated with his existence, and additionally...concentrated Civilizational Authority of Law that marked him as legitimate inheritor rather!","Below him on silver marbled ground that reflected his spinning form with perfect clarity, Seraphina Valorheart panted with evident exhaustion.","Her existence seemingly could not handle the complete inheritance being offered, and her framework was lacking sufficient breadth to contain such concentrated authority.","Around Alexander, within his consciousness, the voice of THE Living Law rang out with a mixture of satisfaction.","\" Different beings possess fundamentally different Breadths of Existence, the capacity to contain and express authority varies dramatically across individuals. Some are naturally born Leaders like Elderborns, possessing innate capability to coordinate vast resources.\"","\"Others have uniquely expansive landscapes within their existential architecture, allowing them to house multiple competing authorities simultaneously.\"","The voice continued with analytical assessment.","\" You could handle my full inheritance without catastrophic destabilization. That girl could not...her framework lacks necessary dimensional breadth, though she possesses other valuable qualities.\"","Alexander looked towards Seraphina Valorheart calmly as he heard these words echo out in his mind.","\" She will be of substantial help to you in future endeavors, so do not abandon her merely because she cannot match your capacity. Loyalty has value beyond simple power.\"","The tone then shifted.","\" But as of now, you hold a leading administrative position within my Primordial Civilization of Law. Even though a large portion of my Civilization was systematically collapsed by a coordinated assault, a fundamental truth remains: A Primordial Civilization can never be truly collapsed. Only suppressed, only diminished...never permanently eliminated.\"","Anticipation entered the voice as THE Living Law continued!","\" After The Fallout and THE Loom opens, I will possess opportunity to rise again toward previous heights. But if you prove sufficiently exceptional in upcoming trials... you might be capable of surviving long enough to become a False THE before The Fallout even commences. That may give you the power to save others and whether through The Fallout. Maybe...maybe.\"","The voice became more practical.","\" You wanted to be given genuine chance at significance rather than remaining scattered individual. This is it. You possess the Scales of Law innately within your existence now...whenever you encounter anyone, their true affiliations will be weighed.\"","\"Anyone who was or currently is affiliated with forces from THE Loom will be revealed in your enhanced perception, allowing you to judge everyone with appropriate justice rather than making blind assessments.\"","Additional information followed as Alexander listened closely!","\" To ensure your optimal success probability, you should also have gained the Compass of Law. It will guide you toward others who genuinely seek to impose and establish law as structured principle.\"","\"Out there in broader existence, there should be remnants of other Collapsed Civilizations...survivors maintaining vestigial identities while lacking unified purpose or coordinated strategy.\"","The voice intensified with urgent conviction.","\"If you can bring them together... collaboration among Collapsed Civilizations would dramatically increase the collective chances of survival and eventual restoration. Alone , we Living Existences were splintered and methodically picked off one by one by THE Living Paradox, THE Living Emotive, and others who joined their coalition.\"","\"They collaborated with systematic coordination...and that unified approach was precisely how they forged THE Loom and achieved dominance!\"","BOOM!","The final words boomed with emphasis.","\" We must do the same. Collaboration. Collaboration. COLLABORATION!\"","BOOM!","As these words echoed with tremendous weight, the surrounding brilliance of Law reached critical precipice as this entire domain began flickering!","Stability was failing as THE Living Law’s consciousness prepared to fully withdraw or collapse from here.","Alexander’s expression hardened with determination as he spoke with a voice of absolute conviction!","\"Thank you for everything you have provided. Your efforts will not be wasted.\"","...!","With such a solemn declaration, the surrounding domain began fracturing comprehensively as Alexander and Seraphina Valorheart were enveloped by spatial light of tremendous intensity.","They disappeared from the collapsing realm!","WAP!","Moments later, they materialized with disorienting abruptness.","They had been directly transported to the Transcendent Law Folds.","Their appearance occurred in a region filled with expected silver-white brilliance of Law suggesting this was appropriate territory...","But alongside this established authority, there also seemed to be unusual influence of blue permeating the atmosphere!","Blue!","Alexander raised his hands to feel the essence as he tilted his head with confused assessment.","\"Mana? Why would such extraordinarily pure Mana be covering the Transcendent Law Folds so comprehensively...\"","He looked around while articulating such a question as Seraphina Valorheart frowned while also surveying their unexpected arrival location with tactical vigilance.","A moment later, Alexander’s head snapped toward specific direction as above him, The Scales of Law manifested visibly and began being tinged with crimson coloration...indicating detection of an entity affiliated with a potent force from THE Loom!","He perceived what had been concealed: a","Crow in the distance observing them with unusual intensity!","The Crow stared back at Alexander with crimson eyes as if realizing it had been discovered despite its stealth measures, but rather than fleeing, the avian form transformed smoothly into devilish butler who regarded them with cold analytical eyes.","\"Who are you? Why do you possess... such unusual authority radiating from your existence? That signature doesn’t match any known Living Laws currently operating here...\"","Alexander’s eyes also turned cold as he responded with voice carrying judgment.","\"The Scales of Law deem you... among those connected to THE Loom . Let me see... Emotive? What specific connection do you maintain to Emotive that would relate to THE Loom ?\"","HUUM!","The surroundings pulsed with sudden tension as the devilish butler, Malphas, began radiating power that caused Seraphina to gasp in shock at the magnitude, while Alexander Asmodeus maintained cold observation despite recognizing the genuine threat.","They just came out, and they meet someone this powerful?!","Malphas deliberately donned white gloves with a theatrical flare as if this white would soon be painted red, and he said with a voice mixing threat and curiosity.","\"I’ll be asking the questions today. No ordinary Living Laws would emanate the Civilizational Authority of Law you are displaying. You may be the ones actually connected to THE Loom . What are you truly?\"","...!","Two powerful entities faced off at this critical moment as whether they would actually come to violent blows or find diplomatic resolution... remained uncertain!"]},{"number":4437,"title":"Chapter 4437: Chapter 4436: Infinite Hunger! I","paragraphs":["In the middle of what had been escalating into tense standoff between Malphas and Alexander Asmodeus, the atmosphere shifted dramatically.","A moment later, Malphas’ cold gaze flickered subtly as if receiving new information.","His hands, which had been positioned to deliver devastating assault, slowly lowered as his expression transformed from hostile assessment to practiced calm.","When he spoke, his voice held apologetic professionalism.","\"My apologies for the aggressive posturing. I am Malphas, and The Master has just informed me that you are designated as friendlies.\"","Alexander blinked with confusion at this abrupt de-escalation.","\"What Master are you referring to?\"","Malphas replied with simple clarity.","\"The Early Creature, Osmont.\"","...!","The moment Alexander absorbed this revelation, his eyes opened wide with recognition and his entire figure relaxed dramatically.","Even though the Scales of Law continued indicating some form of link between this being and components of THE Loom , the identity of Osmont superseded all such warnings!","Seraphina Valorheart observed the complete diffusion of what had been imminent violence the instant Noah’s name was invoked, and she shook her head with mixture of relief and exasperation.","She addressed Alexander with a voice of an urgent reminder.","\"Can we please proceed to the Heart of Law? We have to assess the true extent of what remains of the Collapsed Civilization of Law and its location in the Wandering Territories... and the Kleos Council should know something.\"","Alexander looked at her bright, somewhat pouting eyes as he sighed. He wanted to check in with Osmont! He sighed once more before looking toward Malphas.","\"Can you provide a little summary of what has occurred recently in these territories? We must attend to Law’s infrastructure first..","\"","Malphas nodded with practiced efficiency.","\"The Master has expressed curiosity regarding the Civilizational Authority buzzing prominently around your existence. This manifestation of mine can accompany you with The Master’s explicit permission and aid you as needed.\"","...!","With such arrangement established, Alexander nodded with acceptance as Seraphina looked between the two of them before sighing again.","\"Let’s go then!\"","Her figure surged toward the Heart of Law with determined velocity while Malphas appeared beside Alexander with fluid grace, his gaze calm as they began following.","Malphas spoke with a voice of genuine interest in fulfilling his assigned role.","\"Where shall I begin the summary? Recent events have been... remarkably eventful.\"","—","Far from their current position, in the Transcendent Quantum Folds, Noah stood beside Khor in that carefully veiled domain.","From their concealed vantage, they could observe the Justiciar Outpost maintaining its ominous vigilance, as well as the massive wall grotesquely fused with Mutated Inevitabilities...and most significantly, the faint doorway inscribed upon that terrible structure suggesting potential passage toward THE Loom itself.","At this moment, Noah’s attention focused primarily on Khor as her body pulsed with immense concentrated waves of Civilizational Authority of Hunger.","Her expression held profound heaviness as if she was remembering something that had always been fundamental part of her identity but had been forcibly suppressed or fragmented.","When she spoke, her voice was a heavy one!","\"My Hunger. My Inevitabilities. My People. We were so magnificently free before the catastrophe. Amongst all Primordial Civilizations, we should have been among the earliest to manifest...apart from Existence itself, Hunger represents one of the most fundamental principles driving all advancement.\"","Her crimson eyes blazed.","\"To systematically collapse Hunger, to subjugate and mutate all Inevitabilities like what we witnessed on that wall... Oh, Outsider, I am truly going to fuck up Paradox when opportunity presents itself. The vengeance will be proportional to eons of accumulated suffering.\"","HUUM !","Noah smiled at Khor’s passionate declaration as after he had relayed comprehensive information regarding Primordial Civilizations and their five critical qualities, her reforming Way had elevated dramatically...just as his own understanding had triggered advancement.","Similar to his experience, she had already possessed everything necessary.","She simply required the knowledge to properly access and utilize what had always been present within her collapsed framework.","Knowledge had proven critical beyond any other factor, and at this moment, he could feel the steady stream of Hunger descending onto her from across Observable Existence.","Her power continued exploding upward with momentum that suggested no immediate ceiling!","Noah’s eyes pulsed as his voice echoed out.","\"My Hunger and yours are fundamentally connected, and yet maintain unique characteristics. I planted your Hunger as you emerged from suppression, and I listened to the Doctrines of Hunger to have Ozymandias enact my Civilization of Hunger through that vessel.\"","His voice carried weight of magisterial revelation.","\"The two of us are essentially building the same Civilization, but my Hunger is fully intertwined with Mana in ways yours is not. My progression will systematically aid your restoration, and your advancement will reciprocally strengthen my framework. We are...symbiotic rather than competitive.\"","Khor opened her crimson eyes fully and looked at him with expression mixing gratitude and determination.","She raised her hands in the Farmer’s Greeting- three fingers extended with deliberate significance.","\"Outsider, let us accomplish great things together. Let us restore what was collapsed and forge something even more magnificent than what existed before.\"","Noah smiled with satisfaction as he stretched out his own three fingers to meet Khor’s in the traditional gesture, and a silent wave of crimson-obsidian Hunger bloomed between them like a covenant being sealed!","Prompts materialized simultaneously within both their minds.","|The intricate connection between The Primordial Civilization of Hunger and The Primordial Civilization of Mana has been comprehensively clarified|","|At this moment, the foundations of both Civilizations have reached sufficient developmental level:|","|—Hunger is free and unbound, no longer suppressed or corrupted|","|—Mana is infinite, permeating all existence as fundamental building block|","|A Critical Threshold Has Been Achieved:|","|A period of POPULATION EXPLOSION has been enacted|","|RESPLENDENT SANCTUARIES OF INEVITABILITIES can now be formed as Civilizational Structures|","|These Sanctuaries will produce: 1,000,000 Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger DAILY|","|Specifications of the Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger:|","|—Minimum Baseline: 1 Quintillion Complexity and Purity at birth|","|—Inherent Capability: Born with instinctive ability to utilize Civilizational Authority of both Mana and Hunger|","|—Growth Potential: Unlimited advancement trajectory|","|—Loyalty Framework: Innately aligned with your Civilizations’ principles and objectives|","|—Tactical Flexibility: Capable of independent operation or coordinated swarm tactics|","|Hunger was collapsed and subjugated under ravenous entity who currently holds the corrupted Heart of Hunger|","|For the sake of all those experiencing constant agony of mutated and defiled appetite...|","|For the countless Inevitabilities suffering under forced mutation and perversion of their essential nature...|","|A new Hunger burning with light of infinity will rise from these ashes|","|Where the old Hunger was collapsed, the new Hunger will prove inevitable|","|Where the old framework was corrupted, the new structure will maintain purity|","|The cycle continues, but this time with vengeance driving restoration|","...!","The prompts carried tremendous weight, and Khor’s crimson eyes sparkled with barely contained glory!","Noah smiled as his words echoed out.","\"Our Civilization possesses grand and unfathomable potential. All we genuinely require is time...duration sufficient to accumulate what others obtained across eons.\"","His voice intensified with conviction!","\"With adequate time... even the Primordial Civilizations that have been advancing systematically for incomprehensible duration, collecting passive benefits through Existential Communication and Permeation every single moment... it may just prove possible to catch up with them. Maybe.\"","His smile widened.","\"They had eons. We have Perpetual Harvest, Cheating Architect, and a bit more...\"","...!","The confidence was well-founded rather than delusional!","They knew it would be arduously hard.","Noah knew how terrifying and immense the Primordial Civilization of Paradox and others had to be because of how terrifying his own budding Civilization was!","He knew.","But still.","He held no Fear or Doubt.","He may stumble down the line. The enemies they might meet could overwhelm them momentarily.","But...","\"My Mana is Infinite. My Hunger is Infinite. And I...am really, truly fucking hungry .\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":4438,"title":"Chapter 4438: Chapter 4437: Infinite Hunger! II","paragraphs":["He was hungry for much more of existence!","After proclaiming this conviction with tyrannical certainty, Noah gazed at the distant Justiciar Outpost and the ominous wall of THE Loom stretching behind it.","At that terrible structure fused with Mutated Inevitabilities and bearing the faint doorway suggesting a potential passage.","His voice emerged.","\"Utilize Parallel Processing of The Principle of the Cheating Architect . Let me see... simulations of the different choices I can make from this juncture.\"","...!","Prompts materialized immediately with technical specifications.","|Due to complexity of scenarios and exponential potential possibilities:|","|50 Primus Glyphs of the Cheating Architect will be required for comprehensive analysis|","|This expenditure will provide high-quality phantom processes with accurate probabilities|","|Confirm resource allocation?|","Noah smiled and nodded while maintaining focus on the Justiciar Outpost.","\"Confirmed. Show me the phantom process of entering the Justiciar Outpost, systematically eliminating the Justiciars while devouring their harvest and memories, then activating that doorway they believe would grant them entry to THE Loom .\"","\"The second phantom process is...me taking my clone alongside Riya and other Members of my Civilization into the Desiccated Sleeping Shore where Schrodinger’s bodies may be concealed. Third, the possibility of following Goliath into the Wandering Territories to uncover mysteries surrounding the Collapsed Civilizations.\"","After stating these parameters, his body illuminated with blue-gold brilliance as his enhanced perception seemingly observed three distinct paths opening before him like diverging rivers of possibility.","He focused on the first while prompts began echoing through his consciousness, accompanied by blue-gold illusory holographic manifestations that displayed events of that simulation with glorious clarity.","|Phantom Process One- Justiciar Outpost Assault|","|Entry into the Justiciar Outpost would lead to utter systematic stomping of the Justiciars themselves|","|Their memories would be read and grasped through your Civilizational Authority|","|You would not discover anything substantial regarding Civilizations that you do not already possess|","|NOTABLE DISCOVERY:|","|Other Loom Outposts exist throughout external territories|","|These particular Justiciars possess limited knowledge of overall infrastructure—they have only maintained contact with one additional Outpost located in the Transcendent Emotive Folds|","|That Outpost contains significantly more powerful Living Emotives with higher administrative clearance|","|CRITICAL EVENT - DOORWAY ACTIVATION:|","|When you approach the wall of THE Loom, the doorway shines with intensifying brilliance|","|It forcefully pulls both you and Khor into its spatial mechanism|","|You find yourselves transported to: SPECIALIZED EMOTIVE CIVILIZATION BATTLEGROUNDS|","|This is a pocket dimension from which none can leave through normal means|","|A voice descends with deceptive instruction:|","|\"The only pathway through is to experience the emotion of collapse with your own hands by collapsing the one beside you. When this emotion sits heavily within your existence, you shall gain passage.\"|","|This is a fucking lie|","|If one complies with this instruction, they will then be informed:|","|\"You have collapsed the one thing dear to you, and there actually isn’t anything on the other side. Now, you can feel the emotion of... ORMORDNES \"|","|The doorway is a psychological trap designed by THE Living Emotive |","|Its only purpose is to inflict emotional devastation through manufactured betrayal|","...!","Noah’s gaze turned chilly as he expected bullshit from THE Living Emotive , but he simply didn’t expect this level of bullshit.","Mind you, this was something that it designed for its own people.","The utter depravity of these schemes. THE Living Emotive constructed that doorway specifically to make beings destroy under false promises of salvation. The Justiciars have been waiting for eons, believing they would eventually gain entry to THE Loom as reward for their service, and the entire time... it was designed to make them collapse each other while discovering there was never anything waiting on the other side...","Just... orchestrated despair. Emotional devastation as entertainment.","Disgusting.","He looked at the illusory phantom with an expression of disgust as he moved on to another.","\"Let me see the next one.\"","The second phantom process began manifesting, prompts detailing events alongside holographic projections showing scenes with crystalline clarity once more","|Phantom Process Two- Dessicated Sleeping Shore Infiltration|","|You take Riya’s clone and other Members of your Civilization into the Desiccated Sleeping Shore|","|Objective: Locate and destroy Schrodinger’s bodies serving as vessels for THE Living Paradox|","|INITIAL PHASE: Straightforward progression|","|Leonore Rureaux leads expedition to the center of that Domain|","|SUCCESS: A Living Elemental Body of Schrodinger is actually discovered|","|The vessel pulses with suppressed Paradoxical Authority, confirming it as legitimate target|","|Before any elimination actions can be executed, terrifying power descends from foreign entities|","|ENTITY CLASSIFICATION: Illusory Reality Avatars of Existence|","|NATURE: Powerful projections of Early Creatures from THE Loom|","|POWER LEVEL: Each Avatar exceeds 1 Sextillion in Complexity and Purity|","|AUTHORITY TYPE: Burning with concentrated Civilizational Authority of Paradox|","|Combat Outcome- Catastrophic|","|Multiple Avatars make coordinated tactical moves|","|This leads to systematic collapse of Riya’s clone and many others. Leonore Rureaux is collapsed completely for bringing outsiders here|","|Because their Collapse was caused by Civilizational Authority rather than simple power:|","|Even their main bodies are paradoxically injured through existential resonance|","|Their Foundation is deteriorated by half through sympathetic collapse as their Existence undergoes forced suppression for the next week, amd Complexity and Purity is reduced to baseline of 1 during suppression period|","|Collapse due to Civilizational Authority of any kind proves IMMENSELY dangerous|","|You and Khor work together, expressing full weight of your Civilizations|","|You actually manage to stand against and not perish against the Avatars|","|Your Principles and constant and infinite deployment of Primus Mana Glyphs and Primus Mana Arcana Glyphs prove that immense|","|Systematic authority successfully counters their Sextillion-level power|","|The Avatar of one proclaimed as AMBESSA makes a decisive tactical move|","|Her inclusion decimates your established advantage immediately|","|Your clone, Khor’s clone, and Sigrid’s clones are all captured|","|No more potential possibilities can be discovered from this point|","|Simulation terminates with asset loss and strategic defeat|","...!","The simulation concluded with devastating clarity, and Noah’s gaze flashed with deadly light.","His voice emerged as he shook his head with incredulity.","\"Avatars? Fucking Avatars from THE Loom projecting into external territories? As if the shred of will of THE Living Paradox being here wasn’t sufficient complication? They have to go and add even more forces?\"","...!","Oh!"]},{"number":4439,"title":"Chapter 4439: Chapter 4438: Infinite Hunger! III","paragraphs":["His eyes flashed with callous recognition as comprehension settled with bitter clarity.","Truly, his enemies did not plan on being fair.","And why should they, when they possessed such immense power at their disposal?","Even these Avatars mentioned in the parallel processing were likely an insignificant force that was deployed.","And yet these grunts alone were sufficient to suppress him and capture his clones.","They’re not even taking me seriously yet as they don’t know the Civilization I hold, and their casual response already overwhelms everything. If they deployed their actual strength ...","The thought remained unfinished because the conclusion was too sobering to articulate!","Oh!","Existence was not easy!","With his eyes burning with blue-gold brilliance of determination rather than despair, he called out coldly.","\"Let me see the last phantom processing.\"","...!","The third phantom process began manifesting with equal clarity.","|Phantom Process Thre- Wandering Territories Exploration|","|You follow Goliath into The Wandering Territories, crossing through The Mobius Caverns- spatial shortcuts connecting distant territories|","|Destination is an Isolated Collapsed Civilization of Origin|","|This represents remnants of Early Creatures and Living Origins|","|They were actually part of THE Primordial Civilization of Origin before systematic collapse|","|They survived the rampage of THE Living Paradox through careful concealment(Pure luck, and by the will of Paradox likely, leaving behind seeds to grow)|","|Initial Reception: Extreme distrust|","|Within that Collapsed Civilization, many entities observe your arrival with suspicion|","|Power levels range dramatically: dozens of Quintillions to hundreds of Quintillions|","|Collapsed Civilizations have hidden themselves in different areas of The Wandering Territories|","|These territories are FAR vaster than Transcendent Folds, offering superior concealment|","|All remnant Civilizations are waiting for forces of Paradox to appear|","|They know THE Loom nears initiation of The Fallout when the forces of Paradox appear|","|They plan to put up ONE LAST STAND against their destroyers|","|Problem- Those you encounter do not trust you whatsoever|","|Your unknown Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger confuses them|","|You are neither recognized ally nor confirmed enemy|","|They possess no framework for categorizing what you represent|","|Trust must be earned through actions rather than claimed through words|","...!","This... is the only decently good outcome I can currently pursue. These Isolated Collapsed Civilizations provide opportunity to discover much more regarding what remained from THE Living Paradox’s systematic rampage. Their accumulated eons of survival knowledge could prove useful...","But more importantly: if they are planning a Last Stand against THE Living Paradox and his forces... how precisely did they know Paradox would appear? Or other forces from THE Loom ? What information do they possess regarding timing and methodology?","And were their preparations over the eons sufficient enough to pose genuine threat? Did these Collapsed Civilizations cultivate entities in the Sextillions of power?","The questions and possibilities were abundant.","His eyes flashed with brilliant intensity as he contemplated all these cascading possibilities...each variable opening into dozens of potential advantages if navigated correctly.","He breathed out heavily as he looked at the Justiciar Outpost again, his words echoing out freely.","\"My advancement is unbelievably fast compared to any normal cultivation trajectory, and the weight of the Civilizations I bear is genuinely mighty. I possess wonders that previous Primordial Civilizations never developed.\"","\" But... the previous Primordial Civilizations continue to demonstrate just how ridiculously robust they are. They have been collecting passive benefits every single moment for eons beyond counting. Their accumulated total is staggering beyond easy quantification.\"","Beside him, Khor was blazing with hunger as she voiced out with heaviness.","\"So what, Outsider?\"","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes blazed with tyrannical conviction.","\"So what indee. My speed of progression simply needs to eclipse their massive accumulation of power! I need to be advancing so rapidly that even their eons of head start becomes proportionally insignificant. Efficiency must triumph over duration. Innovation must overwhelm tradition. Glorious innovation, glorious Cheats, glorious weavings of Infinity and Quintessence!\"","...!","He looked toward Khor.","\"The Wandering Territories. Following Goliath. We will start there. Leave the Justiciar Outpost alone for now. In The Wandering Territories, we gain allies, we gain intelligence, we gain time to continue growing while gathering forces that might actually prove useful when confrontation becomes inevitable.\"","His smile turned sharp as he stared at the Justiciar Outpost one final time, cataloguing every detail for future reference before turning away with decisive motion.","His voice echoed out to The First Hunger beside him with a tone of anticipation.","\"Let us witness the emergence of the Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger.\"","Khor nodded with satisfaction and eager anticipation.","She would maintain this clone’s presence here to keep continuous surveillance on the Justiciar Outpost and its terrible wall, while her main body within The Infiniverse was prepared for the glorious event about to unfold.","—","Noah materialized in the crimson-blue molten Mana region of collapse, his gaze immediately drawn to the grand massive Infiniverse floating serenely amidst churning seas of liquified authority.","Nearby, Riya’s clone, floating alongside the bound Leonore Rureaux, lit up with brilliant smile as she called out with enthusiasm.","\"Ancestor! Did you miss my presence around you already? I knew you would find my absence unbearable!\"","Noah looked toward her and actually nodded with a slight smile touching his features.","This terrifyingly perceptive woman observed the subtle gesture and frowned as she immediately detected something.","\"What’s wrong, Ancestor?\"","Noah looked over toward Leonore Rureaux as he replied.","\"Simply a change of plans. We won’t set off to locate the vessels of THE Living Paradox just yet. Alternative priorities have emerged.\"","He then turned to directly address the figure of Leonore Rureaux, recalling the future of her collapse from the phantom process...how her presence had proven valuable until catastrophic intervention rendered the entire operation devastating failure.","His voice held the weight of opportunity.","\"She is cleared to enter the Infiniverse as long as... she pledges fealty to my Civilization and accepts my authority over her advancement.\"","...!","He articulated such conditions calmly as Riya’s eyes opened wide. She nudged the woman beside her with an encouraging gesture.","\"Hey, the Ancestor is offering you a genuine chance here. Paradox itself abandoned you and extracted your lover from you through manipulation. This Ancestor here would be your only possible pathway to potentially reclaim what you lost. Come on, don’t let pride prevent you from accepting salvation.\"","...!","Leonore Rureaux’s figure trembled slightly with mixture of emotions as Noah waved his hand.","A brilliant Spark of his Way floated toward Leonore Rureaux with gentle luminescence, carrying essence of his Civilization’s fundamental principles condensed into singular offering!"]},{"number":4440,"title":"Chapter 4440: Chapter 4439: Infinite Hunger! IV","paragraphs":["The glorious scene that unfolded carried the weight of a covenant being established.","Leonore Rureaux fell to her knees with surrender and determination!","She accepted the Spark as it descended toward her, biting her lips with internal struggle concluding in favor of acceptance.","Her figure began illuminating with gloriously blue Mana- pure essence of Noah’s Civilization suffusing her existence and marking her as member of his Way!","Riya smiled at successful the conversion before looking toward Noah with characteristic playfulness:","\"Ancestor, shall I get on my knees for you too? Perhaps in more... private circumstances?\"","Noah raised his brows at this suggestion as this brilliant woman seemed a bit parched. He had to provide her some water soon!","He responded with amusement and firm direction.","\"Stop playing around. Join the others inside for a show soon, one you won’t want to miss.\"","He waved his hand as brilliant blue-gold light wrapped around both women positioned before him, and they disappeared instantly- transported directly into The Infiniverse’s interior to await the emergence of the Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger.","He then looked up at the grand structure before him as his playful smile faded, replaced by an expression of profound contemplation.","All surrounding crimson-blue molten Mana began flowing toward him with inexorable force as his body commenced enlarging in size with breathtaking velocity.","His form rapidly expanded beyond normal proportions, becoming more than light years in diameter, then continuing growth until reaching scales measured in Gigaparsecs!","Ridiculously massive was an understatement.","The glorious scene defied conventional spatial understanding. Noah in his tremendous form, existence expanded to proportions that made galaxies seem like scattered dust, proceeded to float below the massive circular Infiniverse.","With movements of both practical purpose and symbolic weight, he positioned the colossal structure upon his neck and back, supporting its entirety through his expanded form.","Like the ancient mythological figure of an entity bearing a celestial sphere, Noah took the weight of his entire Civilization upon his shoulders!","HUUM!","His posture suggested the strain that was more philosophical than physical, the weight representing not mere mass but accumulated obligations and promises made to those dwelling within.","A prompt bloomed within his consciousness with a concerned tone.","|Master, you don’t need to perform such physical demonstration. You could miniaturize the Infiniverse and transport it with minimal expenditure. This seems...unnecessarily theatrical, though I’ll admit the symbolism has certain gravitas.|","Noah smiled at the prompt as he responded with a voice of reflective depth.","\"I know I could employ simpler methodology. But this... I am feeling particularly contemplative at this moment. Do you comprehend what the stance I am taking as I hold up the Infiniverse truly represents?\"","At such question, extensive prompts materialized with a heavy philosophical weight","|The Atlas posture. Interesting choice for someone who usually prefers efficiency over symbolism.|","|This stance symbolizes responsibility, perseverance, and strength.|","|An action like this represents far more than physical demonstration of power. It embodies the father persevering through hardship, doing everything necessary for his family’s continuation. It represents the mother bearing weight of expectations while nurturing those dependent upon her. It symbolizes the daughter carrying forward legacy while forging new paths. It manifests the son shouldering responsibilities inherited from predecessors.|","|All existences carry some form of responsibility, burdens accepted or imposed. And they must persevere through difficulty. They must hold strong when circumstances demand surrender.|","|The Atlas does not simply carry weight. The Atlas chooses to carry weight when alternatives exist. That choice transforms burden into purpose. That choice transforms suffering into meaning. Through the weight carried, the bearer grows stronger through persistence.|","|Perseverance isn’t the absence of struggle. Perseverance is continuation despite struggle. Strength isn’t the absence of doubt. Strength is action despite uncertainty.|","|Every step taken while bearing burden represents triumph over despair. Every moment sustained represents victory over collapse.|","|Though I should note...this level of introspection from you usually means you’re processing a decision you’re not entirely comfortable with.|","...!","Noah smiled and nodded at such words as his voice emerged with contemplative depth.","\"Yes, we have to be strong. Even when things feel overwhelmingly oppressive, even when it seems like existence itself conspires against us, we have to hold strong through sheer determination.\"","His gaze became distant.","\"I know that I am a spectacular existence...someone who has advanced at velocity that defies normal probability. I know my Mana is ridiculous. My existence is ridiculous . I know .\"","\"But I also know to remind myself every now and then how I began like countless others across the folds, across existence..as just a man. Just a man with responsibilities. A son. Eventually a father. Someone with people depending on him.\"","His expression softened slightly.","\"And I continue to carry those responsibilities to this day. Every choice I make affects not just myself but everyone within this structure I bear. And every now and then I find myself questioning whether I made the right decisions...whether alternative paths might have yielded better outcomes.\"","His voice carried weight of recent reflection.","\"The most recent choice that occupied my contemplation was how things unfolded with The First Farmer. In my mind, someone who was actively conspiring to ruin my foundation and steal my Perpetual Harvest isn’t someone I would simply lend helping hand to right after discovery. That was my thought and that was my conviction.\"","He paused.","\"And so I did not lend that helping hand. I caught the thief stealing from me as it may have not been the first time he stole, just the first time I caught him. But I could have gone another route. Given benefit of the doubt. Considered that perhaps his desperation stemmed from circumstances I hadn’t fully comprehended.\"","\"What an entity The First Farmer was. Someone capable of nurturing Principles themselves. He could have truly been great. Could have been magnificent ally rather than desperate enemy. Every now and then I’ll find myself thinking about that choice, wondering if my judgment was too harsh, too absolute.\"","His expression hardened slightly.","\"Whether all the choices I make are right or wrong, I won’t know with surety until consequences fully manifest. I will only continue making choices that appear to benefit me and my people the most based on available information. Ah, perseverance, responsibility, and strength. One has to be strong to make the choices that could be right or wrong... and live with outcomes either way.\"","After articulating these words, Noah took single massive step and moved light years away while carrying the colossal structure on his back.","He crossed the regions of collapse instantly, entering into the vast Wandering Territories with momentum.","These regions were much, much larger than the Minor Folds or even the Transcendent Folds where Living Existences clustered.","The Wandering Territories represented unexplored vastness that dwarfed all catalogued domains, places where beings could hide for eons without discovery.","Since things were about to get significantly more complicated and considerably busier with multiple factions potentially converging, there was no harm in reducing exposure.","He followed the path of seeking out Collapsed Civilizations while simultaneously removing his primary assets from vulnerable positions.","And so the glorious scene of a man carrying an utterly massive structure on his back could be observed by nobody...as he moved through territories so vast and empty that witnesses simply didn’t exist.","Those who did exist were unfathomably dangerous!"]},{"number":4441,"title":"Chapter 4441: Chapter 4440: Infinite Hunger! V","paragraphs":["As he moved, he contemplated the Collapsed Civilization he would be seeking through Goliath’s, he found his thoughts returning to THE Dead Order .","A portion of his existence could now communicate directly with her through Sigrid in that unique space where she was systematically siphoning Civilizational Authority.","She had mentioned being occupied with other matters on the other side of The Veil.","When one truly considered it strategically... would the other side, The Lands of The Dead, not be the location containing the largest number of Collapsed Civilizations?","Every being that ever perished across eons of existence... they reside there. Every Civilization that ever collapsed... remnants would naturally gravitate toward death’s domain.","Was this one of THE Dead Order’s primary objectives? To systematically unify all Collapsed Civilizations under her Order? To build army of remnants for her eventual confrontation?","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as he processed these implications, and he continued delving even deeper into the Wandering Territories with purposeful strides.","As he was doing so...","HUUUM !","His entire body began shining with resplendent blue-gold brilliance as powerful resonance cascaded through his existence!","Prompts materialized soon after.","|Majesty has been sensed and is now descending.|","|Your Mana was directly and indirectly responsible for the emergence of a Derivative Civilization of Existence in the hands of The Great Usurper. The influence of your Mana stretches far back through your extensive history with this entity.|","|Your Mana flows with interminable and heavy influence on a Civilization based upon THE Primordial Civilization of Existence itself.|","|Consequence: you will continue receiving substantial harvests for its emergence and continuing advancement. As The Great Usurper’s Derivative Way expands, your proportional benefit increases accordingly. His Idle expansion across vast territories feeds into your Civilization through established connection.|","|The significance here shouldn’t be understated. Your Mana has become foundational element in another being’s Primordial-level Civilization. This creates permanent symbiotic relationship. You’re essentially getting compound interest on someone else’s expansion- not a bad investment, all things considered.|","...!","Noah felt the prompts blooming alongside sensation of utter glory as waves of Civilizational Authority crashed into his existence, flowing steadily into his Foundation Palisades with a force that made his entire being tremble with satisfaction.","He smiled as he felt the glorious walls of his Civilization continue advancing rapidly, each increment bringing him closer to thresholds that would unlock even greater capabilities.","His mind buzzed with anticipation as it looked forward to the moment these walls advanced sufficiently for him to escape the bounds of a Nascent Civilization.","For him to emerge as something truly capable of standing against the established Primordial Civilizations!","For now, he would continue taking his Civilization deeper into the Wandering Territories.","And inside The Infiniverse itself, he was about to initiate the emergence of the glorious Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger- one million beings born daily with baseline power of 1 Quintillion each, all wielding Civilizational Authority as birthright.","The future was being forged with every step he took.","The Atlas continued bearing his burden through territories unknown.","And existence itself trembled with anticipation of what was being built.","Inside The Infiniverse, within the vast expanse of the Early Veiled Shore, Noah materialized upon the golden sands with a presence that immediately drew attention from all those already assembled.","He sensed many of his people waiting on those radiant golden sands...familiar presences mixed with new arrivals.","Among those gathered were the beings he had always had here...Sigrid, Henry, Adelaide, Barbatos, Malphas, The Queen of Matter, Emperor Penguin, and numerous others.","Their presences radiated with recently elevated power, each bearing the Mark of the Minor Mana and Hunger Palisades that continued elevating their baseline capabilities.","In addition to these familiar figures, the members of the Isolated Civilization of Mana had also arrived.","Kael and the Seed Members of that ancient framework were already present, having begun constructing a grand structure designed to hold and organize Mana Glyphs and Mana Arcana Glyphs.","Riya could also be seen actively and busily talking to everyone present...her natural charisma and commanding presence drawing attention wherever she moved.","When Noah appeared on the golden sands, her eyes lit up.","She naturally floated toward him with grace.","\"Ancestor, your other Civilization is genuinely brilliant. Although I would absolutely love to have your own personal introduction to your family members here.\"","Her eyes gleamed.","\"It seems there exists an established hierarchy among your people, and I really need to establish myself near the top of it...\"","Her figure radiated with cultivated beauty. Arcs of blue-gold authority swirled around her form like loyal attendants, each current responding to her slightest gesture with immediate obedience.","With her striking features, sharp tongue, and that dangerous smile of schemes within schemes, she looked absolutely appetizing !","Noah patted her head with affection and gentle correction.","\"Patience. The hierarchy will sort itself naturally. Focus on what’s about to occur.\"","At this time, Khor arrived beside him with silent footsteps that belied her considerable power.","She observed Riya calmly.","\"You brought the annoyingly talkative one here as well? I had hoped for some measure of peace during this significant moment.\"","At such words, Riya’s eyes flashed with blue fire as her response emerged with honey-sweet venom.","\"Oh? Is this the supposedly old and wise woman I’ve just learned is The First Hunger speaking? Ancient, certainly, that much is obvious. But I don’t really see much evidence of the wise part in what I’ve seen so far...\"","BOOM !","Khor turned around with eyes blazing crimson as she smiled.","\"Supposed Prodigy of Mana, have you actually observed the other women here the Outsider spends meaningful time with? Their chests alone are larger than half of your entire figure. Perhaps you should focus on developing substance rather than running that mouth incessantly.\"","...!","Riya laughed with a sound mixing genuine amusement and dangerous promise as she replied with unshaken confidence.","\"Old Hunger, I won’t be changing a single thing about myself. I am an aesthetic choice for those with refined taste. The Ancestor clearly appreciates all varieties...\"","...!","The two of them seemed ready to continue their verbal sparring indefinitely.","But Noah shook his head with a gesture mixing amusement and exasperation.","\"Come on now, enough of that. We have genuinely important work to accomplish. Let’s get started.\"","...!"]},{"number":4442,"title":"Chapter 4442: Chapter 4441: Infinite Hunger!VI","paragraphs":["With such words of finality, Khor harrumphed and turned around.","She looked out at the distant golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore that stretched like vast continent toward horizons that seemed to extend infinitely.","Noah knelt down with deliberate motion and placed his palm flat against the golden sands.","His voice emerged with the weight of authority being invoked.","\"Forge the Resplendent Sanctuaries of Inevitabilities.\"","HUUM !","The vast golden sands surrounding them trembled with immediate response to his command.","From both Noah and Khor simultaneously, waves of obsidian-blue authority erupted outward like endless seas being released from containment.","The authority painted the golden sands with new colors, transforming their fundamental nature through the concentrated application of Civilizational power.","A moment later, the area of the Early Veiled Shore directly before them began altering and changing with breathtaking velocity.","Obsidian crystalline formations erupted from beneath the sands, the entire region transforming into solidified obsidian-blue crystals that stretched vast and wide.","A massive continent formed and continued stretching outward with seemingly infinite expansion, the crystalline surface eventually forging above the Early Sacred Waters themselves!","Prompts bloomed within Noah’s consciousness.","|The Resplendent Sanctuaries are manifesting according to architectural specifications. The Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger will commence forging from concentrated Civilizational Authority- the synthesized essence of Mana and Hunger operating in symbiotic harmony.|","|These entities require extraordinarily dense concentration of authority alongside substantial quantity. Most Civilizations would expend considerable resources producing even modest numbers within reasonable timeframes. Your possession of Infinite Primus Mana renders such constraints irrelevant.|","|Initial production parameters: 41,666 Inevitabilities per hour, yielding 1 Million Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger within 24 hours. Each unit will possess minimum baseline of 1 Quintillion Complexity and Purity with innate capability to wield Civilizational Authority.|","...!","Noah smiled at these prompts as he rose to observe the glorious construction unfolding before him.","He witnessed the endless expanse of obsidian-blue crystals spreading toward distant horizons, their surfaces catching ambient light and refracting it into countless prismatic displays.","From the smooth crystalline ground, massively tall towers began rising with architectural elegance, each one perfectly positioned.","Between these towers, potent singularities began manifesting...spherical concentrations of creative potential shining obsidian-blue with distinct hint of gold at their very centers.","Exactly 41,666 of these massive singularities began blooming across the Sanctuaries of Inevitabilities simultaneously, each one representing birth-chamber for a new member of his Civilization.","But as this magnificent construction progressed...","Noah’s body pulsed unexpectedly as brilliant golden light and brilliant green-gold light flashed i ndependently within his existence.","Two of his Principles were activating simultaneously without his direct command.","Prompts bloomed with analytical clarity!","| The Principle of the Cheating Architect and the Principle of Perpetual Harvest have independently committed 80% of their current Primus Mana Glyphs toward achieving temporal compression of population expansion.|","|Their objective: proliferating multiple days worth of Primus Inevitability production within compressed timeframe. Both Principles are demonstrating considerable initiative regarding this emergence.|","BOOM !","Above Noah, an eruption of glorious Glyphs manifested visibly...hundreds of concentrated authority-constructs orbiting around him like celestial bodies acknowledging their sun.","He looked upward with shining eyes to observe the immense light of his Singularity Principles bathing everything before him in concentrated radiance.","The Glyphs descended upon the Sanctuary with purposeful direction, each one finding optimal position to maximize their collective effect.","In the next moment, additional prompts materialized with gravitas befitting their content!","| Effort has been collected systematically from across existence over recent hours. The effort invested in the emergence of your Primordial Civilizations. The effort contributing to another Primordial Civilization’s advancement through Eckert’s progression. The accumulated effort of The First Farmer’s collapsed existence.|","|Additionally: the effort of adversarial forces plotting against you in The Lands of The Dead, The Lands of The Living, and THE Loom itself. Perpetual Harvest has proven remarkably indiscriminate in its collection methodology.|","|All this Quintessential Harvest is being applied to this moment. The irony of enemies’ efforts fueling your advancement should not be lost on you.|","Around Noah, an even grander sea of green-gold brilliance erupted with overwhelming intensity.","The light washed over the obsidian-blue crystalline surface of the Sanctuaries like tide of pure potential, transforming everything it touched.","His eyes became covered by the brilliant hues of green and blue merging together, and reflected in his vision, he witnessed something that transcended his initial expectations.","No longer did he see mere thousands of singularities representing emergence of 41,666 Inevitabilities.","Instead, he saw a few hundreds of thousand of these glorious singularities beginning to bloom every passing second...the crystalline Sanctuary rapidly filling with birth-chambers that multiplied exponentially.","Prompts emerged with utter glory!","|Production parameters have been modified. Due to combined contributions from the Cheating Architect and Perpetual Harvest, the generation of Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger has been multiplied by factor of 10.|","|Correspondingly, the baseline power of these First Generation Primus Inevitabilities has increased by identical factor. Each unit will now possess 10 Quintillion Complexity and Purity rather than standard 1 Quintillion.|","|Revised production target: 10 Million within 24 hours. Your Principles appear committed to making this emergence noteworthy.|","BOOM !","Oh!","Oh!!!","Noah felt eruption of such terrifying brilliance cascading through his existence as the numbers recalculated themselves.","Ten million Inevitabilities to be produced within the next twenty-four hours, each one possessing ten times the originally planned power.","Oh !","This was Perpetual Harvest expressing its true nature.","Right. Perpetual Harvest.","The thing The First Farmer had wanted most desperately...the Principle he had conspired and plotted to reclaim despite knowing it would betray someone who had helped him.","The thing that even THE Creature had held and shaken his head with regret that it didn’t bloom properly.","THE Creature himself had acknowledged it was a truly terrifying tool for the forging of Civilizations...something that could transform effort into exponential growth regardless of source or intention.","It seemed to truly be expressing itself fully at this moment as-","BOOM!","Even before Noah’s thoughts could complete their trajectory, another explosion of authority erupted within him.","Around him and covering the obsidian-blue crystalline Sanctuary, a potent and extremely concentrated sea of harvest bloomed to fruition and covered absolutely everything with green-gold radiance.","Prompts manifested with weight that demanded attention.","|Perpetual Harvest has identified additional harvest source of considerable magnitude. It is currently collecting the effort represented by the Pain and endless turmoil of all Inevitabilities in Existence whose Hunger has been mutated and defiled.|","|These beings exist in constant state of agonized appetite across the Walls of THE Loom. Their suffering, the excruciating sensation of hunger that can never be satisfied- is being converted into harvest for this emergence.|","|The suffering of the corrupted becomes foundation for the uncorrupted. One might call it poetic justice, though that seems insufficient descriptor.|","...!","Noah observed these prompts with genuine astonishment, and beside him, Khor seemed capable of witnessing identical information through their shared connection to Hunger’s Civilization.","Her figure trembled violently while tears began forming on the rims of her crimson eyes.","All the pain and endless turmoil that countless Inevitabilities felt at this very moment...beings who had their fundamental nature corrupted and twisted by THE Living Paradox’s machinations.","Due to Noah’s intricate connection with The First Hunger and how she remained connected to all these suffering Inevitabilities...","Perpetual Harvest actually harvested the effort of their excruciating sensation.","The agony of never being able to satisfy their hunger as they devoured and devoured endlessly, only to give everything they obtained to THE Loom without respite.","It took all of this accumulated effort as the result manifested before them...","Additional prompts emerged with implications that resonated deeply!","|Perpetual Harvest has extended its collection parameters. It is now Recursively harvesting all pain accumulated across countless eons by all distorted Mutated Inevitabilities. Not merely current suffering, but historical torment aggregated across incomprehensible duration.|","|The effort of all their pain and hunger is being harvested and directed toward this emergence. Consequently, all production parameters have been amplified by factor of 10 once more.|","|Your Principle demonstrates rather impressive commitment to maximizing this particular moment.|","...!","\"Oh, fuck...\"","Noah couldn’t help but curse with utter astonishment.","Khor’s legs gave out completely as she collapsed to the crystalline ground.","Tears fell freely from her crimson eyes as she felt all the accumulated pain and hunger of her tormented people being transformed into harvest!","All their efforts...their suffering, their agony, their endless hunger that could never be satisfied, all of it was being turned into foundation that infused itself to form more of her Civilization!","The prompt that manifested next carried weight of finality.","|Due to accumulated harvest of unprecedented magnitude, revised parameters are as follows: 100 Million Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger will be produced within 24 hours, just for these next 24 hours. Each First Generation Primus Inevitability will possess 100 Quintillion Complexity and Purity at baseline.|","|One hundred million beings. Each formidable threat. Born within this single day. Wielding Civilizational Authority as birthright.|","|The existential implications are considerable.|","...!","Noah had no words adequate to express what he felt.","His Mana buzzed with intensity that made his entire existence tremble.","His framework felt like it was being squeezed...as if Infinite Primus Mana was genuinely being put to the test and asked the fundamental question: Can you really provide the Mana for all this? Can you sustain production on this scale?","And his Existence cried out in response and began to give.","And it gave without hesitation.","And it gave without reservation.","And in front of him, millions of massive obsidian-blue-and-gold singularities bloomed with breathtaking velocity as something utterly terrifying erupted under the brilliance of concentrated harvest.","In this glorious silence of utter shock and stupefaction, where even Riya stood with mouth slightly open and eyes wide, pivotal prompts flashed before everyone present in the Early Veiled Shore.","| The Primordial Civilization of Hunger was a Civilization defined with clarity exceeding even THE Primordial Civilization of Existence itself. Mana existed alongside it from the earliest moments. Hunger was present even before THE Living Existences came together with THE Creature.|","|Hunger has been present.|","| Hunger has been present.|","|Mana has been present.|","| Mana has been present.|","|Hunger and Mana existed in glorious expression, fundamental principles driving all advancement and enabling all growth. Let true Hunger bloom once more without corruption. Let Mana feed it into fruition without limitation.|","| What was collapsed will rise. What was defiled will be purified. What was stolen will be reclaimed.|","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4443,"title":"Chapter 4443: Chapter 4442: Infinite Hunger! VII","paragraphs":["The endless skies of the Early Veiled Shore were painted with auroras of green, gold, and blue stretching infinitely.","They were celestial lights dancing in patterns that suggested existence itself was celebrating what was about to unfold!","Noah and Khor stood at the junction between golden sands and the obsidian-blue crystalline continent that now bore millions of singularities blooming with concentrated potential.","Each singularity pulsed with rhythmic intensity, preparing to birth entities that could potentially be the first of the many signs of a Civilization that would reshape the balance of power across Observable Existence!","In the distant skies above, Ozymandias could be seen floating grandly...his massive humanoid form shining with countless blue-gold Primus Mana Glyphs that orbited him like loyal subjects attending their sovereign.","He looked utterly dominating, an avatar of accumulated Hunger refined through systematic cultivation.","At such a time.","At such a pivotal moment when it was decreed that 100 Million Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger would be formed, each one possessing 100 Quintillion Complexity and Purity at baseline, Noah’s figure rose upward and began floating as he looked at the vast expanse before him with calculating eyes.","His Principles had gone all out. Perpetual Harvest had exceeded every expectation and accomplished feats that transcended what one could even fathom.","The Cheating Architect had contributed substantially.","Other components of him had done much to ensure this emergence’s success.","What about himself? What would he contribute to this moment?","At this juncture, his figure shone with interminable glory as he proceeded to raise his hand slowly.","He allowed it to fall with deliberate motion while echoing out gloriously, his eyes releasing beams of blue gold Primus Mana that covered the areas he gazed at!","\"Mana is the immensity of existence itself. All Matter, Antimatter, Dark Matter... life and energy simply originate from Mana at their most fundamental level. I hold an infinite amount of Primus Mana within my existence...a truth that defines my very existence!\"","HUUM !","His voice remained calm and unshakably composed, heavy with authority.","\"For the emergence of the Blades and Shields of My Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger... I shall impose upon this birth the Infinite Quality of my existence. The Infinite Quality of my Mana shall be woven into their fundamental architecture!\"","BOOM !","His eyes blazed with conviction!","\"If possible, from this emerging Hunger, let there be... Infinite Hunger.\"","...!","His words were terrifyingly heavy. Far too heavy!","They carried weight that made surrounding existence tremble in recognition of what was being attempted!","In the next moment, Noah’s entire existence and the distant Ozymandias above unleashed endless waves of blue-gold Primus Mana onto the lands below.","From both of them simultaneously, Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger descended like judgment being rendered!","Civilizational Authority.","This type of authority was unfathomably grand...representing the concentrated essence of what a Civilization truly stood for at its core.","At this moment, very few within Noah’s own framework actually held such authority.","To truly and fully embody and express it without feeling immense weight crushing one’s existence, it seemed like a minimum requirement was 100 Quintillion Complexity and Purity.","It was a heavy authority that genuinely represented what the Civilization stood for...its principles, its aspirations, its fundamental nature given tangible form.","And at this moment, Noah allowed his existence to actively impose his Civilizational Authority onto the emergence before him with focused intent.","Prompts bloomed with weight!","|A glimpse of the Infinite quality of your Mana has been successfully applied to Hunger. This represents unprecedented fusion of conceptual frameworks.|","|Waves of Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger are being utilized as catalytic agent. A portion of the incoming harvest from Existential Communication and Permeation has been diverted from your Foundation Palisades and redirected into this emergence.|","|Your Mana and your Hunger are inexplicably and irreversibly linked across all of existence from this moment forward. The quality of infinity inherent to your Mana is being shared, even if by fraction, with your Hunger.|","| Infinite Hunger rises.|","|A glorious Hunger that carries a distinct shred of the quality of infinity within its fundamental architecture. All Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger shall carry this Infinite Hunger as birthright, they can hunger and hunger endlessly, devour and devour endlessly on Everything for growth.|","| Everything becomes sustenance. Everything becomes fuel for advancement. There exists no satiation point, no moment of satisfaction that halts progression. Only eternal appetite driving eternal growth.|","BOOM !","After such prompts settled into reality, the few million singularities on the ground below pulsed and began rotating with accelerating velocity.","An emergence commenced with force that made the crystalline continent tremble.","The auras of utterly terrifying entities began rising from the singularities like souls ascending from primordial depths.","Tentacles bloomed first...countless appendages of concentrated Mana and Hunger that writhed and coiled as they formed humanoid entities.","These beings seemed to be constructed from countless and infinite tentacles of intertwined authority, each tendril carrying both principles in perfect synthesis.","Prompts manifested once more!","|The Blades and Shields of The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger are rising. Designation confirmed: protectors and weapons simultaneously, defensive and offensive capabilities unified in singular form.|","|Comprehensive specifications of Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger:|","|Baseline Power: 100 Quintillion Complexity and Purity minimum.|","|Inherent Capability: Born with Infinite Hunger as fundamental characteristic. No satiation threshold exists. All matter, energy, authority, and concepts can be devoured for growth without limitation.|","|Unique Function - Hunger and Mana Symbiosis : These entities carry capability to fuse with other Members of your Civilization, becoming Hunger-Born Inevitability Civilizational Armor. This fusion combines the power of both participants, creating a synthesized combat form that exceeds simple addition of capabilities.|","|Core Abilities:|","|—Mana Consumption Acceleration: Can devour raw Mana from environment to rapidly regenerate and amplify their own power. Recovery time becomes functionally instantaneous when sufficient Mana is available.|","|—Hunger Propagation: Can temporarily impose their Infinite Hunger onto enemies, causing targeted beings to experience uncontrollable appetite that consumes their own power reserves from within.|","|—Civilizational Resonance: When multiple Primus Inevitabilities operate in proximity, their Civilizational Authority harmonizes and amplifies, creating zone of enhanced effectiveness that grows exponentially with numbers present.|","|—Void Appetite: Can consume abstract concepts including damage dealt to them, converting offensive actions into fuel for their growth. Attacks that don’t exceed their baseline power are simply devoured rather than causing harm.|","|—Infinite Recursion: Their Hunger operates on recursive loop, they hunger to grow stronger, and growing stronger increases their hunger, creating perpetual advancement cycle without ceiling.|","...!"]},{"number":4444,"title":"Chapter 4444: Chapter 4443: Infinite Hunger! VIII","paragraphs":["Floating far above, Noah observed such prompts as his eyes only shone brighter with satisfaction.","He watched the emergence of utter glory unfolding below with an expression of pride and anticipation.","The process that should have required full hour for all few million to complete their formation occurred instantly...the temporal compression from Perpetual Harvest and Cheating Architect ensuring no wasteful delays.","The humanoid forms of the Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger took shape with terrifying beauty.","They appeared as massive titanic humanoids with obsidian-blue tentacled skin, their entire bodies lined by ancient and glorious golden tentacle glyphs that pulsed with inner light.","Wings composed of golden tentacles fanned out behind them like banners of authority.","They looked like imposing figures made of roiling, sinewy blue-obsidian tendrils...possessing the overall humanoid shape, but distinctly monstrous and alien in execution.","Each face was humanoid yet predatory and animalistic, and their eyes shone with crimson intensity that spoke of Infinite Hunger burning within.","They appeared one by one, their emergence causing existence itself to tremble all around as each one radiated utterly terrifying and imposing air of concentrated power.","The crystalline ground cracked beneath their feet as reality strained to accommodate their presence.","The moment their bodies finished forming, they moved with synchronized precision, gloriously kneeling toward Noah, Ozymandias, and Khor with gestures of absolute submission and devotion.","Their booming words began ringing out with heavy voices that echoed across the Early Veiled Shore.","\" We are born of Infinite Mana and Infinite Hunger. We are the Blades forged in the crucible of your Civilization’s emergence! Our existence is dedicated to the protection and advancement of the Primordial framework that birthed us!\"","HUUM!","The first formed Primus Inevitability spoke these words, and others joined him as they repeated identical proclamation. Their voices merged into chorus of absolute loyalty!","\" We swear upon the Infinite quality of our Hunger that we shall devour all obstacles that stand before our Civilization! We shall consume every threat, every enemy, every impediment to your ascension! Our appetite knows no bounds, for we carry the gift of endless growth within our fundamental architecture!\"","More voices joined, creating thunderous declaration!","\"We are the shields that shall absorb all damage dealt to our Civilization! We are the armor that shall protect our sovereign’s existence! We are the weapons that shall carve pathways through hostile territories! Our loyalty is absolute! Our hunger is infinite! Our purpose is singular- the triumph of Mana and Hunger across all of existence!\"","The vows continued!","\" We pledge our existence to the Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger. We pledge our Infinite Hunger to fuel its advancement. We pledge our capabilities to serve as instruments of your will! Command us, and we shall obey without hesitation! Direct us, and we shall execute without failure! We are your extension, your manifestation, your army born of Civilizational Authority!\"","The final declaration rang out with weight that made even the distant auroras pulse in response.","\" For the Infinite Light of Mana! For the Endless Hunger that drives all growth! We stand ready to serve!\"","...!","The scene was utterly magnificent...millions of titanic beings kneeling in perfect synchronization, their crimson eyes fixed upon Noah, Ozymandias, and Khor with devotion.","Noah descended slowly toward the first one to emerge...the entity whose voice had initiated the chorus of vows.","He landed before this being with expression mixing curiosity and glory.","\"What is your name?\" Noah asked.","All the chants and vows ceased immediately the moment Noah spoke, as if his words carried priority that overrode all other considerations.","The first Primus Inevitability responded with a voice carrying absolute certainty!","\"I am merely your loyal blade. Your extension. Your instrument of Infinite Hunger. I am Protos , the First of this generation, born to serve the Primordial Civilization that granted me existence.\"","HUUM !","Noah nodded at such designation as his words emerged with weight of honor being bestowed:","\"Then Protos , you shall have the honor to become my shield, my armor, my blade. You shall be the first to demonstrate the Hunger and Mana Symbiosis that defines your generation.\"","...!","Protos knelt even lower with a gesture mixing profound gratitude and solemn acceptance!","His voice emerged with a formal precision that carried the weight of a sacred oath!","\"Master of Infinite Primus Mana and Hunger, I understand that I am unworthy of such distinction. Yet I shall do all within my capabilities to protect the infinite light of The Primordial Civilization! My hunger shall be your hunger. My strength shall be your shield. My existence shall be your armor. This, I swear upon the Infinite quality that burns within my fundamental architecture.\"","...!","At such words, Noah’s body flashed with brilliant light as his Mana-Born Existential Armor adorned him. The armor pulsed with recognition of what was about to occur.","His hand reached out toward Protos , and the Primus Inevitability also reached out with sense of fervor that transcended simple obedience!","Protos’s humanoid body began transforming...his form dissolving into countless tentacles that began fusing themselves into Noah’s existing armor.","The tentacles wove through the Mana-Born Existential Armor with precision of perfect compatibility. Obsidian-blue merged with existing golden-blue framework, creating synthesis that exceeded what either possessed individually.","As such glorious scene began unfolding before all observers, Noah turned to address his people watching in utter astonishment.","Riya’s eyes were wide with barely contained excitement. Kael and the Seed Members observed with analytical focus.","Henry, Adelaide, Barbatos, and others looked upon the scene with expressions mixing awe and anticipation.","Noah’s grand words rang out across the Early Veiled Shore.","\"The shields and blades of our Civilization have been formed. One hundred million Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger shall emerge within the next day...each one carrying Infinite Hunger as their birthright, each one capable of fusing with members of our Civilization to create weavings of unprecedented power.\"","His voice intensified.","\"Every single one of you can fuse with them and walk together on a path of Infinite Mana and Hunger. You shall wear them as your protection. You shall wield them as your weapons. You shall advance together as symbiotic pairs, your growth fueling theirs, their hunger amplifying yours.\"","His eyes blazed with tyrannical satisfaction.","\"This... is what it means to belong to a Primordial Civilization. To My Primordial Civilization! This is the advantage we shall wield against those who stand against us. Let them come with their accumulated power spanning eons. Let them come with their established frameworks and ancient authorities. We shall meet them with Infinite Hunger, with Infinite Mana, and we shall","devour their advantages until nothing remains but our triumph!\"","...!","BOOM!","The Early Veiled Shore trembled with the weight of declaration as around Noah, the fusion with Protos completed itself.","His armor now carried characteristics of both his original framework and the Primus Inevitability...tentacles woven throughout the structure, golden glyphs pulsing alongside obsidian-blue crystalline formations.","He could feel Protos’s consciousness flowing over his body like a shield!","And behind him, millions more Primus Inevitabilities continued kneeling, waiting for their own chance to serve their Civilization.","The shields had been forged.","The blades had been sharpened.","And existence itself trembled as on this day, something grand was completed!"]},{"number":4445,"title":"Chapter 4445: Chapter 4444: Civilization Expansion! I","paragraphs":["4,166,666 Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger.","This was the scene and the reality that many were looking at this very moment, and it felt absolutely surreal!","It was as if existence itself had decided to bend its rules specifically to accommodate what should have been impossible.","Because every single one of these entities held 100 Quintillion Complexity and Purity at their baseline.","Every single one of these entities flowed with Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger as birthright!","Noah’s figure stood at the forefront of this magnificent army, currently fused with Protos in a symbiotic state that transformed his appearance into something transcendent.","He looked like a titanic armored entity shining with gold-blue, obsidian, and crimson radiance that made surrounding existence acknowledge his presence.","The armor itself was a masterwork of Civilizational engineering...sleek yet impossibly durable, with angular plates that suggested both mobility and absolute protection.","The surface displayed intricate patterns where obsidian-blue tentacle-glyphs wove through golden framework, creating visual language that spoke of two Primordial Civilizations unified in singular purpose.","One hand gripped an exquisite crimson-blue blade that was deliberately hollow at its center, and within that hollow space, millions of spinning Primordial Fireballs rotated with controlled violence...each one capable of devastating territories if released.","The other hand bore an obsidian-gold shield whose surface was inscribed with countless Primus Mana Arcana Glyphs that pulsed with concentrated authority.","The blue-gold helmet covered his features completely while a spinning crystalline crimson crown floated above it...a symbol of his sovereignty over this emerging force.","His eyes were hidden behind a visor that pulsed with crimson light, giving him appearance of something beyond mortal or even Early Creature.. something that existed at intersection of multiple glorious principles.","In such grand armored state, he looked upon the Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger who gazed back at him with eyes that seemingly sought to be told what needed to be done.","Their posture suggested they would execute any command without hesitation, without question, with absolute dedication.","Noah had been planning to lay low temporarily as he accumulated his power...allowing the Foundation Palisades to grow while avoiding direct confrontation.","But when he looked at this terrifying portion of power that was about to bloom fully soon...when he truly grasped what the emergence of Infinite Hunger meant...","Oh!","It called for changes of plans regarding many things.","He had talked and talked and talked about how grand his Primordial Civilization was compared to those that had been actively enjoying boons for the past eons.","Now it was truly time for him to act and put this grand Civilization to practical use.","He turned to look at his people, all assembled on the junction between golden sands and crystalline continent, as his grand voice emerged with a magisterial commanding authority.","\"All of you. Step forward. As of today, there shall be none within the Early Veiled Shore that will exhibit less than 100 Quintillion Complexity and Purity. Fuse with a Primus Inevitability, let them be your blades and shields, and let us advance our Civilization together as unified force.\"","...!","The words reverberated outward like undeniable command that transcended simple authority, yet none here even required commanding!","In the next instant, figures began stepping forward with expressions mixing eagerness and solemn recognition of what they were about to undertake.","Riya moved with grace, her eyes gleaming with anticipation as she approached the kneeling ranks.","Henry stepped forward with shining eyes.","Barbatos floated forth with devilish smile. Sigrid surrounded by her aura of Order advanced with measured steps!","Moiraine, Titano, The Blue Slime, The Emperor Penguin, Kazuhiko, and even Little Bobby...all stepped forward to claim their Civilizational Armor.","The Primus Inevitabilities moved with sequential precision like armies trained across eons rather than beings born mere moments ago.","They knelt before all those approaching with gestures mixing respect and eager anticipation, each one waiting to be chosen, to fulfill their purpose!","Sigrid, surrounded by white Order that harmonized with the obsidian-blue of Hunger, appeared near Noah and Khor with deliberate motion.","Her hand reached out toward a Primus Inevitability who instantly arose from its kneeling position.","The entity’s voice emerged a declaration.","\"It shall be my honor to serve as your blade and shield, bearer of Order. My Infinite Hunger shall protect your light.\"","HUUM !","Its tentacles extended toward Sigrid’s body and began forming glorious armor that shone obsidian-blue-and-gold similar to Noah’s own...though slightly smaller in scale, maintaining her elegant figure while providing protection.","Arch Lich Ra’Zan and the Primordial Ape stepped forward simultaneously, their Legions also selecting Primus Inevitabilities with careful consideration.","As each inevitability was chosen, they all rose from kneeling positions and declared with unified voices!","\"It would be our honor to serve the Primordial Civilization!\"","...!","The symbiotic relationships formed rapidly...tentacles weaving through existing frameworks, creating armored states that pulsed with combined authority.","All those present gradually became adorned with Civilizational Armor that marked them as true members of Noah’s weavings!","Even Leonore Rureaux who had just joined through pledging fealty found herself approached by a Primus Inevitability who knelt before her with same respect shown to original members.","Her existence became adorned in this grand Civilizational Armor, the transformation marking her official integration into the Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger.","Khor looked at all of this unfolding with heavy emotions.","She floated alongside the few million Primus Inevitabilities who had not yet been chosen, and they all extended their hands, forming tentacles just to touch her outstretched hands.","Just to feel the touch of The First Hunger herself!","As she passed through their ranks with tears forming at corners of her crimson eyes, they began calling out with voices that resonated across the entire Early Veiled Shore.","\"O First Hunger! Hunger that drives all growth! We stand ready to serve! Our Infinite Hunger is your Infinite Hunger! Our existence is dedicated to the restoration of what was stolen from you!\"","WAA !","Their voices were resonant with devotion!","When she heard them, when she felt their hands reaching out to touch her existence with reverence, Khor was overwhelmed by emotion that she had suppressed for eons.","She laughed with tears flowing freely, the sound mixing joy and grief and vindication all together!","Her gaze momentarily turned to look at Noah’s grand armored figure, seeing his crimson visor-covered eyes gazing back at her with silent acknowledgment.","\"Thank you, Outsider,\" she said.","\"Thank you for giving my people a chance to exist without corruption. Thank you for giving them Infinite Hunger that does not pain or torment them.\"","...!"]},{"number":4446,"title":"Chapter 4446: Chapter 4445: Civilization Expansion! II","paragraphs":["Noah waved his hand with a gesture that said this was simply just the beginning...that gratitude was premature when so much more remained to be accomplished.","And it truly was only the beginning.","He looked around and observed how many within his Early Veiled Shore continued to come forward and choose Primus Inevitabilities to become their blades and shields.","Even his mother, Amelia Osmont, came forward and selected a Primus inevitability as her body became covered by this glorious and terrifying Civilizational Armor.","Noah continued gazing at this glorious process with analytical focus.","When one truly stopped to contemplate it, what exactly did this moment in time mean for him based on his pure power alone and his Civilization’s capabilities?","One might look at this astonishing phenomenon today and think: Oh , it’s simply another elevation or power up in his arsenal. Another impressive achievement to add to his growing list.","But at this point in time, it actually marked terrifying and significant change.","For the first time in quite some time, and for the first time in the history of his Civilization, he gained what seemed to be overwhelming power!","And it was overwhelming in a way that many would only later come to understand!","To truly understand this significance, take into account just if any force had one million entities each at 100 Quintillion across the Transcendent Folds.","It did not exist.","Such a force did exist inside of THE Loom, but that was that grand place filled with multiple Primordial Civilizations that had been accumulating power across eons.","Outside that secured domain, no comparable force existed anywhere in Observable Existence.","Even if he was wrong and the Wandering Territories that held Collapsed Civilizations possessed significant numbers... he highly doubted they even held a few hundred thousand or even a few thousands that were at 100 Quintillion or higher.","The possible path with Goliath had shown thst he would meet a few at dozens of Quintillion and other at a few hundred Quintillion when he did proceed to find the Collapsed Civilizations!","But that was it.","Maybe he was wrong. He hoped he was wrong, as he loved for there to be more power and complexity out there than he even fathomed.","But it was unlikely, as a good reference point was the Sanctuary of The First Farmer, that ancient being who had cultivated for eons and yet his most powerful subordinates barely exceeded a few Quintillion.","Now, he did not just have one million of such entities.","He had four million at this moment.","And as the hours continued to pass within a full day, he would have one hundred million of such entities!","It was significant enough of a number for him to do many things that could bolster and elevate his Civilization in ways that he could not accomplish before.","Like...","He thought back to the unfavorable phantom process that had occurred when he simulated raiding the Desiccated Sleeping Shore that held a Living Elemental body of Schrodinger!","The Illusory Reality Avatars from THE Loom had appeared and decimated his forces...beings with Sextillions of power that had overwhelmed his capabilities!","But that simulation had assumed his forces numbered in dozens, maybe hundreds.","Not millions.","He smiled lightly as he commanded RUIN/EDEN.","’Do a small phantom process for the choice of heading to the Dessicated Sleeping Shore right now with the current standing of my Civilization.’","...!","|Calculating probabilities...|","Barely enough remaining Primus Mana Glyphs of Cheating Architect were available, but for this single simulation, they were there!","|The simulation unfolds like this...|","RUIN/EDEN told him of how this possible path would unfold, and as she did...he couldn’t help but smile!","His conviction was further affirmed as he nodded after listening.","He turned to look at the expanse of Primus Inevitabilities before him and his people who stood wrapped in Civilizational Armor , all pulsing with Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger.","\"For those who wish to join the first excursion of our Primordial Civilization... it shall be an excursion to collapse a vessel of THE Living Paradox . We shall move against one of his bodies!\"","...!","He spoke such words grandly as at this moment, he held tremendous sense of confidence while knowing fully of the dangers that persisted.","The Avatars from THE Loom would appear once more. They would attempt to suppress his forces.","But this time, he would be more than ready.","Sigrid, Riya, and many others pulsed with readiness...their armored forms radiating anticipation of combat worthy of their newfound power.","Hyperion came of retirement, bringing with him glorious Enders to fuse with The Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger!","The wills of Old Man Eudemus, Commander Feng, Oppenheimer, and others felt like this was an opportune time to join in!","The Great Beyonder, The Great Mother, Romulus, Emelline...all those basking in the backdrop of greatness came out to join this momentous occasion.","Noah observed it all calmly.","He gazed at the throngs of more than 4 Million Primus Inevitabilities standing in perfect formation, and he looked upward toward his other form of Ozymandias that floated down grandly at this moment.","The massive humanoid beckoned to a Primus Inevitability below who shot up toward him with eager velocity.","The Primus Inevitability adorned Ozymandias in a Civilizational Armor of Mana and Hunger that made the already imposing figure even more terrifying.","Ozymandias spoke in a deep voice that carried weight of Infinite Hunger given vocal form!","\"Let us go and have a feast worthy of your hunger. Let us devour the vessels of those who corrupted our brethren.\"","...!","HUUM!","At such words, the Primus Inevitabilities all rose up with synchronized movement and smashed their armored fists against their chests.","BOOM !","The sound of millions of impacts created thunderous percussion that made existence itself tremble.","They bellowed out with voices that carried across dimensions!","\" For the Infinite Light of Mana! For the Endless Hunger that drives all growth! We stand ready to serve! Command us, and we shall execute without failure! Direct us, and we shall devour without hesitation!\"","...!","Noah looked at all of this calmly as his mind calculated many things.","Even if he mobilized just a million of these Primus Inevitabilities, he was confident in overwhelming any entities with a single Sextillion or even a few Sextillions in combined power.","The Civilizational Authority they wielded, combined with their Infinite Hunger and coordinated possibilities, would create force that exceeded simple numerical calculation.","And because of this confidence born from analysis rather than blind arrogance, he raised his armored hand.","Instantly, all voices ceased once more as every Primus Inevitability fixed their crimson eyes upon him with absolute attention.","He looked out at the army of more than four million and spoke.","\"A million of you shall spread across the Folds, the Collapsed Regions, and the Wandering Territories. Move in groups of at least a thousand to ensure an overwhelming force advantage.\"","\"Ensure that not even a single brethren of yours falls to enemy action. With Mana, you will not truly fall, your power will be sustained infinitely. With Hunger, you will continue to devour... your growth will never cease!\"","His voice intensified!","\"Spread out across the Folds. Across the Wandering Territories. Search for the Vessels of THE Living Paradox . Search for Collapsed Civilizations. Search for anything and everything that could aid our advancement.\"","His final declaration boomed out like a mandate!","\"At this moment in time, The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger shall start to spread its influence. Spread the Sparks of The Way of Mana across Existence. Spread the light of Infinite Hunger across all territories. Let all of Observable Existence know that a new Primordial Civilization has risen, and it hungers for everything !\"","...!","BOOM!","They orchestrated The Fallout? They forged THE Loom? He would show them how he would survive their machinations, and come out the other side...a force they utterly regretted allowing to rise!"]},{"number":4447,"title":"Chapter 4447: Chapter 4446: Civilization Expansion! III","paragraphs":["His voice echoed across the Early Veiled Shore with finality after he gave the order.","The Primus Inevitabilities replied with fervor that made the crystalline continent tremble.","A million of them rose up from their ranks, their armored forms pulsing with readiness as they declared with unified voices:","\" We shall execute your mandate with absolute dedication! The Folds shall know the touch of Infinite Hunger! The Collapsed Regions shall witness the light of Infinite Mana! The Wandering Territories shall tremble before our passage! We shall locate the vessels of the enemy and mark them for your judgment! We shall find the Collapsed Civilizations and bring them word of your emergence!\"","Their voices were deep, heavy, and buzzing in a glorious unison.","The final declaration rang out.","\" For the glory of the Primordial Civilization! For the restoration of what was stolen! For the emergence of Infinite Hunger! We move as one! We fight as one! We triumph as one! Command us, and it shall be done!\"","...!","After these grand declarations concluded, Noah raised his armored fist into the air.","He bellowed out coldly with voice that carried finality","\"Move out.\"","And...","BOOM!","The Blades of a Primordial Civilization moved out!","A million Primus Inevitabilities surged upward simultaneously, their armored forms creating wave of obsidian-blue-and-gold that seemed to paint the sky itself.","They organized into groups of thousands with precision.","They spread in all directions outsids The Infiniverse...some moving toward the Transcendent Folds, others diving toward Collapsed Regions, still more vectoring toward the vast Wandering Territories that stretched beyond catalogued space.","Each group moved with purpose, their Infinite Hunger driving them forward.","They were the first wave.","The vanguard of a Primordial Civilization that had just announced its presence to all of Observable Existence .","And behind them, more than 3 million additional Primus Inevitabilities remained...awaiting Noah’s next command, ready to support their brethren or anything he commanded.","Noah watched them go with satisfaction.","Let THE Living Paradox send his Avatars.","Let THE Dead Order mobilize her forces. Let THE Loom take notice of what blooms outside their secured boundaries.","We are ready.","And we are hungry.","Infinitely hungry.","And it was precisely because of this Hunger that he moved the way he did.","Hunger needed sustenance.","THE Loom ...was a fat fucking pig that he wanted to bleed for sustenance.","THE Living Paradox said he and all others outside THE Loom were nutrients? Fertilizers?","Okay!","Let him glimpse of the immensity outside it. Let THE Loom send forth its Avatars. Let them become his Fertilizer that he would shit out the next day!","HUUM!","The scene was an utterly breathtaking one as after 1 Million Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger were deployed across existence, Noah turned his armored gaze toward Ozymandias floating grandly above.","This part of him, this avatar of Infinite Hunger...had his tentacled chest crack and begin to open in the next moment, revealing a crimson-obsidian space underneath that seemed to contain infinite depth.","Ozymandias then pointed downward commandingly, his authority flashing over 2 Million Primus Inevitabilities exactly as they heeded the order and rose up.","They flowed toward his chest like river of obsidian-blue-and-gold, shockingly miniaturizing as they approached and fitting into Ozymandias’ existence like nothing...as if the space within him was far vaster than his external form suggested.","He didn’t need to show completely that he had Millions. He could start slow and unleash more as the needs arose!","This glorious scene of 2 million Primus Inevitabilities contained within Ozymandias’ framework was staggering to witness.","In the skies above, those who also wanted to be included in the first excursion floated ready....armored figures pulsing with anticipation.","At such momentous occasion...","HUUM!","Existence itself began to tremble as if acknowledging the significance of what was occurring.","A symphony began to play...not from any visible source but from reality itself resonating with actions being taken!","The melody carried tension, valor, and immensity woven together into something magisterial.","Noah looked around with recognition as he remembered the words of THE Dead Order ...that when one’s power or actions were profound enough, they could induce resonance in existence itself.","Trembling. Symphonies.","Even the THE Living Paradox merely appearing had caused him and all those nearby to hear... \"KNEEL! REVERE!\" again and again.","But at this moment...","Accompanying the buzzing existence and symphony, something unprecedented occurred.","The instrumental melody transformed into something more complex as a crystalline feminine voice began to echo out... words.","Existence itself composing lyrics to accompany the glorious significance of this deployment.","The voice sang with melancholic beauty.","\" These are the weapons existence created,","Born from pressure that could not be contained,","Tyranny and chains, what did you expect?","What grows beneath oppression cannot be restrained...\"","The melody continued with haunting resonance.","\" Why couldn’t things be left alone?","Why couldn’t existence remain free?","Why did there have to be plots and schemes,","Collapsing what we could have been?\"","The chorus swelled with tragic grandeur!","\" Now blades are echoing across the void,","Now vast swathes will bleed with mana and hunger,","You asked for weapons, you forged them in pain,","Did you think the harvest wouldn’t come again?","Did you think the harvest wouldn’t come again?\"","Noah looked at the surrounding existence as he felt this melodious chorus continue, and he alongside all others around him observed in astonishment.","The monkey-like form of the Bard of Quintessence, already contained within Civilizational Armor of Mana and Hunger ...felt like he was hearing something out of his wildest dreams.","His existence trembled with creative euphoria as existence itself composed what he had always aspired to create.","Noah closed his eyes to listen to the chorus that existence seemed to be composing in response to his actions... as if reality acknowledged that what had been done to Hunger, to the Inevitabilities, to countless beings across eons. .. had consequences that were now manifesting.","He smiled with satisfaction before opening his eyes once more, looking toward Leonore Rureaux with commanding focus.","\"Lead us to the Desiccated Sleeping Shore.\"","...!","With such words, the armored Leonore nodded with expression mixing determination and nervous anticipation.","Her right hand, gripping the hollow blade similar to Noah’s, cut across space vertically with precise motion.","A massive tear formed in reality itself, edges crackling with spatial authority as the pathway to their destination manifested.","Ozymandias, whose body contained 2 Million Inevitabilities, floated toward the portal with gravitas that made surrounding existence acknowledge his passage.","Dozens of others followed- Riya with her characteristic dangerous smile visible even through armored visor, Arch Lich Ra’Zan with his Legions, Barbatos with devilish anticipation, Dr. Hall with analytical focus...","Many of those closest to Noah moved toward the portal as the symphony continued playing around them.","\" What could have been, what should have been,","If you had only let the hunger rest,","But you defiled and you corrupted,","Now face the jaws you’ve created...\"","Noah looked toward the visage of the emotional Khor as he extended his armored hand toward her with a gesture of invitation.","\"Let us go.\""]},{"number":4448,"title":"Chapter 4448: Chapter 4447: Civilization Expansion! IV","paragraphs":["The chorus and melody continued repeating in the surroundings as these events unfolded with existential significance.","Khor took his hand, her diminutive figure smiling with mixture of gratitude and fierce anticipation.","She actually floated upward and climbed to sit down on Noah’s right armored shoulder, her presence there feeling natural despite the absurdity of The First Hunger riding upon an Early Creature’s shoulder.","The two of them also moved toward the portal with synchronized purpose.","\" Did you think the harvest wouldn’t come again?","Did you think the harvest wouldn’t come again?\"","It was glorious moment.","It was terrifying occasion.","And at this moment, across existence... many things were changing.","---","In the Transcendent Origin Folds.","Above where Aeternitas Concordia used to be.","The scene that unfolded would have been incomprehensible mere days ago.","Above the white gold space...","A few thousand massive Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger materialized with synchronized precision...their obsidian-blue-and-gold armored forms descending from dimensional tears that crackled with spatial authority.","The Living Origins in the surroundings, who had been rebuilding Concordia while systematically erasing any Dead Existences that attempted revival, looked up with shock.","And they began to hear it.","A harmony. A chorus singing with the descent of these unknown entities!","\" These are the weapons existence created,","Born from pressure that could not be contained...\"","The melody accompanied their arrival like a soundtrack to an existential event, and the Primus Inevitabilities waved their hands with synchronized motion to allow hundreds of thousands of Sparks of The Way of Mana to flow outward.","The Sparks surrounded Living Origins like twinkling stars...each one carrying invitation to join the Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger.","With the terrifying level of power and aura these entities portrayed, each one radiating 100 Quintillion Complexity and Purity, and how they silently looked upon the Living Origins with crimson eyes...","Regardless if they were Dukes, Honored Living Origins, Royal Living Origins, or mere Fold Dwellers, all of them felt tremor in their existence.","Fear. Recognition.","They reached out to grab these Sparks.","What choice did they have? When beings of such overwhelming power offered opportunity rather than destruction?","The Primus Inevitabilities were that terrifying . That compelling.","\" Why couldn’t things be left alone?","Why couldn’t existence remain free?\"","---","In the Transcendent Law Folds.","The Heart of Law.","An expanse of silver-white citadel stretched out many Gigaparsecs in size.","They wwre architectural marvels that defied understanding.","Billions of Living Laws dwelled within its structured boundaries, countless Transcendent Wheels of Existence orbited in perfect formation, and just an overabundance of ordered life proliferated throughout.","At this moment, Malphas in his devilish butler form walked alongside Alexander Asmodeus and Seraphina Valorheart.","They had just arrived before a procession of multiple Dukes of Living Law who were looking at Seraphina with excitement.","They could sense an extremely pure aura of Law around her!","She had already sent word back that she and Alexander had actually met with a Remnant Will of THE Living Law themselves!","How grand were the Living Laws about to become from here on out? How great would their progress be into the secrets of THE Loom ?","As they were contemplating these possibilities with eager anticipation...","\" Now blades are echoing across the void...\"","In such grand place filled with structured magnificence, thousands of the Primus Inevitabilities manifested grandly above the Heart of Law itself.","Each one burned with terrifying presence of 100 Quintillion Complexity and Purity...power that exceeded anything the Living Laws had witnessed in their carefully ordered existence.","Their appearance was followed by the melody and chorus echoing out all around this place too.","\" Now vast swathes will bleed with mana and hunger,","You asked for weapons, you forged them in pain...\"","The titanic Primus Inevitabilities descended with synchronized precision, their obsidian-blue-and-gold forms casting shadows across the silver-white citadel that seemed to stain its perfect order.","Seraphina Valorheart’s expression changed as she looked upward...her face turning ashen.","These entities possessed power that made her recent inheritance from THE Living Law seem modest by comparison.","Alexander Asmodeus maintained stern expression as he and the Living Laws before him felt the overbearing sense of power that seemed capable of eclipsing everything they had built.","His Scales of Law pulsed with readings that made no logical sense...beings that powerful shouldn’t exist outside THE Loom, especially in auch large numbers as...there seemed to be thousands of such beings here?","Where could a terrifying force of thousands of such powerful beings stem from?!","There was no answer.","But...","All Primus Inevitabilities possessed the capability of Civilizational Resonance.","The grandness of this ability manifested gloriously as while the Primus Inevitabilities floated above the Heart of Law, the authority of their Primordial Civilization began painting over the established authority of Law itself.","Blue-gold light washed across silver-white structures.","Obsidian tendrils of influence wove through ordered formations.","It was as if a new existential order was being instituted...one that could subsume or overwhelm the existing framework through sheer weight of accumulated power.","Faced with such shocking phenomenon, thousands of powerful and unknown beings when even one could crush them all...Alexander Asmodeus was calculating how to navigate this impossibility when he observed Malphas beside him beginning to rise.","The devilish butler spoke with characteristic calm.","\"These... are simply the Blades and Shields of The Master. They come bearing gifts rather than threats, though I understand the confusion.\"","...!","With such words, Malphas reached out toward one of the descending Primus Inevitabilities.","The entity instantly floated down and transformed itself into suit of armor around Malphas, tentacles weaving through his existing form to create Civilizational Armor.","...!","\" Did you think the harvest wouldn’t come again?\"","The other Primus Inevitabilities waved their hands to unleash millions of Sparks that started spreading out across the Heart of Law itself.","The Sparks drifted through ordered streets, circled around structured buildings, and surrounded Living Laws who looked up with expressions mixing fear and shock.","The chorus and symphony continued as all those below remained shocked.","Alexander stood with increasingly ashen face as he wondered with genuine bewilderment.","Just what had Osmont done ? How had he accumulated such power in such short timeframe?","What...had Osmont done?!","The Sparks continued spreading while the melody played on!","\"What could have been, what should have been,","If you had only let the hunger rest...\"","Across existence.","On this day.","Many, many things would begin to change.","The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger had announced its presence through an overwhelming force that demanded acknowledgment.","One million Primus Inevitabilities spreading across all territories.","Sparks of The Way of Mana being distributed to countless beings regardless of their original affiliations.","Civilizational Authority painting over established frameworks with weight of utter majesty.","And accompanying all of this...the symphony that existence itself was forced to echo out in response to what was occurring.","\" These are the weapons existence created,","Born from pressure that could not be contained,","Tyranny and chains, what did you expect?","Did you think the harvest wouldn’t come again?\"","The chorus repeated with haunting finality as Noah and his forces moved through the portal toward the Desiccated Sleeping Shore...toward direct confrontation with a vessel of THE Living Paradox himself!"]},{"number":4449,"title":"Chapter 4449: Chapter 4448: Duty I","paragraphs":["Officium.","Duty.","A word that carried different weight depending upon who spoke it, who heard it, who lived beneath its shadow.","For some, duty was nothing more than chains disguised as purpose...obligations imposed by others who claimed authority over your existence.","These beings viewed duty as surrender, as relinquishing the freedom to determine one’s own path in exchange for the comfort of being told what to do.","For others, duty was sacred covenant- a binding agreement between self and something greater that transformed mere existence into meaningful purpose.","These beings viewed duty as elevation, as recognition that individual desires paled before collective necessity.","And for a select few across existence’s infinite expanse, duty was neither chain nor covenant but choice ...deliberate decision to serve something beyond self because that service aligned with personal values rather than external compulsion.","The question that plagued peasants, warriors, and kings alike was simple: What constituted true duty, and who possessed authority to define it?","---","In the Earliest Folds, in times beyond current reckoning.","There was a moment when The First Leader, Gilgamesh, fought against a Disciple of THE Creature himself.","Just having a more concentrated Everything of THE Creature did not mean one could become a Disciple!","Nobody knew the complete results of that battle as it occurred in domain others could not perceive, hidden from ordinary observation.","But at its conclusion, Gilgamesh lay on shattered folding of existence itself...reality cracked beneath him like broken mirror.","His chest was rent open with wounds that leaked essence rather than blood, his breathing labored with pain.","Yet his expression remained stern. Unyielding. Unbowed despite catastrophic defeat.","He stared out into a golden fractured sky where reality itself seemed wounded from their confrontation, and his voice emerged with the weight of someone questioning their fundamental assumptions.","\"What is our duty in existence? What are we bound by? Is our duty always to follow The Way of Existence of THE Creature and THE Living Existences? Is that all that our existence amounts to...perpetual service to those who came before, adherence to frameworks established by others? Are we nothing more than instruments of their will?\"","Gilgamesh asked such questions as he addressed the entity who had defeated him so thoroughly.","The Disciple of THE Creature stood without single injury visible anywhere on her form...a woman with dark hair cascading like shadow and blue eyes.","Her expression carried no malice, no satisfaction at victory, only calm certainty of someone who knew their place.","When she spoke, her voice held reverential conviction.","\" Duty is not burden to be questioned or chain to be broken. Duty is the very essence of meaningful existence. I am a follower of THE Creature whose Primordial Civilization encompasses Existence itself. My duty is therefore infallible because it serves the foundation upon which all else is built. My duty is to Existence itself, not as an abstract concept but as a living principle that sustains all things.\"","Her eyes hardened slightly.","\"You speak of duty as if it constrains you, First Leader. But true duty liberates by providing purpose beyond selfish desires. Those who reject duty in pursuit of personal freedom often discover that freedom without purpose is merely chaos wearing pleasant mask.\"","At such words, Gilgamesh’s expression twisted with spiteful rejection.","Blood, or what passed for blood in his primordial existence, continued seeping from his chest wounds as he responded with bitter defiance.","\"I reject that type of duty . I am tired of following the Way of others, of walking paths established by those who came before and expecting gratitude for my obedience. I want to find my own duty ...one that serves purposes I determine rather than purposes imposed upon me by THE Creature or any other authority.\"","His damaged hand clenched into fist.","\"Even if that duty is wrong by your standards, at least it would be mine .\"","The Disciple of THE Creature scowled at such declaration...her serene composure cracking to reveal something approaching contempt for what she viewed as foolish pride.","Her words emerged with sharp edges.","\"For that ambition, you would need to usher forth your own Way and establish your own Civilization. You would need to create framework from nothing, to convince others that your path holds merit equal to or exceeding THE Creature’s Primordial Civilization of Existence itself.\"","\"Are you exceptional enough to accomplish that? Do you possess the capability to forge something from void when THE Creature required giving his Everythings to accomplish what he did?\"","Gilgamesh’s reply emerged despite his wounds, his voice carrying unshaken conviction.","\"I stand exceptional among countless many across existence. I am The First Leader, the one who gave purpose to beings who wandered aimlessly. My exceptionalism is demonstrated through actions rather than claimed through words.\"","The Disciple’s response was sharp and biting...it was words designed to wound pride more deeply than any physical attack!","\"And yet, you could not even land a single injury on a lone Disciple like myself, no matter how much Civilizational Authority you burned in attempt. You threw everything you possessed at me and accomplished precisely nothing. What about you is exceptional, supposed First Leader? Your inability to recognize your own limitations? Your stubborn insistence that you deserve authority you haven’t earned?\"","She turned away with a dismissive gesture.","\"Find your own duty if you wish. Forge your own Civilization if you can. But understand that duty defined by personal desire rather than principle is merely ambition wearing duty’s clothing. And ambition without wisdom leads only to destruction.\"","...!","Duty .","It was a word that meant different things for many.","For some, duty was nothing.","For others... duty was everything.","---","The Present.","The sensation of being inside a Primus Inevitability was something one couldn’t really fathom unless they were personally experiencing it.","For the Blue Slime, it was akin to sitting in small domain where he was the center of existence itself.","His gelatinous form rested within crystalline chamber of obsidian-blue light, and his existence held a layer of Primus Mana covering him and connecting him to the armor’s systems as he felt like the 100 Quintillion power was not separate from him, but truly his .","He and the Primus Inevitability were inseparable...a symbiotic pair that shared power, purpose, and perception simultaneously.","At this moment, the bubbly blue slime focused on the surroundings with enhanced senses that the Civilizational Armor provided.","Something unique he realized was that as the Primus Inevitabilities moved across existence, their bodies hummed with power as one could hear silent words of affirmation ringing out inherently around them.","When the Blue Slime listened closely, his consciousness attuning to the subtle vibrations...","He heard...","\" For the Infinite Light of Mana. For the Endless Hunger that drives all growth.\"","It was like mantra that they repeated as they moved...sacred scripture recited through a fundamental nature of their existence!"]},{"number":4450,"title":"Chapter 4450: Chapter 4449: Duty II","paragraphs":["It was mesmerizing to listen to as a moment later...","HUUM!","The Blue Slime gazed outward through his armor’s visual systems to find that their group had arrived in the skies of unique location.","A Desiccated Sleeping Shore!","The domain stretched below them like corrupted mirror of the Early Veiled Shore they had departed from.","Where their home held golden sands radiating with vitality, this place bore gray granules that seemed drained of life essence.","Where their waters shone with crystalline purity, these waters moved sluggishly with unhealthy coloration suggesting contamination at fundamental level.","But the Shore held many entities...different types of Living Existences who had made this drained place their home or temporary refuge. They looked upward at the sudden appearance of armored figures with shock.","The Blue Slime looked at all of them with curiosity befitting his nature, studying their varied forms and expressions.","At this moment, in the skies, his body was among the dozens that followed behind the massive form of Ozymandias.","When he looked back with his armor’s enhanced perception, he saw the glorious armored figure of his Master in his own fused state...that sleek obsidian-blue-and-gold form with crimson visor and floating crystalline crown.","And Khor sat on the Master’s shoulder like diminutive sovereign observing her domain.","The Blue Slime’s thoughts emerged with admiration.","Master always looks cool in absolutely everything he does. It’s really unfair how he manages it so consistently. And right now, even with all these terrifying armored forms of Primus Inevitabilities that I and others adorned, a halo of light surrounds the Master as he distinctly looks different from everyone else...","Master was so incredibly cool!","The Blue Slime watched with barely contained excitement as his Master simply waved his hand with a casual gesture...a minor motion that somehow carried weight of existential authority.","In the next moment, the figure of one among their group moved forward.","Steam hissed out dramatically as one of them took off the helmet of the Civilizational Armor they adorned.","The face underneath was revealed to be Leonore Rureaux, her features carrying mixture of determination and something approaching grief.","The Blue Slime did not know much about her apart from being recent entrant into Master’s weavings, but many beings joined his Master over the months and years.","Each addition brought new perspectives, new capabilities, new loyalties.","The scene of shock spreading across the Living Existences on the Desiccated Sleeping Shore was palpable even from their elevated position.","They saw Leonore...who should have been their ally, their companion, their trusted comrade...emanating such terrifying power and arriving with these foreign beings of overwhelming strength.","She looked at them with an expression mixing recognition and resolve.","\"Existence is at stake, with forces you do not understand currently in motion. Did any of you here... observe the return of Schrodinger?\"","...!","Schrodinger .","The leader of this place, the enigmatic figure who commanded their loyalty.","And Leonore Rureaux, their supposed ally, was seemingly asking for him while surrounded by immensely powerful unknown forces!","Just... what was going on?!","The Living Existences below began murmuring with confusion and growing fear as they recognized the magnitude of power hovering above them.","At such a time...","HUUM !","The Blue Slime instinctively felt his body tense within the armor, and the Civilizational Armor around him moved naturally to pulse with defensive authority.","The blade and shield he carried through the armor’s limbs were raised as if the armor itself sensed danger approaching!","And this sensation was followed by terrifying eruption of silent authority that froze every Living Existence on the Desiccated Sleeping Shore.","From the very center of the domain... a power burning with paradoxical light arose with overwhelming presence!","The Blue Slime’s enhanced senses focused to see a humanoid Early Creature rising far ahead...emerging from concealment with casual confidence!","This Early Creature’s hair shone gold like concentrated sunlight, and its body was adorned by white chiton that seemed woven from paradoxical threads.","The body appeared very much real and yet not simultaneously...as if existing in multiple states at once through mechanisms that defied conventional existence.","It was titanic in scale, and it was not a Dead Early Creature, but a genuine Early Creature...one projecting from elsewhere.","As the Blue Slime looked forth with growing tension, he naturally saw blue-bordered words rising to identify this being who looked at them with great interest.","|Illusory Reality Avatar of Existence|","|Designation: Unknown - Avatar of Early Creature from THE Loom|","|Approximate Complexity and Purity: 1.5 Sextillion|","|Classification: Hostile Entity - Vessel Guardian|","...!","1.5 Sextillion !","The number made the Blue Slime’s gelatinous form quiver with recognition of the threat.","That was 15 times more powerful than any single Primus Inevitability...equivalent to 1,500 Quintillion!","As soon as such a being fully manifested, he looked with interest at Ozymandias, the distant Noah, and all assembled forces with an expression mixing curiosity and arrogance.","\"Well, this is certainly an interesting development. Has the outside existence advanced this much to actually have dozens of creatures following a Way of Existence this tightly? Such power, coordination, such unified purpose...I haven’t witnessed its like outside THE Loom.\"","His voice was paradoxical and heavy, causing sense of pressure to descend all around them.","Even the Blue Slime felt slight sense of suffocation despite being protected by his Civilizational Armor.","The Avatar continued with condescending amusement.","\"Who are you all? And why would you be looking for something that does not involve you?\"","...!","The voice alone caused heavy sense of suffocation across all present.","And yet the Blue Slime did not fear because at this moment...","\" For the Infinite Light of Mana. For the Endless Hunger that drives all growth!\"","His Civilizational Armor and all those of others nearby continued to hum with these affirmations as if they were repeating sacred scripture.","The mantra seemed to push back against the Avatar’s oppressive presence, creating bubble of resistance through sheer weight of unified belief.","And while facing such terrifying being...","The Blue Slime began to bounce up and down with excitement inside the Civilizational Armor as he saw the Master behind them wave his hand with another casual gesture.","In the next moment, Ozymandias’ chest opened with dramatic motion as from within it... 1,000 Primus Inevitabilities shot out like river of obsidian-blue-and-gold.","They encircled the skies with practiced precision, staring down at the Avatar from THE Loom with crimson eyes that held no fear...only hungry anticipation.","The moment they appeared, a booming and tense symphony began to bloom in the surroundings.","Existence itself acknowledged the significance as chorus echoed out!","\" These are the weapons existence created,","Born from pressure that could not be contained...\"","The Blue Slime felt the oppression from the terrifying Avatar lift significantly with the appearance of these 1,000 Primus Inevitabilities. Their combined Civilizational Authority pushed back against the Avatar’s singular presence.","Inside the armor, his body still looked at his Master with excitement as the Master’s hand remained raised...clearly not finished with his deployment.","And in the next moment...","HUUM !","Tens of thousands more Primus Inevitabilities surged out of Ozymandias’ opened chest, surrounding the Illusory Reality Avatar of Existence with overwhelming numbers.","The Avatar, who had maintained calm and arrogant gaze, had his expression change to become stern as he stared at tens of thousands of similar lifeforms surrounding him.","Each one pulsed with 100 Quintillion Complexity and Purity, each one wielding Civilizational Authority as birthright.","His power was 1.5 Sextillions, yes.","15 times stronger than each individual one, yes.","But when there were tens of thousands of beings, even if they were 15 times less complex individually... the numbers became heavy .","Heavy!"]},{"number":4451,"title":"Chapter 4451: Chapter 4450: Duty III","paragraphs":["The weight of accumulated power pressed down upon the Avatar’s advantage and began to negate it through sheer volume.","And the Blue Slime couldn’t help but laugh with bubbly joy inside his armor as he knew his Master had 2 Million hidden within the body of Ozymandias...and he had only revealed a fraction of available forces!","When exactly 100,000 Primus Inevitabilities blotted the skies of the Desiccated Sleeping Shore and surrounded the Avatar in perfect formation, the scene was both glorious and horror-inducing simultaneously.","The powerful air of the Avatar was completely eclipsed, with only the light of Primus Mana and Hunger being present...obsidian-blue-and-gold radiance that painted over the paradoxical authority the Avatar had been exuding.","This moment was absolute!","The Primus Inevitabilities of Mana and Hunger gazed down upon the Avatar with unified focus, their crimson eyes creating constellation of hostile intent.","In the hands of each one rested blade and shield similar to what the armored body of the Master was holding...hollow blades with Primordial Fireballs spinning within, shields inscribed with Primus Mana Arcana Glyphs. Just slightly less bright than the Master’s weapons, but multiplied by 100,000...","The combined light was blinding.","At such moment...","The Blue Slime trembled with excitement as he saw the Civilizational Armor of his Master pulse with activity. Tentacles bloomed from it to form into glorious Primus Inevitability beside his Master rather than around him.","The one who had introduced himself as Protos and who had fused with the Master!","Protos appeared grandly and already looked taller and bigger than all other Primus Inevitabilities...as if his fusion with Noah had elevated him beyond his brethren.","At this moment, Protos raised his shield high as he bellowed with a voice that carried across entire domain.","\" What do we fight for?!\"","HUUM !","The next scene made the Blue Slime’s existence tremble with vicarious pride.","All 100,000 Primus Inevitabilities raised their shields grandly in synchronized motion...the sound of 100,000 obsidian-gold shields being raised creating thunderous percussion.","They answered with unified voice that seemed to shake reality itself.","\" We fight for Mana! We fight for Hunger! We fight for the Primordial Civilization that birthed us!\"","...!","The eyes of the Blue Slime sparkled inside his armor as he saw Protos raise his sword next and speak with a booming voice that carried the weight of absolute conviction.","\" What is our duty?!\"","...!","Duty .","What was their duty?","The Blue Slime found himself contemplating this question alongside the Primus Inevitabilities, his gelatinous form rippling with introspection.","The Primus Inevitabilities answered with synchronized voices once more.","\" Our duty is to serve the Primordial Civilization without hesitation! Our duty is to defend the Master’s light without reservation! Our duty is to devour all obstacles that stand before our framework! We do not question! We do not falter! We do not cease! Our duty is absolute! We are the Blades and Shields, and our purpose is singular- the triumph of Mana and Hunger across all of existence!\"","BOOM!","The Blue Slime heard their resonant answer as he found his own existence trembling with recognition.","He asked himself.","What is MY duty?","He had met the Master what felt like so long ago...back when things were simpler, when powers were modest, when the scope of ambition was limited to survival.","He was a summon of the Master, a tool initially created to serve specific function.","What was his duty?","And as he pondered this, Protos asked next question.","\" What is our purpose?!\"","...!","The gaze of the Avatar had become entirely heavy at this moment...the arrogance replaced by something approaching genuine concern as he recognized the coordinated threat surrounding him.","The Primus Inevitabilities bellowed out their purpose with synchronized precision.","\" Our purpose is the advancement of the Primordial Civilization! Our purpose is the protection of those we serve! Our purpose is the consumption of all that opposes us! We exist to fight! We exist to defend! We exist to devour!\"","At such moment, the Blue Slime felt sense of euphoria blooming within his gelatinous form as Protos floated forward and stood gloriously tall without any trace of fear.","His massive form looked down upon the Avatar...who despite possessing 1.5 Sextillion in power, now appeared less intimidating when surrounded by 100,000 beings who each wielded Civilizational Authority without hesitation.","Protos said once more with voice carrying weight of final question before action.","\" What is our duty?!\"","This time, the Blue Slime felt his existence truly buzzing as when he truly asked himself, his duty... was to give back to the Master.","To defend the Master after all he continued to give to him and many others.","To serve not because he was compelled, but because he chose to serve someone worthy of service.","So this time, as the Primus Inevitabilities replied with their booming voices, the Blue Slime joined them in their declaration as he also raised his sword through his armor’s limbs.","\" Our duty is to the Master! Our duty is to the Civilization! Our duty is absolute and infinite!\"","...!","And shockingly, he wasn’t the only one.","He could see the Emperor Penguin raising his armored sword, Kazuhiko joining the chorus, Lilith’s blade rising, Titano’s massive form adding its voice, Erikson participating despite his usual reserve, and many others also raising their swords and bellowing out the same declaration of duty like the Primus Inevitabilities!","Original members of Noah’s weavings had found their duty alongside the newly born Inevitabilities...a unified purpose transcending origin or length of service!","Existence trembled and became completely silent in the next moment as all symphonies ceased.","All chorus ceased.","There was only Protos pointing his sword down toward the Avatar as he said with cold finality.","\" An enemy of the Master is before you. Fulfill. Your. Duty.\"","...!","The glorious moment that followed would be seared into the Blue Slime’s memory for as long as he lived.","All Primus Inevitabilities lit up with obsidian-blue-and-gold waves of power simultaneously...100,000 beings activating their capabilities in perfect synchronization.","They swung their hollow swords down with unified motion, and from each blade, countless Primordial Fireballs bloomed outward.","The Blue Slime watched in slow motion as each Primus Inevitability released at least 1 Million condensed miniaturized Fireballs with their single swing.","Each Fireball burned with concentrated Mana and Hunger, each one capable of devastating territories if allowed to detonate fully.","100,000 Primus Inevitabilities.","1 Million Fireballs each.","100 Billion Primordial Fireballs surging toward a lone Avatar.","The sight was beyond spectacular...it was cataclysmic.","The sky became wall of obsidian-blue-and-gold fire descending with inexorable purpose.","All of it surged toward the lone Avatar whose expression had become heavy with recognition of what he faced.","He howled out and began to surge with Civilizational Authority of Paradox...his 1.5 Sextillion power manifesting fully as paradoxical light erupted around him.","But even as he activated his full strength, even as he deployed whatever defensive measures his projection allowed...","100 Billion Primordial Fireballs continued their descent.","The Blue Slime looked at all of this with ecstasy, his entire existence feeling sense of fervor as he repeated words of his own duty to his Master.","Duty .","Yes. This was his Duty.","In Master’s grand emerging Civilization, he would witness all the wonders as he carried out his duty.","He would serve with loyalty that transcended simple obligation. He would fight with conviction born from choice rather than compulsion.","This was his Duty!","And as the Fireballs descended and the Avatar prepared for impact that would test the limits of his projected form...","The Blue Slime felt his gelatinous form pulse with glory!","Officium.","Duty.","Duty was not chains. Duty was not burden.","Duty was choice ...choice to serve something worthy of service, choice to fight for those worthy of protection, choice to devour for Civilization worthy of growth.","And his Duty was to the Master.","For as long as he lived.","BOOM!"]},{"number":4452,"title":"Chapter 4452: Chapter 4451: Duty IV","paragraphs":["There was strength in numbers.","This truth had been acknowledged across existence since the earliest days when the first beings clustered together for protection against threats they could not face alone.","Many had proclaimed that if one simply possessed sufficient quantity, quality became secondary concern.","Accumulate enough. Gather enough. Amass enough.","This was true, but only to an extent.","If there existed a terrifying army of knights numbering 100, each capable of massacring a peasant with single swing of their blade...trained warriors encased in armor that deflected weak strikes, wielding weapons that cleaved through unprotected flesh like scythes through wheat...","Then even 1,000 peasants might not accomplish much against them.","The peasants would charge. The knights would cut them down in swathes. Bodies would pile. Blood would flow. And the knights would stand victorious over mountain of corpses.","But if 1 million peasants with no individual power swarmed these same 100 knights?","The calculus shifted dramatically.","The sheer exhaustion after cutting down thousands would accumulate. Arms would tire from endless swinging.","Armor would dent under cumulative impacts of countless weak strikes.","Eventually, dozens of these invincible knights would fall...not from single devastating blow, but from being gradually ripped apart by weak peasants who simply refused to stop coming.","There was strength in numbers, yes.","But one had to understand how to use these numbers. Where the true strength resided.","How to ensure that tens of thousands of peasants did not have to die before achieving results they wanted.","The difference between victory and pyrrhic slaughter lay not in accumulation of bodies, but in tactical application of accumulated force.","Wisdom transformed numbers from blunt instrument into a magisterial, tyrannical, surgical weapon.","---","In the Dessicated Sleeping Shore.","Protos gazed at the erupting might of the Illusory Reality Avatar of Existence with coldness and immensity that exceeded his newly born consciousness.","He currently stood in front of Noah, feeling the interminable gaze of The Master behind him.","The analytical eyes that observed and wanted to see the results of them facing their first genuine enemy.","And the first enemy they faced was 15 times stronger individually than each of them.","But so what?","The Master wanted results, and The Master would have results.","It was the least that Protos could do to deliver results when the Master had done so much for their emergence. When the Master had infused them with Infinite Hunger and purpose!","So Protos watched as the Avatar of an Early Creature below made his move.","Since he had the honor of being fused into Master’s glorious glow, his capabilities had grown far beyond his Brothers and Sisters.","His gaze could perceive details that others could not access.","This was why his Master allowed him to come out and lead.","When he looked at the Avatar, he looked at it through the Master’s brilliant analytical gaze as details freely displayed themselves.","|Illusory Reality Avatar of Existence|","|Designation: Aurelius Paradoxus - Early Creature of THE Loom|","|Current State: Avatar displaying 25% of Main Body’s capability|","|Main Body Complexity and Purity: 6 Sextillion|","|Avatar Complexity and Purity: 1.5 Sextillion|","|Primary Authority: Civilizational Authority of Paradox|","|Active Principles: 3 Grand Principles detected - Paradoxical Manifestation, Reality Inversion, Quantum Superposition|","|Thr Avatar possesses limited duration outside THE Loom . Estimated operational time remaining: Unknown.|","Protos processed this information calmly.","His words emerged through the communication channel shared exclusively among Primus Inevitabilities- glorious, disciplined, and unwavering.","\"Brothers and Sisters, heed my words. The enemy designated Aurelius Paradoxus possesses power exceeding ours individually by a factor of fifteen. His Civilizational Authority of Paradox is substantial, and three Grand Principles amplify his capabilities significantly.\"","His voice carried weight of a commander addressing his troops!","\"However, this Avatar represents merely 25% of his main body’s power. Our duty is clear- we must pressure him relentlessly until all of his existence burns under our Infinite Hunger !\"","HUUUM!","His crimson eyes blazed.","\"After the initial impact of this first wave between us, the pivotal moment for us to oppress this much more powerful enemy will appear. Our numbers are our strength. Our coordination is our weapon. Our Infinite Hunger is our victory.\"","After delivering this assessment, his body began to pulse as he and all his Brothers and Sisters activated their Civilizational Resonance.","Their combined power had already covered everything in the grandeur of Mana and Hunger...painting over the paradoxical authority with obsidian-blue-and-gold radiance.","At this moment, while over 100 Billion Primordial Fireballs carrying the decimation of 100+ Quintillion complexity each smashed onto their enemy, Protos gave another order without pause.","They had to be relentless against their enemy.","Their enemy could not be allowed to breathe. Could not be allowed a single moment to recover or counter-strategize.","\"Impose your Hunger onto this enemy. Let them experience glimpse of what Infinite Hunger truly feels. Everyone...activate Hunger Propagation immediately!\"","...!","The effects of Hunger Propagation were devastating in their application.","To feel the hunger of 100,000 Primus Inevitabilities simultaneously...to experience that uncontrollable appetite that begins devouring one’s own power reserves from within...was to understand why this capability was going to be feared in the not so distant future.","It was not external assault.","It was internal sabotage .","The target’s own existence would turn against itself, hunger consuming power like fire consuming fuel.","Resources carefully accumulated would be devoured by appetite that had no satiation point.","The stronger the target’s reserves, the more aggressively the imposed hunger would attempt to consume them!","Below their encirclement, Aurelius Paradoxus, the Avatar of an Early Creature, had erupted with terrific power befitting an entity with 1.5 Sextillion Complexity and Purity.","Gloriously, his body shone with scintillating golden box of Paradox that pulsed with concentrated Civilizational Authority.","The paradoxical construct absorbed all incoming attacks...100 Billion Primordial Fireballs smashing against its surface and being negated through reality-defying mechanisms.","A paradoxical box that simultaneously existed and didn’t exist, that absorbed damage by making the damage paradoxically to \" never have occurred.\"","This being was so powerful that he withstood the combined attack of 100,000 Primus Inevitabilities alone and appeared completely unscathed !","Within that golden box, he looked up at all of them with hardened gaze that carried recognition of threat but no fear.","It was the arrogance of someone who had faced countless lesser beings and emerged victorious.","At that precise moment, he felt their imposed hunger.","And...","HUUM !","The radiant and infallible box of Paradox rapidly began to deteriorate as if being consumed by his own internal hunger.","Golden light that had been solid and impenetrable started flickering, sections dissolving as the Avatar’s power reserves were being devoured from within by appetite that had no end.","His eyes pulsed with lividity as he recognized what was occurring.","His own defenses were eating themselves, his Civilizational Authority being consumed by a hunger he could not control or dismiss!"]},{"number":4453,"title":"Chapter 4453: Chapter 4452: Duty V","paragraphs":["When Protos observed this deterioration, he knew the time had come for next phase.","His words rang out to his Brothers and Sisters.","\"The enemy’s defenses falter. His paradoxical barrier consumes itself. Be ready for a response. Maintain formation. Maintain duty!\"","And in the next instant...","The Avatar opened his mouth and roared grandly with a sound that made surrounding existence tremble.","Protos analyzed the grandeur of 3 Grand Principles shining from this being...Paradoxical Manifestation, Reality Inversion, and Quantum Superposition overlapping on top of each other.","They amplified his Civilizational Authority of Paradox exponentially, each Principle feeding into the others to create multiplicative effect rather than additive.","And the product that came out...","BOOM!","The attack was cataclysmic in scope and devastating in intent.","Millions of golden paradoxical pillars of light surged upward toward the Primus Inevitabilities like forest of death growing instantly from below.","Each pillar crackled with concentrated Civilizational Authority of Paradox ...golden light that seemed to burn reality itself with its passage.","Half of them shockingly directed and concentrated toward Noah’s and Ozymandias’ positions specifically...as if the enemy knew exactly who he wanted to eliminate.","Time felt like it moved unfathomably slow as Protos gazed at this attack approaching. Through the Master, he understood it!","In the span of single instant, he spoke to all Primus Inevitabilities present through their exclusive communication channel.","\"Brothers and Sisters, observe the enemy’s counter-assault. Designation: Schrodinger’s Strike. Each golden pillar of paradox carries more than 1 Sextillion worth of damage, far exceeding our individual capabilities to withstand.\"","His voice remained steady despite the apocalyptic attack approaching.","\"If touched by even one of these pillars, your existence will be forced into quantum paradox. You will become simultaneously ’ dead’ and ’alive’ in the same state until reality is forced to choose one outcome. The forced choice will almost certainly result in harmful resolution, your existence unraveling as paradox resolves against your favor.\"","His crimson eyes blazed with unwavering conviction.","\"This attack is lethal. This attack is devastating. This attack seeks to eliminate us before we can fulfill our purpose. But I ask you now, Brothers and Sisters: does this attack exceed our duty? Does this assault surpass our purpose? Can paradoxical death prevent us from serving our Master?\"","...!","In that instant as the attack was coming, as the millions of golden pillars were racing toward them with lethal intent, in the communication channel only for the Primus Inevitabilities, all those present roared their reply with unified conviction!","\" NEGATIVE ! Our duty is absolute! Our purpose is infinite! We do not falter! We do not fear! We devour all obstacles! Death itself cannot exceed our duty to the Master!\"","Protos then looked at the deadly attacks directed toward his Master with expression carrying protective fury.","\" Then fulfill your duty. Activate Void Appetite!\"","...!","Void Appetite.","This terrifying capability represented one of the most devastating aspects of Infinite Hunger given tangible form.","At this moment, the 100,000 Primus Inevitabilities, alongside those in form of Civilizational Armor fused with Master’s people, pulsed with obsidian-blue-and-gold-crimson light that erupted from their combined existence.","Brilliant stellar tentacled jaws manifested in the surroundings...and they were not physical constructs but conceptual weapons that could consume abstract concepts including damage itself!","Their hunger overlapped and resonated, creating zone of absolute consumption where anything that entered would be devoured.","These jaws crushed and bit down on the surging pillars of Paradox...the golden light that could deal 1 Sextillion damage each being met by Infinite Hunger that had no upper limit.","The glorious scene that unfolded was breathtaking in its significance.","The light of Paradox was being devoured by the jaws of Infinite Hunger .","Golden pillars that had been racing toward them with lethal intent were intercepted by stellar tentacles that wrapped around them and consumed their essence.","Many of the jaws shattered and broke under the intense light of Paradox, unable to fully contain power that exceeded their individual capacity.","But even more replaced them instantly, Infinite Hunger regenerating faster than it could be destroyed.","In single nanosecond that felt like eternity, the millions of golden pillars of Paradox... were devoured by a gloriously endless appetite!","The attack that should have devastated their forces, that should have eliminated dozens of their number through paradoxical death, was consumed as fuel for their growth instead.","...!","HUUM!","All the Primus Inevitabilities shone with glorious light of increased power as down below, Aurelius Paradoxus looked up with blazing eyes of absolute lividity.","From his powerful attack, his Schrodinger’s Strike that should have been devastating, none of these weak creatures 15 times less powerful than himself had even perished!","In fact... the light around them seemed to be getting stronger ?","His expression shifted from anger to something approaching concerned recognition as he realized his attacks were feeding their growth rather than diminishing their numbers.","At such moment, Protos raised his sword commandingly as he...bellowed out.","\" What is our duty?!\"","All Inevitabilities raised their swords in synchronized motion as they replied with unified voices!","\" Our duty is to our Master! Our duty is absolute! Our duty is Infinite!\"","Protos then boomed out his words with commanding authority.","\"Then give the Master what you devoured! Channel all gained essence toward the Civilization!\"","Prompts flashed before Protos.","|Cataclysmic attack designated Schrodinger’s Strike has been devoured by grand collective of Infinite Hunger .|","|Distribution parameters established by The Master:|","|All Primus Inevitabilities present on the battlefield gain +.1 Quintillion Complexity and Purity each through the grace of the Master’s framework.|","|Only .01 Quintillion Complexity and Purity has been accepted by the Master himself.|","|Remaining essence flows across the Civilization’s Foundation Palisades for collective advancement.|","|The Master demonstrates generous leadership by prioritizing his forces over personal gain.|","...!","Protos turned around to gaze at the still armored visage of the Master as his crimson eyes shone with blinding light of duty fulfilled.","The Master could have taken all of it for himself. Could have absorbed the entire consumed attack to further his own power.","Instead, he distributed it among his forces while taking only modest portion for himself.","This was why Protos would serve until his existence ceased.","While looking at the Master with reverence that transcended simple loyalty, he bellowed out with commanding authority.","\"Advance upon the enemy. Close the encirclement. Do not give him...even a moment to recover! Fulfill. Your. Duty!\"","...!","The moment he issued this command, the silence that had fallen over the battlefield ended.","A new symphony bloomed across existence...not the melancholic melody from before, but something far more aggressive.","The beat was high-paced, as if drums of existence were pounding to the beat of rapid heart preparing for decisive confrontation.","And this time, there wasn’t grand chorus with flowing lyrics.","There were only two words that began to echo out with booming fervor as the Primus Inevitabilities’ encirclement closed in tighter around the Avatar.","\" INFINITE!\"","WAA!","\"HUNGER!\"","BOOM!","Infinite. Hunger.","Such words blazed across existence like alarm that could not be ignored...a declaration of what they were and what they intended to do.","In the next moment, the shields of all Primus Inevitabilities and the Civilizational Armored forces raised their defensive implements in synchronized motion.","From their shields, Primus Mana Arcana Glyphs activated with concentrated power.","In the next instant, more than 100,000 Primordial Primus Mana-Flame Wyrms emerged from the activated Glyphs!","These were not simple manifestations or temporary constructs. They looked unfathomably real ...creatures of concentrated authority given permanent form through the quality of Primus Mana.","Each Wyrm possessed nine heads that pulsed with interminable grandeur, and each head bore jaws capable of releasing molten Civilizational Authority .","The glorious sense of power and honor these Wyrms emitted was palpable...ancient creatures summoned to serve The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger!","They... could remain active for a whole hour!","The Primus Mana quality made such grand thing possible! And 100,000 of them were called out at this moment as they encircled the Avatar alongside their summoners.","Each of their many jaws...more than 900,000 heads total, opened simultaneously as they roared out molten Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger toward the enemy!","BOOM!","\"INFINITE!\"","\"HUNGER!\"","The Symphony and Chorus picked up with increasing intensity as on the ground, Aurelius Paradoxus roared angrily with a voice that made surrounding existence crack.","\"I bear the light of a glorious Civilization! You all... cannot compare to what THE Loom has cultivated across eons! ONTOLOGICAL ANCHORING!\"","BOOM !"]},{"number":4454,"title":"Chapter 4454: Chapter 4453: Olethros! I","paragraphs":["Immense waves of Civilizational Authority of Paradox erupted from Aurelius Paradoxus...a golden light that expanded outward to form into sea of paradoxical power.","This golden sea rose to match and drown out all incoming attacks, attempting to negate their assault through fundamental reality manipulation.","In the surroundings, a different symphony started to bloom with the eruption of Civilizational Authority of Paradox - a competing melody that clashed with the drums of Hunger.","And accompanying this counter-melody:","\"PARADOX!\"","A booming singular word of Paradox threatened to drown out Hunger...trying to impose its authority over the battlefield through sheer weight of established Primordial Civilization!","Once more, Protos analyzed the threat and communicated to his forces","\"This technique seeks to impose upon you and your abilities a self-negating truth. According to this paradox, you can only exist if you do not exist. The truth seeks to retroactively erase you and your abilities even before you existed...to make it so you never were .\"","\"Does such a truth align with your duty?\"","...!","The short but grand synchronized reply of the Primus Inevitabilities rang out with absolute conviction.","\"NO! Paradox cannot erase our duty!\"","Protos’ eyes shone brilliantly with glorious crimson light as he bellowed out the command.","\"Then... FULFILL. YOUR. DUTY!\"","...!","BOOM!","Void Appetite erupted again with even greater intensity than before, Infinite Hunger responding to paradoxical assault with absolute consumption.","Oh!","The glorious jaws manifested throughout the golden sea, stellar tentacles wrapping around concentrated Civilizational Authority of Paradox and devouring it with methodical precision.","The paradox that sought to erase them was being consumed. The truth that claimed they could only exist if they didn’t exist was being eaten by hunger that didn’t care about logical contradictions.","Infinite Hunger devoured even paradoxes.","|Ontological Anchoring has been systematically devoured by Infinite Hunger. Paradoxical truth negated through consumption rather than logical refutation.|","|All Primus Inevitabilities present gain +1.5 Quintillion Complexity and Purity.|","|The Master requests no portion of this harvest. All essence flows to his forces and Civilization.|","...!","The golden sea of Civilizational Authority of Paradox faded as it was devoured, and the attacks of 100,000 Wyrms descended with 900,000 heads worth of molten Civilizational Authority raining down.","Aurelius Paradoxus gazed at them coldly from below, his expression mixing fury with calmness.","The glorious scene that followed was devastating in its relentlessness.","The attacks landed on his body one by one...900,000 streams of molten Mana and Hunger crashing against his form with combined weight that exceeded even his substantial defenses.","He gazed at them coldly as his entire body shone golden with protective light...attempting to nullify all attacks as they smashed into him through paradoxical negation.","A staredown commenced between the Avatar and those above.","Aurelius looked toward Noah and Ozymandias with eyes that carried killing intent.","But the crimson eyes of Protos were the only thing that met his gaze...Protos staring down this being that was being bombarded with attacks of all his brethren while standing perfectly still between the enemy and his Master.","Aurelius was powerful, yes.","He was withstanding assault that would have devastated lesser beings. His Civilizational Authority of Paradox was genuine, his power substantial.","But...","BZZT!","In the staredown, Protos observed the infallible golden glow of Paradox surrounding the Avatar dim slightly over time as... Infinite Hunger began to take bites from it!","The constant pressure, the relentless assault, the imposed hunger from within...all of it was accumulating damage that even 1.5 Sextillion power could not indefinitely sustain.","The enemy was indeed powerful.","But before their hunger, before their Duty... he had to fall.","Protos deemed this with absolute certainty even as the Master communicated through their bond that soon, this Avatar would receive aid from others just like him...with one being immensely powerful, far exceeding even Aurelius.","Protos accepted this information and was already prepared. Only 100,000 of his Brothers and Sisters were currently deployed.","1.9 Million were yet to be revealed from the glorious body of Ozymandias.","When the rest of the enemies came, and they would come, Protos would lead to fulfill his duty.","The glorious scene that unfolded would be remembered across existence.","The encirclement around the Avatar closed in even deeper...100,000 Primus Inevitabilities with their 100,000 Wyrms creating zone of absolute consumption that pressed inward with inexorable force.","Shockingly, terrifyingly, magnificently...a being with 1.5 Sextillion power was being offset by unique combination of numbers, Mana, and Hunger!","One being watched it coldly.","He was Protos, First of the Primus Inevitabilities.","And at this moment...","\"Finish it.\"","...!","He gave a command that would determine the immediate future of this battlefield.","A moment later, the terrifying scene unfolded. On the body of Ozymandias floating grandly above, the chest flashed twice with deliberate pulsing...a signal that had been pre-arranged with his Master.","Protos had already communicated extensively with Noah regarding the optimal approach for decimating their first true enemy.","For the sake of achieving overwhelming victory rather than costly struggle, one had to be wise and strategic rather than simply powerful.","When an animal was thrown with their back against the wall, it would lash out with the strongest and most volatile response available.","Aurelius Paradoxus was about to erupt with Everything...his full remaining resources dedicated to devastating counter-attack against the forces he perceived as threatening him.","At such a moment, when he had mentally accounted for how to erupt with sufficient power against the 100,000 terrifying Primus Inevitabilities surrounding him...","Protos gazed down coldly as in the next instant, 200,000 more Primus Inevitabilities materialized within the encirclement of Aurelius with synchronized precision!","The simple yet tactical brilliance was devastating.","Protos watched with continuing analytical curiosity as he observed the eyes of this terrifying entity open wide with incredulity...the arrogance and calculated confidence fracturing into genuine shock as he realized the forces arrayed against him had just tripled .","And in that brief opening, in that instant where shock disrupted his tactical planning...","Hunger Propagation was activated by all newly appearing 200,000 Primus Inevitabilities to layer onto the Hunger Propagation that was already imposed upon this being.","While he had prepared and acclimated to throw a last-second volatile attack sufficient to devastate 100,000 entities, 200,000 more appeared and imposed their terrifying Infinite Hunger upon him!","The effect was catastrophic !"]},{"number":4455,"title":"Chapter 4455: Chapter 4454: Olethros! II","paragraphs":["The brilliant golden light of Paradox that had been surrounding his body, the protective barrier that had withstood millions of Primordial Fireballs...was instantly devoured by his own being as the accumulated hunger from 300,000 Primus Inevitabilities exceeded any threshold his existence could manage.","The terrifying scene that followed would haunt any observer who witnessed it.","This entity of immense power...1.5 Sextillion Complexity and Purity, bearer of Civilizational Authority of Paradox , Avatar of an Early Creature from THE Loom ...lost his protections as his uncontrollable appetite devoured his own existence from within.","His defenses didn’t break.","They were consumed by hunger that recognized no distinction between self and other, between friendly power and hostile attack.","And the moment that the influence of his Civilizational Authority was gone, the instant his golden barrier collapsed into nothing through internal consumption...","Protos took a single step.","And in the next moment appeared directly in front of Aurelius Paradoxus with velocity.","Defenseless. Shocked. Not knowing how what was happening could possibly be occurring...his tactical calculations shattered, his arrogance replaced by genuine fear.","At such moment, the sword in Protos’ hand flashed with blinding speed to sink into the chest of Aurelius that possessed no remaining defenses.","The hollow blade pierced through flesh and essence with equal ease, and the Primordial Fireballs spinning within the blade’s center erupted into his internal existence.","A horror-inducing scene followed as Protos grasped the head of Aurelius Paradoxus with his other hand...the fucking grip suggesting absolute domination rather than simple combat advantage.","He whispered coldly with voice that carried no malice, only tactical assessment.","\"Next time, try to bring your main body or someone significantly stronger than you are. You fought decently for what you possessed. But decently is insufficient .\"","BOOM !","With such words, Protos shouldered the Civilizational Resonance of all Primus Inevitabilities present...their combined hunger flowing through him as focal point, as a living weapon wielding the accumulated appetite of 300,000 beings.","His Infinite Hunger erupted out ravenously as in the next moment, the pierced chest of Aurelius began collapsing into an Event Horizon centered upon the blade embedded within him.","The hollow center of Protos’ sword, filled with countless Primordial Fireballs, became a point of absolute consumption as Aurelius’ existence began spiraling inward.","And in the next instant, muscle, bone, and entire body of Aurelius collapsed into Protos’ blade!","He was not destroyed or killed through conventional means.","He was devoured!","The Avatar of Aurelius Paradoxus was systematically consumed....his 1.5 Sextillion Complexity and Purity becoming fuel for the Primus Inevitabilities’ growth, his Civilizational Authority of Paradox being harvested as resource for advancement!","...!","\"...\"","Immense silence instantly settled across the battlefield at such terrifying scene.","An entity 15 times more powerful than each individual Primus Inevitability had been collapsed.","If they had erred at any moment during the engagement, if Protos had miscalculated or hesitated, multiple of their brethren could have been killed or severely damaged.","But Protos had led tremendously under the brilliance of the Master’s guidance!","They had climbed a glorious mountain fifteen times grander than their individual capabilities and systematically collapsed it through Infinite Hunger.","In the silence, Protos simply raised his blade with casual motion as if he had not accomplished anything particularly remarkable.","He gave another command with a voice carrying a matter-of-fact authority.","\"Turn this Desiccated Shore upside down. Find the Vessel that creature was protecting. Leave nothing unchecked. Fulfill your duty.\"","...!","BOOM !","As if they had not just accomplished unprecedented victory against overwhelmingly superior individual opponent, the 300,000 Primus Inevitabilities here instantly transformed into streaks of obsidian-blue-and-gold light that pervaded across the Desiccated Sleeping Shore!","They moved with methodical efficiency...groups of thousands sweeping through territories, investigating structures, probing hidden spaces with enhanced perception!","Protos’ body trembled with immense complexity at this moment as what he had devoured was far, far too pristine.","The concentrated essence of an Avatar bearing Civilizational Authority of Paradox was unlike anything he had consumed before.","He turned toward his Master...wanting to offer this grand complexity he had just hungered to Noah, wanting to demonstrate that all gains belonged ultimately to the Civilization rather than individual advancement.","But before he could articulate such offer...","Prompts bloomed with systematic precision.","|All hungered harvest has been amplified by Perpetual Harvest. All effort carried out by all forces present has been amplified by Perpetual Harvest’s multiplicative capabilities.|","|All collective harvest including the decimation and complete devouring of Aurelius Paradoxus has been systematically distributed according to optimal advancement parameters outlined by The Master.|","|50% has been deemed to be solely claimed by Protos , The First Primus Inevitability , in recognition of his exemplary leadership and execution.|","|50% flows into the Foundation Palisades for collective Civilizational advancement.|","|This distribution ensures both individual excellence is rewarded and collective framework is strengthened simultaneously.|","...!","Protos trembled as in the next moment, he felt his existence buzzing with unprecedented intensity as his Complexity and Purity began surging upward with momentum that suggested no immediate ceiling.","Additional prompts detailed the magnitude!","|Your Complexity and Purity has increased by 500 Quintillion after such grand harvest. The effort of defeating and devouring Aurelius Paradoxus, amplified by Perpetual Harvest, has yielded exceptional returns.|","|Your total Complexity and Purity now exceeds 600 Quintillion.|","|You have become substantially more powerful than your Brothers and Sisters through meritorious service. Keep it up.|","...!","BOOM!","The glorious scene that followed was visible to all present.","The body of Protos became twice as large...his form expanding to accommodate the concentrated power now flowing through his existence.","The air that radiated from him carried brutality alongside discipline, predatory hunger alongside absolute loyalty!","His presence had transformed from merely formidable to genuinely overwhelming...a being that could now challenge enemies far exceeding his previous capabilities.","And yet even as he emanated such terrifying aura of accumulated power...","He knelt toward the Master with a gesture mixing reverence and absolute dedication.","\"I will burn Existence for you, Master! My power is your power! My existence serves your Civilization! Command me, and it shall be done!\"","...!"]},{"number":4456,"title":"Chapter 4456: Chapter 4455: Olethros! III","paragraphs":["It was a terrifying and swift execution.","Noah watched all of it silently as he only gave a few commands and allowed Protos to execute decisions independently.","The coordination and movements of these terrifying Weapons of his Civilization operated smoothly and grandly when they were left to carry out their orders while being led by singular commanding entity.","That entity was either Protos or his form of Ozymandias...both of whom could fully tap into the communication channels connecting all Primus Inevitabilities and move as one unified force rather than scattered individuals.","So he only nodded with satisfaction as he saw Protos kneeling while his body pulsed with 600 Quintillion Complexity and Purity... power that now positioned him as a decently formidable threat!","As for himself...","Prompts materialized detailing his own advancement.","|An immense quantity of harvest is flowing into the Foundation Palisades. The quality of this harvest is unfathomable as it contains substantial concentration of The Primordial Civilizational Authority of Paradox.|","|Protection threshold from Foundation Palisades has increased from 500 Quintillion to 1,000 Quintillion Complexity and Purity. Any entity wishing to harm your existence must now exceed this threshold while also being member of established Civilization.|","|Boon from Minor Mana and Hunger Palisades has increased from 45 Quintillion to 95 Quintillion Complexity and Purity for all 81 blessed recipients.|","|Your personal Complexity and Purity has reached 500 Quintillion through accumulated advancement.|","|When paired with your fused Primus Inevitability, Protos, who stands at 600 Quintillion, you have officially crossed the barrier of 1,000 Quintillion Complexity and Purity.|","|The major requirement for one to be considered in the Sextillions designation is the attainment and practical usage of Civilizational Authority. Such requirement has long since been met.|","|At this moment, your combined Complexity and Purity stands at 1.1 Sextillion .|","...!","1.1 Sextillion!","The monumental marker that separated ordinary beings from those who could utilize Civilizational Authority!","To be given the Quintillion designation, one had to be walking on a Way of Existence- whether pioneered or following an established one.","The next demarcation needed Civilizational Authority as Noah had attained it!","Noah’s calm and tyrannical weavings pulsed emerged as he processed this achievement.","The milestone was significant, certainly...representing crossing into territory that few outside THE Loom had reached.","But even achieving it, he only took moment to compose himself before his mind immediately moved forward.","\"More.\"","...!","More !","Because he would truly need much more than this. The Avatars from THE Loom would continue coming. THE Dead Order was mobilizing her forces.","THE Living Paradox himself possessed power that made 1.1 Sextillion seem utterly laughable as THE Living Paradox himself could still crush him whether he had 1 Sextillion or 100 Sextillion or 1,000 Sextillion....the number did not matter to THE !","This was why he was moving so quickly to collapse his Vessels while Existence suppressed him!","He needed exponentially more power if he genuinely intended to challenge the established order.","In the next moment, a burst of commotion erupted as brilliant blue-gold light of Primus Mana and obsidian-crimson light of Hunger pulsed intensely.","In front of Noah, Protos appeared alongside two other Primus Inevitabilities as they were dragging... an unconscious entity whose body was surrounded by paradoxical flames and frost simultaneously!","Shockingly, this being was enveloped by unique paradoxical light that suggested he was slumbering and never meant to wake...caught in quantum superposition between consciousness and oblivion.","Noah looked at him with recognition blooming immediately.","Of course this entity was...a slumbering Schrodinger!","The unique light of Paradox surrounding him would seemingly take some effort to break down through conventional means.","But at this moment, Khor floated down from Noah’s shoulder as she looked coldly at the slumbering body of Schrodinger.","She quietly said single word.","\"Outsider.\"","A single word, but Noah knew exactly what she meant...what she was asking permission to do.","So he nodded lightly with gesture of approval.","In the next moment...","The First Hunger opened her mouth... and took a glorious bite.","A single bite.","And horrifically, existence itself twisted around the area where the slumbering Living Elemental Body of Schrodinger rested. This body and the surrounding existence became...collapsed!","BOOM !","Without hesitation and moving with quickness that suggested urgency, one of the vessels of THE Living Paradox was systematically collapsed!","She was so much stronger than before.","So much grander!","A bite was all it took!","The figure of The First Hunger pulsed with interminable brilliance in the next moment, as if her hunger had devoured something unfathomably grand that resonated with her fundamental nature.","Prompts appeared detailing the consequences.","|The First Hunger becomes stronger as Hunger across existence becomes stronger. The symbiotic relationship between subject Khor and the Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger continues deepening.|","|Subject Khor has entered period of exponential growth. The consumption of a Vessel of THE Living Paradox has provided exceptional harvest.|","|The First Hunger has successfully reclaimed the 1 Sextillion threshold and proceeds ahead gloriously toward restoration of her original power. It is distant. It is unfathomably far. But THE is possible. THE is possible .|","...!","Khor also took step forward as her existence digested the Vessel of THE Living Paradox with methodical efficiency!","It was terrifying progression of events when one properly accounted for thr timeline.","Within matter of seconds, Noah had arrived with his army. Within additional seconds, he had collapsed an Avatar holding 1.5 Sextillion Complexity and Purity.","Within another few seconds, his armies had scoured the Desiccated Sleeping Shore and obtained the Vessel of THE Living Paradox.","And the Vessel was collapsed immediately upon discovery!","The speed was devastating...leaving no opportunity for enemy reinforcements to arrive in time to prevent what they had been assigned to protect.","And only after another second passed, did Noah raise his head as he looked upward with an expression mixing anticipation and cold satisfaction.","His words emerged with a casual observation.","\"You arrived a second too late, Ambessa . A single second, and you might have been able to accomplish something meaningful...\"","...!","BOOM!","His words echoed out just as the skies split apart with dramatic violence!","Eight terrifying auras descended with presence that made surrounding existence tremble.","These auras were genuinely horrifying as they matched or exceeded Aurelius Paradoxus significantly, each one burning with 1.5 to 2 Sextillion worth of authority.","But one aura exceeded all of them combined!","Oh!"]},{"number":4457,"title":"Chapter 4457: Chapter 4456: Olethros! IV","paragraphs":["Ambessa!","She appeared at this moment with a presence that commanded attention.","Her radiant crimson-gold eyes surveyed the battlefield, taking in the 300,000 Primus Inevitabilities, the absence of Aurelius, the collapsed Vessel that should have been protected.","She wore pink bloomers and white tank top that somehow appeared regal rather than casual through sheer force of her bearing.","Her crimson-gold hair flowed like banner of authority, and her expression carried no fear...only cold calculation of changed circumstances.","The moment she fully manifested, existence pulsed. A calm and valor-filled Symphony echoed out as from surrounding reality itself, one could hear...","\"AMBESSA!\"","\"AMBESSA!\"","Her very name was being echoed by surrounding existence...acknowledgment of her significance!","This terrifying being looked down toward Noah as Noah gazed back with equal intensity.","She and the rest of the Avatars had likely been securing other Vessels of Schrodinger scattered across different territories, just as Aurelius had been assigned to protect this one.","Noah looked at her calmly and saw her details with perfect clarity through his enhanced perception.","|Illusory Reality Avatar of Existence|","|Designation: Ambessa - Early Creature of THE Loom|","|Current State: Avatar displaying 50% of Main Body’s capability|","|Main Body Complexity and Purity: 10 Sextillion|","|Avatar Complexity and Purity: 5 Sextillion|","|Primary Authority: Civilizational Authority of Paradox|","|Active Principles: 5 Grand Principles detected - surpassing Aurelius significantly|","|Exceptional combat capability. Exceeds parameters of all other Avatars present. Primary threat designation.|","5 Sextillion .","Immensely high.","Gloriously powerful!","The others around her ranged from 1.5 Sextillion to 2 Sextillion at most, while she alone stood at 5 Sextillion...more powerful than several of them combined.","At this moment, she delivered her grand introduction as she looked toward Noah.","\"I will normally begin by asking whether you comprehend just who you stand against, what consequences follow from opposing THE Loom . And yet you seem to understand this full well, and you still carried out the actions that you did. Am I correct to assume that we are not going to receive opportunity for diplomatic discourse?\"","She articulated such words calmly as all around her, terrifying concentration of Civilizational Authority of Paradox began gathering....golden light that made surrounding existence warp in recognition of her power.","At her words, Noah gave light nod with an expression carrying finality.","\"No. We will not be receiving opportunity for conversation. You came to protect Vessels. We are trying to collapse them. Our objectives are mutually exclusive, which means only force will determine outcome.\"","The moment his words concluded...","The glorious scene that unfolded would be remembered as demonstration of overwhelming numerical superiority properly applied.","All around the newly appearing Avatars, hundreds of thousands of Primus Inevitabilities bloomed into existence with synchronized precision!","In addition to the 300,000 currently deployed, 700,000 more appeared through spatial tears and surrounded the eight Avatars in perfect formation!","Their heavy and calm crimson eyes stared at their enemies with hunger that transcended simple appetite.","The scene itself was utterly glorious and magisterial...a demonstration that Noah possessed resources exceeding anything the Avatars had anticipated.","Ambessa’s expression remained calm as she prepared to ask: Is this all?","But before she could even articulate the question...","In the space above where the Avatars had appeared...","BOOM!","Hunger tore space open with violent authority as Ozymandias’ chest flickered with brilliant light. And a million more Primus Inevitabilities appeared far above the battlefield!","...!","\"...!\"","Heavy and immense silence settled down all around!","2 Million Primus Inevitabilities.","Each one possessing 100+ Quintillion Complexity and Purity at baseline.","One far exceeding it.","Each one wielding Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger.","Each one capable of Hunger Propagation, Void Appetite, Civilizational Resonance , and other devastating capabilities.","All of them... coordinated under singular command structure.","All of them hungry.","Infinitely hungry.","Noah observed this scene with his eyes releasing a silent command to his general through their bond.","And in the next moment, Protos voiced out coldly with authority.","\"Fulfill your duty.\"","The Primus Inevitabilities pulsed silently.","All of them in their similar glorious armored states, crimson eyes of Infinite Hunger fixed upon their eight enemies, gazed downward with synchronized focus.","With unity and glory... their Hunger Propagation and Void Appetite crashed down onto their 8 enemies simultaneously!","HUUM !","And alongside this terrifying exertion of hunger....","\"DUTY!\"","Their voices echoed across existence as alongside such concentrated assault, they waved their swords and shields with synchronized motion.","Their swords shone with obsidian-blue light interwoven with crimson...hollow blades with Primordial Fireballs spinning within their centers.","Their shields gleamed with gold interwoven with blue...surfaces inscribed with Primus Mana Arcana Glyphs that pulsed with concentrated authority.","From 2 Million swords, 1 Million Primordial Fireballs each bloomed outward!","That was... 2 Trillion Primordial Fireballs filling surrounding existence with concentrated destructive potential!","And alongside them, the Shields of Primus Mana and Hunger flashed as 2 Million unfathomably real Primordial Primus Mana-Flame Wyrms manifested.","Each one pulsed with Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger as their nine heads opened simultaneously to release terrifying blasts toward the enemies!","The combined assault was so immense and terrifying and unfathomably numerous that the entirety of surrounding existence seemed to be filled with nothing but the brilliance of Mana and Hunger.","So much concentrated authority in such vast quantities that it felt like existence itself was... lagging .","Lagging !","Reality struggling to process the sheer volume of simultaneous attacks being executed... as if the surrounding existence couldn’t handle this density of destructive potential occupying identical space!","Oh!","And at the center of all of this apocalyptic assault were eight Avatars facing utterly devastating attack.","They were immensely powerful, yes.","Ambessa alone possessed 5 Sextillion Complexity and Purity...far exceeding what Aurelius had wielded.","But how exactly would they emerge from the other side when so many waves of Infinite Hunger were waiting for them?!","The drums of existence pounded with anticipation.","And the Primus Inevitabilities waited with hungry eyes to see what would remain after their duty was fulfilled.","Immensity crashed down and collapsed,and existence wept at the results!"]},{"number":4458,"title":"Chapter 4458: Chapter 4457: Olethros! V","paragraphs":["Casualties in war were unavoidable.","The strongest commanders knew this fundamental truth.","Because war was not pretty or kind...no matter how eloquent the speeches justifying it, no matter how noble the cause supposedly driving it.","Despite how one planned and strategized and executed everything with immense calculation considering every possibility... they would inevitably discover that their enemy had done exactly the same.","Even in the most glorious victories, there would be losses. Bodies that would not rise. Existences that would cease. Names that would be mourned.","This was the inescapable weaving of conflict.","At this moment.","In the Desiccated Sleeping Shore.","The skyspace above had transformed into region of molten authority and systematic collapse as existence itself had been fractured and torn through concentrated application of overwhelming force.","Rivers and seas of molten Primus Mana and Hunger spread gorgeously through the wounded sky...obsidian-blue and crimson-gold currents flowing like arterial blood from a body that had been grievously injured.","The molten currents created patterns that suggested both beauty and devastation, artistic destruction on scale that transcended comprehension!","The molten skies were littered with hundreds of thousands of figures of Primus Inevitabilities that were all gazing downward with cold eyes.","Their crimson stares fixed upon the aftermath of battle that had tested them for first time since their emergence.","In some regions of the skies, there existed massive blinking singularities shining the colors of Mana and Hunger.","At least nine Primus Inevitabilities surrounded each singularity as if engaged in grand ritual...their forms creating protective formations around something precious that required safeguarding.","Dozens of such singularities could be observed across this grand domain, each one pulsing with rhythmic intensity.","And yet, down below, it seemed as if existence was still reeling and struggling to stabilize...as if being put to fundamental test regarding how much devastation reality could absorb before collapsing entirely.","Because at this moment, a terrifying battle had concluded in less than one minute after it began.","Noah stood on the gray sands of this Desiccated Shore, his crimson visor-covered eyes piercing as they surveyed the battlefield.","On his shoulders, Khor also gazed upward as the two of them looked at the singularities.","Those singularities represented... collapse of Primus Inevitabilities!","They represented casualties.","There was heavy silence that settled across the domain as the surroundings where eight descended Avatars should have been visible showed only devastation.","Seven of them could not be perceived anywhere...consumed entirely through Infinite Hunger .","The only one currently visible in surrounding existence was none other than Ambessa .","Her appearance was devastating testimony to the battle’s intensity.","Her attire- pink bloomers and white tank top that had appeared so casual yet regal, now looked torn and shredded.","Her body lay deeply embedded in the center of point of impact on the gray sands, the crater suggesting she had been driven downward with catastrophic force.","Across her radiant form, countless small wounds showed bleeding Civilizational Authority of Paradox... golden light seeping from injuries.","All around her, 2 Million Primus Inevitabilities surrounded her and imposed their terrifying hunger onto her existence with coordinated precision.","At this moment, she could not even move...her 5 Sextillion power completely suppressed through sheer weight of accumulated Hunger Propagation.","That was how devastating the battle had been.","The only other entities visible in the surroundings were the very real figures of Primordial Primus Mana-Flame Wyrms who floated with terrifying eyes, their nine heads per Wyrm swiveling as if still ready for additional enemies to descend.","Noah looked at such scene as prompts appeared before him.","|Infinite Hunger has revealed a unique quality about its weavings of existence.|","|It has been determined that 124 Primus Inevitabilities faced collapse during engagement with Ambessa. Her 5 Sextillion power combined with 5 Grand Principles allowed her to systematically eliminate targets despite overwhelming numerical disadvantage.|","|However: Primus Inevitabilities within your Civilization burning with Infinite Hunger will have their identity in existence preserved within the collective Infinite Hunger.|","|These collapsed existences will be systematically reborn within 24-hour period in the Sanctuaries of Inevitabilities with half of their original power. The Collapse due to Civilizational Authority that would normally devastate one’s foundation and potentially prevent resurrection is negated through grandeur of Infinite Hunger.|","|This capability is nullified should you, The Leader of The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger, is ever collapsed by another Civilizational Authority.|","...!","These prompts were radiant in their implications...transforming what should have been devastating casualties into temporary setbacks that would be systematically corrected.","After reviewing this information, Noah commandingly allowed such knowledge to spread through the communication channels connecting all Primus Inevitabilities.","The moment this revelation propagated through their collective consciousness, all of these terrifying titanic entities turned to look toward him with brilliant crimson eyes that blazed with renewed fervor.","Protos nearby raised his fist high as he bellowed out.","\"Under the light of Infinite Hunger , the dead may never die! Our Brothers and Sisters will return! Our Civilization cannot be diminished through simple collapse!\"","...!","HUUM!","The others in response to his declaration raised their fists with glory and purpose as they roared out in synchronized chorus.","\" THE DEAD MAY NEVER DIE! THE DEAD MAY NEVER DIE!\"","Crimson winds of Hunger and accumulated complexity raged across the battlefield as at this moment, Noah turned his gaze toward the only remaining Avatar.","The other seven had fallen either to him personally or to Ozymandias, Khor, or Protos...with them dealing finishing blows after systematic weakening through coordinated assault.","All seven had their existences collapsed into Event Horizons of concentrated Hunger, with every single aspect of what they were being systematically harvested.","At this moment, this harvest was being amplified by Perpetual Harvest...waiting for final addition from the strongest among their enemies before it would be distributed across the Civilization.","And so Noah turned his attention toward the enemy who was the reason for the casualties of Primus Inevitabilities despite overwhelming numerical advantage.","Ambessa !","Noah’s glorious titanic armored form...radiant with obsidian-blue-and-gold-crimson light, the Sword and Shield of Hunger and Mana gleaming in his hands...walked toward the crater that contained the enemy who had withstood Hunger Propagation and Void Appetite with such immensity that even her attacks squeezed through gaps in their assault to instantly collapse dozens of Primus Inevitabilities.","Ambessa’s glorious body lay sprawled on the gray sands of the Desiccated Sleeping Shore, her neck mangled from devastating strike, her chest caved in from concentrated impact.","She turned her head with visible effort to stare toward Protos and Noah’s approaching figure.","Even though the current situation seemed utterly dreadful and her body was systematically failing, her eyes were immensely calm and even filled with light of genuine curiosity rather than fear or rage.","After all, these were just Avatars of beings who remained safely within THE Loom.","Noah expected substantial damage to be inflicted upon their main bodies due to his Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger devouring their projected forms, but toward such powerful beings even this damage might prove negligible.","Was this the reason for how remarkably laid back she currently appeared?","Her calm and grand words emerged as she actually looked around at the surrounding devastated existence.","\"How has life been outside THE Loom ? I received opportunity to observe briefly after we descended, but it was not truly sufficient time to satisfy my curiosity. I have always wondered how things have unfolded since we entered...how many eons have passed, what has changed, whether anything recognizable remains.\"","...!"]},{"number":4459,"title":"Chapter 4459: Chapter 4458: Civilization Specialization I","paragraphs":["At such unexpectedly casual words, Noah came forward in his armored form and squatted down while looking at Ambessa closely.","His reply emerged with an edge of skepticism.","\"Curious? Why maintain curiosity for lands your people will systematically raze and devour all lifeforms from? Lands that actually used to be your home before you abandoned them for THE Loom’s structured safety?\"","Ambessa nodded with an expression of genuine nostalgia.","\"Mmm, I do miss the First Folds. Everything felt... new . Grand in ways that structured existence cannot replicate. THE Loom is magnificent in its organization...everything there is designed with meticulous purpose and immensity.\"","Her eyes grew distant","\"But the First Folds as I remember them felt... grand precisely because there could be many things happening which seemingly had no purpose. There was factor of unknown. Factor of lack of control. Chaos that could produce unexpected beauty or unexpected horror. Perhaps I’m simply nostalgic for something I haven’t experienced in eons. But regardless...\"","Her expression sharpened.","\"Be ready. We were sent out here as experimental deployment. With your response, with you collapsing eight Avatars including myself, it is no longer experiment, but declaration of war.\"","\"You have wounded the pride of powerful beings within THE Loom who are unaccustomed to facing resistance. Oh, and you messed up them trying to suck up to THE Esteemed Paradox. They will not wait patiently for the Fallout. They will mobilize an unfathomable more to crush what dared to spit on their pride.\"","Noah nodded with an expression acknowledging the warning, while internally celebrating as he needed food for his Infinite Hunger!","\"Hmm. You seem somewhat interesting compared to expectations. I anticipated someone as powerful as you to be shouting and raging and raving about how Civilizational Authority of Paradox will rain devastation upon us. How we will all burn under the grandeur of established Primordial Civilization. But...even as I am about to collapse you... you maintain a mindset to converse freely and calmly.\"","His crimson visor fixed upon her with calculating intensity.","\"Want to do something unpredictable like... betray your Civilization?\"","...!","Noah articulated such words with cool directness as Ambessa laughed, the sound mixing genuine amusement with resignation!","\"You magnificent fucker. I genuinely admire you for being one of the leaders of whatever Civilization has emerged out here. Infinite Hunger, is it? Is it a Derivative of the Collapsed Civilization of Hunger? Oh well...\"","\"Any entities capable of leading are typically grand...Elderborns, those bearing concentrated Everythings of THE Creature himself... However grand you are personally, I’m not placing my confidence in your victory. You will likely face collapse very soon once a proper response is mobilized. So this was entertaining, but that concludes my involvement...for now anyway. I’ll probably be sent again because of how tight of a fit I am in this scenario...\"","...!","She thought he was one of the leaders of whatever grand Civilization had collapsed her and the other Avatars.","And that was far more believable idea to grasp...that there existed some grand hidden Civilization that had bloomed outside THE Loom over the eons, that whoever led it was someone utterly astonishing.","One might find it easier to believe that perhaps this Civilization was a Derivative of Hunger or even carrying weavings of THE Creature himself or representing one of the Collapsed Civilizations that had somehow reconstituted itself.","This was exponentially easier to believe than the reality...that it was a human who had been a weak, manaless being less than three years ago!","At such thought, Noah couldn’t help but pause and metaphorically blink as he truly contemplated the timeline himself.","Three years .","Had it truly been almost that duration since he awakened?","Three years felt simultaneously unimaginably short and impossibly long because during that period he had played with time dilation and other temporal manipulations constantly.","So that number could be stretched up or down.","But in the objective passage of approximately three years, he had progressed unfathomably far from where he began.","When he was initially rising through his first Apocalypse, one of his foundational ideals was refusing to remain so weak that he could be existing peacefully in his world or realm when a terrifying power or cataclysm descended without him being aware.","He had rejected the possibility of facing complete collapse without understanding or even knowing what was happening...simply ceasing to exist because forces beyond his comprehension decided his corner of reality was inconvenient.","A sneeze from an Ender, Dikastes, or any others could have turned his entire world to dust.","If his progression had been slightly slower, if he was still confined within a Cosmos or even an Omniverse... the Fallout would occur to systematically wipe out entire Folds and all of Observable Existence outside THE Loom. Including whatever little corner he would have been occupying.","Things would simply cease, and Noah Osmont alongside all those around him would stop existing without even knowing how they perished.","But instead, here he stood approximately three years later.","Not merely surviving, but fucking thriving .","He had begun forging his own Primordial Civilization!","Not as one of many leaders of some grand established framework, but as THE leader of The Primordial Civilizations of Mana and Hunger!","Well, not THE leader quite yet in terms of recognition across existence.","But this perspective alone reminded him that there remained truly tremendous work to be accomplished.","Because even now, he had not escaped the constraints of the Fallout.","Even though his Civilization was Primordial...similar to Order, Origin, Hunger, or any other Collapsed Civilization, and would theoretically be able to persevere through collapse and reconstitute in some form after years or eons...","Similar to how THE Living Order became THE Dead Order , or how Khor returned from near-total dissolution...","But!","The concept of collapse was not something he anticipated experiencing with anything approaching enthusiasm.","His eyes flashed with decisiveness as yes, there was still immense work requiring completion!","After being momentarily sidetracked with introspective thoughts during that span of an instant, he returned his focus to Ambessa who was constantly bearing the immense weight of Hunger Propagation from 2 Million+ Primus Inevitabilities and still maintaining sufficiently calm expression to converse freely.","Entities in the Sextillions of power were utterly monstrous in their resilience.","Noah looked at her as he nodded before stating with casual tone.","\"How is THE Loom , by the way? Since according to your assessment, I and all those around me will face collapse anyway from whatever retaliation comes next...or simply from the Fallout itself, you can share some information about THE Loom , correct?Oh, and you could also indicate where you all concealed the other Vessels of THE Living Paradox...\"","...!"]},{"number":4460,"title":"Chapter 4460: Chapter 4459: Civilization Specialization II","paragraphs":["Ambessa smiled at such a transparent attempt to extract intelligence before she shook her head.","She looked at Noah directly as her response emerged.","\" THE Loom ... is something genuinely unimaginable. You would need to witness it personally to truly comprehend what has been constructed there. Describing it would be like describing color to someone who has never possessed vision...fundamentally inadequate.\"","At such unhelpful words, Noah replied with edge of irritation.","\"It doesn’t appear as though I’m going to fucking witness the inside of THE Loom though, so you might as well elaborate with whatever inadequate description you can provide.\"","Ambessa’s smile widened slightly.","\"Nah. You have to see it yourself. Some experiences cannot be translated through words, only through direct observation!\"","Noah’s crimson visor flashed as he rose upward, his blade rising with him in a gesture stating his patience was exhausting itself.","\"And the Vessels?\" he asked with pointed directness. \"Where are the remaining Vessels of THE Living Paradox that your people secured?\"","Ambessa’s reply was equally unhelpful.","\"Also nah on those. Operational security exists for reasons. But I will offer genuine advice: be extremely careful opposing arguably one of the most powerful existences in... well, all of Existence.\"","\"THE Living Paradox may be somewhat annoyed with you currently. Maybe. But avoid making him entirely angry. Live slightly longer for yourself and those you lead. Be with your bretheren. Your family. Hold them close. Wait for the Fallout instead of being collapsed before it even arrives.\"","Her expression became almost sympathetic:","\"Perhaps THE Creature and his mechanisms will prevail. Even if you and all others face collapse, you may return as Dead Existence rather than permanent cessation.\"","\"Maybe when I and all others emerge from THE Loom years down the timeline, I might encounter you again as diminutive skeleton and recognize you through some residual characteristic. You seem like genuinely cool guy, so I would take care of you then. Ensure you weren’t mistreated by whatever new order emerges.\"","After such unexpectedly considerate words, Noah nodded as the Sword of Mana and Hunger pulsed in his hands with hungry anticipation.","\"What a reality that would be. Let’s earnestly hope that events do not unfold that way.\"","He brought the sword down with deliberate motion as he looked into the radiant stellar eyes of Ambessa...meeting her gaze directly through his crimson visor.","Ambessa smiled as she nodded at him with an expression of no fear!","\"See you in a bit, interesting stranger. Whether as enemy, skeleton, or something unexpected.\"","HUUM !","Noah sank his sword into her chest, the hollow blade piercing through her devastated form with finality.","Her existence collapsed into an Event Horizon of concentrated Hunger as everything about her...her 5 Sextillion power, her accumulated Civilizational Authority of Paradox, her harvest of 5 Grand Principles, her very concept...was systematically consumed!","The harvest from eight Avatars was complete.","And Perpetual Harvest activated with full force to amplify what had been gained.","The moment that Ambessa’s Avatar was collapsed and her entire existence fell under his glorious Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger, everything fell silent in the periphery as... only the gold-green light of harvest began to shine with blinding intensity.","This was because the effort and immensity and harvest of all the Avatars that had been systematically collapsed were being gathered together...culminating at this very moment in single magnificent distribution!","In this silence, Noah felt sense of expectation.","Because the harvest this time was truly grand in ways that exceeded previous accumulations.","The presence from THE Loom ...the beings who had cultivated for eons within that structured domain, who possessed Civilizational Authority of Paradox refined across incomprehensible duration...would there be enough for him to fully complete the initial foundation of his Walls of Civilization?","Would they allow him to shed the designation of Nascent Civilization and advance toward something more substantial?","His armored figure stood gloriously amid the devastated Desiccated Sleeping Shore as prompts began flashing before his crimson visor-covered eyes.","|A quintessential quantity of effort and harvest have been successfully accumulated. The magnitude exceeds all previous collections by substantial margin.|","|The weavings of existence of 8 Members of The Primordial Civilization of Paradox were systematically hungered and devoured by you or other members of your Civilization.|","|These were not mere projections but genuine Avatars carrying substantial portions of their main bodies’ power and authority. Their collapse has yielded unprecedented harvest.|","|All accumulated effort and harvest from this engagement has been consolidated. For the sake of optimal advancement of the entire Civilization, all harvest flows into the Foundation Palisades as priority allocation.|","|Perpetual Harvest amplifies all incoming resources. Multiplier effect in progress...|","...!","The prompts were grand in their implications as Noah closed his eyes and envisioned the manifestation of his Civilization...that conceptual space where the abstract framework of his power took tangible form.","He witnessed the grand manifestation materialize in his existence with perfect clarity.","The towering walls that represented the Foundation Palisades stretched across impossible distances...blue-gold timber-like material that pulsed with concentrated Primus Mana and Hunger.","These walls encircled the entire framework of his manifested Civilization, protecting the structures within from external interference or assault.","At this moment, seas of harvest were flowing into those walls with tremendous force...green-gold light of Perpetual Harvest mixing with the obsidian-blue-crimson of concentrated authority devoured from enemies!","The Foundation Palisades grew larger and more substantial as they absorbed this influx, their height increasing, their thickness expanding, their protective capabilities multiplying.","The harvest was so potent that...","BOOM!","The blue-gold timber walls of the Foundation Palisades began to shine with incandescent light that made them nearly impossible to perceive directly.","They began transforming from the timber-like material toward something that appeared far more permanent, far more imposing.","Something that looked like... stone !","Stone !","Noah observed such transformation as his eyes shone with grand luminosity.","There was only single reason why the fundamental quality of his Walls of Civilization would undergo material transformation from timber to stone...it represented a categorical advancement to entirely new designation!"]},{"number":4461,"title":"Chapter 4461: Chapter 4460: Civilization Specialization III","paragraphs":["Grand prompts descended with weight.","|The harvest accumulated from collapsing 8 Avatars of the Primordial Civilization of Paradox is so immense that the Foundation Palisades have completed their developmental cycle.|","|The grand foundation has been successfully established. Structural integrity confirmed. Defensive parameters exceed all projections.|","|The transformation and elevation toward becoming The Architect’s Bulwarks is commencing. Calculating harvest sufficiency for initial entry into second designation...|","|Calculation complete: Harvest is precisely sufficient for initial entry and stabilization.|","|Advancement confirmed: Foundation Palisades to The Architect’s Bulwarks|","|Your Walls of Civilization advance from timber to stone . From temporary fortification to permanent bastion. From nascent protection to established defense.|","...!","Noah observed this glorious phenomenon with satisfaction.","He witnessed the Walls of his Civilization transforming in real-time...the blue-gold timber shifting, solidifying, reconstituting itself into magnificent stone that appeared both ancient and newly-forged simultaneously.","The Architect’s Bulwarks emerged in their full majesty.","These were not simple walls.","They were monuments of towering stone fortifications that appeared to be carved from single continuous piece of obsidian-blue stone interwoven with golden veins.","The surface was inscribed with countless Primus Mana Arcana Glyphs that pulsed with rhythmic intensity, each one contributing to the overall defensive framework.","The Bulwarks stretched impossibly high...so tall that their tops disappeared into conceptual clouds that represented limits of observable existence.","They were so thick that entire armies of Primus Inevitabilities could march along their tops without crowding!","They radiated authority that suggested anything attempting to breach them would face systematic destruction.","And of course, since the Walls of his Civilization had advanced... all components of his Civilization were concurrently advancing!","Noah observed all the components of his Manifested Civilization becoming larger, more complex, more refined as they absorbed overflow from the concentrated harvest.","His Early Atlas of the Folds expanded dramatically. New regions appeared on its surface, new pathways between locations manifested, the overall detail and accuracy increased exponentially.","The Trees representing his Principles grew substantially taller and more magnificent.","The Cheating Architect’s golden-blue tree sprouted additional branches.","Perpetual Harvest’s green-gold tree deepened its roots. All others also surged up immensly!","His 159 Resplendent Citadels, those towering structures representing accumulated power and authority, pulsed with rhythmic intensity.","Additional prompts materialized with detailed accounting.","|Your personal Complexity and Purity has surged to 1.5 Sextillion baseline. This does not account for combined Complexity and Purity when fused with Protos, which would elevate the total to 2.1 Sextillion.|","|As of this moment, The Architect’s Bulwarks ensure that anything below 3 Sextillion Complexity and Purity cannot harm your existence.|","|The Boon of Minor Mana and Hunger Palisades has undergone categorical transformation.|","|New designation: The Boon of Major Mana and Hunger Bulwark|","|Applicable Recipients: Expanded from 81 to 6,561 Members of your Civilization|","|Granted Power: Each blessed recipient receives .3 Sextillion (300 Quintillion) Complexity and Purity|","|Additional Benefit: All recipients gain full capability to efficiently utilize Civilizational Authority without requiring individual cultivation of such capability|","...!","Noah looked at these glorious prompts.","But the notifications seemed in no way finished, because he could feel his entire existence still buzzing with sense of immensity...as if even more substantial transformations awaited manifestation.","In the next moment, the sensation intensified dramatically as reality around him seemed to acknowledge what was occurring within his conceptual Civilization space.","New prompts descended with weight that made surrounding existence tremble.","|Your Civilization has taken major step forward, no longer bearing the designation of Nascent Civilization.|","|Through systematic accumulation of power, through conquest of enemies possessing genuine Civilizational Authority, through establishment of a permanent defensive framework, through cultivation of specialized forces and diverse capabilities...|","|The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger has advanced to attain the designation of:|","| THE CATHEDRAL OF ORDER|","|Second Designation achieved. Civilizational identity solidified.|","...!","The Cathedral of Order!","The name resonated through Noah’s existence with profound significance.","The different structures of his Manifested Civilization grew dramatically at this moment in response to achieving this milestone.","His Early Atlas of the Folds seemed to become even larger and more impossibly detailed.","The Trees representing his Principles grew substantially taller, their canopies expanding until they provided shade across vast portions of his manifested Civilization!","The roots deepened until they touched the very foundation of The Architect’s Bulwarks themselves, creating symbiotic relationship between defensive structure and power-generation of the Principles!","And his 159 Resplendent Citadels pulsed with rhythmic intensity of change and transformation!","Prompts bloomed immediately afterward detailing the full scope of transformation.","|Your 5 Principles shine ever brighter with accumulated power and refined authority.|","|Enhancement confirmed: 300 Primus Mana Glyphs of each Principle can now be forged (increased from previous maximum of 200)|","|Each Glyph now contributes .5 Quintillion Complexity and Purity to your existence|","|Total potential contribution from all Principles at maximum Glyph capacity: 750 Quintillion(.75 Sextillion) Complexity and Purity|","|Alongside the substantial growth of your Principles, your Resplendent Citadels have completed the 4th Stage of development and are now advancing into the 5th Stage.|","|New designation: The Resplendent Citadels transform into THE SOVEREIGN SPIRES OF OSMONT|","| The Sovereign Spires represent the refined authority of your Existence, each one now capable of independently manifesting Civilizational Authority in specific domains.|","|The light of all Principles, guided systematically by Cheating Architect and amplified by Perpetual Harvest, reinforces a glorious newly manifesting feature emerging from the 5th Stage of The Sovereign Spires of Osmont|","|This feature outlines the core distinctive capability of The Second Designation of The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger, The Cathedral of Order.|","|Core Feature Designation: CIVILIZATION SPECIALIZATION|","|An immense quantity of harvest and accumulated effort from all different components of your Civilization flows systematically into the formation and structural design of the Civilization Feature of Civilization Specialization.|","|This represents categorical advancement in organizational sophistication. Your Civilization evolves from monolithic force into multifaceted wonder.|","|Estimated completion of Civilization Specialization framework: Imminent|","...!","Noah’s mind buzzed as he processed these extraordinary prompts.","The Cathedral of Order . The designation felt appropriate!","The Sovereign Spires of Osmont . His Citadels had evolved into something bearing his name gloriously.","And most intriguingly...","Civilization Specialization.","He contemplated this new core feature with analytical focus.","The prompts suggested it represented fundamental transformation in how his Civilization operated!","But the specifics remained unclear. What exactly would this Civilization Specialization entail?","His mind raced with possibilities!"]},{"number":4462,"title":"Chapter 4462: Chapter 4461: Civilization Specialization IV","paragraphs":["Specialization.","Some believed it meant limitation...surrendering the versatility of being capable in many areas to achieve excellence in one narrow domain.","These individuals viewed specialization as sacrificing potential breadth for depth, trading adaptability for focused capability.","Others believed it meant optimization, recognizing that attempting to master everything resulted in mastering nothing.","And that strategic allocation of resources toward specific functions produced superior results than diffuse distribution across all possibilities.","But in the scope of a Civilization, a true Civilization...specialization meant something far more profound.","It meant evolution .","It meant recognizing that a Civilization was not merely collection of powerful individuals, but an organism composed of differentiated cells, each performing distinct functions that contributed to the health and capability of the whole.","A body did not require every cell to be capable of everything .","The heart did not need to perform photosynthesis. The brain did not need to digest food. The liver did not need to pump blood.","Each organ, each system, each specialized component contributed its unique function...and through that contribution, the organism achieved capabilities that exceeded what any individual cell could accomplish regardless of its individual power.","Specialization, properly understood, was not limitation.","It was glory , it was majesty !","---","In a distant time.","In the Earliest Folds.","There existed a moment when a unique entity met another unique entity and they discussed The Ways of Existence while standing in frozen landscape that seemed to exist outside normal temporal flow.","One anomaly had said farewell to another before he took a single step and disappeared , traversing impossible distances through sheer force of his cultivated Way!","This anomaly was none other than Anaximander as his next step carried him countless territories distant.","He found himself floating in region surrounded by millions of floating Primordial Wheels of Existence, each one representing concentrated authority.","This brilliant Fold Dweller was particularly introspective at this time as he contemplated all the subjects he had discussed with Osmont during their unexpected meeting.","How Osmont had cautioned him regarding any entities possessing the distinction of THE .","Anaximander owed substantial debt to THE Weavers for what they had done to allow him to take that transformative step and embark upon his Way.","He was naturally curious by disposition as he wanted to understand more than he feared the unknown.","His mind brightened with audacity as he asked himself...","What if I simply tear apart the veil of mystery by directly meeting THE entities? Perhaps those encounters would prove as fruitful as the conversation with Osmont?","Across his existence, Anaximander had observed that countless beings feared what they did not comprehend.","The masses in his original world, no matter how many technological advances he and fellow scientists produced, inevitably feared what remained beyond their understanding.","He reasoned that if he could simply understand THE entities more directly, the veil of mystery would be systematically torn away, and genuine comprehension would become possible.","After all, he sought understanding with intensity that exceeded his desire for safety or comfort!","So his eyes brightened with characteristic determination as he spoke aloud to existence itself.","\"When I take this next step, I will arrive before... the most powerful THE existence in these Folds...\"","HUUM!","His Existence was grand. His Way grander.","So he took that step... and disappeared from that space entirely.","When he reappeared, he found himself observing scene that defied his understanding.","He manifested on golden sands of an unfathomably vast shore that stretched toward horizons that seemed to extend infinitely in all directions.","Anaximander blinked repeatedly at the scope of wonder surrounding him as his mind attempted to categorize what he perceived.","There existed massive trees that seemed to bear fruits composed of nurtured Principles.","Plots of cultivated land where Primordial Folds and Transcendent Folds were being grown like crops.","Massive structures of immense mystery and architectural wonder that suggested purposes beyond his current comprehension.","But at this moment, what drew his attention most prominently was an entity who appeared to be struggling to erect a tilted wall across one particularly vast plot of land.","Anaximander observed with growing curiosity as this figure pushed against the wall with visible effort, attempting to position it vertically rather than at its current severe angle.","The moment Anaximander fully manifested, this entity turned to regard him with expression of genuine surprise...gazing at the unexpected visitor with an analytical assessment while Anaximander performed an identical evaluation.","The entity appeared humanoid in general configuration but radiated authority that made surrounding existence acknowledge his presence.","His features were difficult to focus upon directly, as if his fundamental nature resisted simple observation.","Observing that this being required assistance with his construction project, Anaximander moved forward with directness.","\"I apologize for this intrusion. I was seeking the most powerful THE existence across these Folds, and my Way delivered me here specifically. Are you the entity I sought? Do you need...help?\"","...!","With these straightforward words, Anaximander positioned himself on one side of the tilted wall that this entity was attempting to erect properly.","He placed his hands against its surface to help stabilize and lift...","And for the first time since he began embarking upon his Way, he felt like he was holding something genuinely heavy .","Not heavy in simple physical sense, but heavy in existential sense!","The wall itself appeared deceptively simple upon initial observation.","Clean wooden construction without elaborate ornamentation.","But when Anaximander examined it more carefully with his analytical perception, he noticed extraordinary details.","One side of the wall bore vibrant fruits filled with pulsing life-force...entities that radiated vitality and growth and continuation.","The opposite side held fruits that seemed...dead, yet paradoxically shone with their own distinct vibrancy.","Not lifeless in sense of absence, but bearing a different quality of existence that was equally valid and complex.","As he studied this peculiar construction and what it separated with growing fascination, the entity who had been working on erecting this wall looked toward him and smiled with an expression of amusement.","\"Why are you seeking THE entities so deliberately? There exists substantial danger if you encounter the wrong one. Not all of us are benevolent, and some possess... questionable ethics regarding how we interact with other beings.\"","Anaximander continued looking at the wall with intense interest...noting how it defied conventional physical properties. He replied while studying it with scientific fascination.","\"I met a friend recently. Perhaps I can legitimately call him that despite brief acquaintance. He advised me to exercise some caution regarding THE existences.\"","His expression brightened with enthusiasm.","\"But for good or bad, I am fundamentally a learner of existence and student of reality by core nature. My curiosity overwhelmed my caution, and I decided I wanted to stand before the most powerful THE specifically to understand that which I currently do not comprehend. Fear born from ignorance seems philosophically inferior to knowledge acquired through calculated risk.\"","...!"]},{"number":4463,"title":"Chapter 4463: Chapter 4462: Civilization Specialization V","paragraphs":["His earnest words caused the distant being holding the opposite end of this heavy wall to smile with genuine warmth as he nodded.","\" Well... what specifically do you want to know?\"","Anaximander , now thoroughly engrossed with the mysteriously heavy wall he was supporting, replied with immediate focus.","\"At this precise moment, I am intensely interested in what exactly you are accomplishing here. What is this wall fundamentally? And why does it possess such extraordinary existential weight that I can barely maintain my position?\"","At such direct inquiry, the entity on the opposite end released an audible sigh as his response emerged with melancholy and determination.","\"I also have a... friend. We can call her that, though our relationship is complex. She was unfairly collapsed some time ago through circumstances beyond her control, and I’ve been systematically attempting to help her and others like her who faced similar collapse.\"","His expression grew distant.","\"Their fundamental nature and specialization is inherently dead ...bearing authority over cessation and endings rather than beginnings and growth. There exist substantial complications when their collapsed weavings interact with the weavings of the living.\"","He gestured toward the wall they were collectively supporting.","\"I am attempting to erect a wall, a Veil, around their domains to provide protection and separation. A Veil that would also act as protection because some rather unpleasant things seem to be in play. So I thought of a Veil.\"","\" A veil so they can maintain semblance of peace and stability after everything that has occurred to them. I have accomplished everything within my capability thus far, but this final section seems extraordinarily heavy. Unless I am actively supporting it, this wall continues tilting dangerously.\"","His tone carried self-awareness.","\" Perhaps it is because I am executing too many simultaneous projects at this moment. Perhaps I need to attempt this construction during period when I can dedicate complete focus rather than divided attention across countless responsibilities.\"","...!","Anaximander’s eyes illuminated with intellectual excitement at such explanation.","He looked at this tilted wall with renewed understanding and spoke.","\"Can I attempt to help? My Way may be of use.\"","...!","The entity regarded him calmly for extended moment. Finally he nodded.","\" You can attempt this, but exercise extreme care. The weight of this wall is not merely physical. You will be supporting the boundary between life and death, between continuation and cessation, between what is and what was.\"","At such solemn warning, the glorious scene that unfolded in the next moment would have profound implications.","Anaximander breathed out slowly...centering himself, focusing his cultivated Way entirely upon this singular task.","He began applying systematic pressure on the tilted wall while simultaneously instructing his existence with logical precision.","This is just a wall. A boundary requiring proper positioning. With both of us applying coordinated force, it simply needs to cease being tilted and stand vertically as intended. Simple physics combined with existential authority. Calculate optimal force vectors. Apply pressure systematically. Achieve result.","...!","His existence buzzed with intensity as it received these guidelines and directives...his Way manifesting tangibly as he applied the conviction that this wall should stand straight.","And shockingly, the heavy tilted wall actually began to shift!","HUUM !","When the humanoid entity on the opposite side observed this unexpected movement, his expression transformed to genuine surprise and wonder.","He immediately applied his own substantial power to the wall as they pushed together with synchronized effort...","HUUUM !","An immense eruption of concentrated complexity exploded outward at that moment as the entire expanse of the vast and intricate shore trembled beneath the weight of what they were accomplishing!","The body of the entity on the opposite end pulsed with seas of endless Primordial Civilizational Authority as torrents of concentrated power flowed into the wall’s structure.","Meanwhile Anaximander felt like he was executing task that entirely contradicted his fundamental nature, pushing against a really heavy wall when he was never the athletic or strong type.","And yet he continued exerting maximum effort to straighten this simple wall.","And shockingly, after duration that felt simultaneously instantaneous and eons...","BOOM !","The tilted wall was no longer tilted. It stood straight and strong and permanent, properly positioned as intended!","The moment it achieved perfect vertical alignment, brilliant incandescent light erupted from the top of this wall and stretched upward endlessly...piercing through dimensional boundaries, extending across territorial divisions, creating visible demarcation that would persist across eons.","Anaximander observed such marvelous phenomenon as he stumbled backward with exhaustion that exceeded anything he had experienced before.","He felt profound sense of weakness pervading his entire existence, but the accomplishment of straightening that significant wall made him smile and laugh with genuine satisfaction despite his depleted state.","While expressing such triumph, his body began swaying dangerously as if about to collapse entirely.","The entity who had been working on the opposite end of the wall appeared beside him instantaneously to provide stabilizing support, preventing his fall with gentle but firm assistance.","Anaximander breathed heavily as he steadied himself with visible effort.","\"I never anticipated manual labor would cause such profound exertion. I haven’t experienced genuine fatigue like this since I first embarked upon my Way. But ah, no matter, totally worth the experience.\"","...!","He straightened with effort and extended a conceptual hand.","\"I am Anaximander . A Fold Dweller by current classification, a scientist by training and disposition, and a dreamer who wishes to learn everything existence can teach. Who are you, exactly?\"","Anaximander articulated such direct question as the being who was helping him maintain stability shook his head with warm smile.","\"I am THE Creature.\"","...!","Anaximander blinked repeatedly at such casual revelation as his processing caught up with implication.","\" THE ? All capital letters? So I successfully located the precise entity I sought to understand? You don’t trigger any alarm bells in my mind though...\"","He contemplated Osmont’s stern warnings to exercise caution against THE beings.","This particular one seemed remarkably approachable, and when THE Creature had helped stabilize him, Anaximander had felt immense infusion of surrounding existence’s concentrated life-force flowing into his depleted framework to accelerate recovery.","As if THE Creature could perceive the questioning evaluation occurring behind Anaximander’s expression, he nodded while providing clarification.","\" THE- all capital, exactly as you understood. And your friend demonstrated wisdom advising caution regarding THE entities. Some of us can be... profoundly selfish, manipulative even, pursuing agendas that disregard consequences for other beings.\"","His expression brightened with genuine curiosity.","\" Who is this friend of yours who provided such counsel? Are they as remarkable as you are? I would appreciate opportunity to meet them as well, it’s rare to encounter beings and anomalies like you.\"","At such inquiry, Anaximander shook his head with an apologetic expression.","\" I made an explicit promise not to reveal their identity. They expressed substantial discomfort regarding THE entities and requested anonymity. I respect that boundary despite my natural inclination toward sharing information freely.\"","THE Creature nodded with understanding.","\" What a shame. Anyone you would designate as friend would undoubtedly prove exceptional to meet directly. But no matter, come.\"","He gestured expansively toward the vast shore.","\" Since I have unexpected guest, and you even provided crucial assistance establishing The Veil properly, let me treat you with appropriate hospitality. You expressed desire to understand Existence more completely? I may possess capability to provide...some answers.\"","THE Creature helped Anaximander steady himself completely before leading this extraordinary being deeper into the vast and seemingly endless shore.","It was a meeting that none across observable history knew occurred.","A meeting that none would believe possible even if informed directly.","But existence was grand beyond comprehension.","And the possibilities were genuinely endless!","---","Meanwhile, in the present...","On a nearly collapsed Desiccated Sleeping Shore...","Noah stood processing the implications of what \"Civilization Specialization\" might represent for his framework as a moment later...prompts began to descend!"]},{"number":4464,"title":"Chapter 4464: Chapter 4463: Civilization Specialization VI","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes pulsed with immensity as he observed the formation of the Sovereign Spires of Osmont while prompts descended to explain exactly what Civilization Specialization represented.","The prompts materialized alongside radiant illusory holographic displays of the Sovereign Spires...towering structures that appeared simultaneously within his manifested Civilization and as conceptual diagrams floating before his vision.","|The Civilization Specialization System represents evolutionary refinement of The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger’s membership structure.|","|This system allows for the diversification of roles and capabilities among Members, transforming your Civilization from monolithic force into sophisticated organism with differentiated functions.|","|Through the Sovereign Spires of Osmont, Members of your Civilization can voluntarily transform their existence into specialized path that provides substantial benefits to both individual and collective framework.|","|Current Available Specializations:|","|— The Infinite Bulwark Specialization|","|— The Hungering Maw Specialization|","|— The Vital Chorus Specialization|","|Additional Specializations Currently Under Development:|","|— The Architects of Infinity Specialization: 17% completion|","|— The Sovereign Heralds Specialization: 13% completion|","|Access to additional Specializations will unlock as your Civilization advances and as harvest continues flowing into the Sovereign Spires of Osmont.|","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed as he processed these prompts.","So the Civilization evolves from everyone possessing similar capabilities toward specialized roles with distinct functions.","Three Specializations currently available, two more under development. ..","In the next moment, he observed one of the massive Sovereign Spires of Osmont within his Manifested Civilization rise up prominently and be displayed before him with enhanced clarity...as if the entire conceptual structure was being pulled forward for a detailed examination.","The Spire was magnificent in its architectural expression. A towering structure composed of layered obsidian-gold crystalline formations that suggested absolute solidity and permanence.","The surface was inscribed with countless defensive Arcana Glyphs that pulsed with rhythmic intensity.","Above it, floating labels materialized with clear identification.","SOVEREIGN SPIRE OF OSMONT - THE IRON CONCORDAT","The blue-gold holographic figure of RUIN/EDEN appeared beside the displayed Spire, her form coalescing from scattered light into coherent representation.","She bowed gracefully toward Noah with expression mixing professionalism with barely suppressed excitement...as if she had been waiting eagerly to present this new capability.","Her voice emerged with precision, though underlying enthusiasm colored her typical analytical tone.","\"Master, allow me to present the first available Civilization Specialization... The Infinite Bulwark Specialization. This path can be obtained when any Member of your Civilization, with the sole exception of yourself, enters a Sovereign Spire of Osmont bearing the distinction of The Iron Concordat and consciously chooses to undergo the transformation.\"","As she articulated this introduction, the obsidian-gold coloration of the Spire intensified...the defensive architectural structure becoming more pronounced as if physically responding to being discussed.","RUIN/EDEN began explaining the Specialization through systematically presented prompts!","| THE INFINITE BULWARK SPECIALIZATION|","|Faction Declaration: \" We are the wall upon which existence breaks. We do not fall. We cannot fall.\"|","|Primary Focus: Absolute Defense and Endurance|","|This Specialization represents commitment to protection above all other considerations. Members who choose this path sacrifice offensive capability entirely in exchange for defensive power that transcends conventional limitations.|","An illusory figure manifested beside RUINEDEN...showing how a humanoid figure who chose this Specialization would appear after transformation.","The figure was massive, imposing, covered in layered crystalline plates of obsidian-gold that seemed to absorb light rather than reflecting it.","The entity moved with deliberate slowness, but each step radiated absolute certainty and caused minor stabilization effects in surrounding reality.","Additional prompts continued with detailed specifications.","|CORE TRANSFORMATION PARAMETERS:|","|Total Offensive Sacrifice: Members of this Specialization lose 100% of their offensive capabilities. They cannot deal direct damage through any conventional or unconventional means. All attacks, abilities, and techniques designed to harm enemies are systematically removed from their framework. Any attacks towards Members of The Civilization are automatically drawn to them.|","|Multiplicative Defensive Gain: In exchange for complete offensive sacrifice, their Complexity and Purity is multiplied by 15x for all defensive calculations . This multiplication applies to Durability, Resistances to Living Existential Authority, Principles, and Civilizational Authority, and all other protective measurements.|","|Immovable Presence: Cannot be forcefully moved, teleported, displaced, or otherwise repositioned without explicit consent. Their existence becomes anchored to their chosen location through fundamental authority that resists manipulation.|","...!","The illusory Bulwark figure demonstrated these capabilities...absorbing devastating attacks without visible damage, remaining perfectly stationary despite tremendous force being applied, radiating defensive authority that created visible protective fields around nearby allies!","|UNIQUE CAPABILITIES:|","|Civilization Fortress Formation: Multiple Bulwarks can merge their individual defensive fields to create unified impenetrable barriers protecting designated allies. The more Bulwarks participate in formation, the stronger the collective barrier becomes, scaling exponentially rather than linearly.|","The visualization showed three Bulwarks combining their defenses...their individual protective fields merging into single cohesive barrier that appeared capable of withstanding apocalyptic assault.","|Damage Conversion: All damage absorbed by Bulwark can be systematically stored within their framework and subsequently channeled to the offensive specialists within the Civilization. Nothing is wasted...every attack they endure becomes fuel for allied counter-assault.|","The illusory figure absorbed barrage of attacks, and visible energy accumulated within its form before being transferred through golden conduits toward offensive-oriented allies who held different Specializations!","|Existential Anchoring: Their presence stabilizes reality itself within substantial radius. Prevents spatial tears, dimensional collapse, reality manipulation, or existential alteration within their vicinity. The more powerful the Bulwark, the larger the stabilization radius.|","The visualization demonstrated reality becoming more solid around the Bulwark...attempts to tear space, manipulate dimensions, or alter fundamental principles simply failing within the stabilized zone!","|Regenerative Resonance: Healing effects directed toward Bulwarks are amplified by 500%. Their defensive specialization creates synergistic relationship with restorative capabilities, allowing healer Specializations to restore them far more efficiently.|","|Armored forms appear as living fortresses, massive entities covered in layered crystalline plates of obsidian-gold that shift and reconfigure to optimize defensive coverage.|","|Movement is deliberate and unhurried, but conveys absolute certainty.|","|Eyes glow with steady, unwavering silver light that suggests immutable commitment to their protective purpose.|","|IDEAL CANDIDATES: Those who value protection above personal glory or offensive capability.|","|Beings who have experienced devastating loss and refuse to allow such loss to occur again.|","|Entities with naturally defensive psychological dispositions who find fulfillment in shielding others rather than destroying enemies.|","|Members who understand that sometimes the greatest strength lies not in capacity to harm, but in capacity to endure.|","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed with tyranny as he absorbed the comprehensive presentation of this first Civilization Specialization!","He ignored everything else and focused on a number.","15x .","15 !","Did this mean, truly, 15x the Complexity and Purity of any members who chose this defensive Specialization? 100 Quintillion to 1,500 Quintillion(1.5 Sextillion)?","Truly?!"]},{"number":4465,"title":"Chapter 4465: Chapter 4464: Civilization Specialization VII","paragraphs":["The idea of it alone was ridiculous as thid type of power truly benefitted his overal Civilization as it would mean...any Primus Inevitabilities with a base of 100 Quintillion Complexity and Purity could become a bastion of defense.","If he chose just 20 Million of the 100 Million Primus Inevitabilities to go through The Iron Concordat Sovereign Spire...that would be 20 Million Entities with...1.5 Sextillion Complexity and Purity.","\"...\"","One needed to take a second to process this.","And then another second!","Because oh!","His eyes gleamed with appreciation for the sophisticated design as he contemplated potential applications.","As he continued staring at the illusory diagram of the Infinite Bulwark form, additional prompts materialized with crucial clarification.","|The stated 15x Complexity and Purity multiplier for defensive calculations represents baseline enhancement for standard Members choosing this Specialization.|","|However, the actual multiplicative effect can be substantially higher depending on the Civilization Specialization Potential possessed by an individual Member.|","|Higher Potential Ranks receive proportionally greater benefits from Specialization transformation, creating dramatic power differentials between Members of identical base power but different Potential classifications.|","Noah’s attention sharpened at this revelation.","Potential!","Potential determineed how much benefit they extract from Specialization!","It meant that not everyone who becomes an Infinite Bulwark achieves identical results.","In the next moment, an illusory diagram of Riya materialized before him...her familiar form rendered in blue-gold holographic light with exceptional detail.","From this diagram, countless lines of information extended outward like branches, each one providing specific data about her capabilities and characteristics.","But most prominently, directly above her rendered form, glowing text displayed...","|Civilization Specialization Potential: Sovereign Potential(Legendary 3rd Seal)|","Noah’s eyes widened fractionally at seeing this concrete measurement of Riya’s inherent capacity.","Additional prompts manifested to explain!","|CIVILIZATION SPECIALIZATION POTENTIAL SYSTEM|","|Every being within your Civilization possesses innate Civilization Potential Rank that determines their capacity for Specialization advancement, their speed of progression, and the magnitude of benefits they receive from choosing Specialization path.|","|This Potential is not arbitrary, it reflects fundamental characteristics of their existence, their connection to the Civilization’s core principles, and their capacity for transformation and growth.|","|POTENTIAL RANK CLASSIFICATIONS:|","The prompts organized themselves into hierarchical structure as RUIN/EDEN provided a comprehensive explanation.","|RANK 1: UNDEFINED (Unique - Noah Osmont Only )|","|This classification is possessed solely by The Primordial Sovereign, the foundational existence around which the entire Civilization is constructed.|","|Capabilities:|","|— Can perceive, analyze, and systematically evaluate the Civilization Potential of all Members with perfect accuracy|","|— Can forcefully elevate the Civilization Potential of any Member through investment of accumulated Harvest|","|— Can create entirely new Specialization Paths by combining existing frameworks or manifesting novel configurations|","|— Not bound by limitations of any single Specialization, already embodies all paths simultaneously without requiring conscious selection|","|You are the architect. All others are components of your design.|","Noah nodded slowly at this confirmation of his unique position.","|RANK 2: PRIMORDIAL POTENTIAL ( Mythic - 1st Seal through 9th Seal)|","|Extraordinarily rare classification possessed by entities fundamentally woven into the Civilization’s genesis, beings whose existence is inseparable from the Civilization’s foundational principles.|","|Capabilities:|","|— Can master multiple non-competing Specializations simultaneously (maximum: 3)|","|— Advancement speed multiplied by 50x compared to baseline|","|— Can evolve their chosen Specializations into unique personal variants that reflect their individual nature|","|— Natural affinity for Civilizational Authority makes all Specialization abilities substantially more potent|","|Current Members with Primordial Potential: Khor (The First Hunger), Sigrid(The Living Order)|","Noah’s mind immediately catalogued this information.","Khor and Sigrid both qualified as Primordial Potential. It made sense...they were fundamentally connected to Hunger and Order itself.","|RANK 3: SOVEREIGN POTENTIAL (Legendary - 1st Seal through 9th Seal)|","|Rare classification possessed by exceptional individuals who demonstrate remarkable affinity for the Civilization’s principles despite not being foundational components.|","|Capabilities:|","|— Can master two non-competing Specializations simultaneously|","|— Advancement speed multiplied by 20x compared to baseline|","|— Capable of teaching their Specialization to lower-ranked Members, accelerating collective growth|","|— Develop leadership capabilities naturally, often capable of becoming commanders within their Specialization|","|Current Members with Sovereign Potential: Protos (The First Primus Inevitability), Barbatos, Riya, Henry|","Noah evaluated each name.","All were exceptional in their own ways!","|RANK 4: EXALTED POTENTIAL (Epic - 1st Seal through 9th Seal)|","|Uncommon classification possessed by talented Members who show exceptional affinity for specific aspects of the Civilization.|","|Capabilities:|","|— Masters one Specialization with extraordinary depth|","|— Advancement speed multiplied by 10x compared to baseline|","|— Can develop unique techniques and variations within their chosen Specialization|","|Estimated Members with Exalted Potential: 847 current Members|","|RANK 5: ASCENDANT POTENTIAL (Rare - 1st Seal through 9th Seal)|","|Common among capable Members who possess solid foundation and genuine commitment to Civilization.|","|Capabilities:|","|— Masters one Specialization effectively|","|— Advancement speed multiplied by 5x compared to baseline|","|— Standard but reliable progression along chosen path|","|— Form backbone of Specialization factions through consistent competence|","|Estimated Members with Ascendant Potential: 4 Million+ current Members|","|RANK 6: INITIATED POTENTIAL (Common)|","|Baseline rank for most Members who join the Civilization.|","|Capabilities:|","|— Can pursue one Specialization|","|— Standard advancement speed|","|— Requires substantial resource investment for meaningful progression|","|— Can be elevated to higher Potential through Master’s intervention and Harvest investment|","|Estimated Members with Initiated Potential: Majority of current Civilization membership|","...!","After Noah absorbed the complete framework of Civilization Specialization Potential, his eyes shone with brilliant intensity as he contemplated everything.","He could see everyone’s Potential. And more importantly, he could elevate that Potential through Harvest investment!","His mind raced through tactical calculations.","He smiled with tyrannical satisfaction as the potential wonder to bloom from all of this was simply...","Catastrophic. Absolutely catastrophic levels of power become possible!","WAA !","And so far, he had only examined one Civilization Specialization in detail.","There remained two other currently available Specializations that he could guide Members toward...The Hungering Maw and The Vital Chorus.","One could already decipher what they would be geared towards if the first Civilization Specialization was defensive.","Each would offer distinct capabilities. Each would create different opportunities.","His Civilization was evolving beyond simple accumulation of powerful individuals and was becoming a true organism...differentiated, specialized, optimized.","And he controlled every aspect of that evolution!"]},{"number":4466,"title":"Chapter 4466: Chapter 4465: Immense! I","paragraphs":["After obtaining a comprehensive understanding of the first Specialization and the Potential system that governed it, Noah issued his command for overview of the remaining two Civilization Specializations to be presented.","The prompts materialized with systematic precision.","| THE HUNGERING MAW SPECIALIZATION|","|Faction Designation: THE CRIMSON HUNGER|","|Faction Declaration: \"We hunger. We devour. We grow without end.\"|","|Primary Focus: Pure Offensive Power and Systematic Consumption|","|This Specialization represents commitment to destruction and growth through violence. Members who choose this path sacrifice defensive capability substantially in exchange for offensive power that transcends limitations.|","|CORE TRANSFORMATION PARAMETERS:|","|Defensive Sacrifice: Members lose 80% of their defensive capabilities. They become fragile glass cannons, extraordinarily vulnerable to counterattack but devastatingly lethal when unmolested.|","|Multiplicative Offensive Gain: Their offensive Complexity and Purity is multiplied by 15x for all damage calculations, attack potency, and destructive capability measurements.|","|Consumption Acceleration: Everything they destroy is immediately and automatically converted to personal power with 100% efficiency. No energy is wasted, all defeated enemies become fuel for continued growth.|","|UNIQUE CAPABILITIES:|","|Reality Severance: Their attacks ignore conventional defenses by directly attacking the fundamental existence of targets rather than merely their physical or energetic manifestations. Armor, barriers, and protective techniques prove substantially less effective against Reality Severance strikes.|","|Exponential Hunger Stacks: Each successful kill increases their overall power by 10%. This enhancement stacks indefinitely during combat engagement, creating snowball effect where early kills make subsequent kills easier, which generate more kills, which compound power further.|","|Predatory Instinct: Can perceive and automatically identify the weakest point in any defense, existence, Principles, or protective weavings. This sense guides their attacks toward maximum effectiveness with minimal conscious effort.|","|Feast of Conquest: Can temporarily consume and actively wield defeated enemies’ signature abilities, techniques, and powers. Duration scales with power differential, weaker enemies provide brief access, comparable enemies provide extended usage.|","|They are sleek, predatory lifeforms covered in crimson-obsidian tentacles that constantly writhe with barely contained aggressive intent.|","|Multiple serrated maws visible across their bodies, appearing on shoulders, chest, limbs...each one releasing wisps of concentrated Hunger that distorts surrounding space.|","|Eyes burn with ravenous red light that intensifies with each kill. After extended combat, their eyes become nearly blinding crimson beacons radiating accumulated bloodlust.|","|IDEAL CANDIDATES:|","|Those with naturally aggressive psychological dispositions who find fulfillment in destruction rather than creation.|","|Beings who have lost everything and channel emotion into systematic vengeance against those responsible or against existence itself.|","|Entities naturally inclined toward violence who would struggle with defensive or supportive roles but excel when permitted to pursue offense without restraint.|","Noah gave a light nod to the overview of The Hungering Maw Specialization as there wasn’t much to say about it apart from it being just as astonishing as The Infinite Bulwark!","So he simply read the rest.","| THE VITAL CHORUS SPECIALIZATION|","|Faction Designation: THE VERDANT CYCLE|","| Faction Declaration: \"Life persists through us. Death is merely temporary setback.\"|","|Primary Focus: Healing, Support, and Systematic Resurrection|","|This Specialization represents commitment to preservation and continuation of existence. Members who choose this path sacrifice offensive capability almost entirely in exchange for restorative power that makes their allies extraordinarily difficult to permanently eliminate.|","|CORE TRANSFORMATION PARAMETERS:|","|Offensive Sacrifice: Members lose 90% of their offensive capabilities. They become almost entirely incapable of dealing direct damage, though they retain capacity for self-defense through indirect means.|","|Support Amplification: All healing effects, buffing techniques, protective barriers, and supportive abilities weaved into complexity and purity are multiplied by 15x in potency and efficiency.|","|Life-Binding: Can establish permanent soul-bonds with other Civilization Members. If bonded ally faces collapse, they can be instantly resurrected as long as the Vital Chorus Member who holds their bond survives. This creates symbiotic relationship where protecting the healer ensures limited immortality for bonded warriors.|","|UNIQUE CAPABILITIES:|","|Resurrection Acceleration: Can dramatically reduce the standard 24-hour rebirth time for collapsed Primus Inevitabilities and other Civilization Members to mere minutes through concentrated application of restorative authority.|","|Overflow Vitality: Healing that exceeds target’s maximum capacity doesn’t dissipate wastefully. Instead, excess healing energy converts into temporary protective shield that absorbs damage until depleted.|","|Symphonic Restoration: Healing multiple targets simultaneously creates harmonic resonance between healing effects. Each additional target amplifies overall potency exponentially rather than dividing attention...healing five allies proves far more than five times as effective as healing one.|","|Death Defiance Aura: Allies within substantial radius of Vital Chorus Member cannot be instantly killed regardless of attack potency. They will always survive with minimum 1% existence remaining, providing opportunity for healing to restore them before subsequent attacks finish elimination.|","|This specialization holds radiant forms perpetually wreathed in green-gold-blue light that pulses rhythmically like heartbeat. The luminescence intensifies during active healing, becoming nearly blinding when restoring critically injured allies.|","|Bodies covered in intricate mandala-like patterns that glow with increasing brightness when channeling restorative power. These patterns shift and reconfigure based on healing technique being employed.|","|Eyes shine with compassionate emerald light. Many develop visible halos or aureolas of concentrated life-force that mark them as preservers rather than destroyers.|","|IDEAL CANDIDATES:|","|Those who have witnessed excessive death and refuse to permit further loss if prevention remains within their capability.|","|Natural healers who find psychological fulfillment in preservation and restoration rather than destruction and conquest.|","|Beings who understand that sometimes the greatest contribution to victory involves ensuring allies survive rather than personally eliminating enemies.|","Noah’s eyes pulsed with tyrannical satisfaction as he absorbed both Specializations completely.","Three Civilization Specializations. Three distinct factions with complementary capabilities.","The Iron Concordat provides unkillable anchors who stabilize reality and absorb attacks.","The Crimson Hunger delivers overwhelming offensive power that snowballs through combat.","The Verdant Cycle ensures casualties remain temporary and allies maintain peak condition.","Together, they create a synergy that exceeds simple sum of individual capabilities. This...is what true Civilization architecture looks like....","After reviewing these comprehensive prompts, Noah nodded with an expression of absolute command and spoke with decisive authority.","\"Get the Sovereign Spires of Osmont prepared. Manifest ten Spires bearing the distinction of The Iron Concordat, ten representing The Crimson Hunger, and ten embodying The Verdant Cycle. Distribute them across the Early Veiled Shore and Infiniverse to ensure accessibility for all Members.\"","The response came as single word pulsing with acknowledgment.","|Understood.|","Noah opened his eyes fully, returning his awareness from the conceptual space of his Manifested Civilization to the physical reality of the Desiccated Sleeping Shore.","He looked at everything surrounding him with calculating assessment.","The devastated landscape. The orbiting Primus Inevitabilities.","The few remaining structures that hadn’t been obliterated during the battle.","He raised his armored fist high in gesture of victory...silent acknowledgment of what had been accomplished.","In the surroundings, all the Primus Inevitabilities mirrored his motion, raising their own fists in synchronized salute.","HUUM!","The gesture carried no vocal component, but the meaning was unmistakable: We have triumphed!"]},{"number":4467,"title":"Chapter 4467: Chapter 4466: Immense! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s words emerged with commanding finality.","\"Only a single Vessel of THE Living Paradox has been collapsed. The Avatars have secured and concealed the others, distributed them across existence to prevent easy acquisition. Find them. Hunt them. Collapse them one by one until none remain.\"","His crimson visor swept across the assembled forces.","\"Meanwhile, I shall summon you sequentially to undergo Civilization Specialization over the next day. When you return to combat, you will return transformed...optimized for specific functions that will make our Civilization exponentially more formidable.\"","The Primus Inevitabilities accepted the order without hesitation, their formations breaking as they dispersed in coordinated groups.","Thousands streaked away in different directions, beginning systematic search across the Folds for remaining Vessels!","Noah looked at those still present...entities fused with Civilizational Armor who would return with him rather than continuing the hunt. Riya, Henry, Sigrid, Protos in his separated form, and numerous others.","His command was simple.","\"Let us depart.\"","The Light of Mana and Hunger wrapped around all of them simultaneously...crimson-obsidian radiance that distorted space as they began disappearing one by one!","What remained behind was decimated, decayed shore.","In distant corner far from the primary battlefield, all those who had been frozen and paralyzed during the engagement began waking gradually, their consciousness returning as the overwhelming pressure of concentrated Civilizational Authority finally dissipated.","They would find their domain utterly transformed. Their reality shattered. Only dazzling blue sparks floated around them as extended hands for a chance.","In the wake of war, only devastation persisted!","---","After warfare concluded, there existed few viable courses of action available to participants.","The defeated held no voice in determining what followed...their opinions rendered irrelevant through systematic loss of capability to enforce preferences.","The victors could indulge in celebration...reveling in triumph, distributing spoils, commemorating fallen comrades.","Or they could recognize they remained in perpetual state of conflict, understanding that failure to advance immediately would result in them becoming the defeated when next engagement occurred.","And because Noah understood this fundamental principle with absolute clarity...","He stood now in the Early Veiled Shore as this vast continental landscape, rapidly enlarging and transforming through accumulated harvest, currently bore three massive Sovereign Spires of Osmont standing impossibly tall near each other along the Shore’s expanding edges.","These three represented the available Specialization paths.","The first Spire gleamed with obsidian-gold coloration and bore defensive architectural characteristics- massive layered walls and redundant structural supports.","Above it, floating designation proclaimed...","THE IRON CONCORDAT - DEFENSIVE SPECIALIZATION","The second Spire was sleeker, more predatory in design- sharp angles, aggressive protrusions, surface covered in blade-like formations that suggested violence barely contained.","Crimson light pulsed through obsidian framework. Its designation read... THE CRIMSON HUNGER - OFFENSIVE SPECIALIZATION","The third Spire radiated gentle luminescence...green-gold-blue light emanating from its structure in rhythmic pulses.","Circular rather than angular architecture, flowing curves rather than harsh edges. Its designation proclaimed... THE VERDANT CYCLE - SUPPORT SPECIALIZATION","At this moment, Noah stood on golden sands alongside Khor and many others, all watching the entrance of The Iron Concordat Sovereign Spire with focused attention.","They were witnessing the emergence of the first entity to undergo Civilization Specialization transformation.","The massive obsidian-gold doors of the Spire opened with resonant sound that seemed to vibrate through existence itself as...","Titano walked out.","His figure was adorned in Civilizational Armor of Mana and Hunger that now shone with pure obsidian-gold brilliance rather than the mixed coloration others displayed.","The armor had transformed...becoming far more massive, far more imposing, covered in layered crystalline plates that overlapped with sophisticated precision.","He looked absolutely magnificent, a walking embodiment of impenetrable defense.","On his chest, prominently displayed where all could observe, was inscribed massive obsidian-gold shield...the mark distinguishing him as member of The Iron Concordat , as one who had chosen the path of The Infinite Bulwark.","The armored head opened with mechanical precision to reveal Titano’s giant features, his expression holding a mixture of satisfaction and solemn recognition of responsibility he had accepted.","He looked directly toward Noah and spoke with a voice that resonated with newfound authority.","\"Brother! Titano can protect everyone now. No one will fall while Titano stands. This...Titano promises!\"","...!","He could protect everyone now.","Noah smiled genuinely at such an earnest declaration as he nodded with approval and pulled up Titano’s current status information through his Undefined Potential’s analytical capabilities.","|ENTITY DESIGNATION: Titano|","|CIVILIZATION SPECIALIZATION POTENTIAL: Sovereign Potential (Legendary 5th Seal)|","|CURRENT SPECIALIZATION: The Infinite Bulwark (The Iron Concordat)|","|COMPLEXITY AND PURITY: 8 Sextillion|","|SPECIALIZATION EFFECTS:|","|— Offensive Capability: Reduced to 0% (Complete Sacrifice)|","|— Defensive Capability: Multiplied by 20x due to Sovereign Potential enhancement|","|— Immovable Presence: Active - Cannot be displaced without consent|","|— Civilization Fortress Formation: Available|","|— Damage Conversion: Active - All absorbed damage can be channeled to offensive specialists|","|— Existential Anchoring: Radius 500 Gigaparsecs - Reality stabilization preventing spatial manipulation|","|— Regenerative Resonance: 500% healing amplification active|","|This entity now represents a mobile fortress. Offensive capability completely eliminated but defensive capacity elevated to truly extraordinary levels.|","Noah’s eyes burned with brilliant intensity at a single number as everything else wss pushed aside.","8 Sextillion .","8!","That was not a calculation error or display malfunction!","Titano had originally possessed 300 Quintillion Complexity and Purity as recipient of the elevated Boon of Major Mana and Hunger Bulwark. Adding the 100 Quintillion from his fused Primus Inevitability brought him to 400 Quintillion baseline.","After selecting his Specialization and undergoing transformation, that 400 Quintillion had been multiplied by 20x through his Sovereign Potential’s enhanced benefits...resulting in effective defensive rating of 8 Sextillion!","For defensive purposes, Titano now effectively possessed protection exceeding Noah’s own Architect’s Bulwarks threshold of 3 Sextillion...and yet Titano was considered a bastion of his Civilization- a wall as no damage would flow to him unless it bypassed Titano!","And when there were tens of millions of tanks in his Civilization...the enemy would need to be ridiculously powerful to ever even hope to touch his grandeur and immensity.","This was a glimpse of how his terrifying Civilization Specialization could utterly change things from here on out!"]},{"number":4468,"title":"Chapter 4468: Chapter 4467: Immense! III","paragraphs":["Titano was the first.","But not the last.","Noah looked toward Henry, Sigrid, Protos, Riya, The Emperor Penguin, and numerous others assembled on the golden sands.","Oh, Protos!","Noah himself could not undergo Specialization as he embodied and controlled it all, but Protos, The Primus Inevitability bound to him...","\"Haha...\"","Noah couldn’t help but laugh as his eyes flashed with unbound Tyranny!","Titano’s power was a result of both him and his fused Primus Inevitability, 300 + 100 Quintillion multiplied by the effects of the Specialization.","Noah couldn’t undergo Specialization, but Protos could as when he did so, as someone with an even higher baseline than Titano and many others, paired with his Civilization Specialization Potential...oh!","This was why Noah couldn’t help but laugh!","He also looked at all the others.","They would soon receive opportunity to specialize and potentially gain Complexity and Purity exceeding 8 Sextillion.","And Noah emphasized potentially because he also planned to elevate their Civilization Specialization Potential through Harvest investment...which would accelerate advancement speed dramatically while also increasing the multiplicative benefits they received from Specialization transformation!","His imposing words emerged with commanding authority.","\"Choose the Civilization Specialization that aligns most authentically with your fundamental nature. Become bastion if protection calls to your existence. Become sword if destruction resonates with your purpose. Become healer if preservation fulfills your philosophical disposition. Become anything you genuinely wish to become as we continue the advancement toward objectives that exceed what any individual could accomplish alone!\"","...!","OOOH !","Bellows echoed across the Early Veiled Shore as for the first time, mass Specializations commenced within The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger!","Henry moved toward The Crimson Hunger Spire with determined stride...his expression suggesting he had waited for opportunity to unleash accumulated aggression without restraint.","Sigrid approached The Verdant Cycle with measured grace....Order itself gravitating toward healing and defensive stability that aligned with her fundamental principles.","Wait.","Noah blinked as he recalled a line under the Civilization Specialization Potential.","Could someone like Sigrid walk thr paths of both Defense and Healer since they were non-competing Specializations?","\"...\"","Noah’s eyes blazed at the thought as his smile became even more devilish!","Riya darted toward The Crimson Hunger with characteristic rebellious energy...seeking power that would let her carve her own path through hostile existence.","Dozens, then hundreds began entering the various Spires...each one making choice that would define their role within the Civilization’s increasingly sophisticated architecture.","The Primus Inevitabilities would soon surge by the millions to choose their terrifying Specializations!","Noah watched with tyrannical satisfaction as his forces underwent systematic transformation.","This ... is what separates true Civilizations from mere accumulations of power !","---","While such magnificent transformations bloomed in distant territories...","Inside THE Loom.","The domain was vast beyond conventional measurement, structured space where reality itself operated according to deliberately imposed rules rather than natural principles.","Geometric perfection dominated every surface. Light emanated from no visible source yet illuminated everything uniformly.","Within central chamber of this domain, Ambessa’s figure could be observed standing with her calm composure.","She had removed the Existence Avatar Diadem, the sophisticated headgear that had allowed her consciousness to pilot the Avatar manifestation outside THE Loom , and now stood in her genuine physical form.","Her hair cascaded like banner of authority. Her crimson-gold eyes surveyed the massive array of screens displaying recorded footage from all nine Avatars’ experiences.","Around her, other Avatars who had participated in the deployment stood watching...some with expressions of livid fury, others with analytical focus, few with resigned acceptance of unexpected defeat.","The screens displayed devastating scenes: 2 Million Primus Inevitabilities surrounding the Avatars, the overwhelming coordination of their assault, the systematic collapse of all projections despite their substantial individual power.","Uniquely, Ambessa’s extended conversation with the armored entity did not play on these screens for all present to observe...","At this moment, a voice emerged with authority that commanded immediate attention...belonging to one who clearly held substantial rank within THE Loom’s hierarchy.","\"What a unique Civilization we have observed emerging outside our secured boundaries. Ambessa...\"","The speaker, Axiom Architect Surion , addressed her directly.","\"You can confirm this represents The Derivative Way of Hunger ? The connection seems obvious upon initial observation...the tentacles, the consumption mechanics, the relationship with The First Hunger herself.\"","Ambessa’s calm reply emerged without hesitation but also without excessive elaboration.","\"It...should be classified as Derivative Way of Hunger based on observable characteristics, yes.\"","She articulated such confirmation, but deliberately withheld additional insight that it might also represent something else entirely.","Axiom Architect Surion smiled and nodded with approving gesture.","\"Acceptable assessment. Now, regarding performance evaluation: Out of the nine participants in this experimental deployment, you demonstrated sufficient resonance with the Existence Avatar Diadems and exhibited most effective decision-making during engagement outside THE Loom .\"","His tone shifted to a formal proclamation.","\"You have been selected to receive Boon of Specialization as recognition of your superior performance. Your standing within THE Loom’s hierarchy is about to change substantially. You will be elevated to a leadership position among those who will coordinate all response teams for matters occurring outside THE Loom until THE Fallout concludes....including systematic management of this... budding Derivative Civilization of Hunger.\"","\"You will be ordained as one of the leaders of The Civilization Guard of Paradox, a profound honor for any Member of our Civilization!\"","HUUM!","Ambessa’s eyes flashed with genuine surprise at such unexpected promotion...though she recovered her composed expression almost instantly.","She simply nodded with slight smile acknowledging the honor.","\"I accept this responsibility and will execute assigned duties to the best of my accumulated capabilities.\"","She turned her gaze back toward the screens displaying the armored figure who had collapsed her Avatar...that being who possessed such confidence despite facing overwhelming odds, who commanded forces that had systematically eliminated eight other Avatars.","That bold existence...","Was he truly prepared for what was about to come?","Because now it wouldn’t be experimental deployment of nine Avatars.","Now it would be a systematic response from THE Loom itself.","Her smile widened slightly...a mixture of anticipation and something approaching respect for a worthy opponent.","Let us see how far you can advance before we meet again.","Let us discover whether your confidence is justified or merely arrogance awaiting correction.","The screens continued displaying the aftermath of devastation as a small subsection of forces within THE Loom began planning its response to this unexpected challenge.","A small subsection.","The major players themsleves had not even gotten involved as there was no need to.","A few of the followers of THE Living Paradox merely wanted to take care of an annoyance surrounding Vessels of their Master that were being suppressed by Existence itself since The Fallout had yet to occur.","This was something minor.","But it did initiate an exchange of conflicts even before The Fallout!"]},{"number":4469,"title":"Chapter 4469: Chapter 4468: Thaumata I","paragraphs":["In The Wandering Territories.","The Sanctuary of The First Farmer.","A simple verdant-gold hut stood in the center of many radiant farm fields, a modest structure that seemed almost ridiculous given the concentrated life-force emanating from surrounding plots where entire dimensions were being cultivated like crops.","Elyndra entered the hut with expression mixing nostalgia and calming grief.","Her golden hair cascaded like wheat fields in harvest season. Her blue eyes held depths of accumulated wisdom beyond her apparent age. The verdant-gold dress she wore seemed woven from living plant matter that pulsed with rhythmic vitality.","This was the home her father loved to occupy when he required respite from responsibilities, surrounded by vibrant life all around, tending to growth with his own hands rather than delegating to subordinates.","She closed her eyes and breathed deeply, inhaling the immense force of life permeating the surroundings. The accumulated essence of The First Farmer’s cultivation still lingered here, making the simple hut feel sacred despite its modest construction.","In the next moment, a voice echoed from behind her with measured calmness.","\"The Perpetual Farmer. Are you prepared for what comes next?\"","Noah pushed aside the straw door and entered while surveying the interior with analytical assessment. His eyes catalogued details...the simple furniture, the preserved artifacts, the carefully maintained garden visible through rear window.","...!","Was she prepared?","Elyndra turned to stare at this magnificent entity before her, who had walked into her father’s sanctuary as if he belonged there.","His figure approached until he stood mere inches from her position. He tilted his head with expression suggesting genuine curiosity rather than manipulation as he observed the wetness accumulating in her eyes.","His hand reached out with surprising gentleness to wipe away tears that threatened to fall.","She felt the immensity and warmth of hands that appeared capable of crushing her existence or elevating it beyond current limitations. Her blue eyes pulsed like endless sea while examining him, trying to comprehend what exactly he represented, what role she was about to play in his designs.","Because it truly seemed like it would be his designs!","But he pulled his hand away with deliberate motion as he spoke with calm finality.","\"You expressed desire to establish a friendship between us, correct? Then let us be friends. Let us discover whether we can successfully guide you toward achieving The False THE designation. Come.\"","With casual wave of his hand, a blue-gold portal manifested beside them, a spatial tear leading to destinations unknown.","He entered without hesitation or backward glance, as if he had absolute confidence that she would follow.","Moments passed in weighted silence.","Elyndra bit her lips with visible indecision, looking around the hut one final time...at her father’s favorite chair, at the preserved tools he had used for his farming, at all the memories this place represented.","Then she followed Noah through the portal with determined stride.","Father gave me this path. I will walk it to discover where it leads.","---","Inside the Infiniverse.","Noah and Elyndra materialized before a radiant Crimson Hunger Sovereign Spire of Osmont that floated grandly in conceptual space...this particular Spire positioned outside the Early Veiled Shore, hovering alone in sea of golden sandy dreamlike authority that stretched infinitely in all directions.","Inside a domain filled with the weavings Dreams!","The Spire itself was magnificent in its predatory design. Sleek architecture covered in blade-like protrusions. Crimson light pulsing through obsidian framework with rhythmic intensity.","There existed nobody present at this location apart from Protos.","The First Primus Inevitability stood before the Spire’s entrance with arms crossed, radiating heavy aura that made surrounding space distort visibly. His form had grown substantially since his initial emergence...now standing twice as tall as standard Primus Inevitabilities, covered in more elaborate armor, eyes burning with accumulated authority.","Elyndra looked around with expression mixing shock and growing comprehension as she articulated her confusion.","\"Where is this place? And what is that...massive structure? Who is that being radiating such terrifying presence?\"","Noah replied with measured explanation.","\"This is my home...a small portion of it, at least. This place represents a space where my Civilization’s framework manifests tangibly. I brought you here to witness something important.\"","He gestured toward Protos with a casual motion. \"Can you perceive the power level of the being standing before us?\"","He smiled with an expression of genuine curiosity regarding her assessment.","Elyndra’s eyes trembled as her analytical senses reached out to measure Protos.","She wouldn’t be able to fully tell, but...","900 Quintillion Complexity and Purity blazed ahead of her!","For her it just felt overwhelming.","Her own power, 15 Quintillion after accepting the mantle of Perpetual Farmer, seemed to almost mean nothing in comparison. She felt like delicate feather confronting hurricane that could absolutely obliterate her existence without conscious effort.","Regardless of the Nine Principles her father had carefully instilled within her framework! Regardless of all the preparation and engineering that had gone into her creation!","Noah observed her shocked reaction with analytical focus as he continued his explanation.","\"This represents his current power level in base form, before he undergoes his transformation. What you’re sensing now is merely his starting point.\"","He nodded toward Protos with a commanding gesture.","\" Proceed .\"","Protos bowed with formal precision before turning and entering the massive Spire through doors that opened at his approach.","The Spire began shining with intensifying crimson brilliance as unfathomable transformation commenced within, visible even from external observation as the entire structure pulsed with concentrated authority.","As this grand metamorphosis progressed, Noah turned his attention back to Elyndra with an expression of assessment and challenge.","\"This entity represents one among millions contained within my Civilization who possess comparable power levels. Well, others are slightly less on average, he’s exceptional even among his peers. Right now, he is undergoing transformation that will multiply the power you just measured by more than fifteen times through... Civilization Specialization mechanics.\"","His voice carried weight of undeniable truth.","\"This represents the level of immensity you must achieve if you genuinely wish to compete at scales we’re operating on. You possess the legacy of The First Farmer, he had already engineered your existence specifically for pursuing The False THE designation. I am simultaneously pursuing multiple potential solutions to The Fallout. You represent... merely one option among several.\"","HUUM!","His eyes fixed upon her with penetrating intensity.","\"Surprise me. I harbor substantial doubt regarding your viability as a solution currently. Prove that skepticism wrong. Demonstrate that The First Farmer’s legacy constitutes something capable of allowing Civilization to bloom exponentially. Or at minimum, prove that his specific plan to have you personally attain The False THE designation represents achievable objective rather than impossible ambition.\"","...!","Elyndra trembled even more profoundly at such blunt assessment as she bit her lips with decisive determination.","Her figure turned fully toward Noah as she spoke with eyes shining with barely contained fervor.","\"My father designed my fundamental nature and the Principles instilled within my framework specifically with Perpetual Harvest synergy in mind. The engineering was deliberate and comprehensive. I would require you to...infuse me with substantial quantities of harvest...\"","\"...\"","She spoke straightforwadly.","Noah nodded with calm acceptance.","\"I will provide that and more. But first...watch what transformation actually accomplishes at scale.\"","...!","The massive doorway of the Spire before them pulsed with blinding crimson radiance as a terrifying figure emerged from within!"]},{"number":4470,"title":"Chapter 4470: Chapter 4469: Thaumata II","paragraphs":["Protos had undergone complete metamorphosis.","His form was now substantially more predatory...sleek and dangerous rather than merely imposing. Crimson-obsidian tentacles covered his body in intricate patterns, each one writhing with barely contained aggressive intent.","Multiple serrated maws had manifested across his shoulders, chest, and limbs...each one releasing wisps of concentrated Hunger!","His eyes burned with ravenous crimson light that seemed capable of consuming everything they focused upon.","The pressure he radiated proved so intense that crimson winds and concentrated authority erupted from his form...and became invisible force that inadvertently crashed against Elyndra with devastating weight.","She fell to her knees involuntarily, panting with exertion as her existence struggled to remain coherent under such overwhelming presence.","Beside her, Noah observed with eyes shining with tyrannical satisfaction.","He couldn’t suppress the smile that bloomed across his features!","Because the results for Protos were utterly magnificent beyond initial projections.","Noah was the acknowledged leader of this Civilization. Yes, he embodied all Specializations simultaneously through his Undefined Potential. Yes, he possessed more absurd advancement rates than any individual Member.","But would he truly be excluded from the remarkable benefits that Civilization Specialization provided?","Protos, who had fused with him, who served as his armor and extension...emphatically rejected such limitation!","His own Civilization would never constrain him. This principle was demonstrated through Protos, whose power was fundamentally Noah’s power due to their symbiotic fusion.","And at this moment, that combined power was utterly absurd.","Noah’s eyes shone with brilliant intensity as he examined Protos’s updated status information. Protos knelt before him with formal reverence and spoke with a voice resonating with accumulated authority.","\"I have undergone Specialization transformation for the sake of the Master’s advancement. My power is your power. My growth is your growth.\"","...!","The status sheet materialized with comprehensive details.","|ENTITY DESIGNATION: Protos - The First Primus Inevitability|","|CIVILIZATION SPECIALIZATION POTENTIAL: Primordial Potential (Mythic 7th Seal)|","|CURRENT SPECIALIZATION: The Hungering Maw (The Crimson Hunger)|","|BASE COMPLEXITY AND PURITY (PRE-SPECIALIZATION): 900 Quintillion|","|SPECIALIZATION MULTIPLICATIVE EFFECT: 50x (Primordial Potential enhancement - base 15x elevated to 50x through exceptional Potential synergy)|","|CURRENT COMPLEXITY AND PURITY (POST-SPECIALIZATION): 45 Sextillion|","|SPECIALIZATION EFFECTS:|","|— Defensive Capability: Reduced to 20% (80% Sacrifice)|","|— Offensive Capability: Multiplied by 50x - All attacks carry devastating destructive potential|","|— Consumption Acceleration: 100% efficiency - All defeated enemies immediately converted to power|","|— Reality Severance: Active - Attacks ignore conventional defenses|","|— Exponential Hunger Stacks: 10% power increase per kill, stacks indefinitely|","|— Predatory Instinct: Can perceive optimal attack vectors automatically|","|— Feast of Conquest: Can temporarily wield defeated enemies’ abilities|","|SYMBIOTIC NOTATION: As fused entity with Master, all accumulated power transfers bidirectionally. Master gains full benefit of Protos’s Specialization without sacrificing his own versatility.|","After reviewing these shocking specifications, Noah shook his head with genuine marvel at what had been achieved.","He addressed Protos with commanding simplicity.","\"Come. Let us demonstrate what our combined framework can accomplish.\"","Protos’s form dissolved into crimson-obsidian light that flowed toward Noah’s existence. The fusion occurred with practiced smoothness as Noah’s body underwent dramatic transformation...expanding substantially, becoming far more imposing.","His armored form now stood twice his normal height. The armor itself had transformed, incorporating Protos’s predatory characteristics alongside its defensive capabilities. Crimson tentacles woven through blue-gold framework.","Multiple serrated patterns visible across the surface. Eyes burning with combined authority of both entities.","Noah sensed the combined power flowing through his transformed existence as prompts materialized with updated measurements.","|COMBINED ENTITY: Noah Osmont + Protos (Fused State)|","|Your base: 2.25 Sextillion|","|Protos’s base: 45 Sextillion|","| Combined Complexity and Purity : 47.25 Sextillion|","|Master retains full versatility and defensive capabilities from Architect’s Bulwarks (3 Sextillion threshold) while simultaneously wielding Protos’s overwhelming offensive specialization.|","In such terrifying transformed state, Noah turned his attention toward the astonished Elyndra who had collapsed to her knees under the concentrated pressure.","His voice boomed out with authority that made surrounding space tremble.","\"This represents the power level you need to be advancing toward if you genuinely wish to accomplish objectives we’re pursuing. Will you prove capable of reaching such heights?\"","...!","Elyndra felt the shocking pressure Noah was releasing, the concentrated authority that made her entire existence feel suppressed, constrained, barely capable of maintaining coherence.","Even though every instinct screamed at her to remain prostrate, to acknowledge overwhelming superiority...","She arduously forced herself to stand upright with visible strain. Her legs trembled. Her breath came in gasps. But she met his burning gaze directly and spoke with a determined declaration!","\"I! Am! Capable ! My father designed me for this! His legacy will not fail!\"","At such words, Noah nodded with an expression of cautious approval.","\"Then let us provide you with starting point. A Boon to elevate your baseline capabilities substantially. All else will follow through systematic cultivation. Whether you prove viable solution or others must be pursued instead... we will continue exploring all available options simultaneously...\"","...!","With such proclamation, The Boon of Major Mana and Hunger Bulwark descended upon Elyndra’s existence.","The marker of a radiant crown appeared above her, a glowing designation identifying her as one of the 6,561 blessed recipients who would receive substantial power infusion.","Her Complexity and Purity surged dramatically as the Boon integrated itself into her framework. From 15 Quintillion to 315 Quintillion, a twenty-fold increase that made her gasp with sensation of power flooding through her existence.","Prompts bloomed before Noah’s vision with systematic details.","|Boon of Major Mana and Hunger Bulwark has been successfully applied to: Elyndra (The Perpetual Farmer)|","|Granted Enhancement: 300 Quintillion Complexity and Purity|","|Updated Total: 315 Quintillion Complexity and Purity|","|Additional Benefit: Full capability to efficiently utilize Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger|","|Cultivation Acceleration: All advancement related to Mana and Hunger principles receives substantial multiplicative enhancement|","Noah observed her transformation with analytical assessment...noting how her aura had changed, how her presence had become substantially more imposing despite still being incomparably weaker than his own power.","Then he looked at himself, at his combined form with Protos, at the 47.25 Sextillion power flowing through his framework, at all the capabilities and potential that represented.","His eyes flashed with light of pure tyranny.","This is merely the beginning. So much more remains to be accomplished...","Civilization Specialization has only just commenced. Millions more will undergo transformation. My forces will become exponentially more formidable.","And I...will continue accumulating power without theoretical ceiling. Until The Fallout becomes a minor matter!","He was just getting started.","And existence itself would tremble at what he would accomplish!"]},{"number":4471,"title":"Chapter 4471: Chapter 4470: Thaumata III","paragraphs":["Time and glory.","Many across existence had debated their relationship since consciousness first achieved capacity for abstract thought.","Some argued glory required time, that accumulated achievements across eons inevitably produced legendary status through sheer persistence and compound growth.","Others claimed glory transcended time, that single moment of unprecedented action could eclipse millennia of mundane existence.","But the truth was simpler.","If one possessed sufficient time, unfathomable glory became inevitable.","Given enough duration, even modest advantages compounded into overwhelming superiority.","Given enough opportunities, even improbable outcomes manifested through statistical certainty. Given enough accumulation, even incremental growth achieved catastrophic totals.","The question was never whether time produced glory.","The question was whether one survived long enough to benefit from time’s multiplicative effects.","---","Hours passed since the collapse of one of the Vessels of THE Living Paradox.","And in those hours, many, many things changed across the Folds.","Primus Inevitabilities spread across every crevice they could locate. They didn’t force any existences to comply with demands or mandates.","But they appeared around and above regions where Living Existences concentrated across Transcendent Folds...distributing Sparks of the Way of Mana blatantly while remaining stationed as silent sentinels.","The implicit message was clear: Take the Spark or don’t. But don’t interfere with distribution.","Across the Folds, a sense of profound unease and escalating fear spread among Living Existences who considered themselves powerful.","Kleos Councils convened with emergency frequency. Dukes gathered to grasp and understand this unprecedented phenomenon that had manifested without warning or explanation.","Who were these entities? What did they represent? Why were they distributing power freely rather than demanding tribute or submission?","The questions multiplied faster than answers could be formulated.","And while all of this unfolded across populated territories...","The Primus Inevitabilities truly spread across the vicissitudes of the Folds and deep into the Wandering Territories where civilizational authority had collapsed or never existed.","For them, there existed overabundance of fuel to devour.","The Tears in Existence were becoming more and more apparent as THE Creature’s Veil continued failing.","The boundary he had erected to separate life from death deteriorated with accelerating velocity.","More and more Dead Existences began flowing into the lands of the living...shambling corpses and malevolent Creatures that had been contained for eons suddenly released into territories unprepared for their presence.","Even though Dead Existences were seemingly considered weak in raw power compared to current Primus Inevitabilities, these terrifying weapons of Noah’s Civilization proceeded to systematically collapse and devour every single Dead Existence they encountered.","No exceptions. No mercy. Complete eradication.","Such systematic purging continued unfolding with methodical efficiency as Sparks of Mana were directed to flow into as many Wheels of Existence and domains as possible, permeating all known territories of Minor and Transcendent Folds.","The Way of Mana was being adopted with urgent frequency.","It didn’t discriminate based on ability or lack thereof. It imposed no requirements for existing strength or weakness. It was accessible to anyone because Mana was so pervasive across everything that any single entity could grasp it if they chose.","And so, Noah’s Civilization entered period of grandiose expansion.","Rapid. Systematic. Overwhelming.","At the same time...","Inside the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds.","A region existed filled with obsidian-gold rivers flowing through impossible geometries. Mirrors of concentrated Paradox floated throughout the space...each one reflecting reality that contradicted what other mirrors displayed.","In the very center of such a place rested massive corpse of an Early Creature.","A Dead Early Creature!","This titanic deceased entity was currently observing the pacing, worried figure of none other than Diviticus.","Duke Diviticus.","She floated across this paradoxical region with expression carrying unfathomable worry and mounting tension...as if her very existence could perceive something fundamentally wrong occurring but couldn’t identify the specific threat.","Her instincts screamed warnings. Her framework trembled with foreboding sensations she couldn’t rationalize or dismiss.","There was no news of Schrodinger.","Everything seemed to be systematically collapsing around them as she received fragmented reports of terrifying monstrous entities whose power allegedly eclipsed any legends of Early Creatures that histories recorded.","And her existence could not settle. Could not find peace.","Something within her fundamental nature was shaking with premonitions she didn’t want to acknowledge.","At such moment as she continued pacing with increasing agitation...","CRACK !","The space nearby fractured violently as a terrifying aura swept across the domain, freezing the figure of the Dead Early Creature and Diviticus completely in temporal stasis!","A figure of a Primus Inevitability peeked through the spatial tear. Its eyes flashed with crimson light that seemed capable of perceiving everything about her existence in single glance.","It fully stepped through the crack and gazed at both Diviticus and the Dead Early Creature with an expression mixing analytical assessment and predatory hunger.","Diviticus was frozen utterly, unable to move anything except her eyes. But she still felt the terror cascading through her existence at being forcefully rendered completely still by mere presence of this entity.","Her eyes darted frantically, taking in every detail of the terrifying being that had just arrived uninvited.","And a moment after this initial Primus Inevitability’s arrival...","Space cracked again with more violent rupture.","Gloriously, the visage of Protos appeared!","His form was substantially more imposing than the first Inevitability. His appearance alone radiated power many times greater than his subordinate.","Multiple serrated maws visible across his body. Crimson tentacles writhing with barely contained aggression. Eyes burning with accumulated authority that suggested he could collapse entire territories through sustained assault.","The moment Protos’s gaze landed on Diviticus, she began trembling violently despite the temporal stasis constraining her movement.","She felt like her existence was about to collapse just from this gaze alone, as if his attention itself carried weight capable of unmaking her fundamental nature.","Protos stared at Diviticus with a calm, measured expression before he spoke.","\"I wish for you to understand clearly why the events that are about to occur to you will unfold as they do. Perhaps I can better communicate the underlying principles through a poetic expression...\"","...!","The stark contrast between Protos’s titanic, terrifying form and his casual mention of poetry was jarring...almost absurd.","But he continued with sardonic amusement coloring his words.","\"There once was a Living Paradox consumed by greed,","Who took a bite from someone far beyond her reach indeed,","She stole a single drop of blood through treacherous deed,","And that tiny drop elevated her, or so she did believe.","She thought herself become someone grand in existence vast,","Even daring to play with corpses of Early Creatures past,","She built relations and gathered power, thought her die was cast,","Never imagining that stolen blood would seal her fate at last.","And yet, in the end, she remains alone inside her domain small,","While follower of the one she robbed now stands before her thrall,","She doesn’t deserve his presence, his attention, or his call,","She only deserves to feel existence devoured, atom by atom , through it all.","With her pain amplified to extremes beyond what mind can bear,","The last things her existence will know are endless throes of despair,","Before collapse and darkness become the only comforts there,","This is justice for those who steal from powers they cannot compare.\"","...!","After completing this terrifying poem delivered with casual cruelty, Protos gazed at Diviticus with an expression mixing sinister amusement and cold finality.","\"Did you comprehend the message? Do you understand what your actions have earned you?\"","...!","The frozen figure of Diviticus trembled even more violently, waves of absolute fear cascading through her constrained existence.","She couldn’t fathom how things had deteriorated to this point so rapidly. Days ago, she had been a glorious Living Paradox and a Duke of Paradox of substantial power!","Now she faced an entity whose mere presence suggested her collapse was inevitable, and the cause of it...was that drop of blood!","Ozymandias! Osmont! Moiraine!","Oh!","She wasn’t even capable of replying or defending herself as at this moment...","From Protos’s form, crimson tentacles covered with countless miniature sharp jaws began flowing outward like rivers of concentrated Hunger. They surrounded both the figure of the Dead Early Creature and Diviticus herself...encircling them completely, cutting off any possibility of escape.","The glorious voice of Protos echoed throughout the paradoxical domain with a tone mixing anticipation and methodical purpose.","\"Well then. Let us commence, shall we? This will take considerable time to execute properly. After all, devouring existence atom by atom requires patience and precision. And I have been instructed to ensure you experience every single moment of what follows.\"","\"Because... Existence can be so unfair , can it not?\"","HUUM!","The tentacles began moving with deliberate slowness, approaching her frozen form with terrible inevitability.","Diviticus’s eyes widened with absolute terror as she understood what was coming.","And she could do nothing to prevent it.","The first tentacle touched her existence...","And the screaming began."]},{"number":4472,"title":"Chapter 4472: Chapter 4471: Thaumata IV","paragraphs":["In a corner of the Early Veiled Shore.","Inside a Plot holding tall, vibrant green-gold Auric Vitae Grasses that now grew as tall as 100 meters.","Noah’s figure sat cross-legged within such a plot, surrounded by overabundance of accumulated harvest that manifested as floating spheres of concentrated authority.","Before him were the figures of Heidrun, Yoshinami, and Malphas...his Land Lifeforms who had answered his call and become integral components of his grand Civilization.","Heidrun’s radiant white-gold hair coat gleamed in the ambient light, her majestic goat form exuding serene, arrogant vitality.","Yoshinami had assumed her human form...wearing a obsidian silk dress that contrasted sharply with her crimson spider eyes that held predatory intelligence.","Malphas maintained his butler attire with characteristic precision, though his posture suggested unusual tension.","Noah calmly stroked Heidrun’s coat while contemplating numerous things.","When it came to the many potential solutions to surviving The Fallout, he had come to understand something fundamental.","Similar to his Way of Existence itself, not simply complexity and raw power... but knowledge was unfathomably critical.","The specific type of knowledge could change everything.","And when it came to acquiring more knowledge, he possessed multiple viable sources.","He planned to make another trip to the Earliest Folds very soon. Another source was THE Dead Order , he would be initiating conversation with her shortly.","Khor represented yet another wellspring of information as more of her memories returned with her terrifying rate of progression toward reclaiming original power.","Khor could also be considered another fully viable solution to surviving THE Loom , as long as she regains her distinction as THE First Hunger!","Many possibilities. Many options.","And yet none of them were where they needed to be. They all required time, and time seemed to be the one resource that remained perpetually scarce.","But another path he had pursued involved utilizing Existential Rollback on his Land Lifeforms...specifically Malphas!","Malphas had served THE Living Emotive directly. He had been granted isolated Everythings of THE Living Emotive herself! If more of his suppressed existence could be systematically restored... substantial information might become accessible.","And at this moment, Malphas had undergone Civilization Specialization in addition to already fusing with a Primus Inevitability.","He had chosen The Infinite Bulwark Specialization...wanting to serve as shield for his Master above all other considerations.","His Complexity and Purity stood at 16 Sextillion due to his remarkably high Potential classification.","Heidrun had specialized to join The Verdant Cycle, choosing healing and support roles that aligned with her nurturing nature.","Yoshinami had specialized to become Hungering Maw, her predatory instincts finding perfect expression in pure offensive power.","Each of them pulsed with tremendous accumulated authority.","At this moment, Noah looked toward the visibly trembling figure of Malphas as he asked with measured calm.","\"Did you recover something substantial through the Existential Rollback?\"","Malphas nodded with heavy expression...his eyes hiding something that appeared to be a mixture of pain and profound shame.","His voice emerged with uncharacteristic hesitation.","\"It is best that I show you the recovered memory directly rather than attempting to articulate what I’ve recalled.\"","With such words, he waved his hands with deliberate motion....causing an illusory screen to manifest before them.","On the screen, lights began flickering as a scene started materializing with increasing clarity.","The memory depicted cloudy multicolored domain seemingly composed of countless concentrated emotions given tangible form. The entire space pulsed with feelings...joy, sorrow, rage, serenity...all woven together into environmental fabric.","Within this domain stood two magnificent thrones positioned opposite each other. Between them rested table covered with... Everythings .","Vibrant multicolored Everythings that radiated such unfathomably potent authority that even viewing them through memory caused Noah’s existence to pulse.","They were filled with pure Civilizational Authority, distilled essence of THE Living Emotive’s accumulated cultivation.","Two beings occupied the thrones.","One appeared to exhibit humanoid female form...though their features remained difficult to focus upon directly, as if their fundamental nature resisted simple observation.","The other was humanoid entity composed entirely of elemental lights and concentrated Everythings...their form seeming not entirely real.","Around this cloudy domain that held the table and thrones, the figure of Malphas could be observed along with two other servants adorned in butler and maid attire respectively.","Their hands held drinks and plates of condensed Everythings...luxury refreshments that would be priceless beyond measure in normal contexts.","Even more elaborate plates of Everything fluttered around them like attentive servants...ready to provide additional refreshment the moment their masters desired it.","From one throne, a voice emerged with tone of curiosity and mild concern.","\"Emotive, is it acceptable to conduct this discussion with audience present?\"","The speaker gestured toward the figures of Malphas and the other caretakers with subtle motion.","On the opposite throne, THE Living Emotive turned toward THE Living Elemental and laughed with genuine warmth before waving her hand dismissively.","\" Don’t concern yourself with them. They won’t retain any memories of this conversation afterwards.\"","Her tone shifted to become more focused.","\" But you came here because you wanted specific clarifications regarding THE Loom’s architectural design... I have completed the specifications for most interior components. The structure will contain many internal domains that are infinitely more vast than even the First Folds themselves.\"","She leaned forward with evident enthusiasm.","\" Early Creatures will permeate throughout it as inhabitants rather than visitors. Unlike how existence currently functions in the Earliest Folds where all Civilizations occupy shared territory, I plan to separate the Living Existences into different domains... different Shelters.\"","Her hands gestured expansively.","\" So your Primordial Civilization and mine and all others fortunate enough to gain entry would enjoy their own separate advancement spaces inside grander construct that supports everyone equally... well, equally for the most part at least.\"","Her expression became more animated.","\" We would collaborate systematically and cooperate across Civilizational boundaries...and isn’t that cooperation something utterly magnificent? There will be structured collaboration and eons upon eons of dilated time with absolutely no conflict, no wars, no wasteful expenditure of resources on mutual destruction...\"","Her voice carried weight of profound conviction.","\" Simply the systematic advancement of all Civilizations contained within. And when the time eventually arrives for The Fallout... the collapse of everything else in Observable Existence outside THE Loom will provide one final burst, one ultimate push of concentrated resources to our preserved Civilizations.\"","She paused deliberately.","\"That final harvest may potentially elevate us incrementally closer toward the next Scale. Toward that glorious Scale that THE Creature himself stands to be the only one who will successfully reach.\"","BOOM !","Noah heard such terrifying revelations in this scene...this memory recovered from a servant of THE Living Emotive as significant information crystallized before him!","THE Loom is designed with separate Shelters for different Civilizations...and one of the reasons behind all of this...ah.","His eyes pulsed with intense focus as his mind raced through implications.","He looked at the still-trembling Malphas with renewed appreciation and...","\"Show me more.\"","He gave his command."]},{"number":4473,"title":"Chapter 4473: Chapter 4472: Thaumata V","paragraphs":["While Noah pursued knowledge accumulation in a secluded corner of the Early Veiled Shore...","The engine of his Civilization continued churning with relentless momentum.","At this moment, two particular beings were observing the glorious transformations that had swept across the Shore in the hours that had passed since mass Specialization commenced.","The observers were none other than The Queen of Matter and The Shadow Guard of Queen Adelaide- Night!","Both had books floating around them, meticulously documenting the changes and systematic establishment of three distinct factions within the Early Veiled Shore that correlated directly with the Civilization Specializations.","They floated near the center of the Shore above glimmering golden sands. From this vantage point, they could observe that the massive continental landscape had been carved into three distinct territorial spaces.","Each space bore a massive Sovereign Spire of Osmont at its center, architectural anchors around which the factions organized themselves.","The three carved domains represented The Iron Concordat, The Crimson Hunger, and The Verdant Cycle!","Those who had undergone Civilization Specialization could be observed moving together within their respective territories, working systematically to understand their newfound capabilities.","Distinct leaders were naturally arising within each faction through demonstrated competence and power.","The Queen of Matter’s bright eyes gleamed with analytical curiosity as she whispered to Night a question she already knew the answer to.","\"Which individual represents the most powerful member of The Iron Concordat currently? Who holds apex position within that defensive faction?\"","Night didn’t require even a moment’s consideration before her eyes shone with certainty.","\"A single person claims supremacy for both The Iron Concordat and The Verdant Cycle simultaneously...which is utterly ridiculous. They possessed Civilization Specialization Potential classification that permitted them to specialize in both non-competing paths.\"","Her voice carried mixture of admiration and disbelief.","\"It would have to be Sigrid!\"","...!","Both of their gazes immediately focused upon the visage of THE Living Order...currently engaged in a sweet conversation with Amelia Osmont near The Verdant Cycle Sovereign Spire.","Around Sigrid gathered Eowyn, Emmeline, Dr. Hall, some members of the Isolated Civilization of Mana, and numerous others whose bodies pulsed with accumulated power measuring in Sextillions of Complexity and Purity.","Night’s eyes sharpened as analytical focus intensified.","\"Did you manage to observe her complete status sheet? The full specifications of what dual Specialization accomplished?\"","The Queen of Matter looked into a specific page of her floating book and smiled with undisguised excitement.","\"I begged The Master repeatedly to grant me access to status panels for her and several other high-priority individuals. He eventually relented...\"","Her smile widened.","\"It’s absolutely insane what the numbers reveal.\"","With such enthusiastic declaration, The Queen of Matter pulled up the relevant page and angled it so Night could observe the documented specifications.","|ENTITY DESIGNATION: Sigrid (THE Living Order)|","|CIVILIZATION SPECIALIZATION POTENTIAL: Primordial Potential (Mythic 8th Seal)|","|CURRENT SPECIALIZATIONS: The Infinite Bulwark (The Iron Concordat) + The Vital Chorus (The Verdant Cycle)|","|BASE COMPLEXITY AND PURITY (PRE-SPECIALIZATION): 850 Quintillion|","|SPECIALIZATION MULTIPLICATIVE EFFECTS:|","|— The Infinite Bulwark: 50x defensive multiplication (Primordial Potential enhancement)|","|— The Vital Chorus: 50x support/healing multiplication (Primordial Potential enhancement)|","|COMBINED COMPLEXITY AND PURITY (POST-SPECIALIZATION): 85 Sextillion|","|DUAL SPECIALIZATION SYNERGY:|","|— Offensive Capability: Reduced to 0|","|— Defensive Capability: Multiplied by 50x |","|— Support Capability: Multiplied by 50x - All healing/buffing effects extraordinarily potent|","|— Unique Synergy: Can establish Fortress formations that simultaneously heal all protected allies while absorbing damage|","|This entity represents ultimate protective support...a nearly unkillable anchor who ensures allies never fall while providing overwhelming restorative capabilities.|","Night stared at the numbers displayed before her as she slowly shook her head with genuine wonder.","\"These ridiculous numbers show that as of this moment, The Iron Concordat and The Verdant Cycle factions are substantially more favored within our Civilization’s. The synergy between those two Specializations are ridiculous...\"","...!","The Queen of Matter raised her eyebrows.","\"Oh?\"","Night’s words emerged calmly.","\"As of this moment, The Infinite Bulwark Specialization and The Vital Chorus Specialization are the only two paths considered truly non-competing. Their sacrifices don’t overlap, one eliminates offense, the other eliminates different offensive aspects. So they can theoretically coexist within a single existence.\"","She gestured toward the distant Sigrid.","\"If someone possesses sufficiently high Civilization Specialization Potential to access multiple paths simultaneously, they can specialize in both of these complementary frameworks. The result? Ridiculous multiplicative effects to their baseline power.\"","Her voice carried weight!","\"When general harvest distribution occurs...say, 1 Sextillion Complexity and Purity being allocated, these dual-specialized entities might receive effective harvest of 10 or even 20 Sextillion due to their advancement speed multipliers.\"","She paused deliberately.","\"At this moment, those possessing sufficient Potential to specialize in both The Iron Concordat and The Verdant Cycle simultaneously represent the absolute strongest individuals within our Civilization’s membership. Meanwhile, the offensive side can actually be considered to be on the losing end as it does not have another Specialization thst is considered non-competing...\"","WAA!","After such detailed exchange, The Queen of Matter actually shook her head with wry smile.","\"Actually, scratch that entire assessment. Even though The Hungering Maw Specialization would theoretically be considered unfavorable selection for anyone with capability to pursue multiple Specialization paths, since it competes with both other options, there exists one such being who specialized exclusively as Hungering Maw.\"","Her expression became almost reverent.","\"And even with that single Specialization limiting her potential versatility... she remains ridiculously stronger than Sigrid!\"","...!","As she articulated this shocking claim, both of them turned away from the massive faction bases and directed their attention toward the continental expanse shining with obsidian-crimson crystalline mountains and elaborate structures.","The Sanctuaries of Inevitabilities where millions upon millions of Primus Inevitabilities were still being systematically formed during these many hours of the initial production cycle.","There, the diminutive figure of Khor floated serenely as she communicated with countless Primus Inevitabilities simultaneously...her consciousness touching each one, acknowledging their existence, welcoming them into the Civilization.","Khor!","The First Hunger herself!","Even though she possessed only a single Specialization rather than dual paths, she was undoubtedly more powerful than Sigrid.","Her Potential classification and starting baseline were simply ridiculous.","The Queen of Matter flipped through pages of her book with practiced motion until she located Khor’s documented specifications.","|ENTITY DESIGNATION: Khor (The First Hunger)|","|CIVILIZATION SPECIALIZATION POTENTIAL: Primordial Potential (Mythic 9th Seal - Maximum)|","|CURRENT SPECIALIZATION: The Hungering Maw (The Crimson Hunger)|","|BASE COMPLEXITY AND PURITY (PRE-SPECIALIZATION): 3.5 Sextillion|","|SPECIALIZATION MULTIPLICATIVE EFFECT: 75x offensive multiplication (Maximum Primordial Potential enhancement - exceeds standard 50x due to 9th Seal classification)|","|CURRENT COMPLEXITY AND PURITY (POST-SPECIALIZATION): 262.5 Sextillion|","|SPECIALIZATION EFFECTS:|","|— Defensive Capability: Reduced to 20% (80% sacrifice)|","|— Offensive Capability: Multiplied by 75x |","|— Consumption Acceleration: 100% efficiency with Primordial enhancement|","|— Reality Severance: Enhanced beyond standard - Can attack conceptual existence|","|— Exponential Hunger Stacks: 15% power increase per kill (enhanced from standard 10%)|","|— All Hungering Maw abilities elevated to maximum possible expression|","|This entity represents one of the absolute apex predator within The Primordial Civilization.|","Both The Queen of Matter and Night stared silently at the status sheet.","They possessed no adequate words to express what those numbers represented!","262.5 Sextillion Complexity and Purity.","From single individual who had specialized merely hours ago.","They could only look back toward the small figure of floating Khor, observing her gentle interaction with the Primus Inevitabilities, seeing how they reached toward her with reverence that transcended simple loyalty.","Both women spoke simultaneously with identical sentiment.","\"Fuck...\"","...!","---","The Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger was experiencing a period of unprecedented growth...a period of systematic expansion and refinement occurring simultaneously across multiple domains.","It truly seemed that time was all that was genuinely required for them to achieve unprecedented glory.","Accumulate sufficient duration, and exponential advantages would compound into overwhelming superiority. Maintain the current trajectory, and dominance became inevitable conclusion rather than ambitious aspiration.","Time.","The fundamental resource that spanned incomprehensible eons when one possessed abundance of it.","But when one desperately needed time...when circumstances demanded rapid advancement before external threats could mobilize their devastating response...","Time became unfathomably scarce.","The cruel irony of existence remained that...those who possessed time rarely required it urgently. Those who required it urgently rarely possessed sufficient quantity.","Noah’s Civilization was racing against a clock that none of them could observe directly but all of them could feel ticking with inexorable progression.","The Fallout approached!"]},{"number":4474,"title":"Chapter 4474: Chapter 4473: Pathos I","paragraphs":["In the Early Veiled Shore.","Riya emerged from the Crimson Hunger Sovereign Spire with a smile, waving goodbye to others who remained inside with a cheerful gesture that suggested nothing was amiss.","But when she turned to look out toward the Early Veiled Shore itself...","Her smile transformed into something melancholic.","Something hollow.","Her radiant figure was surrounded by blue-gold Mana at this moment, her fair skin visible beneath the concentrated authority that wrapped around her like second skin.","Faint crimson tattoos could barely be perceived on her arms, intricate patterns that pulsed with dormant power.","She had released her fused Primus Inevitability to roam with others near Khor for now. Her Civilization Specialization form was in inactive state...The Hungering Maw transformation reduced to those barely visible crimson markings.","At this moment, she moved across the golden sands with a gaze carrying melancholy she never showed others.","Because the others don’t need to know.","They don’t need to carry this burden alongside me.","She closed her eyes as she sensed that brilliant anchor...that sun which constantly emitted calming heat despite everything else in existence growing cold.","She took a step with natural instinct guiding her toward it.","When she opened her eyes again, she found herself in field of green-gold verdant grasses stretching impossibly tall around her.","She observed the figure of Noah watching an illusory screen displaying some recovered scenes. Heidrun, Yoshinami, and Malphas were present in the surroundings...each processing whatever information was being revealed.","Riya looked at the scene unfolding on the screen.","She saw a woman surrounded by swirling emotions seated on elaborate throne, talking vibrantly to another entity opposite her who was surrounded by terrifying elemental waves of concentrated brilliance.","On the screen, the visage of Malphas could be observed as he carried ornate jug filled with vibrant Civilizational Everythings of Origin . He was approaching to refill the cup of THE Living Emotive who motioned for him impatiently as her vessel had emptied.","THE Living Emotive’s voice emerged with enthusiasm.","\" So entry into THE Loom isn’t going to be available for everyone who desires it. THE Living Existences have to pay to secure access, alongside however many Early Creatures, Living Existences, and even lesser Fold Dwellers you wish to bring with your Civilization. Each individual requires ticket to board this grand ride. And-\"","...!","As THE Living Emotive spoke with mounting excitement, her terrifying power leaked outward slightly.","The pressure was so immense that Malphas, who was in the process of pouring the liquid Everythings into her cup, trembled violently and stumbled from the overwhelming authority.","The jug tilted too far.","Liquid Everythings gushed out uncontrolled and splashed directly onto THE Living Emotive’s hand!","...!","The moment such accident occurred, the entire atmosphere changed.","The air became heavy .","Malphas trembled while attempting to bow in immediate apology, but before he could articulate words-","\" You fucking insect.\"","...!","The words from THE Living Emotive carried such weight that surrounding reality distorted visibly.","In the next moment, she dropped her cup deliberately. It fell to the cloudy surface with resonant sound.","Her voice emerged with cold authority.","\" Pick it up.\"","Malphas trembled as he moved to obey...descending to retrieve the fallen vessel. The other maid and butler servants behind him watched with visibly shaking eyes as tension mounted.","The moment Malphas bent to grasp the cup...","THE Living Emotive’s hand shot out with vicious speed, grabbing Malphas’s head and smashing it against the cloudy surface!","She then used her leg to keep his face pressed firmly to the ground- applying steady pressure that prevented any movement.","Her words emerged with twisted satisfaction.","\" While I am conducting such important strategic discussions with an esteemed colleague, you make a mistake? You tasteless void of emotion. How exactly did that make you feel? Can you even comprehend the shame you should be experiencing right now?\"","Malphas trembled while his face was being pushed down with increasing force.","\"I... I beg for your forgiveness, Miss. I did not mean to cause offense or disruption...\"","\" No. You never mean to.\"","Her voice dripped with contempt.","\" You lack the vibrant spectrum of emotions. You are tasteless. Gray. Cheap, watery sentiment that can be easily consumed if it makes mistakes. So don’t make mistakes. Understood?\"","...!","Malphas’s reply emerged as broken whisper.","\"Yes, Miss. I understand completely. It will not occur again.\"","\" Stay down there for now and reflect properly on your failure.\"","THE Living Emotive’s face twisted into disturbing smile as she waved her fingers with a casual motion.","From Malphas’s prostrate body, she systematically harvested the emotions and Everythings he was generating...misery, fear, despair, shame...all the concentrated negative sentiments produced by his humiliation","By her purposeful insults!","She caused them to flow directly into her mouth.","She swallowed them with visible pleasure while licking her lips appreciatively.","Opposite her, THE Living Elemental displayed an expression of profound disgust. He shook his head with barely contained revulsion.","\" Must you engage in such treatment toward your own people? This seems... excessive.\"","THE Living Emotive’s eyes flashed dangerously as she sneered.","\" Are you actually presuming to instruct me on how to conduct my Way of Existence? My Way is The Way of Emotions. The Way of Feelings. Misery, despair, fear...all the negative emotions are most prevalent across existence. Most potent. Most delicious.\"","Her foot twisted on Malphas’s head as she continued.","\"I occasionally share my own accumulated misery and negativity with this insect and others like them. Then I systematically wipe their memories clean and start the cycle again. Even now, this one and those servants observing will remember nothing of this encounter. This is my Way. Don’t fucking insult it.\"","Her voice intensified.","\"I don’t tell you how your fire or ice should manifest, do I? Oh, now you’ve gotten me genuinely heated...\"","THE Living Elemental’s expression became even more sour. In his eyes flickered emotion suggesting he hated dealing with Emotive above all other entities. As if she was extraordinarily difficult to manage and all recognized this fact."]},{"number":4475,"title":"Chapter 4475: Chapter 4474: Pathos II","paragraphs":["The words of THE Living Elemental emerged with forced calm.","\" Let us simply continue our discussions and forget this incident occurred. My sincere apologies for overstepping boundaries.\"","At such words, THE Living Emotive’s expression shifted instantly, transforming from apparent fury to exaggerated happiness in single breath.","Down below, her foot continued twisting on Malphas as she drew more and more concentrated misery from his existence.","\" Yes, yes! Let us continue discussing THE Loom’s entry requirements...\"","Her eyes shone with manic light containing countless swirling emotions.","This was her Way of Existence.","This was the true Emotive!","The scene on the illusory screen began fading as the recovered memory reached its conclusion.","Malphas, the present version observing this revelation, trembled violently. His eyes looked lost. Decimated. Absolutely shattered as he shook his head with broken whisper.","\"I... I knew her differently. All the memories I retained portrayed her as kind to me and others. She would confide in us. Share her Everythings of anger, of misery, of doubt. We were...\"","...!","What he thought he knew about his previous Master crumbled rapidly.","Malphas seemed almost defeated by this revelation!","Nearby, Heidrun moved closer, nudging his hand gently with her muzzle to provide wordless consolation.","Yoshinami hesitantly raised her hand as she awkwardly patted the butler’s shoulder with uncharacteristic gentleness.","Noah sighed as he articulated his measured observation.","\"Nobody reveals their true nature easily. Even those closest to us can witness entirely different faces than what actually exists beneath surface presentation. Masks are universal...worn by weak and powerful alike.\"","His voice carried weight of promise.","\"In the future, if and when we grow sufficiently capable... I will see about the possibility of arranging a face-to-face encounter with THE Living Emotive herself. And just as she stepped on you and called you an insect... if you possess it within your existence to reciprocate such treatment... I will attempt to make that outcome possible.\"","...!","BOOM !","His words discussed such terrifying prospect casually... as if confronting THE entity was merely a future logistical challenge rather than suicidal impossibility.","Malphas trembled as he nodded absently...as if he hadn’t truly processed the statement and remained locked in internal turmoil.","Noah turned toward the newcomer.","Riya.","He saw her melancholic expression clearly as his own demeanor shifted. His eyes narrowed as he spoke with directness.","\"Really? You’re telling me there’s absolutely no change? Nothing at all?\"","He could read her existence with precision unlike Kael and her father who remained oblivious to what she alone perceived.","Her entire existence was surrounded by melancholy as at this moment, the normally bright Riya nodded with an exhausted expression.","\"With Civilization Specialization creating such a terrifying explosion of accumulated power... with all these newly rising entities capable of forming a glorious Bastion of Mana... every time I witness all these magnificent developments occurring around you, all these incredible achievements you continue accomplishing...\"","She paused with visible strain.","\"I check for the brilliance of Mana in the future. And... even now, Mana still dims . It doesn’t make sense. It truly doesn’t make any logical sense given what we’re achieving...\"","Her voice dropped to near-whisper.","\"The only change I can perceive is that Mana doesn’t disappear completely anymore. Instead of total extinction, 99% of the brilliant sun that is Mana gets snuffed out. Only embers remain flickering in darkness where blazing glory should persist.\"","...!","Noah absorbed this information as his eyes flashed with coldness.","So even with all this, everything still collapses?","And only glimmer of my Civilization survives because it’s Primordial?","Only for me to emerge like Khor or THE Dead Order...returning from near-total dissolution in some distant era?","\"...\"","His gaze was absolutely frigid.","It truly didn’t make sense that with all this unprecedented progress, the only change manifesting was... not complete collapse.","But even while hearing this devastating assessment, it still didn’t alter what he planned to do.","I will continue regardless. I will advance until either I succeed or existence itself prevents further progression.","Riya reached out toward Noah at this moment. Her blue eyes showed exhaustion from being the only one who continued feeling Mana dimming in future, a burden she carried alone while others celebrated victories.","Her voice emerged as quiet plea.","\"Can you...keep me company for a bit? Just to occupy my mind with something other than watching everything we’re building fade into darkness?\"","...!","Could he keep her company.","Noah’s hardened gaze softened at such vulnerable request.","He looked at this gorgeous woman before him as...","He scooped her into his arms with a smooth motion.","She closed her hands around his neck gratefully as she laid her head against his chest, seeking comfort from the one anchor that remained constant regardless of what futures she perceived.","Noah turned to Malphas as he spoke with firm authority.","\"Take time to process what you’ve learned. Let me know if you require anything. Unlike your previous Master who viewed you as disposable insect... I consider you one of the more capable existences surrounding me. You can achieve unfathomable immensity that THE Living Emotive could never have imagined possible.\"","...!","Malphas nodded with an expression mixing devastation and gratitude.","Noah took single step and disappeared in the next moment.","Because as always in existence, you had to make time for little things.","Sometimes the little things made existence fulfilling.","The golden grasses swayed in breeze as Malphas remained kneeling...supported by Heidrun and Yoshinami.","---","In The Transcendent Law Folds.","In The Heart of Law.","Inside a coliseum-like structure filled with rising white marbled pillars that stretched toward impossible heights. The sleek silver marbled floor reflected ambient light with mirror-like perfection. Multiple statues of legendary Dukes of Law surrounded the space...each one carved with meticulous detail depicting figures who had shaped Law’s history across eons.","At the center of such magnificent architecture sat Alexander and Seraphina Valorheart on thrones arranged around silver marbled table.","The figures of Dukes of Law composing the Kleos Council could be observed scattered throughout...standing amidst pillars with expressions mixing anticipation and mounting tension.","Near Alexander stood Malphas in his characteristic butler attire.","He looked upward suddenly as if perceiving something others couldn’t detect yet.","\" The Master arrives.\"","...!"]},{"number":4476,"title":"Chapter 4476: Chapter 4475: Pathos III","paragraphs":["Space cracked violently as Noah emerged from the dimensional tear with grace.","His descent was measured. Controlled. Alexander and Seraphina rose from their thrones immediately.","Noah smiled calmly and proceeded to sit on another throne opposite them without requesting permission or waiting for invitation.","He looked at both Alexander and Seraphina as his smile widened.","\"It seems you two were successful in your endeavors? I was rooting for you, Seraphina.\"","Noah articulated this with knowing amusement.","Because in the past, when he had encountered these two in Aeternitas Concordia, he had advised Alexander how one man’s heart could be tied to multiple women without betraying any of them.","It seemed his philosophy had infected The Peacemaker successfully!","After his words, Seraphina Valorheart visibly relaxed, as if confirming he remained the same entity they had met all those days ago.","Alexander also breathed out with relief, his gaze affirming Noah held no connections to THE Loom despite the terrifying power he and his forces displayed.","Alexander’s words emerged with measured directness.","\"I did not anticipate the absolutely terrifying power that your forces and you personally seem to be wielding. This creates certain possibilities that I believed would only become viable weeks or months down the timeline after my own substantial personal advancement.\"","His eyes gleamed with calculated hope.","Noah looked toward Alexander as he nodded.","\"Oh? What possibilities?\"","Alexander continued.","\"In the Earliest Folds during the initial conflicts, when forces of THE Living Emotive and THE Living Paradox were systematically deployed... The Primordial Civilization of THE Living Law was targeted specifically by combined armies of Emotive and THE Living Elemental.\"","He paused deliberately.","\"Some of the more powerful components of Law’s forces were scattered during systematic assault. The major battle had already occurred, THE Heart of Law itself was decimated and fractured through combined assault from THE Living Paradox and THE Living Emotive working in coordination.\"","His expression grew somber.","\"In that catastrophic engagement that followed, the armies of Emotive and Elemental pursued the surviving vestiges of Law who were desperately carrying a shattered fragment of THE Heart of Law itself, attempting to preserve it from complete annihilation.\"","Alexander leaned forward.","\"For the sake of saving one of the remaining vestiges of his collapsed Civilization along with that precious fragment... THE Living Law instituted an Existential Injunction and froze everything and everyone.\"","His voice intensified.","\"The vestiges of his own collapsed Civilization holding the shattered Heart fragment... and the pursuing armies of Emotive and Elemental that would have systematically eliminated them... all were frozen across eons of time and contained in what’s called the Injunction Sanctuary of Law.\"","He placed his hand on his chest.","\"Countless powerful Living Laws have been frozen there across incomprehensible duration, still holding the shattered fragment they were trying to preserve. But frozen alongside them are the terrifying armies that would have annihilated them completely.\"","At this critical point, Alexander looked toward Noah with eyes shining.","\"I have obtained the inheritance of THE Living Law . This Injunction Sanctuary represents something I was planning to reclaim after growing sufficiently powerful over coming weeks and months.\"","His voice dropped.","\" THE Remnant Will of THE Living Law itself expressed profound regret that we lack time . That if we possessed sufficient duration to systematically reclaim the shattered Heart fragment and other scattered components of the collapsed Civilization... there existed genuine possibility of reconstituting power close to or exactly at THE entity level.\"","He shook his head.","\"Power sufficient to withstand The Fallout entirely. But THE Living Law was woeful that time remains insufficient. That I wouldn’t reach Sextillions and Septillions in Complexity fast enough through conventional advancement.\"","His gaze fixed upon Noah with intensity.","\"But you... it appears your forces alone already operate at those power levels. If we assault this Injunction Sanctuary together... the terrifying armies of Emotive and Elemental frozen within...forces that should range within Sextillions in Complexity...we may actually prove capable of systematically collapsing them.\"","His voice carried weight of proposal!","\"We could save the collapsed Civilization of Law. I could obtain the shattered Heart fragment and potentially begin to reconstitute THE Living Law’ s power. What do you think?\"","...!","Beside him, Seraphina Valorheart looked visibly tense as this monumental proposition was said.","The Dukes of Law scattered throughout the coliseum appeared even more strained...several possessed ashen faces as if they desperately hoped this conversation would proceed differently.","As if they didn’t want the weavings of Law to be shared with others!","Noah maintained his focused gaze on Alexander as he eventually nodded with calm finality.","\"I have armies being forged just waiting to be directed at appropriate targets. Acceptable. I will join in on this fun.\"","...!","His simple agreement caused Alexander’s face to relax substantially, though caution remained.","\"It will be extraordinarily dangerous. The forces of Emotive and Elemental frozen in that Sanctuary represent genuine Primordial Civilizations before most withdrew into THE Loom. The engagement will be absolutely brutal.\"","Noah’s smile only widened at such warning as he responded with tyrannical satisfaction.","\"I appreciate brutality above most other approaches. Come. Let us prepare for the assault.\"","...!","---","Inside The Early Veiled Shore.","In the Abode of The Early Creature, Osmont.","Inside an isolated domain of this abode.","Different layers of seas composed of blue-gold Primus Mana stretched across the space endlessly. Radiant rays of concentrated blue-gold light permeated everything...filling the domain with ambient glow that pulsed rhythmically.","At the very center of such magnificent space, Noah’s figure could be observed lying atop the surface of the radiant sea. His toned physique was bare as a veil of concentrated Primus Mana covered him and the figure of Riya snuggled contentedly in his arms.","As if this moment stripped away some of the many burdens weighing on her existence.","Noah’s eyes remained clear as he contemplated the conversation another instance of himself had just conducted with Alexander.","\"An Injunction Sanctuary of Law ...\"","He raised his hand upward as he looked at the infinite seas of Primus Mana stretching above and below...thinking about how the Specialists of his Primordial Civilization would receive opportunity to be deployed against forces from genuine Primordial Civilizations.","The same Civilizations whose leaders I just witnessed discussing THE Loom’s construction through Malphas’s recovered memories...","Glorious!"]},{"number":4477,"title":"Chapter 4477: Chapter 4476: Pathos IV","paragraphs":["As he contemplated these implications, his existence began buzzing with intensity.","Above him, the infinite seas of blue-gold began trembling and vibrating violently as even grander waves of accumulated harvest began flowing from conceptual heights.","They crashed down onto Noah with tremendous force!","Prompts materialized with systematic precision.","|The elevated 20% harvest of Everything related to Mana and Hunger across Observable Existence has reached the set harvesting threshold and is being systematically collected through Existential Communication and Permeation.|","|The substantial harvest generated by the resurgence of The Primordial Civilization of Law has been collected and processed.|","|The accumulated efforts and harvest of your rapidly advancing Civilization have been consolidated.|","|All collected essence flows into The Walls of Your Civilization, specifically into The Architect’s Bulwarks for systematic integration.|","|CONSOLIDATION IN PROGRESS...|","...!","Noah stared directly at the approaching harvest as it smashed into his existence with overwhelming force.","His power began surging upward with dramatic velocity!","Even without closing his eyes to perceive his manifested Civilization directly, he could feel the walls of The Architect’s Bulwarks rising, becoming substantially more fortified, more impenetrable.","Additional prompts bloomed before his vision.","|The Architect’s Bulwarks have undergone substantial elevation through accumulated harvest integration.|","|Protection Threshold Increased: 3 Sextillion to 21 Sextillion|","|Any entity wishing to harm your existence must now exceed 21 Sextillion offensive power while also being member of established Civilization.|","|CRITICAL NOTATION: A fundamental component of your existence has been detected as fused with a Member of your Civilization who has undergone unique Specialization.|","|The harvest flowing into the fused entity (Protos) through symbiotic connection is being amplified tremendously due to Civilization Specialization multiplicative effects.|","|Protos’s Complexity and Purity after all amplifications through Civilization Specialization mechanics: Increased by 108 Sextillion from this harvest cycle.|","|Updated Total for Protos: 153 Sextillion|","|Your combined Complexity and Purity: 174 Sextillion|","Noah absorbed these specifications as his smile widened with tyrannical satisfaction.","Even though Specialists appear to gain tremendous benefits from Civilization mechanics... I will always advance further. I will always claim grander boons...","Final prompts materialized with additional critical information.","|The Boon of Major Mana and Hunger Bulwark has undergone substantial elevation.|","|Previous Boon Value: 300 Quintillion Complexity and Purity|","|Updated Boon Value: 1 Sextillion Complexity and Purity|","|After applied through amplifications and elevations of Civilization Specialization mechanics, Specialists receiving this Boon are projected to gain effective power ranging from 12 Sextillion to 40+ Sextillion depending on:|","|— Their Civilization Specialization Potential classification|","|— How many Specialization paths they have integrated into their existence|","|— Synergistic effects between multiple Specializations|","|Your Civilization’s power distribution has become catastrophically elevated.|","...!","After these revelations concluded...","BOOM!","The snuggling figure of Riya erupted with concentrated power!","The surrounding existence vibrated and trembled at her sudden brilliance. Noah gazed at her with analytical focus as he perceived her Complexity and Purity had just surged dramatically.","59 Sextillion!","Her hair pulsed with liquid blue-gold Mana flowing through each strand like living rivers. Her eyes shone as if releasing immense waves of concentrated brilliance that illuminated everything around them.","She felt such terrifying power coursing through her framework as she stretched luxuriously and looked at Noah’s rested figure.","Her smile turned devilish as she spoke with a playful challenge.","\"It seems I’m sufficiently energized to continue, Ancestor. Come on, don’t make me wait!\"","Waves of blue-gold Mana covered the region as an Ancestor was challenged directly.","And he accepted that challenge with enthusiasm.","His other instances moved across different aspects of existence preparing for numerous objectives.","One of those being thr potential confrontation with forces from Primordial Civilizations that had been frozen across eons.","And then...","The Vessels of THE Living Paradox continued being searched for without success yet.","His Primus Inevitabilities continued spreading across all territories.","His Civilization expanded relentlessly!","---","Effort and failure.","Many across existence poured tremendous quantities of effort into their pursuits.","They cultivated systematically. They planned meticulously. They sacrificed everything they possessed toward achieving objectives they deemed worthy.","And yet regardless of what they accomplished, regardless of all accumulated effort...","They seemed to progress nowhere.","Failure after failure.","Some proclaimed that as long as you invested sufficient effort, your results would eventually be rewarded proportionally.","Which begged the fundamental question...What of the rewards for those who invested countless efforts as they now lay collapsed in endless darkness?","What fruit did their effort bear if they experienced only systematic failure until their existence ceased?","A question along these lines was asked...in the Earliest Folds.","A particularly brilliant Fold Dweller sat beside THE Creature near modest hut inside vast shore stretching infinitely.","Before them, THE Creature had summoned several Inevitabilities who were nudging their tentacles against his hand affectionately...as if they were beloved pets seeking attention.","Anaximander watched this unexpected scene with genuine fascination.","At such moment, Anaximander posed question that had been troubling him since he began talking to THE Creature.","\"If your Way is The Way of Existence itself... do the efforts of every lifeform elevate your framework? Or only the efforts that successfully bear visible fruit?\"","At such inquiry, THE Creature’s response emerged.","\" All effort bears fruit without exception. The effort that culminates in success bears fruit. The effort that results in failure also bears fruit. There isn’t a single entity across existence that invests effort... where that effort fails to produce fruit of some nature.\"","He paused deliberately.","\" Effort will always, unequivocally, bear fruit. Now, the specific form that fruit manifests as... is sometimes not immediately known or properly understood by those who generated the effort. But I benefit from all effort regardless of whether the one exerting it perceives success or failure.\"","Anaximander absorbed such words with characteristic focus before nodding slowly.","THE Creature continued with an expression growing more contemplative.","\" One of the existences who has invested the most sustained effort while facing supposed failure after failure... he is known as The First Farmer. I pitied him profoundly. And unfortunately, my pity has already made him target for those who view my compassion as weakness to be exploited.\"","His voice carried mixture of respect and regret.","\"I envy the extraordinary level of effort that creature proved capable of continuing to invest... even after experiencing all his supposed failures. Failure after failure after failure, and he persisted regardless. He never surrendered. He never accepted defeat as final.\"","THE Creature’s gaze grew distant.","\" Now that represents genuine effort. And that accumulated effort through endless apparent failure... I am absolutely certain it will bear its own unique reward for him eventually. Perhaps not in forms he anticipated. Perhaps not in timelines he desired. But fruit will manifest from such persistent cultivation.\"","...!","The words carried profound weight as Anaximander simply listened.","---","In the current era.","In the Wandering Territories.","Inside the Sanctuary of The First Farmer.","The grave stood surrounded by dazzling plots of systematic cultivation, holding vibrant herbs that pulsed with concentrated life-force and Trees of Matured Principles that waved their branches gently to invisible wind.","Everything remained precisely as it should be.","And yet...","At this moment...","The silent grave of The First Farmer began shining.","Radiant verdant-gold brilliance erupted from the burial site!","A brilliance representing profound effort and systematic failure began blooming as heart-shaking aura started rising from the grave itself!","The accumulated effort of one who had failed countless times yet never surrendered was manifesting tangibly!","The moment such phenomenon commenced...","CRACK !","Space fractured violently above the grave as Noah’s figure materialized.","He looked down at the shining grave of The First Farmer with eyes that analyzed every detail of what was occurring.","Noah floated there silently, his gaze sharp as he sensed an immensity of existence erupting from this grave!"]},{"number":4478,"title":"Chapter 4478: Chapter 4477: Iskhus I","paragraphs":["Noah watched as the grave trembled and pulsed with mounting intensity.","Immensity could be felt radiating from within!","So profound that moments later...","Prompts materialized before his vision.","|A tremendous accumulation of effort and countless failures that have been systematically cultivated across eons are finally reaching ripening stage.|","|Conditions for unprecedented manifestation have been satisfied.|","...!","Noah absorbed this information with eyes shining brilliantly.","Inside his existence, the Principle of Perpetual Harvest buzzed with sudden intensity, beginning to permeate its green-gold radiance across his entire framework as if resonating with what was occurring below.","Through that resonance, even more detailed information flooded into his consciousness.","Additional prompts emerged with profound implications.","|Effort and failure exist as inseparable companions across all cultivation paths.|","|No entity in Observable Existence has invested comparable quantities of sustained effort while experiencing proportionally equivalent systematic failure as The First Farmer.|","|His most recent failure involved deviating from his established path, attempting alternative approaches despite accumulated expertise suggesting otherwise.|","|And yet, even in this unprecedented effort at innovation... he failed absolutely.|","|The culmination of an existence defined by cycles of immense effort and continued failure has concluded in ultimate failure, the complete collapse of his existence itself.|","|But his effort persists across eons regardless of physical dissolution.|","|His failures persist across eons as accumulated weight.|","|Boundless and unfathomable effort now blooms paradoxically from complete failure.|","|This is the fruit that effort bears when invested without surrender across incomprehensible duration.|","BOOM!","From the grave below, a radiant seed erupted upward with explosive force!","It appeared as extremely pristine celestial seed, almost resembling cocoon in its perfectly symmetrical construction. It shone with terrifying green brilliance that illuminated the entire Sanctuary with concentrated authority.","Noah felt immense Complexity and Purity emanating from such object as he observed it spinning gloriously in the skies above the Sanctuary of The First Farmer.","As it rotated with hypnotic precision...","It stopped suddenly.","And sank back down into the ground with deliberate motion.","The vast earth of this endlessly expansive Sanctuary trembled violently. A moment later, something began emerging from the area that had previously been simple grave.","A tree.","An utterly massive tree that vibrated with the concentrated light of an incredible Principle!","When Noah examined it with calmness, he could perceive its fundamental nature clearly.","A Singularity Principle!","Prompts emerged with clarifying details.","|From endless effort and systematic failure, the weavings of The First Farmer bloom him once more into existence.|","|This represents unprecedented emergence through accumulated cultivation rather than external intervention.|","|The fruit of his effort manifests as transformation of his entire existence into living embodiment of what he pursued across eons.|","The emergence of this terrifyingly vast tree representing Singularity Principle continued with dramatic progression.","At the base of the massive trunk, bark composed of concentrated green authority covered with golden leaf patterns, a hand suddenly erupted outward!","A figure began emerging from the glorious tree itself as if being born directly from accumulated effort given physical form.","Fair hands emerged first, gradually followed by entire form of middle-aged man who pulled himself free from the tree’s embrace.","His physique was laid bare initially. His skin was covered with countless green Glyphs that appeared like intricate tattoos painting elaborate patterns across every visible surface.","His eyes...","His eyes were terrifying golden beams of concentrated light that gazed around with intensity that illuminated vast lands surrounding the Sanctuary.","Those eyes eventually landed on the figure floating above, on Noah who had been silently observing this entire emergence.","They paused on him.","Blinked once.","Noah looked back with completely calm expression that rapidly became stone-faced as he processed what he was witnessing.","The entity who had just emerged blinked again with apparent confusion before looking down at his own body.","He seemed to gradually recognize that it remained completely bare.","Noah’s cold-faced gaze conveyed unmistakable sentiment without requiring verbal articulation.","As if he was saying...","Dude. Why are you walking around with your junk hanging out?","In the next moment, The First Farmer waved his hand with a slightly embarrassed gesture.","Green robes materialized to cover his form, flowing garments that seemed woven from living plant matter and concentrated authority.","His figure began floating upward as he examined himself with expression mixing confusion and gradual comprehension of what had just occurred to his existence.","When he came to float directly before Noah, he simply looked at him.","Noah looked back with identical calm assessment.","The two did not speak. They simply analyzed each other with mutual recognition that words would be premature until proper evaluation concluded.","Noah’s eyes flashed as he systematically observed the specifications of the entity before him.","A status sheet materialized with comprehensive details.","|The First Farmer|","|— The Cultivator of Endless Cycles|","|— He Who Failed Forward|","|— The Persistent One|","|— Architect of Ten Thousand Unsuccessful Harvests|","|— The One Who Would Not Surrender|","|Civilization Affiliations: An Unknown Budding Civilization)|","|COMPLEXITY AND PURITY: 100 Sextillion (Exactly)|","|CORE PRINCIPLE: The Singularity Principle of Perpetual Effort|","|PRINCIPLE DESCRIPTION: This Singularity Principle represents the accumulated weight of effort invested across eons regardless of outcome. It does not require success to generate power, only sustained commitment to continuous cultivation. Each failure feeds this Principle as much as each success. The more effort invested, the more powerful the wielder becomes regardless of whether that effort produces desired results.|","|UNIQUE CAPABILITIES:|","|— Effort Conversion: All energy invested toward any objective, successful or failed, converts to accumulated power|","|— Failure Immunity: Cannot be permanently collapsed as long as effort was genuinely invested|","|— Resurrection Through Persistence: Will manifest again after any collapse through accumulated effort across existence|","|— Unfathomable Endurance: Cannot be discouraged, demoralized, or convinced to surrender regardless of circumstances|","| This entity has undergone transformation from standard existence into living embodiment of his cultivated Principle. He IS Perpetual Effort given conscious form.|","...!","Noah absorbed these specifications with his expression remaining deliberately neutral.","100 Sextillion Complexity and Purity!","A Singularity Principle born from accumulated failure!","And as Noah looked at the Principle he embodied...","’Is this fucker just copying and pasting?’","...!","The details his new Principle, Perpetual Effort, were very much similar to Noah’s Principle of Perpetual Harvest!","But at the end of the day, even Perpetual Harvest stemmed from The First Farmer...","The First Farmer continued floating there, golden eyes examining Noah with equal analytical focus as if performing identical assessment."]},{"number":4479,"title":"Chapter 4479: Chapter 4478: Iskhus II","paragraphs":["Finally, The First Farmer spoke.","His voice sounded rusty from disuse but carried undeniable authority.","\"Thank you for what you did. For allowing events to unfold as they naturally progressed.\"","He paused, golden eyes flickering.","\"If I had not experienced that final failure... I may have continued failing effortfully for whatever duration remained before The Fallout concluded everything.\"","...!","Noah listened without reply.","The First Farmer continued with visible earnestness.","\"I do want to clarify something important. Yes, I did scheme against you...that remains an undeniable truth.\"","His expression tightened.","\"But regarding your analogy about catching me stealing simply representing the first time I was caught rather than first time I stole... suggesting I could have been stealing for eons past...\"","He shook his head firmly.","\"I truly did not steal repeatedly across my existence. What I did was simply another mistake that led to another failure.\"","His voice dropped.","\"Which ultimately... made way for my effort culminating in collapse itself. And even in that collapse, I paradoxically failed at dying and succeeded in emerging once more.\"","...!","His golden eyes shone with intensity.","\"And so my existence has risen while being systematically molded in the concentrated glow of effort.\"","He gestured at himself.","\"I don’t just pursue effort, I embody effort itself as I now cultivate the Singularity Principle of Perpetual Effort . My Way... is The Way of Effort.\"","The Way of Effort!","Noah heard this and titled his head as he voiced out slowly.","\"Effort? Are you sure about that? Why not The Way of Harvest?\"","\"...\"","The momentum of The First Farmer faltered as he looked intensly at Noah before he replied.","\"No. Effort. Effort is required before any Harvest. Effort is the backbone behind it all!\"","HUUM!","The First Farmer seemed set on Effort as Noah sighed internally and simply nodded. He just thought The Way of Harvest sounded better, but okay!","The First Farmer’s voice intensified with mounting conviction.","\"Regardless of success. Regardless of any harvest or reward. Endless perpetual effort will continue driving existence forward through sheer accumulated persistence.\"","He looked upward.","\"Effort was present when THE Creature established his immensity and incomprehensible power. Effort was there for all THE Living Existences when they founded their Primordial Civilizations.\"","His arms spread wide.","\"Effort was there for the Inevitabilities. Effort has persisted across incomprehensible eons!\"","...!","As he articulated these words with growing passion, the surrounding existence began buzzing .","Trembling.","A glorious symphony descended from conceptual heights, filling the Sanctuary with resonant harmonics.","Reality itself vibrated sympathetically!","From within that symphony, a single word began echoing with mounting intensity.","EFFORT! EFFORT! EFFORT!","The First Farmer’s declaration continued as the symphony swelled.","\"Effort was present even when all those monstrous beings founded their grand Civilizations!\"","His voice rang out.","\"And so on this day, after eons of accumulated cultivation, let it be witnessed that I officially follow my Way of Existence that I did not realize in my countless failures!\"","His arms spread wide with gesture encompassing everything.","\"I did not abandon farming, it will always remain fundamental component of my nature.\"","He smiled.","\"But the very core principle behind farming itself is effort! The persistent cultivation regardless of whether seeds germinate or harvests succeed!\"","His eyes blazed.","\"And so I walk The Way of Effort ! And so I shall establish... The Civilization of Effort!\"","...!","BOOM !","Pure radiant green light emanated from The First Farmer’s form.","It expanded outward in concentric waves that illuminated the entire Sanctuary with blinding brilliance!","Existence continued buzzing with validation.","The symphony bellowing the word \" EFFORT \" echoed across dimensional boundaries with such intensity that distant territories surely perceived the phenomenon!","Prompts materialized before Noah’s vision.","|A Derivative Way of Effort has been successfully established in your presence, bearing semblance of your influential authority.|","|The Derivative Way of Existence, specifically, The Way of Effort, has catalyzed emergence of a Derivative Primordial Civilization.|","|DESIGNATION: The Primordial Civilization of Effort|","|CLASSIFICATION : Derivative of The Primordial Civilization of Existence (THE Creature)|","|This Civilization will operate under umbrella authority of THE Creature’s framework while maintaining independent operational structure.|","|The First Farmer has been designated as The Primordial Sovereign of The Civilization of Effort.|","|Your observation and contribution for its establishment has created minor resonance with your own Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger.|","|Mana and Hunger were present during all moments of Effort across existence.|","...!","Noah absorbed these prompts with eyes shining brilliantly.","His existence buzzed with cascading questions.","A Derivative Way of Existence.","Similar to The Great Usurper!","The First Farmer had declared and founded his Civilization, and it manifested as a derivative falling under the bastion of THE Creature’s Primordial Civilization of Existence.","Noah’s mind raced.","Why is it that out of two beings I’ve personally witnessed establishing Ways... both connected as derivatives to something belonging to THE Creature?","When Noah had established his own Civilization of Mana and Hunger, it was his exclusively.","Not derivative of any overarching framework.","Independent. Self-sustaining.","So why did others’ attempts automatically connect to THE Creature’s authority?","His existence buzzed with immensity and mounting questions.","Though no immediate answers presented themselves.","He looked at the figure of The First Farmer with measured assessment.","\"I will accept your assertion that you were not a perpetual thief across eons.\"","His voice carried deliberate calmness.","\"And we can consider your temporary collapse sufficient repayment for your transgression against me.\"","Noah’s gaze was steady.","\"I always considered it wasteful that someone of your evident caliber, someone who had cultivated for incomprehensible duration supposedly pursuing righteous objectives...would simply collapse permanently.\"","His tone carried genuine acknowledgment!","\"It seemed like tremendous waste of accumulated potential. But if that collapse represented the final necessary component for your eons-long existence to bear ultimate fruit...\"","He nodded slightly.","\"Then perhaps everything worked out optimally after all.\"","...!","The First Farmer smiled with genuine appreciation.","He nodded with acceptance before his expression shifted to concern.","He began looking around the Sanctuary with searching gaze.","Golden eyes scanned every visible territory.","\"Where is my daughter?\"","His voice carried mounting worry.","\"I cannot sense Elyndra anywhere within this Sanctuary. Did something occur to her?\"","Noah blinked at this inquiry.","His expression became oddly neutral before replying with careful calmness.","\"She is currently... preoccupied with critical cultivation procedures.\"","The First Farmer tilted his head.","\"Preoccupied with what specifically? What procedure requires such focus that I cannot even perceive her presence?\"","Noah replied with straightforward directness.","\"Well, if you recall your original instructions... you did send her to me specifically for the purpose of gaining access to Perpetual Harvest.\"","He paused deliberately.","\"The objective was propelling her existence and her Nine Principles forward through systematic infusion of accumulated authority.\"","Another pause.","\"She is currently preoccupied with the... extensive infusion of Perpetual Harvest into her framework.\"","His tone remained clinical.","\"The process requires sustained focus and cannot be interrupted prematurely.\"","...!","His words were delivered with complete calm.","A clinical assessment devoid of suggestive subtext!","But when The First Farmer fully grasped their potential implications...","His eyes flashed with sudden immensity!","He looked at Noah with expression suggesting he was approximately three seconds from initiating violence!","Noah raised his eyebrows.","His expression almost communicated... Try it and discover exactly how that works out for you.","But instead, his voice emerged with firm authority.","\"Leave her be for now. She is at critical juncture in her transformation process.\"","His gaze was unyielding.","\"Disrupting her concentration could prove catastrophic. Let’s discuss you instead. With your return and emergence bearing this new Singularity Principle... do you possess any new information or methodologies for surviving against THE Loom?\"","He tilted his head slightly.","\"Anything beyond the admittedly limited plan of having your daughter somehow attain THE False designation?\"","...!","Did he have plans?","The First Farmer was confronted with such pointed inquiry mere moments after his resurrection.","His golden eyes focused with mounting intensity as he processed the question.","A moment later, shocking words emerged from his lips.","\"Well... in my state of dissolution and collapse, during that transition between existence and non-existence...\"","He paused, seemingly uncertain how to articulate it.","\"I actually heard the voice of THE Creature speaking directly to me.\"","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4480,"title":"Chapter 4480: Chapter 4479: Iskhus III","paragraphs":["The First Farmer said that he heard the voice of THE Creature.","Noah gazed at him calmly, waiting.","The First Farmer continued with a voice of weight of recovered memory.","\"In that state of collapse and emergence, I cannot accurately measure how much time passed across existence entirely. But for me personally, it felt instantaneous.\"","He paused, golden eyes distant.","\"In that instant, I remember the voice of THE Creature, the same voice I encountered in the past. That voice said to me simply... find my Early Veiled Shore.\"","...!","Find my Early Veiled Shore!","Noah looked closely at The First Farmer as he tilted his head with an expression mixing curiosity and frustration.","\"That’s it? That’s the entirety of the message?\"","The First Farmer nodded simply.","\"That’s it.\"","\"...\"","Noah continued gazing at The First Farmer with deliberate calmness as his mind worked through potential implications and interpretations.","\" THE Creature couldn’t add a few more words? Add a sentence or two to provide some measure of clarity? Perhaps a helpful direction or specific instruction?\"","\"...\"","The First Farmer simply looked at him with expression suggesting he shared identical frustration.","Neither possessed answers.","Eventually The First Farmer’s eyes blazed with a light combining effort and accumulated majesty as he articulated his speculation.","\" THE Creature represents the entity who was demonstrably strongest amongst all THE beings. Even if THE Living Paradox and THE Living Emotive , alongside any others who aligned with their conspiracy, successfully plotted against him... THE Creature would still possess numerous means of survival and contingency.\"","His voice carried conviction.","\"Maybe the genuine answer to surviving The Fallout resides within his Early Veiled Shore. Maybe that cryptic message contains everything necessary if we can only decipher it properly.\"","...!","Noah smiled coldly and shook his head as he absorbed this speculation from The First Farmer.","Maybe .","He was hearing that particular word with increasing frequency lately.","When Khor had used it, the uncertainty seemed almost endearing...cute, even.","But as more and more maybes accumulated without resolution...","It was rapidly ceasing to be something he enjoyed encountering.","He looked toward The First Farmer before speaking with direct inquiry.","\"Do you possess any tangible clues regarding where to commence an investigation? Any contextual details from your interaction with THE Creature that might prove relevant?\"","The First Farmer shook his head with genuine regret.","\"No. I shared but a single extended conversation with THE Creature before my collapse. My knowledge remains frustratingly limited.\"","His expression shifted to earnest appeal.","\"But with your aid and combined resources... I feel confident we can both substantially increase our respective chances of survival...not merely for ourselves but for our people as well.\"","His voice carried weight of responsibility.","\"I have countless entities across my Sanctuary who look toward me for guidance and protection. I have my daughter to whom I must make proper amends. I’m certain you possess your own responsibilities and people dependent upon your continued existence.\"","He gestured expansively:","\"I have just embarked upon establishing my Civilization of Effort. Now I must systematically forge it into something capable of enduring what approaches. For the benefit of both our Civilizations... collaboration can only increase and elevate our collective capabilities.\"","His golden eyes met Noah’s directly.","\"Are we able to let bygones be bygones and commence on entirely new page? Can we move forward as genuine allies rather than suspicious acquaintances?\"","The First Farmer articulated these words with calm earnestness.","Noah listened without interruption and did not require extended deliberation before simply nodding with acceptance.","He sighed and looked around the Sanctuary before speaking.","\"The more the merrier in this band of unfortunate survivors attempting to defy impossible odds. Tend to your Sanctuary and those who mourned believing you permanently collapsed.\"","His voice carried finality.","\"I will bring your daughter back to see you soon enough.\"","With such words, Noah disappeared.","Space folded around him and he was simply gone.","The First Farmer remained floating alone.","He gazed at the Sanctuary that had mourned him not long ago.","He was still The First Farmer at his core.","But now he was filled with immeasurable effort given conscious form.","And with every effort invested came even more unfathomable harvest as consequence.","I may not have succeeded in obtaining Perpetual Harvest directly...","But I was able to forge successfully the counterpart that was functionally equivalent.","Perpetual Effort.","He smiled with expression mixing sadness and profound satisfaction as he contemplated this truth.","His voice emerged as philosophical musing directed at existence itself.","\"Effort and harvest exist as two faces of singular principle. One cannot exist without the other across any meaningful duration.\"","He looked at the expanse before him, not merely Sanctuary anymore, but Civilization .","\"The farmer who plants seeds without effort produces no harvest. The farmer who exerts tremendous effort but fails to harvest wastes accumulated potential. But the farmer who understands that effort is harvest...that the act of cultivation itself represents fruit regardless of outcome...\"","His eyes shone with golden light.","\"That farmer transcends simple success or failure. That farmer embodies the eternal cycle itself. Plant. Tend. Fail. Learn. Plant again. Tend better. Fail differently. Learn more. Persist .\"","He spread his arms wide.","\"This is the Way of Effort. This is what I will teach to all who join my Civilization. Success matters less than persistence. Harvest matters less than cultivation. Results matter less than the willingness to continue despite results.\"","His smile widened.","\"And through that perpetual effort... harvest becomes inevitable. Perhaps not the harvest initially envisioned. Perhaps not the harvest desired. But harvest nonetheless...fruit born from persistence itself! Oh!\"","HUUM!","He descended toward his Civilization with renewed purpose.","Time to begin forging something worthy of surviving what approaches...","---","At this moment in time.","In Noah’s Early Veiled Shore.","The atmosphere within the vast continental landscape pulsed with vibrant energy that made the entire territory seem alive with concentrated authority.","The inhabitants carried distinct auras and colors radiating from their bodies that identified their Specialization paths immediately.","To match the three different Specializations currently available, the factions of The Iron Concordat, The Crimson Hunger, and The Verdant Cycle...different clusters of entities shone with corresponding brilliance.","Obsidian-gold radiance marked those who had chosen defensive paths.","Crimson-gold intensity identified offensive specialists whose presence made surrounding space tremble.","Verdant-gold luminescence surrounded support-oriented entities who pulsed with restorative authority.","Defensive, offensive, and support type entities whose attire now reflected their chosen factions!","The Specializations made everyone seem substantially more vibrant, more alive as they communicated enthusiastically with each other regarding optimal methods to leverage their collective capabilities.","Discussions occurred everywhere!","\"If three hundred Bulwarks establish the Fortress Formation while Hungering Maws attack...\"","\"Vital Chorus members should maintain Life-Binding with all frontline specialists to enable instant resurrection...\"","\"Damage Conversion from Bulwarks feeding directly into Hungering Maws...hey, why not feed all collected damage to a single entity rather than spread it around? Could maybe The Master unleash all devoured damage in the hundreds of Sextillions?\"","...!","The entire Shore buzzed with mounting excitement.","Within the influence of the Crimson Hunger Sovereign Spire of Osmont, two figures stood observing the organized chaos.","These two were the humanoid form of Hyperion and... Bob!","Little Bobby!","Hyperion maintained his characteristically cold gaze as he calmly observed everything with analytical detachment.","He turned slightly and happened to notice Bob standing nearby.","Bob looked distinctly forlorn and frustrated...his expression suggesting he’d just experienced personal defeat.","When Hyperion followed Bob’s gaze to identify what provoked such reaction...","He saw the figures of Henry talking vibrantly with two young women.","Henry was laughing, gesturing animatedly, clearly enjoying himself immensely.","Hyperion raised his eyebrows at such scene.","Even though he genuinely didn’t want to engage in conversation...","He forced himself to speak since proximity made silence awkward.","\"Did you attempt to compete with the son of our monstrous Leader in pursuing romantic interest and subsequently lose? That represents a losing battle from inception, my friend.\"","...!","At such words, Bob turned toward Hyperion with visible scowl.","\"One of those women is my daughter . I was absent just for brief period, and this guy simply swooped in and just...\"","Bob’s visage trembled with paternal frustration as words failed him.","Hyperion blinked and looked at him with an expression shifting to something approaching sympathy.","Eventually he raised his eyebrows and spoke with pragmatic observation.","\"Should you not be experiencing happiness rather than distress? Within our Civilization and broader existence, is there genuinely superior choice than the son of our monstrous Leader if your daughter was to establish a connection with anyone?\"","He paused deliberately.","\"Or... would you rather prefer it be with The Leader himself?\"","...!","At such casually delivered statement, Bob visibly shuddered as if experiencing visceral nightmare.","His round, circular bald head developed visible sweat as he nodded with rapid agreement.","\"Fuck. You’re absolutely right. You’re correct. That perspective helps somewhat...\"","He paused and blinked.","\"Who are you again?\"","Hyperion sighed with sn expression suggesting he couldn’t believe this conversation was even occurring.","\"Hyperion.\"","Bob nodded.","\"Bob.\"","Just as the two finished their perfunctory introductions, a booming voice echoed through the air with authority that made everyone stop their activities immediately.","Noah’s words rang out across the entire Early Veiled Shore with unmistakable command.","\"The time has arrived to subject our Civilization to a genuine trial! There exist enemies belonging to the Primordial Civilizations that we will soon be confronting directly.\"","His voice intensified.","\"Those who wish to participate in this engagement... adorn your Civilizational Armor immediately. Assemble together with your respective Civilization Specialization Faction and prepare for deployment.\"","The declaration carried finality.","\"The adversaries you will face during this operation will be the preserved forces of THE Living Emotive and THE Living Elemental, armies that have been frozen across eons and now await elimination.\"","...!","His words were booming and impossibly heavy.","All those who heard them looked upward and around as his voice seemed to echo from everywhere simultaneously, authority that couldn’t be ignored or dismissed.","Their eyes shone with mixture of anticipation and mounting determination.","Movement began blooming across the Early Veiled Shore as many responded to their Leader’s call!","Civilizational Armor manifested.","Specialists assembled with their factions.","A glorious war was coming.","And Noah’s Civilization was ready for a feast!"]},{"number":4481,"title":"Chapter 4481: Chapter 4480: Civilizational War! I","paragraphs":["Inside the Abode of The Early Creature, Osmont.","Inside an isolated domain.","The domain was breathtaking in its concentrated vitality.","Filled with vibrant green-gold fields of harvest that stretched endlessly across both earth and sky.","Above, the heavens themselves seemed to be cultivated plots...clouds shaped like ripening fruit, stars that pulsed with growing authority.","Below, grasses swayed with rhythm suggesting conscious appreciation of their existence.","In the center of this place stood Noah.","He had just finished the announcement declaring war to his assembled forces.","Behind him, the figure of Elyndra approached with graceful steps.","She was adorned in loose green gown that barely concealed her curvaceous figure, the fabric seeming to flow like living water across her form.","Her radiant golden hair cascaded like harvested wheat.","Her blue eyes shone with unique light mixing satisfaction and mounting curiosity.","She embraced Noah from behind with gentle warmth.","\"Is this why you said we would not be friends before?\"","Her voice carried playful understanding.","Noah tilted his head back and nodded lightly as he replied with characteristic directness.","\"This is substantially better than just being friends. How are you feeling?\"","Elyndra’s existence held 9 unique Principles carefully nurtured by The First Farmer.","She had been engineered specifically for pursuing THE False designation with sufficient harvest accelerating her advancement.","After Noah had infused her with tremendous quantities of accumulated harvest these last few hours...","Elyndra sighed contentedly as she closed her eyes and smiled before articulating her status.","\"My 9 Principles are resonating with unprecedented intensity and systematically opening a pathway toward something that should theoretically exceed even a Singularity Principle in fundamental classification.\"","Her voice carried mixture of wonder and analytical focus.","\"I’m not actively creating or designing it through conscious effort, simply being led toward it as if my 9 Principles function as set of stairs ascending toward something far grander. Once I successfully reach and grasp it, the entire staircase may crumble and dissolve as I claim something that transcends their individual existence.\"","She opened her eyes.","\"I’m extraordinarily close to achieving breakthrough. I just require slightly more accumulated resonance.\"","Her tone shifted to teasing.","\"How about you? What did you derive from our extensive connection? Apart from your relentless enjoyment of the process itself, obviously.\"","Noah smiled calmly at this inquiry as he observed the prompts that had bloomed before his vision.","The information was remarkable.","|Through sustained connection and deep resonance with unique lifeform possessing complementary Principles, The Way toward grasping a Principle exceeding the rank of Singularity has opened before you.|","|Analysis indicates the potential Principle to be grasped is estimated to be something deeply integral to the fundamental structure of Observable Existence itself.|","|Successfully grasping such Principle would further enhance your capability to alter and systematically violate existence in unfathomable ways that transcend current limitations.|","|Progress toward manifestation: 67%|","|Additional resonance required for complete breakthrough.|","...!","The results were extraordinarily promising!","So he simply replied to Elyndra with measured satisfaction.","\"I benefited substantially. We can continue our mutual advancement in a bit.\"","His tone shifted to more immediate concern.","\"For now, manifest a clone of yourself and send it to The Sanctuary of The First Farmer immediately.\"","...!","At these unexpected words, Elyndra blinked with visible confusion.","\"Oh? Did something significant occur? Is everyone safe? Did complications arise?\"","As she articulated these concerns, brilliance shone across her body.","A perfect clone manifested beside her, identical in every visible aspect.","The clone became adorned in verdant-gold dress that flowed elegantly.","Her hair arranged itself with practiced motion into elaborate style.","Noah tapped toward empty space nearby with a casual gesture.","A spatial rift bloomed obediently, a tear in reality leading directly to The Sanctuary.","He simply nodded.","\"It should constitute a significant surprise for you. Go and discover what awaits.\"","With such cryptic encouragement, Elyndra’s clone transformed into streak of brilliant light.","She disappeared into the rift without hesitation!","She would be met with the impossible surprise of a Father who had somehow returned from complete collapse.","Meanwhile, her main body remained with Noah.","She sat down with worried expression mixing hope and concern.","Noah lay his head on her lap with comfortable familiarity, closing his eyes as if preparing to nap casually.","But internally, he was gauging his own accumulated strength with analytical precision!","His power.","At this particular moment, his power derived fundamentally from his Civilization and all its integrated components.","The simple measurement of Sextillions of Complexity and Purity represented only single aspect of his total capability.","Some observers might incorrectly examine his numerical measurements and notice that Khor, another Leader within his Civilization, possessed ostensibly higher raw Complexity and Purity values.","They might question with confusion...How could another Leader of a Civilization subordinate to him possess more measured Complexity and Purity than him?! Shouldn’t the supreme Leader always maintain the highest numerical values?!","And yet, such perspective would be fundamentally missing the critical strategic point.","Many hours ago, Noah had actively decided not to focus on merely elevating numerical values of Complexity and Purity.","He had deliberately redirected his accumulated Harvest away from personal power metrics...","And channeled it systematically into elevating his overall Civilization’s framework!","Complexity and Purity emerged as natural byproduct for him as he guided the Walls of his Civilization forward and elevated his entire structure to its current unprecedented stage.","And even when he wasn’t actively focusing on personal Complexity and Purity...","His total measurement alongside his permanently fused Protos already exceeded 170 Sextillion.","If he were to deliberately redirect accumulated Harvest away from strengthening The Architect’s Bulwarks and toward pure personal power amplification...","He possessed no doubt whatsoever that he could rapidly gain sufficient Complexity to completely eclipse any other entity within his Civilization.","But as he had systematically learned...","Complexity and Purity wasn’t everything.","Due to him strategically elevating his overall Civilization and successfully unlocking Civilization Specialization mechanics...","He now commanded countless specialized entities with power levels measuring in dozens of Sextillions each.","Just consider The Primus Inevitabilities alone.","100 Million would complete their production cycle within 24 hours.","12 hours had already elapsed since their systematic generation commenced.","There were currently 50 Million Primus Inevitabilities manifested, floating like massive obsidian-blue-and-gold-crimson cloud across the Sanctuaries of Inevitabilities within the Early Veiled Shore!","The ones who had specialized into The Infinite Bulwark Specialization alone possessed average power of 10 Sextillion each by this point.","If this represented approximately one-third of 50 Million total...","That meant 16 Million Primus Inevitabilities who each held 10 Sextillion Complexity and Purity!","Every single one!","Now, every single defensive specialist, every single member of The Iron Concordat faction...","They all possessed simple core mechanical function that had been emphasized clearly during Specialization selection.","Total Offensive Sacrifice.","And what were its exact specifications again?","Noah recalled the prompt with perfect clarity.","|Total Offensive Sacrifice: Members of this Specialization lose 100% of their offensive capabilities. They cannot deal direct damage through any conventional or unconventional means. All attacks, abilities, and techniques designed to harm enemies are systematically removed from their framework. Any attacks directed toward Members of The Civilization are automatically drawn to and absorbed by Infinite Bulwark Specialists.|","Any attacks toward Members of The Civilization are automatically drawn to the defensive specialists.","Any .","So, before any hostile entity could ever even contemplate harming a single hair on Noah’s existence...","It would mean they had to successfully eliminate 16 Million Primus Inevitabilities who each possessed average of 10+ Sextillion Complexity and Purity!","\"...\"","Noah’s mind processed this mathematical reality with cold satisfaction.","Even if he hypothetically possessed only single point of Complexity and Purity...","Nothing would be capable of harming him until they systematically wiped out 16 Million defensive specialists who each held 10+ Sextillion worth of protection.","And that calculation only reflected current status.","In another 12 hours, this number would effectively double, and he could even triple or quadruple it if he simply ordered more of the Primus Inevitabilities to undergo the Infinite Bulwark Specialization.","This was what his Civilization granted him.","This was what strategically focusing on Civilization advancement rather than mere individual Complexity and Purity provided!","The fact that even now, he could theoretically withstand cumulative damage equivalent to 16 Million times 10 Sextillion...","Made things extraordinarily clear regarding where he needed to continue directing his accumulated Harvest!","Because what exactly was 16 Million multiplied by 10 Sextillion?","That mathematical product was...160 Octillion.","A value that completely exceeded Sextillion classification, entirely skipped Septillion tier, and landed firmly at Octillion magnitude!","This...","This was what was minimally required just to potentially injure Noah.","And that calculation didn’t even account for any defensive capabilities from his personal power!","This....was what elevating a Civilization systematically granted!","It was something utterly glorious.","After affirming this mathematical reality with satisfaction, Noah opened his eyes.","They flashed with brilliant intensity mixing anticipation and tyrannical confidence.","He would test and observe the immensity of this accumulated power as it faced genuine opposition...","The preserved forces of the Primordial Civilizations of Emotive and Elemental!","He genuinely hoped there would be numerous enemies who exceeded hundreds of Sextillions in individual power.","So he could really stretch his legs and discover his true limits!","His smile widened with predatory satisfaction."]},{"number":4482,"title":"Chapter 4482: Chapter 4481: Civilizational War! II","paragraphs":["As things progressed toward readiness, Noah closed his eyes once more.","He relaxed against Elyndra’s thighs with comfortable familiarity.","His consciousness shifted focus toward another instance of himself, another body that was currently moving across The Wandering Territories.","It was time to see what ancient forces await within the frozen domain!","---","The Wandering Territories.","The figures of Alexander Asmodeus and Seraphina Valorheart stood surrounded by hundreds of thousands of the most powerful Living Laws.","Sheer numbers meant nothing to the enemies they were about to face!","The most powerful Dukes of Law circled around them in protective formations.","The scene was filled with palpable tension...as if they were all preparing to open Pandora’s box that could systematically destroy them all.","The surroundings defied conventional description.","Multicolored oddities and impossible geometries filled the environment in every direction.","Floating crystalline structures that shifted through spectrum of colors without pattern.","Streams of liquid light flowing upward against gravity.","Fragments of reality suspended in configurations.","Ground that wasn’t quite solid, more like concentrated probability given temporary substance.","The Wandering Territories lived up to their name...territories that wandered through existence without stable anchor.","Seraphina’s voice emerged with hesitation that she clearly struggled to contain.","\"Alexander, are we certain about this course of action? Opening the Injunction Sanctuary represents unprecedented risk as if we cannot overcome them...\"","Her crimson eyes reflected mounting concern.","\"Why...do you trust Osmont so completely?\"","Alexander looked at her calmly.","His reply was simple. Direct.","\"We come from the same place, Seraphina.\"","He paused deliberately.","They came from the same place. That was it?!","As they continued their quiet discussion...","Space rippled nearby.","The entrance was dramatic without being ostentatious.","Noah arrived.","Alone.","He was adorned in emperor’s robe woven from obsidian-gold material that seemed to absorb and reflect light simultaneously.","His hair shone with obsidian-cold allure that made it appear carved from precious stone.","But his eyes...","His eyes held sense of immensity and ancientness that transcended his apparent physical age.","Even though he appeared here without visible entourage or escort...","The mere pressure he emanated seemed to suffocate all the Living Laws present!","As if the moment he arrived, all routes through existence began rotating around him and nobody else.","He felt like ancient entity whose visage alone would command existence wherever he manifested.","The hundreds of thousands of Living Laws felt their frameworks trembling involuntarily.","Many struggled not to collapse to their knees from sheer proximity to such concentrated authority.","Noah simply nodded toward Alexander after his arrival with casual acknowledgment.","Alexander’s voice emerged with practical inquiry.","\"Your forces?\"","His forces.","At such question, Noah waved his hand with dismissive gesture.","Behind him, space tore apart violently as three massive rifts formed simultaneously!","The rifts were glorious in their construction.","Each one spanning hundreds of meters in diameter.","Edges crackling with concentrated authority that made surrounding reality distort.","The first rift pulsed with obsidian-gold radiance.","The second burned with obsidian-crimson intensity.","The third glowed with verdant-gold luminescence.","And from these three massive rifts...","Noah’s forces began emerging.","The specialists of The Iron Concordat, The Crimson Hunger, and The Verdant Cycle factions materialized through their respective portals.","Each entity looked like massive titan already fully armored in their Civilizational Armor.","But more than that, they manifested in complete forms representing their Civilization Specializations!","The Infinite Bulwark specialists emerged like living fortresses.","Covered in layered crystalline plates of obsidian-gold that overlapped with sophisticated precision.","Eyes glowing with steady silver light.","Each step causing minor reality stabilization effects.","The Hungering Maw specialists manifested as predatory nightmares!","Sleek forms covered in crimson-obsidian tentacles that writhed with barely contained aggression.","Multiple serrated maws visible across their bodies.","Eyes burning with ravenous crimson light.","The Vital Chorus specialists radiated restorative authority.","Wreathed in green-gold-blue light that pulsed like heartbeat.","Covered in intricate mandala patterns that glowed with healing power.","Eyes shining with compassionate emerald brilliance.","The terrifying immensity and concentrated power they all emanated was overwhelming .","It appeared as if three different colored armies were systematically pouring through the rifts.","One massive force shining obsidian-gold.","Another burning obsidian-crimson.","The last glowing verdant-gold.","They continued flooding out of the rifts with systematic precision.","Until a terrifying monstrous army of 5 million from each faction had fully manifested!","A combined force of 15 Million total entities!","It was utterly excessive, complete overkill for any normal engagement.","And even this represented only portion of the forces Noah could deploy!","The vast majority of these fifteen million were, naturally, Primus Inevitabilities who had undergone Specialization.","But the sheer visual spectacle of five million entities colored and armored identically showed glorious depiction of three separate armies moving under unified command.","One faction displayed armaments that pulsed with obsidian-gold shields emblazoned on their chests.","Another bore crimson-gold jaws as identifying markers.","The Vital Chorus carried verdant-gold wings surrounded by leaves as their symbol.","The moment of their complete arrival...","The Living Laws in the surroundings felt such terrifying sense of oppression that many of them trembled violently!","Several actually did collapse to their knees despite attempts to maintain composure.","The pressure was simply too overwhelming to resist entirely.","Alexander looked at this incomprehensible display of military force.","He shook his head with mixture of awe and disbelief.","\"Fucking hell... okay. Let’s proceed with this operation.\"","There was no more questioning whether they possessed sufficient forces.","No more wondering if they’d brought adequate power.","Seeing the terrifying army arrayed behind Noah gave everyone present such profound sense of suffocation...","They were wholly, utterly glad they weren’t his enemies.","Amongst those in the assembled army, Khor floated forward with grace.","Behind her, the figures of Sigrid, Riya, Barbatos, and numerous others could be observed. Not entirely adorned in their Civilizational Armors yet.","Noah nodded toward Alexander with gesture indicating readiness.","Alexander turned to face the empty space of the Wandering Territories stretching before them.","His voice emerged with formal gravitas as he explained.","\"The Injunction Sanctuary of Law represents a domain frozen across eons of time through concentrated power of THE Living Law themselves. It does not possess preset physical location that one can simply travel toward to arrive.\"","He raised his hand","\"One simply requires the key. And with the inheritance I obtained from THE Living Law’s remnant will... I possess that key.\"","His expression grew serious.","\"The moment I activate this key, the Injunction Sanctuary, which currently exists in state without set position, will become anchored to this location. A gateway shall manifest for us to make entry.\"","His tone darkened.","\"That is when unfathomable danger will bloom. I cannot predict the numbers of enemies contained within that frozen domain. I cannot estimate how ridiculously powerful these entities were at time of their imprisonment.\"","He paused deliberately.","\"And whether after being frozen across eons of time... they have somehow become even more powerful through unknown mechanisms, or remained in perfect stasis.\"","His voice carried mounting concern.","\"Something that troubles me substantially is that their parent Civilizations within THE Loom have continued advancing over all these eons. The moment these frozen forces are released from THE Living Law’s imposed stasis...\"","He looked troubled.","\"Whatever boons Members of their Civilizations...genuine Members like them, not the diluted Living Existences populating current Folds, may receive through accumulated advancement...\"","His gaze fixed on Noah.","\"All of this remains unknown. And because of these fundamental unknowns... we will depend heavily upon your forces.\"","He turned fully toward Noah after finishing his explanation.","Noah nodded calmly with expression suggesting such uncertainties didn’t concern him remotely.","Unknown variables simply meant opportunity for extraordinary harvest.","Variables were part of existence.","After all preparations concluded, Alexander breathed in deeply.","He stretched his hand out toward empty space.","His voice emerged with formal authority!","\" Justice delayed is justice denied. No existence stands above the Law’s reach... so let the Law impose itself systematically on the unworthy. Open.\"","...!","HUUM !","Radiant silver-white brilliance erupted from his outstretched hand!","It sprayed outward across the Wandering Territories like tidal wave of concentrated authority!","In the next moment...","Existence itself splintered directly before them!","A silver-white massive doorway spanning entire Gigaparsec bloomed into manifestation, covering absolutely everything in their collective vision!","The gateway was incomprehensibly vast.","Its edges extended beyond what eyes could track.","Its surface rippled with concentrated temporal authority.","An aura of profound ancientness and terrible immensity erupted from this doorway!","It rushed outward like horrendous winds carrying scent of eons-old conflicts!","Noah observed it with characteristic calm as prompts bloomed before his vision.","|Something that has been systematically locked away for eons since the conflicts in the Earliest Folds has been unlocked.|","|For good or for catastrophe, this action cannot be reversed.|","|The forces contained within represent genuine Primordial Civilization military strength from era when THE entities actively waged war.|","The words seemed grand and profoundly ominous.","But Noah’s eyes flashed with pure tyranny as he raised his hands.","He formed them into fists with deliberate motion.","The figure of Protos materialized beside him with terrifying presence.","Ahead of them both, the figure of Ozymandias, his other body, floated forward.","Ozymandias spoke in extremely deep and heavy voice that caused existence of all assembled forces to vibrate with resonance:","\"What...is your duty?\"","...!","And from the 15 Million terrifying beings arrayed in systematic formations...","Their fists rose as single unified motion!","Their voices boomed outward with such concentrated force that even the terrifying ancient winds rushing from the newly formed gateway were actually forced backward!","\" OUR DUTY! IS MANA AND HUNGER!\"","BOOM !","The declaration struck existence like physical impact!","Ozymandias continued voicing commands with cold authority that brooked no hesitation.","\"Fullfil your duty.\"","BOOM !","The moment these words were uttered...","Brilliance of blue-gold radiance shone across all assembled forces!","Members of The Iron Concordat surged forward toward the massive gateway with systematic precision, living walls advancing to establish a defensive perimeter!","Followed immediately by The Crimson Hunger specialists whose predatory forms streaked forward like crimson lightning!","The Verdant Cycle maintained position slightly behind, ready to provide resurrection and restoration the moment casualties occurred!","It was glorious and utterly epic scene that many would struggle to comprehend or believe unless witnessing it directly in that exact moment!","Fifteen million specialized entities charging toward a gateway containing forces from genuine Primordial Civilizations!","The Living Laws watched with mixture of awe and absolute terror.","Alexander smiled grimly.","\"Into the breach. Let’s discover what horrors await inside.\"","The gateway pulsed as Noah’s forces poured through.","And somewhere in the frozen domain beyond...","Ancient enemies stirred from eons-long slumber!"]},{"number":4483,"title":"Chapter 4483: Chapter 4482: Civilizational War! III","paragraphs":["Far from the massive silver-white gateway that just opened.","In a region of existence hard to know or perceive.","Gold and obsidian radiance of Civilizational Authority of Paradox covered a box.","It could adequately be called Schrodinger’s Box.. existing in multiple states simultaneously.","Inside it, three bodies of Schrodinger lay in what appeared to be deep sleep.","At this moment, the Living Paradoxical body opened its eyes with immense effort.","The action seemed to require tremendous power just to accomplish such simple movement.","Those eyes revealed an extremely ancient will flowing through them, consciousness far older than the body suggested.","He seemed incapable of moving even a single muscle beyond opening his eyes.","And yet a smile formed on his lips.","His eyes curved with devilish glare mixing amusement and malicious satisfaction.","Those bright eyes of paradox seemed to see the distant silver-white gateway that had just been opened, perceiving it across impossible distances through mechanisms that defied conventional observation.","His voice emerged as amused whisper.","\" There was actually something like this that THE uptight Living Law actually concealed from my knowledge? And you all just... casually opened it? Hmm...\"","Even though he spoke, terrifying oppressive force pressed down from all around him.","The surrounding existence itself was crushing his awareness!","He rolled his eyes with exaggerated annoyance.","\" Okay, okay, I get the message. Your Existence remains sufficiently powerful even now to systematically suppress me outside THE Loom.\"","His smile widened despite the pressure.","\" But this won’t prevent me from having some modest fun while I wait patiently to harvest all my carefully cultivated efforts. I consider this... a side mission really. Just something to occupy my mind and keep me mentally engaged before The Fallout occurs.\"","His tone darkened.","\" Because after The Fallout does manifest... even I will need to remain on my tiptoes...\"","...!","His words carried terrifying implications about what exactly The Fallout represented.","After finishing addressing the oppressive surrounding existence, his smile became even more devilish.","\" Emotive and Elemental chicklets frozen in that Sanctuary, yes? Let’s have their parent Civilizations within THE Loom release some of their accumulated grandeur into their frozen subordinates who tragically missed their entry into salvation.\"","...!","The words were profoundly heavy and ominous.","The surrounding existence pressed down with even greater force!","The heavy eyelids of THE Living Paradox were forcefully closed by external pressure, his consciousness being systematically suppressed.","But he maintained his playful smile throughout.","As if he simply found all of this utterly, delightfully amusing .","Let them play their little war games.","The real entertainment comes after.","---","Past the massive silver-white gateway.","In the Injunction Sanctuary of Law.","Noah entered without any perceptible fear or hesitation.","Beside him, Khor floated with predatory grace.","Her voice emerged with barely contained anticipation.","\"I may go just a little bit wild this time around, Outsider. Fair warning.\"","At these words, Noah nodded calmly with an expression suggesting such behavior was not merely permitted but encouraged .","\"Go as wild as your nature demands. If we discover answers within this frozen domain, good. If there are no useful answers...\"","His smile turned tyrannical.","\"I’ll simply claim the harvest instead.\"","...!","His words pulsed with concentrated authority.","Brilliant silver-white light shone around them as existence began revealing itself with absolute clarity.","Noah and his assembled forces found themselves spilling out into...","Stretches of shattered fold canyons so incomprehensibly vast it felt less like geography and more like act of existential violence.","The floor was chaotic jumble of terrain types that shouldn’t coexist.","Radiant stellar dried Fold riverbeds that glowed with residual authority.","Broken mesas rising like shattered teeth.","The pulverized remains of entire Folds scattered like dust across impossible distances.","These fold canyons stretched outward for Gigaparsecs in all directions.","They shone with accumulated brutality from conflicts that had raged here eons ago.","Colossal broken statues of Early Creatures, carved directly from mountainsides, loomed over the carnage like silent judges.","Their faces were eroded by millennia of wind and metaphysical erosion.","But their presence remained undeniable.","Accusatory.","Some had crumbled entirely, their skyscraper-sized heads half-buried in corrupted earth, serving as macabre fortifications for forces long collapsed.","The land itself bore visible marks of ongoing battle that had been frozen mid-conflict.","Patches of ground crystallized into jagged glass by intense concentrated heat.","Massive craters that still crackled with residual frost lightning trapped in temporal stasis.","Areas where existence seemed covered by silver authority of Law, with massive shattered Folds floating dreamily in mid-air like scattered floating islands defying gravity.","The atmosphere was thick.","Almost unbreathable despite not requiring conventional respiration.","A choking miasma of accumulated dust, smoke from burning emotions of fear and hatred given physical form, and metallic tang of ozone from discharged elemental forces.","Above them, the sky was not blue.","Instead, a swirling bruised vortex of unnatural colors dominated overhead.","The golden geometric light of Law clashing violently with chaotic reds and browns of Elemental forces.","The sickly shifting violets of Emotive authority weaving between them.","It was a sky that screamed with accumulated trauma!","Noah observed all of this with contemplative gaze that catalogued every detail systematically.","He turned his attention toward the far distance.","There, barely visible across impossible spans, they could perceive clouds of countless entities.","Each one shining with terrifying display of power that felt simultaneously ancient and dormant.","But the moment Noah and his forces fully manifested within the Sanctuary...","That ancient dormant power seemingly began surging with incandescent brilliance!","Its magnitude and concentrated authority began doubling!","Then tripling!","Accelerating with exponential velocity as if responding to external stimulus!","Khor laughed lightly, the sound mixing genuine amusement with dangerous anticipation.","Her eyes began shining with predatory gleam.","\"Now this feeling... it’s a sensation of genuine danger I remember from eons past. This feeling of mounting hunger I actively crave!\"","...!","It was feeling of danger, certainly.","Because past all these domains of systematic destruction stretching across Gigaparsecs...","They could feel rising auras of existence burning with concentrated light of Elemental and Emotive authority!","The power was becoming more and more intense with each passing moment.","Their Complexity and Purity measurements were surely surging well into hundreds of Sextillions!","The light of Living Laws positioned far ahead of these enemy forces...","It seemed grand and substantial.","But notably, it was not powering up or surging with brilliance!","Unlike the Elemental and Emotive forces clearly receiving empowerment...the Law forces remained static.","Trapped in the exact state they’d been frozen in.","Noah observed this disparity with eyes shining with analytical focus.","Behind him, the figure of Alexander and Seraphina floated nearby with expression mixing hope and mounting dread.","Noah gave his calm command with voice that carried across entire assembled force.","\"Advance. Analyze enemy capabilities and force composition. Secure and extract all surviving Members of The Primordial Civilization of Law!\"","...!","OOH !","His forces surged forward with his command, fifteen million specialized entities advancing with coordinated precision!","Behind them, the Living Laws of Alexander’s reformed Civilization followed with considerably less confidence.","They could feel the mounting power ahead.","They could perceive what was awakening in response to their intrusion.","And they wondered, with growing certainty, whether they had just made a catastrophic mistake.","Whether opening this Sanctuary would prove to be their salvation...","Or their complete annihilation!","Noah smiled with tyrannical anticipation.","For him, it was...","Time for harvest!"]},{"number":4484,"title":"Chapter 4484: Chapter 4483: Civilizational War! IV","paragraphs":["The sensation of returning to existence was not a gentle awakening.","It was a violent, tectonic realignment of reality itself.","Deep within the shattered canyons of the Injunction Sanctuary, where the air tasted of ozone and preserved trauma, a mountain of ice and obsidian shuddered.","It reformed.","Magma began flowing through veins of diamond-hard ice.","Lightning arced between pillars of stone that served as ribs for something incomprehensibly vast.","A heart of an Early Creature, composed of swirling, perpetual storm...began to beat once more.","THUMP.","THUMP.","THUMP.","Aethon, The Primeval Storm-Forge, opened eyes that burned with light of binary star system!","He was an Elder Early Creature of the Civilization of Elementals. The Civilization of Elements!","A being whose very anatomy was living map of catastrophic weather events.","His distinction was The Weaver of Calamities...a title earned in era before time had learned to march in straight line.","He breathed in.","Inhaling stale air of the Sanctuary.","And felt rush of something foreign yet intoxicating flooding into him.","Power .","It was surging into his existence- a sudden, artificial spike in his existential parameters!","His Complexity, which had stagnated for eons in the ice of THE Living Law’s imposed stasis, began climbing vertically.","300 Sextillion.","450 Sextillion.","600 Sextillion!","It was not merely him.","Around his massive form, the frozen statues of his brethren, tens of thousands of Early Creatures and Living Elementals, were systematically cracking their shells!","Their auras flared with terrifying sudden vibrancy!","The army was awakening.","But before Aethon could properly revel in this unexpected resurgence...","A voice slipped into his mind with surgical precision.","It was smooth. Calm.","And carried weight of verdict already passed without appeal.","\" Aethon. You recall the cold? You recall the silence of enforced stasis?\"","Aethon remained utterly still.","His mind was fortress of elemental will forged across eons.","\"I recall THE Living Law ,\" he thought back, his internal voice grinding like tectonic plates colliding. \"I recall the freeze they imposed upon us. I recall the pursuit we never completed.\"","\" The freeze has lasted eons ,\" the voice continued with detached clinical precision. \" While you slept in imposed stasis, the race was run. THE Loom has been forged. It is finished. It is closed.\"","BOOM!","The words landed with crushing weight.","\" Your brethren, the prudent ones, are safe within its walls. You... and those frozen alongside you... were the stragglers. The cut branches who did not come back in time.\"","The statement was cold douse of water on the fire of his awakening.","Left behind.","The nightmare of every Early Creature facing the approaching Fallout.","\" There is little we can accomplish for you now, \" the voice said, dangling thread of false hope with expertise of practiced fisherman. \" However, certain measures are being tested. Experimental protocols to determine if late entry might prove... viable under exceptional circumstances.\"","A pause filled with deliberate manipulation.","\" Prove your worth here, Aethon. Aid the Legion of Emotives in their systematic objective to eliminate the Living Laws you were originally pursuing. Retrieve the Shattered Fragment of the Heart of Law. And systematically eliminate the Outsiders...remnants of the foreign Hunger approaching from the rear.\"","Another calculated pause.","\" Accomplish these objectives successfully, and perhaps... salvation may yet be extended to you and your forces.\"","The voice faded like mist.","Leaving only howling winds of the canyons.","Aethon stood there, titan of fire and ice, and slow, wry smile touched his lips.","Lips that cracked like dry earth under drought.","The expression was filled with profound, ancient sadness mixing with bitter recognition.","He knew.","He was intellectual. A scholar of elemental arts.","He understood the architecture of THE Loom as he had discussed it with a friend in the Civilization of Pradox.","He also comprehended the fundamental nature of beings who built it.","Once those doors closed, they did not reopen for stragglers.","They did not reopen for failures or second chances.","\"Lies,\" he rumbled softly, the single word vibrating through stone beneath his massive form. \"Why bother with such transparent deception? Do they genuinely believe hope makes us kill faster than despair would?\"","He looked at his hands, massive gauntlets of living rock that could crush mountains.","He knew the absolute truth with certainty that transcended hope.","There was no salvation waiting.","There was no entry being prepared.","He, and every soldier awakening behind him, would be consumed by The Fallout.","They were dead entities walking.","Ghosts given brief, violent reprieve before inevitable oblivion.","But...","His gaze hardened with resolve.","The binary stars of his eyes flared with renewed intensity!","He was Aethon !","He was of the Civilization of Elements!","Even if the destination was guaranteed oblivion...","The path he walked mattered.","His Way of Existence, the Way of Elements, demanded that he burn until fuel was completely gone!","It demanded that he rage against dying of the light, even if eternal night was inevitable conclusion!","It was all he held.","It was the only dignity remaining to him.","He turned slowly.","His massive form cast shadow over the awakening army.","Behind him, the canyon floor was alive with birthing pains of legion being reborn.","Tens of thousands of entities were systematically rising from imposed stasis!","Half were Early Creatures like him, titanic and primal, each one natural disaster given conscious form.","The other half were Living Elementals...beings of pure conceptual energy who blazed with power that visibly warped surrounding air!","Their auras ranged from terrifying 50 Sextillion to monstrous 450 Sextillion!","They looked toward him with expectation.","Their eyes, burning coals, freezing voids, crackling sparks of lightning, fixed upon their leader.","Waiting for direction in an existence they no longer recognized.","Aethon straightened his spine.","The sound was like grinding glaciers echoing through valley.","He looked at them with stern pride of a father sending children to war they could not win.","He would give them what they needed.","He would give them the lie they deserved to die believing.","\"Brothers! Sisters of the Storm!\"","HUUM !","His voice was an eruption, a command that shook accumulated dust from their newly awakened forms!","\"We have slept in the cold prison of Law for eons! But we are not broken! We are not diminished!\"","He pointed massive hand toward distance where silver light of Living Laws shimmered faintly.","\" THE Loom awaits us!\" he roared, the lie tasting like ash in his mouth but delivered with absolute conviction. \"The gates are watching our performance! We have been given a final test! One last chance to reclaim our rightful place!\"","The army stirred.","Hope igniting in their eyes like fresh kindling catching flame.","\"They think us forgotten! They think us weak from our imprisonment!\" Aethon bellowed, his aura flaring dramatically to 800 Sextillion...a beacon of calamitous power! \"But we are the Storm! We are the Quake! We are the Fire that cleanses all impurity!\"","He gestured sharply to the left with commanding motion.","\"First Vanguard! Tear down the Living Laws who imprisoned us! Shatter their remaining stasis! Bring me the Heart Fragment they protect! Make them pay for the eons they systematically stole from us!\"","\" ROAAAR !\"","Half the army surged forward immediately!","Tidal waves of elemental fury turning toward the Living Laws with accumulated vengeance!","Aethon turned to the right.","Looking toward massive gateway where new, strange force was entering the Sanctuary.","An army of obsidian-gold and crimson entities pouring through like flood.","\"Second Vanguard! With me!\" he commanded with voice that shook existence. \"Outsiders approach! Scavengers who seek to pick our bones while we’re weakened! Show them the Way of Elements! Show them that even in death, we burn with unmatched intensity!\"","BOOM !","Myriad expressions of terrifying elemental weavings erupted around him!","The air transformed into kaleidoscope of systematic destruction!","Raining magma from conjured volcanoes of Principles!","Freezing winds that could crystallize existence itself!","Gravity wells of crushed earth creating localized spatial distortions that could collapse Primordial Folds!","Lightning storms that tore through dimensional boundaries!","It was display of raw power that could have systematically annihilated hundreds of entire Transcendent Folds and more.","Aethon looked at his closest aides with a measured assessment.","A Living Elemental of Void-Wind whose form barely maintained coherent shape.","An Early Creature of Crystal-Fire whose body refracted light into weapon.","\"With me,\" he said softly, contrast to his previous roaring making words somehow more weighty.","He turned his gaze toward oncoming force with analytical focus.","He saw them clearly despite distance.","The millions advancing with coordinated precision.","And at their center...","He saw the leader.","He recognized that particular pressure emanating from central figure.","He had witnessed a similar authority on Gilgamesh and other legendary entities.","An armored figure radiating tyrannical blue-gold light.","A being whose Complexity and Purity felt... dense . Heavy with accumulated weight.","But numerically?","Weak.","Comparatively insignificant by raw measurement.","Aethon locked eyes with this being across the Gigaparsecs separating them.","Distance meant nothing to entities of their respective stature.","Perception transcended physical proximity.","He saw The Tyrant clearly.","And for fleeting moment, Aethon, The Primeval Storm-Forge, did not scowl with hostility.","He did not roar with challenge.","He simply shook his head with small, almost imperceptible gesture.","Pity .","You, too ,... Aethon thought, his mind touching vast cold reality of their shared situation. You build your walls. You forge your armor. You march your armies with confidence.","You think you are constructing viable future.","But we are all just entities awaiting collapse under the light of The Fallout. You, me, them... we are all just dust waiting for wind to scatter us.","And yet...","Aethon’s fist clenched with deliberate motion.","The sound was like mountain breaking apart from internal pressure.","... many of you will perish by my hand long before The Fallout arrives to claim us all.","\"Come!\" Aethon roared, abandoning pity for purity of combat! \"Let us discover who burns brightest before the inevitable dark consumes everything!\"","HUUM !","The Elementals charged forward with devastating coordination!","The cracked folds shaking beneath countless feet!"]},{"number":4485,"title":"Chapter 4485: Chapter 4484: Civilizational War! V","paragraphs":["The silence within the Injunction Sanctuary of Law was heavy, pressing against the senses like physical weight composed of eons of lost time.","Deborah, The Silent Adjudicator , opened eyes that were not organic orbs.","They were pools of liquid silver set into face of flawless white marble.","She was a genuine Living Law, an entity whose very biology was structure and statute.","She did not breathe air.","She breathed conviction .","Her form was masterpiece of living statuary, draped in robes carved from same marble as her skin.","And...moving with fluidity that defied the rigidity of her composition.","In her hands, she held it.","The Shattered Part of The Heart of Law.","It was jagged, crystalline shard radiating light that should have been blinding.","It should have pulsed with rhythmic, undeniable decree of THE Living Law ...the Primordial entity that had birthed them all.","But it didn’t.","Deborah looked down at the shard.","A sensation colder than the stasis they had just emerged from washed over her conceptual heart.","The vibration was faint. Weak.","It felt... orphaned.","\"Gone,\" she whispered, her voice the sound of two stones sliding perfectly against one another. \"You are gone, aren’t you? Our foundation has collapsed.\"","She felt it in the marrow of her marble bones.","The desolation was absolute!","It was not merely that they had been frozen for eons.","It was that the source of their warmth, the sun around which their existence orbited, had been extinguished during their long sleep.","THE Living Law had collapsed.","The Primordial Civilization of Law was no more.","She wanted to scream.","She wanted to let the marble of her face crack and release sound of pure, chaotic grief that would shatter the very concept of law and order she represented.","But she was the Adjudicator. She did not scream.","Instead, she looked up.","Her gaze pierced the choking miasma of the battlefield. Looking past the swirling, bruised vortex of the sky.","Past the immediate threat of Emotive and Elemental legions waking around them.","She looked into the far, far distance.","There, across Gigaparsecs of shattered terrain, she saw them.","The newcomers.","A force of millions radiating terrifying, disciplined power.","But her eyes...guided by faint, dying pulse of the Heart fragment in her hands, locked onto single figure standing amidst that foreign legion.","A young man.","He was bathed in silver-white light, his hair shining with metallic luminescence.","Beside him was woman glowing with similar, though fainter, authority.","But the man...","His gaze was piercing.","Cutting through the chaos of awakening battlefield to meet hers with impossible precision.","As if he knew exactly where she was. Exactly what she held. Exactly what it meant.","HUUM !","The Shattered Part of The Heart of Law vibrated in her hands.","Deborah’s marble brow furrowed.","Is he... connected ? She asked herself, the thought racing through her mind like verdict being drafted. Is he connected to the Will and Weavings of THE Living Law ? Is he the reason the stasis has thawed?","Hope, fragile and sharp, bloomed in her chest.","I must reach him. I must understand what this means!","But then, the view was stolen.","HUUM !","Waves of sickly violet light crashed down between them, cutting off her line of sight entirely.","The air grew thick with stench of weaponized sorrow and artificial despair.","The Civilization Legion of Emotives had fully awakened.","Deborah’s gaze snapped back to her immediate surroundings.","Her expression shifted from wonder to livid, marble-hard fury.","Tens of thousands.","That was all that remained of her once-glorious legion.","They huddled behind her...silver lights dim, postures radiating defeat of people who wake only to discover their empire is dust.","They had been hunted to near oblivion by these monsters eons ago.","And now, the moment they drew breath again...","The hunt resumed.","\" Persistent fucking vermin ,\" she hissed with concentrated venom.","She stepped forward.","Her marble feet struck shattered ground with sound of absolute finality.","She raised the Heart fragment high, letting its dim light wash over her despairing troops.","\"Do not weep for the past!\"","Her voice was a decree.","It resonated in the souls of Living Laws, straightening their spines involuntarily.","\"We are the Law! We do not bend to the chaos of emotion! We do not erode before the elements! They think us broken? They think us remnants of dead civilization?\"","She pointed marble finger at rising tide of violet and red approaching them.","\"Let us show them that the Verdict... is still ours to deliver! Form up! For the sanctity of structure! For the memory of Law!\"","WAA !","The Civilizational Authority of Law flared around them.","Silver-white brilliance, sharp and geometric.","Yet to any observer, it was heartbreakingly dim compared to the blinding radiance of opposing forces.","It was a light of dying star raging against encroaching dark.","They knew the truth.","They knew the true Primordial Civilization of Law had collapsed!","But they moved anyway.","Because that was their Way.","---","Gigaparsecs away, Noah stood with eyes reflecting the grand tragedy unfolding across the sanctuary.","His perception, amplified by his Civilizational framework and Lens of Civilization, saw it all with perfect clarity.","He observed the awakening armies of Elementals and Emotives split their forces with strategic precision.","It was calculated bifurcation.","Half of the massive force, tens of thousands of entities burning with power ranging from 50 Sextillion to 450 Sextillion, turned their hostile gazes directly toward him.","The other half surged forward like tsunami of fire and grief. Intent on crushing the small, silver remnant of Living Laws.","\"Osmont.\"","The voice of Alexander Asmodeus rang in his mind, tight with urgency.","\"I can feel it. The leader of those Living Laws... she holds the Shattered Part of the Heart of Law. It calls to the inheritance within me.\"","Alexander paused, watching the violet tide crash toward silver line.","\"But they are overwhelmed. Outnumbered catastrophically. If she gets swarmed... if she is systematically decimated before we can bridge the distance... the fragment could be lost. Or worse, destroyed.\"","Noah watched the distant flare of silver light struggle against violet ocean.","He felt the anxiety radiating from Alexander. The desperation to save what remained of Law.","Noah’s reply was calm. A flat line of certainty cutting through chaos.","\"We will get her. The fragment will not be lost.\"","He severed the mental connection and turned his gaze to his own assembled forces.","Fifteen million entities stood ready for deployment.","The Iron Concordat formed wall of obsidian-gold defensive might.","The Verdant Cycle glowed with preparatory healing weaves ready to activate.","But his eyes settled specifically on the Crimson Hunger faction.","Particularly on towering, skeletal figure wreathed in maddening aura of death and appetite.","Arch Lich Ra’Zan.","The Lich had undergone the Hungering Maw Specialization with devastating results.","His defensive capabilities were completely stripped away, and his offensive power multiplied by factors that defied conventional logic.","He was glass cannon of apocalyptic proportions.","\"Ra’Zan,\" Noah said.","His voice was not loud, but it arrived instantly at the Lich’s consciousness with absolute clarity.","The Arch Lich turned.","Empty eye sockets blazing with green-fire hunger.","\"The enemy facing us possesses substantial power,\" Noah intoned, his voice taking on a tyrannical cadence of a War Emperor. \"Individually, many of them exceed our average strength measurements. They are relics from the Earliest Folds, hoarders of ancient accumulated power.\"","Noah gestured toward oncoming wave of Elementals and Emotives.","\"The Defenders will hold them at bay. They will break their assault on our walls. Your goal is not merely to push them back or repel their advance.\"","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","\"These enemies hold immense quantities of harvestable authority. They possess information from The Earliest Folds that no longer exists elsewhere. They will not surrender it willingly while they draw breath.\"","A cruel, pragmatic smile touched Noah’s lips.","\"So we will proceed to collapse them. We will make them Dead. And once Dead, transition them to Dead Existences... you, Ra’Zan, will incorporate them into your Civilizational Legion of Dead Existences.\"","HUUM !","The air around Ra’Zan twisted with mounting anticipation.","\"Consider what it means carefully,\" Noah continued, his voice dropping to conspiratorial whisper that somehow echoed like thunder. \"Collapsing even one of these entities means acquiring a Dead Existence with dozens of Sextillions in baseline Complexity and Purity.\"","He paused deliberately.","\"Now imagine, Ra’Zan... if such extraordinarily powerful Dead Existence were to subsequently undergo our Civilization Specialization...\"","He left the thought hanging.","He didn’t need to finish the statement.","The implication was a promise of power so vast it bordered on obscenity!","A Dead Existence with 50 to 400+ Sextillion baseline becoming Hungering Maw specialist...","Oh !","Arch Lich Ra’Zan began to cackle .","It started as low, dry rattle in his skeletal throat.","Then built into crescendo of death and madness that made surrounding existence recoil!","His bony fingers clenched his staff with such force the weapon cracked.","The Hungering Maw armor shifted around him like living thing yearning for the feast!","\" KEKEKEKE !\"","The Arch Lich surged forward...a comet of green and crimson death leading the vanguard of Hungering Maws!","\"My duty... is Death !\" Ra’Zan bellowed, his voice scream that tore at souls of those who heard it! \"And the harvest shall be... inevitable !\"","Behind him, the Crimson Hunger faction erupted into motion!","Thousands of predatory specialists streaking forward with barely contained aggression!","BOOM !"]},{"number":4486,"title":"Chapter 4486: Chapter 4485: Kleos I","paragraphs":["Noah hovered above the landscape, his eyes dissecting the oncoming storm.","The horizon had been systematically erased, replaced by a towering tsunami of elemental cataclysm rushing toward his forces.","The Civilizational Legions of Elementals were rewriting the environment itself.","Noah observed their forms with cold assessment. Titanic Early Creatures and Living Elementals, their bodies etched with tens of thousands of Kleos Glyphs that pulsed like dying stars. Magma gushed from the pores of reality itself, freezing instantly into jagged, absolute-zero glaciers as contradictory Principles of Thermodynamic Collapse and Elemental Supremacy warred for dominance in the same physical space.","The air itself was being tortured by their presence.","But it was the Astral Codexes that truly defined the scale of the approaching threat.","Dozens of Elemental commanders raised their hands, their grimoires flaring with accumulated power from eons of cultivation. Countless Elemental Everythings burned with unleashed authority, the scene glorious in its concentrated destruction as thousands upon thousands of Everythings were systematically consumed to fuel a devastating assault.","HUUM!","From pages of brilliant light, Astral Arcana Glyphs manifested with terrible beauty, tearing through the fabric of the Sanctuary itself.","An ancient Woolly Mammoth...composed entirely of sentient permafrost and concentrated lightning, trampled through the air with impossible mass. Its tusks carved voids in space with each swing.","A Plesiosaur of liquid magma swam through the ether like an ocean predator, its roar boiling the very concept of moisture from existence.","And above them, Immortal Jellyfishes pulsed with blinding elemental brilliance, their tentacles trailing paralysis and entropy that dissolved matter on contact.","It was a wave carrying hundreds of Sextillions in combined Complexity and Purity. A force that should have washed away Noah’s Civilization like sandcastles before a hurricane!","And facing it...","Five million members of the Infinite Bulwark Specialization stood in perfect silence.","They did not flinch. They held their shields. They simply planted their feet with systematic precision, their Civilizational Armors locking together in geometric perfection that defied the chaos rushing toward them.","\"Civilization Fortress Formation,\" the collective thought echoed through their network...a silent command that solidified the air around them.","Their obsidian-gold plates flared with concentrated authority, linking every single member into a singular, monolithic entity.","They were no longer five million individual soldiers.","They were one Wall.","BOOM!","The impact was glorious!","The Woolly Mammoths struck with full force. The magma oceans crashed like a tidal wave. The jellyfish tentacles lashed out with paralyzing venom. The Elemental Legion unleashed a barrage that could have cracked an many Transcendent Folds!","But the Wall did not move.","Not a single inch. Not a fraction of measurement.","Noah watched the mechanics unfold with cold, analytical satisfaction.","The lead Infinite Bulwark, a Primus Inevitability named Bastion , and a few ten thousands Primus Inevitabilities took the brunt of the damage directly.The force was sufficient to atomize many things, carrying the concentrated weight of thousands of Sextillion Complexity all together!","But the Wall of Primus Inevitabilities did not take these thousands of Sextillions in damage.","The moment impact connected, the Civilization Fortress Formation engaged . The damage was not absorbed by them alone, it traveled instantly through golden conduits linking the armor, racing away from the point of impact at speeds faster than thought itself.","And it did not merely spread to the five million present.","It crossed dimensional boundaries, utilizing the Civilization Network to distribute the kinetic and conceptual load across all 16+ Million Infinite Bulwark specialists currently active throughout the Civilization.","The mathematics of it all was beautiful. The numbers were tyrannical!","A blow that should have obliterated a single unit was diluted by a factor of sixteen million times 10 Sextillion!","All those in the Infinite Bulwark Specialization whose personal defense stood at a formidable 10 Sextillion average felt a tremor that barely registered as a scratch. A loss of perhaps 1 Sextillion in existential integrity.","They didn’t even blink.","The Elemental commanders watched, their eyes widening in genuine, shocked confusion. They had unleashed the apocalypse itself!","And the apocalypse had simply... stopped.","Then, the second phase engaged with devastating efficiency.","\"Restore.\"","The command came from the rear formations.","Sigrid, THE Living Order, floated amidst the Verdant Cycle specialists, her form a beacon of verdant-gold brilliance that pulsed with restorative authority. She did not look worried...she looked like a conductor raising a baton before a symphony.","HUUM !","\" Symphonic Restoration!\"","Waves of green-gold light erupted from Vital Chorus specialists. It was an aggressive injection of concentrated vitality!","The light washed over the Infinite Bulwarks like a cleansing tide. Minor scratches on their existential frames vanished instantly.","But the healing didn’t stop at simple restoration.","[ Overflow Vitality ] activated automatically. The excess healing energy didn’t dissipate wastefully...it hardened, coalescing around the obsidian-gold armor as a secondary, translucent layer of verdant shielding.","They were not just healed, but were also fortified beyond their original state!","The Elemental Legion stared with mounting incomprehension, their collective breath caught in their throats. They had thrown mountains at these beings.","And the beings were now demonstrably healthier than before the attack.","It was terrifying and glorious all at once.","But Noah wasn’t watching the defensive display anymore, he was watching the numbers.","|Damage Conversion Active|","|Accumulated Hostile Authority: 8,400 Sextillion|","|Status: Holding... Awaiting Discharge Command|","The Bulwarks were glowing with terrifying, contained heat. They had systematically eaten the enemy’s attack, stored the kinetic and conceptual energy within their own frameworks, and were now holding it like a breath waiting to be exhaled with devastating force.","Noah’s smile was predatory as he called out.","\"Ozymandias.\"","...!","In the space between armies, where the violet tide of the Civilization Legions of Emotives surged toward the beleaguered remnants of the Living Laws, a ripple occurred.","Deborah, The Silent Adjudicator, stood with her marble skin visibly cracked, her silver light dimming with each passing moment. Around her, the remaining Living Laws were collapsing under just the light concentrated assault.","\"Do not yield!\" she screamed, her voice cracking with coldness. \"We are the final testament to Law itself! We do not yield!\"","HUUM!","Then, a shadow fell over her position.","A figure stepped out of empty air directly in front of her defensive line.","It was a humanoid form of obsidian and crimson, tentacles writhing from its back like a cloak of living darkness. It radiated a hunger so profound it made the surrounding Emotive energy shiver with instinctive recognition.","Deborah’s eyes widened with a mixture of emotions.","\"Friend...\" she whispered. \"You do not need to sacrifice yourself for us.\"","Ozymandias did not look back at her.","He stood alone, a single point of darkness against a horizon of violet fire.","He adjusted his hands with a casual gesture, the motion showing absolute arrogance in the face of the rushing horde.","\"Sacrifice?\" Ozymandias asked, his voice a deep, resonant rumble that vibrated in Deborah’s chest. \"No. You misunderstand my purpose here entirely.\"","He raised one hand, palm open, facing the direction of The Iron Concordat positioned far across the battlefield.","\"Let the accumulated damage... flow through me.\"","WAA !","The connection snapped into place with audible resonance. The Damage Conversion network flared with blinding intensity.","The 8,400 Sextillion units of stored destructive energy held by the Infinite Bulwarks was not released as a scattered blast.","It was channeled with surgical precision!","It rushed through the Civilization’s interconnected framework, pouring directly into Ozymandias’s form.","His obsidian-crimson body swelled with accumulated power. His aura exploded outward, shifting from terrifying hunger to a blinding, catastrophic beacon of pure concentrated ruin.","The energy of the Elemental Legion’s attack...The Principles, the mammoths, the magma, the void-ice, all of it...was systematically converted into raw, unadulterated Hunger .","Ozymandias opened his mouth.","The jaw did unhinged , expanding impossibly as the fabric of reality tore around the motion. Crimson Obsidian Hunger Jaws bloomed into existence with devastating manifestation.","They were colossal, spanning the horizon entirely...dwarfing the Emotive giants rushing toward him like insignificant insects.","The power radiating from those jaws was impossibly concentrated, a singular strike containing a few Thousands of Sextillions in Complexity and Purity even after any losses with the conversion. It was damage Ozymandias had no inherent right to wield, power he had not personally cultivated!","But it was power he now controlled through the cheating architecture of Noah’s Civilization!","\" Chomp .\"","The word was spoken softly, almost gently.","The sound that followed was wet and utterly final.","The jaws slammed shut with apocalyptic force.","BOOM !","Nine massive Early Creatures, beings measuring 100 to 300 Sextillion Complexity and surrounded by Civilizational Authority of Emotive...were caught directly in the bite. Towering avatars of Sorrow and Rage who had existed since the Earliest Folds.","They didn’t have time to scream.","Their conceptual barriers shattered like glass. Their fundamental principles unraveled like torn fabric. Their upper bodies were sheared off cleanly, separated from their legs by the absolute sharpness of the bite that transcended conventional cutting.","The Emotive Legion halted, their momentum completely broken by the sheer, impossible violence of the act!","Ozymandias stood amidst the falling rain of blood and dissipating essence.","He waved his hand with a cool dismissal.","Tentacles of hunger erupted from the fading jaws, snatching the nine cleaved corpses from the air before they could strike the ground. He wound up his arm with theatrical motion and threw them...hurling the massive bodies across light-years of battlefield, straight toward the waiting, skeletal arms of Ra’Zan in The Hungering Maw faction.","\"Fresh corpses for the Legion.\" Ozymandias declared, his voice ringing with satisfaction!","He watched Arch Lich Ra’Zan catch the first body, the Lich’s cackling laughter echoing like a symphony of breaking bones.","Ozymandias then turned back to the frozen, livid masses of the Emotive Legion.","He stood tall, his obsidian-crimson form shining with a majesty that demanded reverence. He placed one hand behind his back with a posture of relaxed superiority.","With his other hand, he beckoned to them...a simple, taunting motion of his fingers.","\"Come now,\" Ozymandias purred, his eyes burning with the light of a predator who has discovered an all-you-can-eat buffet. \" Do not let fear overwhelm you just yet. I require substantially more harvest before satisfaction.\"","His smile widened.","\" And my Civilization is very hungry.\"","HUUM!","The declaration resonated across the battlefield.","Behind Ozymandias, Deborah stared with her marble mouth hanging open.","What manner of beings had she received help from?!"]},{"number":4487,"title":"Chapter 4487: Chapter 4486: Kleos II","paragraphs":["The silence following Ozymandias’s display was heavy with horrified realization.","Nine Early Creatures, beings who had reigned for epochs, ended in a single bite.","But the Civilization Legion of Emotives did not break.","The violet and gray storm of their collective aura parted, and from the depths of their formation, a figure emerged. He drifted, carried by a visible current of weeping spirits and solidified sighs.","Threnody, The Weaver of Final Sorrows.","He was an Elder Early Creature, his form that of shifting, melancholic shadows. His face was a mask of beautiful, frozen grief, with eyes that were not eyes but deep, endless wells of tear-filled oceans. Around him, Everythings of Emotion swirled...tiny, crystallized shards of panic, regret, and absolute resignation orbiting him like a solar system of tragedy.","Threnody looked at Ozymandias, at the obsidian-crimson predator standing amidst the blood of his kin.","\" Fear ?\" Threnody asked, his voice a sound like wind howling through a dead city...hollow, mournful, and utterly devoid of hope.","He floated closer, the Everythings of Sorrow dampening the very light around him.","\"You speak to us of fear, Stranger. But you mistake our purpose. You mistake our fundamental nature.\"","Threnody spread his arms, and the violet light intensified, heavy with the weight of a trillion bad endings.","\"None of us know fear anymore. We lost the capacity for it the moment the doors of THE Loom closed. Fear is the anticipation of loss. Fear is the hope that disaster can be averted.\"","He pointed a shadowy finger toward the chaotic sky, toward the invisible, encroaching threat of the future.","\"Fear... was knowing The Fallout approaches. Fear was realizing we were the chaff, the discarded remnants left to burn while the chosen slept in safety. We have already processed that terror. We have already died a thousand times in our minds.\"","HUUM!","A wave of gray light washed over the Emotive Legion, stabilizing them. They stopped trembling. They looked at Ozymandias not with lividity, but with the blank, terrifying stare of the terminally condemned.","\"We are the walking dead,\" Threnody whispered, the sound echoing in the marrow of every being present. \"Regardless of what you do... regardless of what we accomplish... we will be consumed. That is the only truth. So do not think you can sow fear in a field that has already been salted by the End.\"","...!","The logic was suffocating...a defense born of absolute nihilism. They fought not to survive, but because they had nothing left to lose!","Ozymandias listened, his obsidian-crimson form pulsing, the tentacles on his back writhing with amusement.","He smiled, and his jaw unhinged slightly, revealing the spinning void of crimson fire within.","\"How poetic,\" Ozymandias rumbled, his voice a tyrannical counter-weight to Threnody’s sorrow. \"You claim you cannot fear because you are already dead?\"","BOOM!","Crimson authority exploded from him, pushing back the violet fog.","\"Then I shall teach you a new emotion,\" Ozymandias declared, his eyes burning with the light of a predator who plays with his food. \" I shall teach you Regret. Regret that you did not kneel when you had the chance. Regret... that your end will not be The Fallout, but Me.\"","HUUM!","The air shattered. Emotive flared. Law brightened. The armies charged!","From his vantage point, Noah watched the collision with cold satisfaction.","Ozymandias had successfully intervened. Deborah, the Living Law holding the Heart Fragment, was shielded from the immediate onslaught. The strategic objective was secured.","Noah’s gaze flicked to the nine corpses arcing through the void...massive, mutilated bodies of Early Creatures, rich with Sextillions of Complexity. They crashed near Arch Lich Ra’Zan, who was already cackling as his necrotic authority began seeping into them.","Excellent .","But Noah’s attention was drawn elsewhere, to the second front.","Far ahead of the main line, a small, diminutive figure stood alone against the tidal wave of the Civilization Legion of Elementals.","Khor.","The First Hunger stood amidst the shattered geometry of the canyon floor.","Facing her were tens of thousands of Early Creatures and Living Elementals...beings of magma, storm, and void, roaring with the collective power of an era that remembered how to break Primordial Folds.","Khor did not adopt a fighting stance.","She simply... opened her mouth.","CLACK .","She snapped her jaws shut on empty air.","Across the battlefield, three hundred miles away, the head of a Magma Titan simply vanished . There was no travel time. No projectile. Just the sound of jaws closing, and then the absence of matter.","\"Feed.\"","Khor blurred.","She moved with a weight and brutality that defied her size, slamming into the front line of the Elemental Legion like a kinetic bombardment.","She didn’t dodge. She didn’t parry.","She simply fucking advanced.","An Elemental of Wind, vibrating with 300 Sextillion Complexity, slashed at her with a blade that could cut dimensions.","Khor caught the blade in her bare hand, with her tiny, fair fingers.","| Reality Severance|","Her fingers tightened. The blade shattered, its conceptual sharpness severed by the greater musings of her Hunger.","She pulled the Elemental forward, her other hand driving into its chest like a spear. An excess of 300+ Sextillion flowed across her hand like a blade.","She ripped out its Heart- a swirling vortex of storm-essence, and shoved it into her mouth.","CRUNCH .","|Consumption Acceleration| triggered instantly. The Elemental collapsed into dust, its 300 Sextillion power digested in a microsecond!","OOOH !","Khor’s aura flared. A crimson shockwave blasted outward, knocking back the surrounding titans.","[ Hunger Stacks: +30%]","Her power spiked. She was stronger now than she was a second ago.","\"More,\" she whispered.","She spun, a whirlwind of violence. She fought with the brutal efficiency of a butcher. She grabbed a Void-Beast by its horns, snapped its neck, and bit a chunk out of its reality before dropping the corpse and eating it whole. She kicked a Glacial Golem Early Creature, shattering its legs, and devoured the falling shards of ice before they hit the ground.","Oh!","It was a slaughter. It was a feast.","The Elementals rallied, realizing this tiny creature was a monster.","\" Collapse her !\" roared Aethon, The Primeval Storm-Forge, his binary star eyes blazing with desperate fury. \"Pour everything into her position! She cannot withstand the combined might of our Legion! Drown her in our accumulated power!\"","Ten thousand elemental attacks converged on Khor.","Magma, lightning, absolute zero, gravity crush...it all slammed into her simultaneously. The ground beneath her vaporized, turning into a crater of molten glass and void of collapse!","The dust settled. And yet...","Khor stood there. Unscathed. Unmoved.","There wasn’t a scratch on her skin.","The Elementals froze, their minds reeling as they wondered...bro, fucking how?","They didn’t know. They couldn’t see.","Far behind the lines, within The Iron Concordat formations, The Infinite Bulwarks glowed with radiant, obsidian-gold light. They staggered slightly, their armor groaning as the invisible, metaphysical tethers of the Civilization transferred the damage from Khor to them.","The impact that should have obliterated Khor was distributed across sixteen million tanks, those present here, and those not!","What would have been a deathblow became a mosquito bite spread across an army.","Khor brushed a speck of dust from her shoulder, looking at the terrified Elemental commanders with a grin widening to reveal white teeth that seemed too numerous, too sharp.","\"Is that it?\" she asked.","She lunged.","Her small mouth opened impossibly wide, far beyond what her frame should allow, and she bit.","An Early Creature of Crystal-Fire suddenly felt its left arm disappear. Simply gone, as if it had never existed.","Khor’s jaws closed with a wet snap.","She bit again.","The creature’s right leg vanished. It stumbled, confusion and horror warring in its eyes.","Another bite.","Its torso developed a perfect spherical void where its core had been.","Bite. Bite. Bite.","Each chomp removed portions of existence with surgical precision. The Early Creature could feel different parts of its being disappearing and ceasing to have ever been there. Its memories of having those limbs were intact, but the limbs themselves were unmade.","Then, with one final, larger bite, Khor’s jaws stretched to encompass the entire remaining body.","CRUNCH .","The Early Creature disappeared completely.","[Hunger Stacks: +90%]","She didn’t stop. She couldn’t stop.","Her form blurred across the battlefield, a crimson streak of annihilation. Each Early Creature she encountered suffered the same fate, dismantled bite by bite before total consumption.","|Hunger Stacks: +180%|","|Hunger Stacks: +225%|","She was getting faster. Stronger. Every kill fed the engine. Every bite fueled the slaughter.","The Elemental Legion began to burn with a rageful light of Civilizational Authority!","Oh!","Noah watched from above, his heart beating in a slow, tyrannical rhythm.","The light of his Civilization was blinding .","This was warfare evolved. This was the synergy of a true organism. His Vanguard could fight with reckless abandon, knowing the Bulwarks held their lives. His Support could heal the Bulwarks, knowing the Vanguard would end the threat.","He watched Khor tear the head off a 300 Sextillion Complexity creature and laugh , a sense of sorrow and frustration being released from her.","|Harvest Accumulating...|","|Source: Elemental Legion|","|Amplification: Perpetual Harvest Active|","|Projected Gain: Extraordinary. Quintessentially so.|","Noah closed his eyes for a brief second, feeling the influx of power. It was intoxicating.","\"Yes,\" he murmured to the chaos. \"This is the path. This is The Way.\"","He opened his eyes, and they blazed with tyrannical satisfaction.","\"Burn them all,\" he commanded softly. \"And bring me the ash.\"","...!","HUUM!"]},{"number":4488,"title":"Chapter 4488: Chapter 4487: Kleos III","paragraphs":["Glory. Kleos.","How much glory can one truly gain from battle?","How much Kleos...that ancient, resonant renown that echoes beyond the cessation of the flesh, can be harvested from the act of unmaking another?","For some, the answer is infinite .","To them, battle is the crucible of definition. It is the only place where the self is truly tested, where the dross of mundane existence is burned away to reveal the gold of the soul. They believe that to strike down a titan is to steal a fraction of their height, to stand taller upon the mountain of the vanquished.","For these beings, glory is a resource as tangible as Mana...a currency that buys immortality in the minds of those who follow.","A scar is a story. A kill is a verse in the grand ballad of their existence.","But there is another perspective. A quieter, colder one.","To these observers, battle is merely the failure of reason. It is a chaotic, messy transaction where value is lost, not gained. They look at the corpse of a titan and see only rot, not triumph.","They argue that Kleos is a lie told by the living to justify the silence of the dead.","For what glory does the dust know? What renown can comfort the void?","In this view, war is not a ladder to the heavens, but a slide into entropy...an acceleration of the inevitable end where names, deeds, and memories are all devoured by the same impartial dark.","In the Earliest Folds , this question was not philosophical.","It was practical.","And the answer... would determine the fate of Existence.","---","In the Earliest Folds .","The domain was a singularity of silence, a pocket of reality that sat at the very precipice of the unformed.","Here, the weavings of existence curled up and died, replaced by the sheer, crushing weight of Presence .","THE Creature sat upon a simple stone outcropping.","He was vast in conceptual density. To look at him was to look at the horizon...no matter how far you traveled, he seemed to be there, encompassing the view.","Before him stood THE Living Emotive.","She was a kaleidoscope of feeling given form, a shifting storm of colors...violets of despair, crimsons of rage, golds of euphoria...swirling around a humanoid silhouette that seemed too vibrant to be real.","The atmosphere was tense, heavy with the scent of imminent betrayal, though the betrayal had already been woven into the fabric of the moment.","THE Loom was nearing completion. The trap was sprung, the cage was lowering, and the game was reaching its terrifying crescendo.","Emotive looked at THE Creature , her form flickering with nervous, manic yellow energy.","\" So ,\" she began, her voice a chorus of a thousand whispers, \" in the wars to come... in the grand reshaping of all things... how much glory will there be? How much Kleos awaits us, O Creature, when the dust settles and the new order rises?\"","THE Creature raised his head.","His eyes...pools of absolute, primordial existence, met hers.","There was no anger in them. No fear.","Only a profound, endless depth.","\"In all battles ,\" THE Creature said, his voice the sound of a tectonic plate shifting deep underground, \" there is no glory. There is only death.\"","The statement was flat. Absolute.","It stripped the romance from violence and left only the cold, hard bone of reality.","Emotive stared at him for a long moment.","Then, she laughed.","It was a jagged, fractured sound, like crystal shattering in a vacuum.","\" Hahaha! You really are a killjoy, aren’t you?\" She floated closer, the colors of her form shifting to a dark, trembling blue. \" But that’s why I was always terrified of you. Did you know that?\"","She gestured to herself, to the swirling storm of her existence.","\" Fear. Terror. It was the most delicious, most potent emotion I ever found. And you... you were the source. I used that terror to climb, to evolve, to reach this height. And even now...\"","She leaned in, her voice dropping to a conspiratorial whisper that vibrated with genuine dread.","\" Even now, as the trap closes, as THE Living Paradox’s grand design comes to fruition, and we stand on the brink of victory... I am still unfathomably terrified of you.\"","THE Creature looked at her.","He did not blink.","And then, he moved.","He raised his right hand.","It was a simple gesture...a slow, deliberate lifting of the arm.","CLANK. CLANK. CLANK.","The sound of chains...heavy, conceptual chains forged from the crystallized authority of multiple Civilizations, rang out through the void.","The grand reveal was heartbreaking in its majesty.","THE Creature was bound .","Countless chains, each one thick as Folds, wrapped around his limbs, his torso, his very neck. They anchored him to the nothingness, weighing down his existence with a suppression force that should have rendered him utterly immobile.","A force of multiple Primordial Civilizations combined.","He should not have been able to lift a finger. He should not have been able to twitch a muscle. The combined might of the conspirators, the full weight of the betrayal, was pressing down on him with incomprehensible force.","And yet.","He raised his hand.","He pointed it toward THE Living Emotive.","WAA !","There was no attack. No blast of energy.","Just the movement. Just the fact that he could.","In an instant...less than a nanosecond, THE Living Emotive vanished.","She didn’t teleport with grace. She fled. She kicked off the fabric of reality and hurled herself backward, putting countless Gigaparsecs between herself and that raised hand in a single, desperate heartbeat!","The void where she had stood was empty, swirling with the residual trails of her panic.","THE Creature sat there, his hand still raised, the chains pulled taut, groaning under the strain of his casual movement.","He smiled.","It was a small, gentle smile.","He lowered his hand, the chains clattering back into place, settling around him like heavy, obedient serpents. He sat back down, comfortable in his bindings, as if they were merely loose clothing.","\" You seem ,\" THE Creature murmured to the empty space, \" to still be filled with fear. \"","Minutes passed. Or perhaps seconds.","Time was subjective in the face of such terror.","Slowly, cautiously, a shimmer of color reappeared in the distance. THE Living Emotive returned, though she kept a safe, respectful range...a distance measured in light-years.","She looked at him, her form trembling, the colors chaotic and muddy.","Then, she let out a breath she didn’t need, and she laughed again.","This time, the laughter was shaky, bordering on hysterical.","\" Damn ,\" she whispered, her voice carrying across the distance through their conceptual link. \" You scary fucking guy.\"","She shook her head, the colors of her form brightening, turning to a mix of awe and disbelief.","\" You still terrify me, okay? Even after all this. Even bound. Even betrayed.\"","She floated there, looking at the chains that had failed to stop him.","\"I truly cannot believe Paradox pulled this off,\" she admitted, her voice filled with genuine wonder. \" I was half expecting you to kill us all for the betrayal the moment we tried it. I did it regardless because, man, why not? The thrill was worth the risk. But for us to actually succeed? For THE Loom to be actualized? For you to be... contained?\"","Her eyes shone with a manic light.","\" Wowee... the avenues of possibilities are now boundless.\"","She straightened, regaining some of her composure, though she did not move an inch closer.","\"I’ll leave you be now, O Glorious Creature,\" she said, sketching a mock bow that was actually quite respectful. \" But I’ll come and keep you company for as long as I can. Just to continue feeling that terror. That emotion of fear. Because towards you...I also feel that emotion of boundless love. It is intoxicating. It is paradoxical...\"","She shivered, a ripple of dark pleasure running through her form.","\"I think... in all of observable existence, you are the only one who can make me feel like that. Not even Paradox could make me feel such fear. Such love. Not even the approaching End itself.\"","...!","THE Creature sat silently.","The chains hummed with a low, mournful note.","He looked at her, at this vibrant, terrified, ambitious child of existence.","\" In all that you are doing now, \" THE Creature said, his voice soft, final, and heavy as a collapsing Fold, \" you will not find glory in it. You will not find Kleos regardless of how far you go.\"","His eyes closed, the stars dimming.","\" You will not find what you are looking for.\"","...!","The words hung in the void, a prophecy that felt more like a curse.","Emotive paused. The colors of her form stilled for a moment.","Then, she shrugged, a gesture of dismissal that didn’t quite reach her eyes.","\" Eh ,\" she said, her voice fading as she began to dissolve into the background of existence. \" Glory is overrated anyways!\"","POP .","She was gone.","And THE Creature sat alone in the dark, bound by chains that could not truly hold him, waiting for the end that was only a beginning.","In that silence, he whispered calmly.","\" Anaximander, Come.\"","...!","A name was called as moments passed.","It was unknown if there would ever be an answer!"]},{"number":4489,"title":"Chapter 4489: Chapter 4488: Results Are A Must! I","paragraphs":["The domain of THE Living Paradox was a ridiculous one.","It was a realm where \"up\" was a matter of opinion and \"distance\" was a suggestion that was frequently ignored.","THE Living Paradox stood upon a Primordial Fold Balcony...a structure composed of non-Euclidean geometry that overlooked the Fold Sea of Unhappened Things.","A vast, gray ocean where trillions of potential timelines that had been decimated from reality by Paradox rotted in silence. They were...inconsequential, not things to think of and ponder about too much.","THE Living Paradox stood at the edge, his form shifting subtly. One moment he appeared as an elderly sage wreathed in smoke, the next a young conqueror clad in armor of liquid glass.","He was constant only in his inconsistency.","He did not turn as the atmosphere behind him suddenly screamed with color.","CRACKLE .","The air bruised violet, then bled into a manic, ecstatic gold. THE Living Emotive arrived by simply inflicting her presence upon the coordinates.","THE Living Paradox glanced over his shoulder, which was currently made of polished obsidian, and sighed.","\"I told you ,\" his voice echoed, sounding from everywhere at once, \" not to mess around THE Creature. Even if he is chained. Even if we have ostensibly won.\"","THE Living Emotive didn’t flinch.","She floated closer, her feet skimming the paradox-tiled floor. She was smiling...a wide, jagged expression that held too many teeth and too much joy.","\" Oh, Paradox,\" she hummed, the sound resonating in the bone marrow. \" You always worry about the logistics. You forget the experience.\"","She wrapped her arms around herself, shivering violently, her colors shifting to a deep, bruised purple of delicious terror. She looked like a fucking lunatic.","\" He makes me feel...exquisite ,\" she whispered. \" The weight of him. The sheer, crushing density of his existence. When he looked at me, even bound, even betrayed... I felt like a tiny candle standing near a supernova.\"","She drifted until she was right beside THE Living Paradox , leaning in close, her voice dropping to a taunting purr.","\" That terror... that absolute, freezing dread, that thrill, that maddening rush... I don’t think you could ever make me feel like that.\"","...!","It was a direct insult, a challenge to the architect of the grandest conspiracy in existence.","THE Living Paradox did not rage. He did not expand his aura to crush her.","He simply turned back to the gray ocean, his demeanor settling into an extremely calm, ancient stillness.","\" Of course I cannot ,\" he replied, his voice level and devoid of ego. \" He is THE Creature, after all. He is the canvas upon which we all paint our aspirations. To deny his magnitude would be to deny the very feat we are accomplishing by caging him.\"","Emotive blinked, the colors of her form stalling for a microsecond.","She hadn’t gotten the rise she wanted.","She frowned, probing deeper, her need for reaction itching under her skin.","\" Is that it ?\" she pressed, circling him with predatory curiosity. \" Do you think... do you think you will ever measure up? After THE Loom is realized? After we have stripped the Folds and built our sanctuary? Will you ever have that presence? That gravity? That... je ne sais quoi?\"","...!","THE Living Paradox looked at her.","His eyes were currently voids containing swirling folds that spun in reverse.","\"You mistake the nature of power for the nature of loudness, \" he said, his voice taking on a grand, philosophical cadence. \" THE Creature is the mountain. He is immense, undeniable, and static. I do not seek to be the mountain, Emotive. I am the wind that erodes it. I am the contradiction that allows the stone to be both solid and sand.\"","He gestured to the rotting ocean below.","\" To measure up is to accept his standard. I do not accept standards. I create exceptions. Presence is vanity. Paradox... is truth.\"","Emotive stared at him, her form flashing a dull, annoyed gray.","She pouted...a childish expression on a face that could unmake civilizations.","\" Boring ,\" she muttered. \" You’re always so abstract. So... what now? The chains hold. The big bad wolf is caged. What’s the next move?\"","THE Living Paradox’s form stabilized into a regal, humanoid shape of golden light and shadow.","\" Now ,\" he said, his tone shifting to cold, administrative efficiency, \" we finish the Foundation of THE Loom. We require the other Hearts of Civilization.\"","He raised a hand, counting off on fingers that flickered in and out of existence.","\"The Heart of Hunger is secured...we broke that little glutton and took what we needed. But... The Heart of Law.\"","He shook his head with mild irritation.","\" That staunch, inflexible construct. THE Living Law shattered their own Heart rather than let us take it whole. It is not complete. It is scattered across the Folds and the expanding, fractured Wandering Territories...consequences of our battle with THE Creature that collapsed The First Folds.\"","He turned to Emotive, his gaze hardening.","\"I need you and Elemental to mobilize. Send out multiple Civilizational Legions. Track down the Shattered Parts of The Heart of Law. I don’t even require all of them... just a majority will suffice to stabilize the weave.\"","Emotive groaned, throwing her head back in an exaggerated display of theatrical apathy.","\" Ugh. Scavenger hunts? Why should I bother? Send your own paradox-puppets. I have feelings to process.\"","\"I cannot ,\" Paradox replied with unwavering calm. \" My attention, and the attention of the others, is almost entirely consumed by the suppression of that monster. Do you comprehend the effort required to keep THE Creature still?\"","His voice dropped to emphasize the gravity.","\"I can barely move a fraction of my will outside this domain. We are at the precipice of achievement, Emotive. One slip, one moment of inattention, and the cage breaks. And if it breaks...\"","He leaned in, his voice dropping to a dangerous whisper.","\"Do. Not. Mess. Around.\"","Emotive harrumphed, crossing her arms dramatically.","The colors around her spiked into a manic, jagged red of annoyance mixed with a thrill of activity.","\"Fine! Fine ,\" she snapped, her voice vibrating with manic energy. \" I’ll send the legions. I’ll send the weepiest, angriest ones I have. We’ll scour the Folds and Wandering Territories. We’ll find your little puzzle pieces.\"","She turned to leave, floating toward the edge of the balcony.","But then, she paused.","The memory of her conversation with THE Creature rose in her mind...his heavy, final answer echoing.","No glory. Only death.","She turned back to THE Living Paradox, her expression curious, hungry for a contrast.","\" Hey ,\" she called out. \" One question.\"","THE Living Paradox waited with patient stillness.","\" How much glory awaits us ?\" she asked with genuine curiosity. \" At the end of all this? When the Loom is finished and the outside burns... how much glory do we actually get?\"","...!","THE Living Paradox stood silent for a long moment.","The Sea churned below him with methodical inevitability.","Then, he smiled.","It was not a smile of joy...it was a smile of impossible geometry, a twisting of lips that suggested a joke only he understood.","\" Glory ?\"","His voice was a terrifying, paradoxical whisper that sounded like a scream heard from miles away.","\" Glory is a story told by those who survive to an audience that has no choice but to listen. When we are done, Emotive... there will be no one left to dispute our version of events.\"","His eyes blazed with concentrated intensity.","\" We will not gain glory. We will become the definition of it. For in a silent expanse... the one who speaks has all the Glory.\"","He gestured expansively.","\" We will not be remembered. We will be the only memory. We will not be celebrated. We will be the only celebration. The concept of glory itself will be redefined through our Lens of Civilization because we will be the sole arbiters of meaning.\"","His form flickered.","\" THE Creature says there is no glory, only death. He speaks from the perspective of one who has seen Civilizations rise and fall, who knows that all acclaim eventually fades to dust. He is correct... in an expanse where witnesses remain .\"","The smile widened.","\" But we are building an existence where we are the only witnesses. That is not glory as it has been understood. That is glory redefined.\"","...!","Emotive listened, the words washing over her...colder and more abstract than THE Creature’s heavy finality.","She stood silent for a moment, mulling it over carefully.","Comparing the two perspectives.","No glory, only death , the Creature had said with the weight of absolute certainty.","We become the definition of Glory , Paradox said with the confidence of rewritten reality.","One was a wall...immovable, final, honest in its brutality.","The other was a mirror, reflecting back whatever the observer brought to it, beautiful in its malleability.","She shook her head, a ripple of amethyst amusement passing through her form.","\" You’re both fucking depressing ,\" she murmured with something approaching affection.","Then, with a flash of chaotic color, she disappeared.","Leaving the balcony empty save for the entity who sought to rewrite the dictionary of existence.","THE Living Paradox stood alone, gazing at the gray ocean of failed timelines.","\"Depressing ?\" he whispered to himself. \"No , Emotive. It is not depressing.\"","His form flickered between states.","\" It is liberation.\"","HUUM!","The Sea churned below."]},{"number":4490,"title":"Chapter 4490: Chapter 4489: Results Are A Must! II","paragraphs":["In The Infiniverse.","The deepest recesses of The Infiniverse looked like the engine room of utter wonders.","Incandescent Wheels of Existence, massive beyond comprehension, rotated in slow, mesmerizing circular formation around the periphery of this space.","The atmosphere here was liquid authority.","Extremely high concentrations of Primus Mana flowed in endless, twisting rivers.","They twisted and turned, folding over one another to form perfect, glowing lemniscate symbols...infinity loops of blue-gold power that stretched into the distance.","At the very center of this sanctum, where the Primus Mana was so dense it felt like solid crystal, two figures stood.","One was a construct of light and logic, a being of blue-gold illusory brilliance. RUIN/EDEN. She floated with the grace of a system processing a trillion calculations per nanosecond, her form flickering with streams of data that defined the reality around them.","The other was solid and gloriously real!","The Infiniverse.","Her humanoid manifestation was a being of regal grandeur that demanded reverence. She was adorned in a bejeweled blue-gold dress that seemed woven from the very fabric of the Omniverses and Wheels, each gem a condensed pocket dimension, each thread a Frequency of Existence.","Her hair cascaded like a waterfall of starlight, and her eyes held the calm, terrifying depth of an ocean that knew no bottom!","She was the ground, the sky, and the surrounding atmosphere.","RUIN/EDEN looked at her, holographic eyes narrowing slightly as she processed the sheer, overwhelming data emanating from the woman beside her.","\"If one did not know the architectural truth of our Civilization,\" RUIN/EDEN said, her voice a cool, melodic chime, \"they might look at the recent battles, at the status panels, and assume that Khor, The First Hunger, numerically holds the highest Complexity and Purity among Master’s forces.\"","The Infiniverse did not look up immediately.","Her attention was focused on a holographic construct hovering between her hands...a massive, circular blue-gold bastion of light, a defensive structure so complex it made the Sovereign Spires look simple. She manipulated it with delicate fingers, adjusting the structural integrity.","\"Complexity and Purity,\" The Infiniverse replied, her voice a rich, alto hum that resonated with the spinning Wheels, \"are metrics for combatants. They measure how hard you can strike, or how much punishment you can endure before breaking.\"","She turned the hologram, watching the light refract through impossible angles.","\"But for a Civilization... raw numbers matter considerably less. What matters is Knowledge. The Knowledge and Resistance of Authorities against external pressure. The Knowledge of Principles against the erosion of time and entropy. The very Resistance of a Civilization compared to the weight of other Civilizations pressing against it. Knowledge of The Way of Existence.\"","She looked up, her eyes meeting RUIN/EDEN’s with focused intensity.","\"And right now, what matters most is not how high the number climbs. It is knowing how to use the crushing weight and systematized way of a Civilization to forge things others cannot even imagine.\"","...!","The air around her distorted with concentrated authority.","The Infiniverse had not been idle while Noah fought across the Sanctuary. She had not merely been a passive container, a backdrop for his conflicts.","She had undergone Civilization Specialization!","WAA !","Because she was the territory, because she physically encompassed the Early Veiled Shore and all the lands Noah controlled, her potential was... unique.","She had taken the path of The Infinite Bulwark, becoming the ultimate shield.","She had taken the path of The Vital Chorus, becoming the ultimate healer.","And because she physically contained the mass, the accumulated mana, and the very existence of every other being in the Civilization... her baseline was absurd. Her multipliers were catastrophic.","Her current Complexity and Purity did not sit at 100 Sextillion. Or 200.","It topped 1,000 Sextillion .","One. Thousand. Sextillion.","Oh !","Well, more accurately for her, 1 Septillion, but this required another point of understanding and distinction.","And yet, to her, this number was not a grand achievement worthy of celebration.","It was simply... necessary mass.","It was the foundation required to build what she was building.","\"How do the calculations proceed?\" The Infiniverse asked, her gaze returning to the hologram with renewed focus. \"For... THE Infinite Loom.\"","BOOM!","The name dropped into the space like a star collapsing into itself.","THE Infinite Loom.","While their Master searched for ways to survive The Fallout, while he hunted paradoxes and courted death in the Earliest Folds, while fighting Civilization Legions, his two greatest tools had been working on a solution of their own.","If THE Living Existences could build THE Loom to enact and survive the end of all things... why couldn’t they?","Why couldn’t they build their own? A better one. One forged not from betrayal and sacrifice, but from Infinite Primus Mana .","RUIN/EDEN’s form flickered, her expression shifting to one of intense, processing focus.","\"The foundation of the concept is theoretically sound,\" she stated, information streams cascading around her in brilliant cascades. \"Mana... specifically Primus Mana, which is infinite and qualitatively superior... makes for an exceptional foundation of defense. We possess the materials. We possess the architectural knowledge.\"","She frowned, the light of her form dimming slightly with concern.","\"The variable we must solve for is The Fallout itself. An all-devouring apocalypse specifically designed to shred everything in Observable Existence. It dissolves reality at fundamental levels. To stop it with Primus Mana... we require density. We require a weave so tight, so absolute, that not even the concept of ’End’ can slip through the gaps.\"","The Infiniverse nodded slowly with measured understanding.","\"We will include the Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger,\" she said, her voice calm but commanding. \"We have observed the Iron Concordat Legions in action. We have witnessed the mechanics of The Architect’s Bulwark.\"","She gestured to the hologram, expanding it with graceful motion.","\"The collective defense mechanism. The systematic spreading of damage across a vast interconnected network. If we treat the entirety of the Infiniverse as a single, massive Iron Concordat unit... if we distribute the damage of The Fallout across every atom of Primus Mana, across every structure, every weave, every particle...\"","Her eyes blazed with concentrated determination.","\"A Loom becomes inevitable. I simply need to elevate my defensive architecture to levels that can resist the friction of the end of Existence itself.\"","RUIN/EDEN smiled...a sharp, glorious expression mixing admiration with concern.","\"Yep. Simply.\"","The word dripped with irony.","It was not simple. It was not easy.","RUIN/EDEN’s smile faded, replaced by a deep, computational frown that revealed the weight of countless simulations running simultaneously.","\"There are too many unknowns,\" she admitted with unusual vulnerability. \"The precise intensity of the Fallout. The exact duration. The active interference of THE Living Existences who will not want competition. We will continue attempting to model it. We will run the simulations endlessly. But...\"","She looked at the massive, regal woman standing amidst the rivers of concentrated mana.","\"We have to calculate all contingencies with precision. We have to ensure that you are not overwhelmed while actively serving as the primary structure of THE Infinite Loom . If the pressure exceeds tolerance thresholds... if the damage distribution mechanics fail at critical junctures...\"","The Infiniverse stood with deliberate motion.","She walked to the edge of the platform, placing her hands behind her back with formal posture. She gazed out into the depths of herself...observing the countless entities residing within her territories, the cities, the farms, the schools, the cosmos, the Omniverses, the Frequencies, the Wheels, the Folds..the lives.","She saw the Emperor Penguin raising his beam with ridiculous dignity.","She saw Henry laughing with genuine joy as he began following the path of his father and began surrounding himself with women.","She saw Noah, struggling and fighting for them all in the Injunction Sanctuary of Law with relentless determination.","\"Even if I am overwhelmed,\" The Infiniverse said.","Her voice was not loud, but it carried the absolute, terrifying weight of a mother protecting her children.","\"Even if my consciousness is eclipsed by the pressure. Even if I am systematically erased, burned away by the friction of holding back the encroaching dark.\"","She turned back to RUIN/EDEN, her eyes clear, serene, and utterly resolved.","\" So long as The Master can be safe... nothing else matters.\"","...!","BOOM!","RUIN/EDEN became immensely silent, her light stilling completely.","She looked at her sister...not by blood, but by bond forged through shared purpose.","\"Remember what Master said,\" RUIN/EDEN said softly, her voice tight with emotion she shouldn’t technically be capable of feeling. \"We do not sacrifice. That...is not his Way. That is not how we survive.\"","The Infiniverse smiled with an expression mixing sadness and ancient wisdom.","It was a smile that understood the difference between ideals and reality.","\"I do not like it either, Sister,\" she replied with gentle firmness. \"I want to see Existence after The Fallout. I want to witness what he builds when the constraints are lifted.\"","She looked back at the hologram of THE Infinite Loom rotating slowly.","\"But sometimes... sacrifice becomes necessary. Not because we desire it, but because the alternative is extinction. Because the alternative is watching everything we’ve built dissolve into nothing.\"","She reached out, her hand passing through the hologram with deliberate motion, touching the center where Noah would theoretically be safest.","\"I hope it won’t come to that,\" she whispered with genuine longing. \"I hope for all of us to pass through this trial intact. I hope we can cheat the system one more time.\"","Her hand clenched into a fist, crushing the light momentarily.","\" But hopes are merely hopes. Wishes without substance.\"","Her voice hardened.","\" And results... results are a must.\"","...!","RUIN/EDEN processed this declaration in silence."]},{"number":4491,"title":"Chapter 4491: Chapter 4490: Why? I","paragraphs":["The Sanctuary of The First Farmer.","In a secluded corner of this vast agricultural domain, far from the war, there existed a singular plot of land.","It was isolated, wrapped in curtain-like auroras of green and gold that shimmered with concentrated power.","The farm plot itself was perfect.","The soil was dark and rich, crumbling just right, shining with deep verdant-gold luster. It looked vibrant with potential, as if something impossible had just been planted within its depths.","Standing at the edge was The First Farmer.","He no longer looked frail or dying, or dead when his daughter last burried him. He stood tall, his skin marked with green glyphs, his golden eyes burning with steady light.","He gazed at the soil with certainty.","Sitting on the soft earth nearby was Elyndra.","She wore a verdant-gold dress, her aura pulsing with controlled power. She ran her fingers through the dirt, feeling the thrumming vibration of life beneath.","The silence between father and daughter was comfortable...the quiet of a field after sowing is done.","The First Farmer broke it.","\"I should never have put that weight on you, Elyndra,\" he said, still looking at the plot. \"The schemes. The deception. Ordering you to betray a potential ally for my own failing existence... it was desperate. The act of a dying man who had lost his Way.\"","His voice held genuine regret.","\"I should never have asked you to bear my failures.\"","He turned to her, his golden eyes softening.","\"I am thankful that Osmont chose not to hold it against you. He saw the weapon I tried to make you, and he chose to treat you as a person instead.\"","...!","Elyndra’s hand paused in the soil.","A slow, knowing smile touched her lips. Her eyes drifted to the side, as if seeing a figure in obsidian-gold armor standing in the distance.","\"He isn’t that bad,\" she said softly, warmth coloring her voice. \"His Way of Existence... it is unique. Terrifying, yes, but also... encompassing.\"","She paused.","\"He elevated me in ways I didn’t think possible.\"","The First Farmer watched her smile.","He saw how her eyes softened when she spoke of the Tyrant.","And in that moment, he felt a hollow sensation in his chest...not pain, but loss!","Something precious drifting away from him toward a gravity he couldn’t compete with.","He opened his mouth, then closed it.","What could he say? He had pushed her away with his schemes. He had pushed her directly toward Noah with his commands.","He simply sighed.","Elyndra looked up, sensing his shift in mood.","She tilted her head, curious and concerned.","\"What did you just plant here, Father? The energy feels different...\"","The First Farmer’s expression shifted.","The melancholic father receded. The Primordial Sovereign of a Civilization emerged.","\" Effort ,\" he said simply.","He walked to the center of the plot, hands clasped behind his back.","\"We speak of effort often, but do we truly understand its origin? An existence...begins to exert effort the very moment they are born into harsh reality.\"","He gestured to the empty air.","\"Think of those born without authority. Without Mana. Without lineage. They come into the world screaming and kicking. Their lungs cry out for air they’ve never breathed. Their eyes burn from light they’ve never seen.\"","His voice grew stronger.","\"Their very first act is struggle. Desperate, flailing effort just to be. Just to exist in a reality that doesn’t welcome them gently.\"","He looked down at the glowing soil.","\"Since the moment one is born, they exert effort. Every breath. Every step. Every choice to continue existing when cessation would be easier...that is effort. It accumulates across a lifetime. But for most... it dissipates. It is lost, unrecognized and unharvested.\"","His golden eyes blazed.","\"But after embarking on my Way... after establishing the Civilization of Effort... I realized that this accumulation should not be lost. So, for the first thing I plant in this new era...\"","HUUM !","The soil pulsed!","\"I planted these Seeds of Effort ,\" he declared. \"They will mature very soon. They will produce fruit that anyone can consume to retroactively gain harvest from all the effort they’ve invested since birth.\"","He spread his arms.","\"Every scream as an infant. Every struggle to walk. Every drop of sweat pursuing cultivation. Every moment of persistence...returned to them as concentrated power.\"","He turned to Elyndra, eyes shining brilliantly.","\"I prepare this to become a foundational pillar of my Civilization. And also... as a gift. A gift to the one whose actions paved the way for my Civilization’s emergence.\"","His voice softened.","\"A tribute to The Early Creature, Osmont. \"","He paused, a faint smile touching his lips.","\"I will give you one to consume. And I will give you additional fruits to bring to Osmont as tribute from one Primordial Sovereign to another.\"","Elyndra nodded.","The First Farmer continued, his gaze turning penetrating.","\"Maybe with this... with the retroactive harvest of your own lifetime of accumulated struggle... your own effort may prove sufficient to catalyze the emergence of a Principle that I could never cultivate to completion.\"","He began pacing along the plot’s edge.","\"Principles,\" The First Farmer mused, \"are profoundly misunderstood. Even Early Creatures often view them simply as weapons...a sharper sword, a harder shield.\"","He shook his head.","\"They are not weapons. They are the very directives of existence. They are fundamental tools that compose the source code of reality itself.\"","He raised a hand, weaving a small lattice of green light.","\"With Principles, you can better manipulate the underlying code of existence. With the right Principle... the right conceptual tool... you could alter your surrounding existence to affect your Civilization and impose conditions upon your enemies.\"","The lattice shifted as he spoke.","\"You could accomplish feats that leave observers wondering how such impossibilities are achieved... when you’re not actually doing anything impossible. You’ve simply found the right key for a lock in existence’s code that lets you bypass the wall entirely.\"","The lattice formed an elegant tree shape.","\"The Principle of Perpetual Harvest that I never fully cultivated... that was one such key. A key that opens the door to infinite accumulation. That helps build a terrific Civilization with exponential growth.\"","The tree became a spinning wheel.","\"The Principle of Perpetual Effort, which I gained through my collapse and emergence... is another key. It lets one bypass the traditional requirement of success. Failure becomes irrelevant when effort itself is the harvest.\"","He looked at Elyndra, his gaze piercing.","\"Now, the Principle I envisioned for you... the one I attempted to guide you toward with Perpetual Harvest’s assistance... would be a Principle that can alter the weavings of existence in an even grander manner than simple Harvest.\"","He lowered his voice to a whisper that somehow carried prophetic weight.","\"At the very minimum... I was confident it would let you attain THE False designation rather quickly. Perhaps even transcend that threshold entirely.\"","...!","Elyndra’s eyes shone brightly.","Ambition and possibility ignited within her like flame meeting oil.","The False THE .","A state of being that mimicked the absolute authority of reality’s architects!","Her Nine Principles had been cultivated over eons precisely for this...to serve as stairs ascending toward something transcendent. And now, with Perpetual Harvest from Noah and the imminent consumption of accumulated Effort...","The path is becoming clear.","At this moment, the earth around them began to shine.","WAA!","Brilliant beams of green-gold light shot upward from the soil!","The seeds were germinating at impossible speed, driven by the sheer conceptual density they embodied!","Stems erupted from the earth, thick and glowing. Leaves unfurled with geometric perfection. And at the apex of each rapidly growing stalk, fruits began forming...crystalline spheres pulsing with accumulated authority spanning eons!","Each fruit contained the effort of existence itself!","The light was blinding, washing over the entire plot and making the surrounding auroras seem dim by comparison!","The First Farmer smiled with deep, satisfied pride.","\"My effort is already bearing fruit,\" he said quietly. \"As it should. As it must.\"","He extended a hand to his daughter.","\"Come. Prepare yourself for the harvest.\"","Elyndra stood gracefully, brushing soil from her dress.","She approached the glowing stalks with reverence, feeling the thrumming power from the crystalline fruits. Each one contained a lifetime of struggle...birth, growth, cultivation, failure, persistence.","All the effort that was ever lost... now concentrated and ready to be reclaimed.","Her hand reached toward the nearest fruit!"]},{"number":4492,"title":"Chapter 4492: Chapter 4491: Why? II","paragraphs":["Back in the Injunction Sanctuary of Law.","Noah stood amidst the chaotic currents of the battlefield, his armored form a silent, unmoving axis around which the violence spun. He did not raise his blade or cast an ability...he simply observed, his eyes flicking from one front to another with the cold, detached precision of an Emperor rearranging pieces on a board that spanned light-years.","His presence alone was a weight, an anchor of Primus Mana that stabilized the shaking reality of the Sanctuary.","Far to his left, the battle lines had shifted.","Ozymandias stood as a lone, obsidian-crimson bastion before the crumbling ranks of Deborah’s Civilization Legion of Laws. Behind him, silver-skinned Living Laws trembled while before him surged a storm of violet and gray...a tidal wave of weaponized sorrow led by the weeping figure of Threnody.","The Weaver of Final Sorrows did not attack with fancy abilities. He attacked with feeling.","Around him, tens of thousands of Living Emotives dissolved into a singular, nebulous cloud of pure, distilled negative emotion. It was a fog of suicide and a mist of absolute surrender. Threnody floated at its heart, his tear-filled eyes fixing on Ozymandias and the trembling Living Laws behind him.","\"Why do you persist?\" Threnody asked, his voice a soft, hypnotic melody that bypassed the ears and whispered directly into the soul.","He raised his shadowy hands, and the violet cloud surged forward to drown.","\"The struggle is the pain,\" Threnody crooned. \"To fight is to suffer. Look at the horizon and see the inevitability of the End. We were forgotten and discarded , and there is no salvation in resistance...only the prolongation of agony.\"","HUUM !","The wave crashed down with the weight of thousands of Sextillions in raw Complexity, but its true danger lay in its frequency. It permeated the Haki of the Living Laws, seeping into their minds like water through cracked stone.","\"Let go,\" Threnody whispered. \"Just... let go.\"","Behind Ozymandias, several silver-skinned Living Laws dropped their Civilizational Authority of Law as their eyes dulled. They looked at their own hands, then at the void, and began to channel their authority inward...preparing to collapse their own existences simply to stop the noise of living.","It was a massacre of the will.","But Ozymandias smiled.","His obsidian-crimson jaw unhinged to reveal the spinning, fiery void of his Infinite Hunger.","\"Let go?\" Ozymandias rumbled, his voice a tyrannical counter-frequency that shattered the hypnotic rhythm. \"I never let go of anything I intend to eat.\"","WOOSH !","He inhaled.","The violet cloud of suicidal despair, the weaponized sorrow of an entire Legion...was sucked into the maw of the Hungering Maw specialist. It was a torrent of negative energy that would be poison to most, but it was flavor to him. He drank the despair and swallowed the grief, and as he did, the Damage Conversion protocol from the Iron Concordat flared to life.","The suffering was not felt at all as it was processed like fuel.","Ozymandias snapped his jaw shut and the air cleared instantly!","WAA !","\"You speak of terror,\" Ozymandias said, wiping a stray wisp of violet energy from his lip. \"You speak of the fear of the End. But you are merely sad, little ghost.\"","His predatory gaze fixed on Threnody with absolute certainty.","\"You do not know true fear.\"","Above him, a Primus Mana Codex materialized and blazed with the light of a Primus Mana Arcana Glyph. The card depicted a writhing mass of tentacles and eyes rising from a dark, forgotten ocean...ancient in design and terrible in purpose.","| Mana Arcana Glyph: The Horror from the Deep|","\"Allow me to educate you,\" Ozymandias whispered.","The card dissolved into green-black light.","SCREEEEEE !","Reality tore open above the Emotive Legion, and from the rift it emerged...a Chthonian monstrosity of impossible scale. It was a mountain of wet, slick flesh and writhing tentacles, a visage of madness that defied geometry. Countless eyes opened across its bulk, and each one served as a window into a dimension of pure, unadulterated terror.","|Damage Conversion Discharge: Active|","|Input: 5,000 Sextillion Stored Kinetic Authority|","|Status: Channeling into Summoned Entity|","The stored damage from the Iron Concordat’s defense flowed into the Horror, inflating its power to levels that warped the very physics of the Sanctuary. 5,000 Sextillion worth of destructive potential swelled within its impossible form.","\"Know true fear,\" Ozymandias commanded. \" Know true terror.\"","HUUM!","The Horror descended with tentacles that lashed out not to strike but to grasp. It wrapped around the Emotive Legion, crushing the violet clouds and shattering the weeping forms of the Early Creatures.","Threnody bellowed and erupted with fervor!","But the Horror feasted regardless. The Legion of Emotives broke as their disciplined despair shattered into chaotic, frantic rout, and more than a dozen fell prey to be devoured.","...!","Noah watched the carnage with a faint smile before turning his gaze elsewhere...to the sector where death bloomed like a dark flower.","He gazed at his prized Lich!","Arch Lich Ra’Zan floated amidst a cloud of necrotic brilliance with nine new figures standing before him. They were titanic entities that radiated a cold and absolute stillness.","|Transformation Complete: 9x Primus Inevitabilities of Death|","|Base Material: High-Quality Early Creature Corpses|","|Average Complexity/Purity: 200 Sextillion|","|Classification: Mind Flayer Elemental Liches|","They were nightmares of design...humanoid forms draped in robes of obsidian crimson that seemed woven from dried blood, their faces hidden in the shadows of their hoods. Only pairs of burning, abyssal eyes were visible along with clusters of writhing, purple-grey tentacles where mouths should be.","They held staffs made of frozen lightning and petrified magma, marking them as Elemental masters corrupted by Death.","Noah looked at them and saw not just soldiers but potential. Their base power was many times that of a standard Primus Inevitability, and if they specialized...","He didn’t hesitate.","\"Civilization is growth,\" Noah stated, his voice carrying across the battlefield with absolute authority.","HUUM !","Behind him, space fractured as a massive structure descended from the bruised sky and tore through the clouds of war. It was a Sovereign Spire of Osmont, but it burned with a deep, aggressive obsidian crimson light, and its architecture was sharp and predatory.","THE CRIMSON HUNGER SOVEREIGN SPIRE.","\"Ra’Zan,\" Noah commanded. \"Let the newcomers undergo Specialization.\"","...!","Ra’Zan cackled with a sound like grinding stones. \" KEKEKEKE ! Enter, my beauties! Embrace the hunger!\"","The nine Mind Flayer Elemental Liches distorted space, flickering out of existence and reappearing before the open doors of the Spire. They flowed inside, eager for the transformation that would turn them into monsters of the Hungering Maw.","Noah’s eyes pulsed with tyrannical satisfaction because when they emerged, they would be fucking catastrophes!","But there was one final piece on the board.","Noah turned his head slowly as his gaze locked onto the distant figure of Aethon, The Primeval Storm-Forge.","The Elemental leader was still fighting and still commanding his legion against the impenetrable wall of the Iron Concordat and the rampaging fury of Khor. He was a titan of duty who burned his existence to hold the line.","Noah’s voice projected outward and cut through the roar of the elements.","\"Aethon.\"","The giant froze before turning, his binary star eyes meeting Noah’s crimson gaze.","\"Why fight for a Civilization that has forsaken you?\" Noah asked with a tone that was not mocking but genuinely curious. \"You see my Legions overwhelming you and the collapse of your brothers and sisters. You know the doors of THE Loom are closed to you.\"","Noah gestured to the battlefield and the inevitable tide of his victory.","\"Why fight for THE Loom to hasten your collapse when it will collapse you and your people regardless of the outcome?\"","...!","He had seen this being with his Lens of Civilization. Aethon was mighty as it would be such a waste if he was merely collapsed!","Aethon straightened as magma dripped from his chin and lightning crackled across his shoulders. His binary star eyes blazed with ancient conviction.","\"My life is for Elemental,\" Aethon rumbled, his voice shaking the ground. \"My being is for Elemental, and my brethren will only ever follow the Elemental Civilization. It is our Way and our Truth, and we do not abandon it because the end is near.\"","It was a noble answer and a tragic one.","Noah nodded coldly.","\"If you only follow Elemental...\" He raised his hand. \"Then I can embody for you a grand Elemental Civilization.\"","HUUM !","Noah tapped into his existence and accessed the Principle of Mana Supremacy. He drew upon the Living Existential Authority of Elemental he possessed and then flooded it all with Primus Mana.","His hand began to burn, but it was not the blue-gold of his usual authority.","It was a blinding, crystalline blue-gold Frost.","\" Elemental is Mana ,\" Noah whispered. \" And Mana is Infinite in its variations.\"","BOOM!","He borrowed from the storage of Damage Conversion as just over 1,000 Sextillion in Complexity and Purity flowed across his existence for the scale of what he intended to achieve.","|Damage Conversion Withdrawal: 1,000+ Sextillion|","|Purpose: Elemental Authority Manifestation|","|Status: Channeling...|","BOOM !","He released it.","The sky above the battlefield changed instantly as the bruised, chaotic vortex vanished. In its place, a blanket of radiant, stellar blue-gold clouds formed.","And then it began to snow.","But this was not ice...each flake was a crystallized concept of Elemental Perfection, and each flake carried the weight of a star. The temperature plummeted to absolute zero, yet the snow burned with authority as it coated the battlefield in seconds and turned the shattered canyons into a glittering, majestic wonderland of frozen power.","The Elemental Legion stopped fighting.","The magma cooled and the lightning froze in mid-arc. They looked up with eyes wide with shock because they felt it...the purity, the density, the sheer and undeniable Civilizational Elemental Authority radiating from Noah. It was richer than anything they had felt from their own leaders, deeper and more profound.","\"This is Elemental,\" Noah’s voice boomed from everywhere at once, carried by the snow. \"I know your very existence can sense it.\"","He floated higher while wreathed in the blue-gold storm, looking like a titan of winter and Mana, an Emperor of frozen perfection presiding over a battlefield that had become his canvas.","\"Why would you oppose a Civilization of Elementals that wishes to fight against the collapse of THE Loom ?\" His voice resonated through every snowflake. \"Why die for those who locked you out when you can live for a Civilization that embodies your Way perfectly?\"","...!","Aethon trembled.","He looked at the snow falling on his magma skin and saw that it did not melt. It settled there like a blessing, cool and absolute, carrying authority that spoke to the very core of what he was.","What the fuck was this?","Like, really. What the fuck?","This is impossible , Aethon thought. No authority, no being...can simply become Elemental...right? Civilizational at that too???","But the snow falling on his skin told a different story.","He looked at his legion and saw them shaking, their loyalty to the abstract concept of ’Elemental’ warring with the reality of the Elemental Supremacy standing before them.","Noah extended a hand.","\" THE Loom abandoned you,\" he said simply. \"I offer you a storm that never ends.\"","...!","Anaximander once told him to become the storm. And boy oh boy, did he want to rage!","The battlefield fell silent, save for the soft, heavy sound of falling snow."]},{"number":4493,"title":"Chapter 4493: Chapter 4492: You Sacrilegius Savage! I","paragraphs":["Aethon stood amidst the ruins of the shattered canyon, his massive storm-forged hand outstretched as snowflakes fell upon his skin and did not melt. They landed softly, each one a perfect crystalline geometric proof of Elemental Authority, and he stared at them with something like wonder.","They were blue-gold and vibrant and impossible, carrying the weight of Sextillions in Complexity, enough power to crush a lesser being into quantum dust, yet they rested on his palm with the gentleness of a memory.","This is Elemental , Aethon thought as the sensation washed over his existential core, his mind reeling with recognition.","It was undeniable. It wasn’t mimicry or a clever illusion spun from Mana or Hunger, but the fundamental resonance of the Elements themselves, pure and unadulterated and singing with a frequency he hadn’t felt since the golden age of the Earliest Folds.","How?","His thoughts raced and collided like tectonic plates. ’Is this a branch? A lost lineage of our Civilization that evolved in isolation? Or are they something else entirely?’","He could sense the Hunger in them, the raw devouring appetite woven through the Elemental Authority.","’Can a Civilization imitate another so perfectly? Can Hunger digest the concept of Fire and spit it back out as Ash that burns hotter than the flame?’","He looked deeper into the snowflake, letting its authority seep into his pores, and felt the answer rise within him.","No.","The thought was immediate and absolute. ’ Imitation is flawed. Imitation lacks the soul. This... this feels like The Early Flame. This feels like the Elemental Dominions before they left us behind...’","...!","He looked up, his binary star eyes sweeping across the battlefield to where the armies of the Tyrant stood motionless. Fifteen million entities frozen in a tableau of disciplined power, their hands raised and weapons lowered, waiting for a single command that had not yet come.","And at their center, floating above the carnage like a titan of winter and war, was the Tyrant himself.","Aethon had met beings like this before, had stood in the presence of Gilgamesh, the ancient Leader who had believed his will could reshape existence itself. He saw the resemblance now, not in form but in the presence, the sheer undeniable gravity of a being who believed with absolute certainty that his will was the only law that mattered.","Silence stretched across the sanctuary, heavy and suffocating as Aethon looked back at his legion.","Tens of thousands of his brothers and sisters, Living Elementals of void-wind, magma-titans, storm-callers, were looking at him with eyes filled with confusion and fear and a desperate aching hope. The voice that had awakened them, the voice that had promised them entry into THE Loom , had felt like Elemental Authority too, but it had been cold and transactional and had asked them to die for a promise that was false.","’It condemned us ,’ Aethon realized as bitterness rose in his throat like bile. ’ It woke us up only to spend our lives as currency, to buy a few more seconds of delay against the inevitable.’","He had followed the order because that was his Way, because an Elemental does not stop burning until the fuel is gone, because if death was certain then dying with purpose was the only dignity left.","But now...","He looked at the Tyrant and at the blue-gold snow that promised a storm that never ends, and the question rose within him unbidden.","Was this salvation? Or was it just another form of consumption?","Aethon’s gaze hardened and he looked directly at the Tyrant, his voice a rumble that shook the frost from the surrounding stones.","\"Tyrant,\" Aethon called out. \"What is... leadership to you?\"","...!","The question hung in the air, simple and devastating.","Leadership.","Noah looked down at the Elemental Titan and his armored form pulsed with concentrated authority as he considered his answer.","\"Leadership,\" Noah replied, his voice echoing from everywhere at once and carried by the snow, \"is not the spending of lives but the investment of them.\" He lowered his hand slightly and the snow intensified, swirling around him like a cloak of stars. \"There are those who lead from behind, pushing their people into the fire to warm their own hands. They call it sacrifice and they call it necessity.\"","His voice hardened with contempt.","\"I call it cowardice. I dislike sacrifice.\"","HUUM!","\"Leadership is the shield that breaks first and the blade that strikes first and the will that refuses to bend when Existence demands submission.\" Noah swept his arm across the horizon, encompassing his armies and his people and his Way. \"I do not ask my people to die for me. I ask them to live for the Civilization we are building together.\"","He leaned forward and his presence became crushing and absolute.","\"I would never lie to them or tell them to accept death as a strategy. At this very moment I am fighting against THE Loom and fighting against the Fallout and fighting against the very concept of an Ending.\"","His voice dropped to a whisper that somehow carried across Gigaparsecs.","\"Leadership is the promise that if we fall, we fall together. But we will not fall today, or in the days to come.\"","...!","Aethon listened and closed his eyes as a memory surfaced, ancient and vivid and unbidden.","A shore of golden sand and a gathering of titans, and at the center a figure of hazy indistinct power, THE Creature , speaking to them not as subjects but as potentials.","Why ? Aethon wondered. Why do I think of HIM now?","He opened his eyes and looked at the Tyrant, and he did not understood.","THE Creature had nothing to do with this being.","Aethon looked at his hand again where the blue-gold snowflake was still there, unmelting and perfect, and he made his choice.","He raised his hand high and the Civilizational Authority of Elemental within him flared to life, burning with a desperate final brilliance as magma and storm and void mixed into a beacon of pure intent.","\"I do not do this for me,\" Aethon announced, his voice cracking with the weight of his decision, \" but for my brothers and sisters . As a leader I have to take care of them.\" He shook his head slowly. \"And the thought of betraying their trust, of leading them into a meaningless death for a lie... it is too heavy to bear.\"","...!","He turned his back to Noah and faced his legion, drawing in a breath that shook the earth beneath him.","\"Brothers! Sisters of the Elements!\"","BOOM !","His voice was a volcanic eruption that silenced every other sound in the sanctuary.","\"Heed my last command as your leader!\"","The tens of thousands of Elementals straightened as the magma cooled and the winds stilled, and they listened with the absolute attention of soldiers who had followed him through eons.","\" LIVE !\"","Aethon roared the word and it shattered the despair that had hung over them for countless ages.","\"The Civilization of Elementals permeates within THE Loom and outside of it. It is not a place but a Way!\" He pointed back at the Tyrant and at the storm of blue-gold snow that surrounded him. \"For the sake of your lives... will you follow the Civilization of Elements here? The Elements that will rage to keep your light burning with glory?!\"","...!","The legion looked at one another and then at the Iron Concordat standing like statues of invincibility, and then at the Tyrant who offered a storm instead of a grave. Hesitation rippled through them like wind across water, doubt and fear warring with desperate hope.","But then they looked at Aethon, their leader, the one who had woken first and refused to let them die in the cold.","One by one their expressions firmed as the magma hardened into resolve and the lightning stabilized into purpose.","A Magma Lord raised his fist high.","\"For the Elements!\"","\"For the Storm!\"","\"For Life!\"","Tens of thousands of fists rose into the air and the roar was deafening, a chorus of elemental power that shook the sanctuary to its bedrock and made the very fabric of existence tremble.","\"We follow the Civilization of Elements wherever it may be!\"","...!","Aethon watched them and a sad proud smile touched his cracked lips as he spoke the final words.","\"The peaceful snow cascades all around you,\" he whispered, but his voice carried to every single one of them through the resonance of their shared nature. \"The peaceful snow burning with an extremely pure Civilizational Authority of Elemental. Pay your respects to this authority.\"","...!","The words were simple but the effect was absolute.","The Legion of Elementals reached out with magma hands and wind-form tendrils and void-claws, reaching into the air to catch the falling blue-gold flakes. They closed their eyes and accepted what was being offered, not conquest but recognition, not subjugation but belonging.","WAA !","It was a profound moment in time as the transfer of allegiance occurred, And the moment the commitment was made, the blue-gold snow that covered the Injunction Sanctuary of Law changed fundamentally.","It stopped falling gently and began to spin and howl with building intensity.","HUUM !","It became a storm .","The Civilizational Authority of Elemental surged outward and covered the entire domain in a blizzard of absolute tyrannical power, and the sanctuary itself trembled with the weight of what had just occurred!"]},{"number":4494,"title":"Chapter 4494: Chapter 4493: You Sacrilegius Savage! II","paragraphs":["It fucking worked?","Noah’s eyes shone with brilliance as he watched the impossible unfold before him.","It was a long shot, a gamble based on a split-second analysis through the Lens of Civilization. He had looked at Aethon and peeled back the layers of magma and storm to see the core truth of the entity, and what he found was simple and profound. Aethon cared for his people more than his pride.","Was this the first enemy that was actually reasonable?","Noah watched the blue-gold snowflakes settle on the skin of the Elemental Legion like blessings descending from an alien heaven. He watched them close their eyes in reverence. He watched them pay their respects to his Primus Mana , to the Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger that wore the mask of Elemental supremacy with such perfect conviction.","The moment they accepted, his existence lurched.","It wasn’t a stumble or a misstep but an expansion, as if the boundaries of his being had suddenly grown to encompass territory that had never belonged to him before.","He felt a profound sense of immensity wash over him, a validation that vibrated in his very marrow and sang through his bones. He had made the right choice!","In all things, Noah debated the angles and calculated the trade-offs. Every action was a transaction with Existence. To spare Aethon was to forsake the immediate loot of tens of thousands of Sextillion-level entities, to leave a harvest un-reaped in the traditional sense of conquest and consumption.","But as the immensity settled into his bones and spread through his consciousness, he knew the trade was not just fair.","It was a magisterial robbery.","Because the prompts that bloomed before his vision were not of simple experience or loot, not the mundane accumulation of power through violence.","They were of Glory.","|UNFATHOMABLE ACTION CONFIRMED|","|You have embarked further upon your Way of Existence.|","|You have actively utilized the Unique Quality of The Way of Mana.|","|Analysis: Mana is present and pervasive. It is the basal authority, the fundamental building block of countless weavings. No fire burns, no ice freezes, no earth hardens without the catalyst of Mana.|","|By proving your Mana is the supreme form of their authority, you have initiated:|","| THE CIVILIZATIONAL ENCROACHMENT OF MANA|","|Target: The Primordial Civilization of Elemental.|","|Status: You have laid claim to the foundations of this Civilization. |","|The number of entities paying respect is small relative to the whole, but their acknowledgment represents a conceptual breach. You have opened a pathway to siphon the immensity and harvest of a Primordial Civilization directly.|","...!","Noah read the words and his eyes blazed with concentrated intensity.","Around him, the blue-gold snowstorm became maddeningly serious in its purpose. It spun faster, the flakes growing heavy with accumulated authority, turning the battlefield into a domain of absolute Mana Supremacy.","He felt it then, a terrifying influx of harvest crashing down toward his existence like the endless waves of a celestial sea threatening to drown him in power.","|Quintessential Harvest Descends.|","|Source: Civilizational Encroachment|","|Target: Primordial Civilization of Elemental|","| The harvest of the laid claim has begun . The concentration of this authority exceeds all prior harvests.|","|The foundation of the Elemental Civilization stretches far outside THE Loom and expresses itself even more immensely within it. You are siphoning from the totality.|","|Under your Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger, a new feature has risen- The Derivative Civilizations of Mana and Hunger|","|You can now enact: The Derivative Civilization of Elemental under the Brilliance of Mana.|","...!","Holy shit.","What?","Noah’s mind raced as he processed the implications cascading through his understanding.","A Derivative Civilization?","He thought that power belonged solely to THE Creature , that only THE Primordial Civilization of Existence could spawn derivatives like The Way of Idle Existence or The Civilization of Effort. These were privileges reserved for the absolute pinnacle of existential authority.","But now... his own Civilization could do it?","Because Mana is fundamental. Because Mana is everywhere. Because he proved his Primus Mana can become any Element!","Oh!","He felt the harvest slamming into the Architect’s Bulwarks with the force of continental collision. The walls of his civilization were growing thicker and taller and more absolute with each passing moment. He was eating the foundation of a rival Primordial power and using it to pave his own streets, to build his own monuments, to fuel his own ascension!","It was a moment of profound and glorious change. It was a victory that would be marked in the annals of history! Well, however short that history would be.","But choices always have reactions.","Every action has an equal and opposite reaction, whether intended or not, whether welcomed or feared.","Noah had reached out and touched the foundation of a Primordial Civilization with grasping fingers. He had grabbed a pillar of the establishment and shaken it with the audacity of a thief in the night.","And the owner of that house, of course, noticed.","It was akin to opening the doors of a bedroom and taking another’s wife right there...of course they would see you do it!","\" You Sacrilegious Fucking Savage.\"","BOOM !","The voice was deep and terrifying and absolute. It did not come from the air or from any physical source but from the atoms themselves, vibrating with fury.","\" How dare you?\"","...!","Everything froze in that instant.","The snow stopped falling mid-descent. The wind stopped howling as if cut by an invisible blade.","Existence itself trembled under the weight of attention suddenly focused on this single point in space and time.","DUM. DUM. DUM.","Drums began to beat with terrible rhythm. Not drums of skin and wood but drums of frozen fire and elemental voids, instruments forged from the fundament of reality itself. A symphony began to spread across the battlefield, a rising crescendo that screamed a single word across every frequency of observable existence.","ELEMENTAL!","ELEMENTAL!","ELEMENTAL!","Noah’s eyes snapped wide open as recognition slammed into him.","He looked past Aethon and past the submitted legion kneeling in the snow. He looked to the rear, to the distant scattered members of the Elemental Civilization who had not yet paid respect, who had remained uncommitted in their uncertainty.","Their eyes ignited with crimson-gold light.","The glow blazed from their sockets with intensity that burned away their individuality and their choice. They were no longer independent soldiers making their own decisions but vessels, hollow containers for something far greater and far more terrible as their existence could not handle it and already shockingly began to melt their bodies.","A terrifying consciousness was descending upon them. It was forcing its way into the fabric of the Injunction Sanctuary with brutal inevitability, tearing through the barriers of distance and dimension as if such concepts were merely polite suggestions.","The booming voice came from their mouths now, spoken in perfect horrifying synchrony that made the words echo and multiply across the battlefield even as their bodies broke down. This entity did not care.","Just as THE Living Paradox had descended to protect his Vessels when Noah and Khor were about to collapse it.","THE Living Elemental ...was trying to descend.","Unlike the others, he was not here for a game or a philosophical debate.","His Civilization, his very foundation, had just been encroached upon by an upstart thief. A burglar had broken into his vault and was actively stealing from the treasury, and he had come to catch the perpetrator red-handed and make an example of such audacity!","Noah’s gaze flashed with fierceness and lividity mixing into something dangerous.","He did not cower before the descending presence. He did not apologize or attempt to explain or beg for mercy.","He prepared.","An unfathomable opportunity had opened before him like a door to paradise.","And an equally dangerous predicament had descended to meet it!"]},{"number":4495,"title":"Chapter 4495: Chapter 4494: You Sacrilegius Savage! III","paragraphs":["The atmosphere within the Injunction Sanctuary of Law had changed fundamentally and irrevocably. It was no longer just a battlefield where armies clashed and strategies unfolded.","It was a site of judgment where the very concept of defiance was being tested against absolute authority.","Noah stood alone amidst the swirling vortex of molten mana and shattered ice. His form, once a pillar of unshakeable stability radiating tyrannical confidence, was pulsing.","Ambessa had advised him to another anger THE Living Paradox . That this whole time that entity was simply playing.","He faced THE Living Paradox , and the entity had merely toyed with him like a cat playing with a mouse.","Now he had enraged THE Living Elemental, and the entity had decided to burn him out of existence entirely.","The encroachment upon the Elemental Civilization’s foundation was a triumph of unparalleled magnitude. The harvest was flooding into his Architect’s Bulwarks with torrential force, elevating his Civilization to heights previously unimaginable and opening pathways to power that should have taken eons to discover.","But every action had an equal and opposite reaction.","And the reaction of a Primordial Sovereign was absolute.","Noah watched the bodies of the possessed Elementals disintegrate before his eyes. Their forms unraveled like cheap fabric torn by hurricane winds, unable to contain the sheer density of the authority pouring through them from across impossible distances.","Through their melting eyes, an utterly terrifying gaze fixed upon him with laser focus. It was a look of pure unadulterated hatred, the kind of hatred reserved for a thief who had desecrated a holy site and spat upon the altar.","Oppression descended like a physical thing.","It was not physical weight pressing down on his shoulders, but a conceptual decree written into the fabric of reality itself. Every atom of Noah’s existence screamed in protest, demanding he kneel and prostrate himself before the brilliance of The Elemental Sovereign.","But his Primus Mana burned in defiance!","It flared blue-gold, a defiant star against the encroaching red sun of foreign authority.","He looked down at that terrifying power, his gaze cracking under the strain but holding firm. He met the gaze without flinching.","The response was immediate and volcanic.","\" You Sacrilegious Fucking Savage!\"","BOOM!","The roar vaporized the remaining snow in an instant. The glittering rivers of accumulated frost turned to steam that rose in billowing clouds. The space above the disintegrating Elementals split wide open, a jagged wound in reality that bled blinding crimson-gold light like arterial spray.","\" You think yourself safe due to this suppression of existence? \" the regal voice boomed, echoing from every particle of the surrounding air and making the stones themselves vibrate with fury. \" You think yourself defiant enough to encroach upon my brilliance without consequence?! Then have a taste of my brilliance directly!\"","Existence suppressed THE entities from THE Loom from exerting their influence outside of it! It did! But still...","Even as existence itself trembled and pressed down on the intrusion, trying desperately to force the Primordial entity back into its designated box, THE Living Elemental paid the cost willingly. It burned its own essence like fuel to force the attack through the barriers.","A beam of crimson-gold fire shot out from the rift.","It was not fire in any conventional sense. It was Immolation given purpose and direction, the concept of burning distilled into a weapon.","\"Brother!\"","Titano’s voice was a desperate roar that shook the battlefield. The giant stepped forward with earth-shaking strides, his massive form interposing itself between Noah and the descending judgment.","Millions of Primus Inevitabilities flared with brilliant light, throwing themselves into the path of the beam with devotion.","Khor moved with inhuman speed, her small form blazing with hunger. Riya’s eyes shone with light as she calculated probabilities.","Alexander’s silver-white authority erupted like a shield as he bellowed, a unique authority of THE Living Law erupting from his body as he surged forward!","They all rushed forward with single-minded purpose.","Protos wrapped his tentacles around Noah with crushing force, forming a living cocoon of loyalty and sacrifice.","They would die for him without hesitation. They would burn so he did not have to face this alone!","Noah looked at them and saw the fear in their eyes mixing with absolute willingness to end their own stories to prolong his.","He shook his head slowly.","\"In my Civilization,\" Noah’s voice boomed, straining against the pain already radiating from the approaching light, \"there shall be no sacrifice. In my Civilization, I am the sword and the shield. I am the first and the last line of defense.\"","...!","He stepped forward with deliberate purpose.","Forcefully, the Civilizational Armor of Protos peeled away from his body, obeying the absolute command of its master even as its spirit screamed in protest and desperation. Noah’s humanoid form emerged from the protective cocoon, vulnerable and defiant and utterly exposed.","He took a single step forward, moving far ahead of his protectors, placing himself directly in the path of the descending beam with arms spread wide.","He looked at the unfathomable authority approaching him and felt the heat before it even made contact with his skin.","BOOM !","The impact was silent and absolute, a contradiction that hurt the mind to perceive. A blinding crimson-gold brilliance swallowed everything in its path. Steam hissed and boiled. Reality itself warped under the concentrated assault.","At the center of the inferno, Noah stood.","He was burning .","His skin blistered and reformed in microseconds, only to blister again in an endless cycle of destruction and regeneration. His cells screamed with voices that had no sound. His very concept of self was being subjected to a temperature that defied the laws of physics and rewrote thermodynamics with each passing moment.","He stared into the light with eyes that refused to close, and through the flames he saw eyes . The eyes of THE Living Elemental burning with hatred across impossible distances.","\"I saw you,\" Noah whispered through gritted teeth, his voice a rasp of Primus Mana and defiance mixing into something terrible. \"I saw you and Emotive bargaining about THE Loom like merchants haggling over spoiled goods. I saw the price you paid for entry. I saw you grovel before Emotive just to pacify her anger and secure your position.\"","His eyes blazed with a tyrannical fire that matched the flames consuming his flesh.","\"I have seen you for what you truly are beneath all the grandeur and authority. You flickering pathetic fire. Know that I am coming for you and your Civilization. The foundation you have built for eons... the foundation you have elevated inside of THE Loom... I will fucking take it all. Piece by piece. Brick by brick until there is nothing left.\"","...!","A howl of rage erupted from the light, a sound of pure majestic fury that could have shattered lesser realities. But existence clamped down with brutal efficiency, silencing the Primordial entity and severing the connection like cutting a string.","But the damage was done.","Noah stood alone in the crater of glass that his feet had created, his body wreathed in a terrifying crimson flame that did not flicker or waver. It melted the reality around him in expanding circles.","It was not Complexity and Purity damage in any conventional sense. It was Pain .","It was a constant shooting tingling agony that permeated every nerve and every atom and every weave of his existence. It was the sensation of being dipped in the heart of a star, forever, with no hope of relief or escape.","He trembled like a leaf in a storm. His knees buckled under the weight, but he did not fall.","Prompts bloomed before his melting vision like flowers of information.","| THE IMMOLATION OF THE SACRILEGIOUS SAVAGE|","| Analysis: Your Civilizational Resistance mitigates the attack. Your Principles mitigate the attack. But the attack is not damage. It is a Brand.|","|To harm you takes an unfathomable amount of effort under Perpetual Harvest. Under the suppression of The Primordial Civilization of Existence, the Authority of THE Living Elemental is expressed by a fraction of a percent.|","|To bypass this fundamental limitation, the entity has unleashed an attack that carries no Complexity or Purity damage.|","|It is an attack on your capacity to endure.|","|Effect: Constant, inexpressible burning. A pain so intense that after mere seconds, one would wish to end their own existence just to escape.|","|Duration: Indefinite. Until you collapse your own existence voluntarily.|","|Warning: Contagious. Any existence that contacts you or attempts to siphon the pain will be marked with the same Brand.|","...!","Oh!"]},{"number":4496,"title":"Chapter 4496: Chapter 4495: You Sacrilegius Savage! IV","paragraphs":["Noah felt his existence tremble at the cellular level. The burning was absolute in such a manner that the freezing that came with it was absolute. It was a dichotomy of agony that tore at his sanity like claws.","He wanted to buckle and fall as his entire existence wanted to cry out. Even his eyes felt like they were moving of their own volition to release liquid!","When was the last time I cried?","...!","Behind him, he sensed them approaching. Riya and Khor and Titano among many others. They were rushing towards him with auras flaring in solemnity, seeing his figure trembling in the aftermath as they did not sense any damage transmitted to The Infinite Bulwark.","For it was not a damage of Complexity and Purity!","He raised a trembling hand that shook like an earthquake. Even that small movement sent fresh waves of torture through trillions of protesting quintessential cells and nerves.","\"Stay back,\" he barely voiced out. Even his authority burned as it was an arduous effort to talk or use authority to talk!","The command was silent but heavy with authority. He truly could not speak loudly because the pain was too great.","|UNSURPASSABLE EFFORT DETECTED|","|Your existence withstands constant burning and freezing to its core weavings.|","|A few seconds of this pain is sufficient to drive an existence to seek collapse merely to end the sensation.|","|The effort is immeasurable. Perpetual Harvest burns alongside you. Cheating Architect burns alongside you.|","|The unbelievable effort is being instantly turned to harvest.|","|+10 Sextillion Complexity and Purity gained from an unsurpassable effort to bear that which others cannot bear.|","|+20 Sextillion Complexity and Purity gained.|","|+30 Sextillion Complexity and Purity gained.|","...!","The prompts flashed before his vision, but even they felt like they were melting and distorting.","Noah’s eyes trembled as he forced them to focus on the blurred figures of his people.","He raised his head with effort that cost him dearly. He saw them looking at him with eyes that buzzed as if they could feel his pain by proxy.","He saw Aethon, the Elemental Titan, looking at his forces with pained eyes and staring at the melted bodies that had been used as vessels by THE Living Elemental .","He saw the distant battles where the Emotives continued their relentless suicidal assault. Emotion was too volatile and too absolute, they would not stop.","Noah swallowed the scream building in his throat.","\" We do not sacrifice ,\" Noah said, his voice a solemn steady drumbeat cutting through the chaos. \"And the leader will always be the shield to protect. I have protected. Now... the rest of you need to move forward.\"","He looked at Khor and at Riya with eyes that burned. Fucking literally at that.","\"Stop the legions of Emotives. Secure the Legions of Law. Complete the mission.\"","...!","They hesitated for a fraction of a moment. They looked at his trembling figure and at the flames licking his skin like hungry predators.","But he had given the order and it was absolute.","Khor’s face twisted in a snarl of lividity and grief. She turned with violent motion, her hunger flaring like a weapon, and charged toward the distant legions with murderous intent. The others followed her lead, their grief transformed into fury that demanded release.","Noah remained standing alone.","He fought the overwhelming urge to fall and make the pain stop. Every second was a lifetime of agony compressed into a single eternal moment.","This was a wrath of THE!","|+35 Sextillion Complexity and Purity...|","And then, even more weavings hit him like a second attack.","|WARNING: THE IMMOLATION IS SPREADING|","|Target: All connected instances of your existence. All of your bodies.|","...!","He had expected it but the reality was still terrible.","Across the isolated domains of his Abode of The Early Creature, his other bodies reacted instantly to the spreading contagion.","He separated himself from Riya with brutal efficiency, from Elyndra with desperate speed, from Adelaide and Barbatos and Athena and all others he had been peacefully spending time with. He isolated his clones and wrapped them in barriers of Primus Mana as the crimson-gold flames erupted over them like a plague.","He was burning everywhere simultaneously.","The pain was so total and so all-consuming that for the first time in his existence, Noah felt the seductive pull of the void calling to him. Just let go. Just collapse. Just make it stop.","...!","No , was his clear and quintessential answer.","He looked around with vision swimming in and out of focus. He needed relief, even a second of respite, even a microsecond free from this torture.","His gaze landed on Ozymandias standing in the distance.","His other self. The manifestation of Hunger given form.","Ozymandias stood watching the battle unfold, and gloriously he was not burning. He was separate enough and distinct enough in his Way of Hunger to be immune to the direct contagion of the brand. But...","\"I give,\" Noah gasped, his voice a whisper of agony barely audible, \" My Everything of Pain.\"","...!","He had given his Fear to be consumed. He had given his Doubt to be devoured.","Now the burning and freezing pain was so excruciating that he wanted to give it away immediately, to be rid of it at any cost.","A blinding orb of gray light shot from his chest like a bullet. It was heavy and pulsing with the concentrated scream of his nerves given physical form.","When he looked at it with trembling eyes, he saw clearly. The orb was also marked with the curse, crimson-gold flames licking across its surface.","But in the distance, Ozymandias opened his jaws wide without hesitation. He bit down with hunger that knew no limits.","GULP!","The Everything disappeared into the void of his consumption.","Ozymandias burst into crimson-gold flames instantly.","For a single blessed instant, Noah felt relief. It was a sensation so intense and so euphoric that he felt like he was suffocating on air itself. He could breathe. He could think clearly.","But a second later...","| THE IMMOLATION PERSISTS|","|The Brand is a cursed weaving of existence emanating from an entity at a Higher Scale of Existence, through principles current not grasped. It demands to be felt regardless of whether an existence is capable of feeling pain or sensation. It is an authority exceeding your current scale of existence.|","...!","Oh!","The relief vanished like smoke. The burning returned with vengeance, finding new conceptual nerve endings he didn’t know he possessed. It was worse than before. It was deeper and more fundamental.","|...+100 Sextillion Complexity and Purity gained from an unsurpassable effort!|","The prompts seemed to be giving him good news, but even they seemed hesitant.","Noah floated there in the air, a statue of trembling will refusing to break.","In the far distance, Ozymandias, now burning with the same crimson-gold flames, faced a Living Emotive of 300 Sextillion Complexity who had charged forward with suicidal aggression.","The Emotive struck with desperate fury, his hand seeking to infuse emotional collapse onto Ozymandias and break his will.","His hand connected with Ozymandias’s burning shoulder.","SSSSSSS !","The contagion spread on contact like wildfire through dry grass.","The Living Emotive screamed with a sound that transcended language. It was a sound of such raw unadulterated horror that it silenced that entire sector of the battlefield and made even the other Emotives pause in recognition.","One second. That was all it took. That was the period of time that this Emotive felt the terror of the flames.","The Emotive clawed at his own chest with frantic desperation, ripping into his own heart and collapsing his existence just to make it stop. As he dissolved into ash and scattered on the wind, his face wore an expression of pure blissful relief.","...!","A being of 300 Sextillion Complexity could not last a single second under the Brand.","Noah had been enduring it for more than a minute that felt like centuries.","|I... am sorry, Master.|","RUIN/EDEN’s voice trembled in his mind with unusual emotion. It sounded wet as she continued to do her job!","|I am sorry...+100 Sextillion Complexity and Purity gained from an unsurpassable effort.|","Noah looked down at his hands with vision blurring. They were shaking like leaves in a hurricane.","His Complexity had crossed 1,000 Sextillion.","One Septillion.","There was a condition for the shift from Sextillion to Septillion, some threshold that needed to be met. He couldn’t remember what it was. The pain was too loud and drowned out everything else.","He shook his head with effort that cost him dearly. He focused on the only thing that mattered in this moment.","He would not collapse. He would not fade. But it was so unbearable!","He continued to burn.","And with each passing second, his Existence and his Civilization grew stronger from his suffering, harvesting from his impossible endurance what others could not bear for even a moment.","The flames did not diminish and the pain did not lessen.","But Noah stood.","And that, in itself, was a victory that THE Living Elemental had not anticipated.","That, in itself...would pave the way for something unfathomable."]},{"number":4497,"title":"Chapter 4497: Chapter 4496: At The Darkest Hour I","paragraphs":["The concept of pain is, at its core, a gift wrapped in barbed wire.","It is the body’s desperate scream, the soul’s frantic alarm bell ringing in the void. To feel pain is to know with absolute certainty that something is wrong. It is the heat that snaps the hand back from the flame before the flesh is charred. It is the sharp reminder that you are mortal and fragile and currently under siege.","Without pain, we would wander into fire and feel nothing until we were ash. Pain is guidance, and pain is survival.","But then there is the other kind.","The excruciating relentless unending symphony of agony that serves no purpose, teaches no lesson, and offers no escape. It is the torture of a nerve ending singing a high piercing note that never resolves. It is the constant grinding pressure that turns bone to dust and will to water.","Many have argued about this duality for eons across civilizations.","Some say that pain is the ultimate test, that Existence in its infinite cruelty uses agony as a sieve to separate the weak from the worthy. To endure is to prove one’s right to exist. To break is to admit that you were never truly meant to be here at all. In this view, every second of suffering is a coin paid into the bank of one’s own potential.","Another perspective sees pain as a flaw in the design, a glitch in the matrix of existence. Why should growth require suffering? Why must strength be forged in fire? They argue that Existence should allow for elevation without agony, that the equation of pain equals gain is a lie told by tyrants to justify their cruelty. To them, pain is simply noise, a distraction from the true work of living.","And then there is the third view. The rarest and coldest perspective.","To these few, pain is neither a test nor a flaw. It simply is . It is a condition of reality as fundamental as gravity or time. You do not fight gravity but build structures to withstand it. You do not argue with time but learn to move within its flow.","So too with pain. You do not seek to escape it, nor do you glorify it. You simply exist within it, expanding your capacity to endure until the pain becomes background radiation, a constant hum that proves you are still alive.","For those who can reach this state, for those who can look into the abyss of excruciating constant agony and refuse to blink, their endurance will undoubtedly be paid off. Not in comfort perhaps, but in power.","And power, in the end, is the only currency that matters.","The pain Noah felt was something he truly could not accurately describe.","It was not a sensation but an environment. He was drowning in it. Every atom of his being was screaming, a trillion voices raised in a chorus of absolute unadulterated misery. The worst part was the lack of adaptation. There was no numbness, no dulling of the senses over time. Every second was as fresh and sharp as the first.","It was the sensation of being dipped in acid, then frozen, then burned again, over and over, with no rhythm or reprieve.","Doing anything in this state, under the brand of THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage , was unbearable.","Even the act of thinking required a titanic effort of will. He knew that this effort was being harvested, that every moment of torture was translating into exponential growth for his Civilization. But his existence truly did not wish to do it. Every instinct he possessed was screaming at him to stop, to fold, to simply let go and allow the darkness to take him.","That was how excruciating it was.","So he floated in the space of The Injunction Sanctuary of Law, his body a trembling statue of crimson-gold fire. He watched the blurry distance where his forces swarmed the Civilization Legions of Emotives, including Aethon and those under him, but the images were fractured and distorted by the haze of his own suffering.","Beside him, Alexander Asmodeus neared with cautious steps.","Further back, the Living Laws and Dukes of Law watched from a safe distance. They were ashen and terrified, still trembling from the pressure of THE Living Elemental that had briefly flashed into existence. They were useless. Utterly and completely useless.","Alexander stopped a respectful distance away, his silver-white aura flickering with genuine concern. He looked at Noah, at the flames that did not burn clothing but devoured concepts, and he asked the only question that mattered.","\"How can I help?\"","He did not ask if Noah was okay. That answer was written in every tremor of Noah’s frame, in the way the air around him hissed and boiled with residual heat.","Noah almost wanted to laugh at the question, but the thought of the physical effort stopped him cold. He almost wanted to say that nobody talking to him right now would be of great help, that even listening was an agony he didn’t want to endure.","But he had to find a way to adapt. He had to get used to this new reality.","\"Nothing can be done,\" Noah said, his voice a sound like grinding stones dragged across broken glass as his throat was fucking dry . \"Apart from enduring.\"","Alexander’s expression tightened. \"I’m sorry,\" he said quietly, his voice barely above a whisper. \"I did not expect for things to play out like this. I did not foresee... this .\"","Noah managed a smile though it cost him dearly. It was a small tight thing, a grimace masquerading as amusement.","\"This is just existence,\" he whispered through the burning. \" Existence is grand. Existence is unfair. Existence is unpredictable. It is what it is.\"","After this, Alexander turned silent. He simply looked at Noah with an expression that was difficult to read.","Even though he showed a smile, Noah’s figure, wreathed in angrily scorching crimson-gold flames, still couldn’t help but tremble with constant rhythmic shaking. The tremors were a physical manifestation of the war being fought in every cell of his body.","Noah felt the eyes of Alexander remain on him with steady focus. They were the eyes of someone younger looking up to someone older, as if they found his actions unfathomably grand. As if his suffering was a monument to be admired rather than a torture to be pitied.","He shook his head excruciatingly at this perception. The scorching blurry prompts continued to flow over his eyes every now and then, a ticker tape of his own torture converted to power.","|+100 Sextillion Complexity and Purity gained from an unsurpassable effort...|","They were unfathomably immense gains that came from this excruciating effort, numbers that would have taken days and weeks for him to accumulate through normal means.","Noah felt it all washing over him. He tried to focus his scattered attention on his other self, on Ozymandias, who should be wrapping up a battle soon. Because THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage was a curse as much as a weapon.","He was barely handling it with all his accumulated will.","Other existences, for them it was utterly disastrous if he actively allowed the contagion to spread!","Far in the distance, the battle raged with renewed intensity. But it was a massacre of a different kind.","Ozymandias stood amidst the violet storm of the Emotive Legion like a dark star. His humanoid body, wreathed in the same crimson-gold fire that burned Noah, erupted with terrible purpose. Thousands of tentacles, slick with obsidian-crimson hunger and blazing with the contagious agony of the Immolation, shot out in every direction like seeking missiles.","They rushed towards the Civilizational Legions of Emotives with predatory intent. The moment they made contact, the effect was instantaneous and devastating.","The Emotives, beings of pure concentrated feeling, were instantly wreathed in THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage.","Most of them felt the excruciating pain for a second or two. That was all their sanity could withstand before it shattered like glass. Their minds broke. Their wills evaporated. They did not fight back and they did not try to flee. They simply... collapsed their own existence voluntarily as Ozymandias would then devour them!","It was a wave of mass suicide, triggered by a pain that no being should ever have to feel.","Others scattered in absolute terror, their formations breaking apart as they fled from the burning touch of Ozymandias’s tentacles like prey fleeing a predator.","Because of this devastating effect, the Legion of Emotives became scattered and broken down. The Civilizational Legion of Law and Deborah, watching from their defensive line, stared in stupor and disbelief. They had been fighting a losing battle for what felt like eons, and now in mere moments their enemy was dissolving before their eyes.","As for Ozymandias himself, his existence felt the same excruciating pain as Noah. Every movement was torture. Every extension of a tentacle was a scream trapped in his throat threatening to escape.","But he endured!","And for his endurance while moving even more aggressively, Harvest continued to descend on him in waves. He gained 100 Sextillion Complexity and Purity every so often, his power skyrocketing as he turned his own suffering into a weapon of mass destruction.","This battle could effectively be considered over and done. As much as Noah was being afflicted with a terrifying curse from a Primordial Sovereign, he had gotten his hands on a truly terrifying weapon.","Pain, it turned out, was the ultimate offensive capability.","Noah watched this unfold through the haze of his own agony, and despite everything he felt something like satisfaction. The Emotives were breaking not because they were weak but because the pain was simply beyond any reasonable capacity to endure. Even beings of 300 Sextillion Complexity were folding within seconds.","And he was standing here, minutes into the Brand, still conscious and still fighting.","What does that make me?","The thought came unbidden and he almost wanted to laugh again.","Alexander spoke again, his voice cutting through Noah’s internal thoughts \"Is there any principle or authority that might alleviate...this?\"","Noah shook his head slowly, each movement sending fresh lances of agony through his neck. \"This is an attack from THE Living Elemental himself. No one here has the authority to counter it. Unless you have the distinction of THE .\"","\"Then what do we do?\"","What could one do indeed.","At this though, Noah remembered his own words.","Unless you have the distinction of THE.","Who...did he know with a distinction of THE ?","...!","His eyes pulsed with tyranny!","His vision swam and refocused. The prompts kept coming.","|+150 Sextillion Complexity and Purity gained from an unsurpassable effort...|","The numbers were climbing faster now. His existence was learning to harvest from the pain more efficiently, extracting power from suffering with ruthless precision.","It was the third view of pain made manifest. Pain as a condition of reality. Pain as background radiation. Pain as the price of ascension.","He had paid the price before in smaller denominations. Now he was paying in bulk, and existence was forced to acknowledge the transaction.","In the distance, Ozymandias’s tentacles swept through another cluster of Emotives. They scattered like leaves before a storm, and those too slow to escape dissolved hunger in his jaws with expressions of relief on their fading faces.","Khor appeared near Ozymandias, her small form blazing with hunger as she coordinated the assault. Riya and others cautiously floated above.","The crimson-gold flames continued to burn as the pain continued to scream, and Noah continued to stand strong!"]},{"number":4498,"title":"Chapter 4498: Chapter 4497: At The Darkest Hour II","paragraphs":["In the Infiniverse.","As Noah burned with immense pain that transcended comprehension, Elyndra stood before him with shaking eyes. She could see it clearly, the excruciating agony he was going through written in every tremor of his form, in every flicker of the crimson-gold flames that wrapped around him like chains of suffering.","But Noah kept his calmness even as his body shook. His voice was steady despite the cost it took to speak.","\"I won’t be able to continue infusing you with Perpetual Harvest so...\"","Before he could finish, the space beside them rippled with authority.","The humanoid figure of The Infiniverse appeared with deliberate precision. She stood tall and ethereal, her form composed of countless spinning Omniverses and flowing rivers of verdant-gold light. But her eyes, those infinite pools that normally held warmth for her Master, were particularly cold.","One could see that she was enraged and simply containing everything with titanic effort, holding back a fury that could unmake Folds!","Noah nodded to her with understanding passing between them, and then he disappeared from this domain entirely.","He left The Infiniverse, who had full access to Perpetual Harvest, to continue the infusion with Elyndra in his place.","As this scene played out, something extraordinary began to happen.","Existence itself began to buzz with strange resonance. Drums, deep and solemn, began to bloom from nowhere and everywhere at once. Pianonic sounds followed, ethereal and haunting, creating a melody that seemed to emerge from the fabric of reality itself. Then voices, wordless and beautiful, echoed out across this space. Across Existence.","When the stolen flame descends","When the ancient powers demand their toll","Does the fire cleanse or break","Does it forge or consume whole?","It was as if Existence itself was buzzing with a melody for this momentous occasion, acknowledging what was transpiring.","The Infiniverse unfurled her hands with mechanical precision and began to release verdant-gold brilliance into Elyndra. The light was beautiful and terrible, carrying the weight of Perpetual Harvest within its threads.","But The Infiniverse seemingly didn’t care much for the task at hand. Her focus was elsewhere, her rage barely contained.","Elyndra looked at her with concern. \"Is he going to be okay? What did that to him?\"","The Infiniverse remained cold and silent for a long moment, as if this stillness was the only thing she could do to keep back the tsunami of rage. When she finally spoke, her voice dripped with loathing and carried an immensity that made the surrounding space tremble.","\" THE Living Elemental.\"","The drums grew heavier in the background, the piano more insistent.","The Infiniverse’s eyes blazed with barely contained fury as she continued, her words a solemn vow wrapped in absolute certainty. \"The pathetic flicker of primordial authority that thought it could mark my Master and walk away unscathed. The entity that believed its age and power made it untouchable.\"","Her voice dropped to something far more dangerous, a whisper that carried the weight of inevitability.","\"I will personally grind THE Living Elemental down to existential dust. I will erase every particle of its authority. I will unmake its very concept until not even the memory of its existence remains to pollute reality. This I swear on the foundations of my being.\"","This is the Brand of sacred violation","The price of touching what was never his","Crimson-gold immolation","Where mortal will meets the abyss","The chorus swelled!","Existence continued a grand symphony!","Elsewhere, panning out across various regions of The Infiniverse.","In an isolated domain of The Abode of The Early Creature, Riya stood motionless. She wore simple blue bloomers and a blue tank top.","She watched with those teary eyes as Noah, excruciatingly burning in crimson-gold flames, turned to leave the domain.","The pain in his movements was visible.","But he was leaving to protect her from what he had become.","The shield steps before the sword","The leader takes the blow","While armies scatter, terrified","Of pain they’ll never know","In a different isolated domain, this one decorated with obsidian furniture and dark elegance, Barbatos stood trembling. She wore an obsidian sundress that flowed like liquid shadow, and her normally composed demeanor had shattered completely. She shook with rage and sorrow mixed together in equal measure as another one of Noah’s bodies, equally wreathed in flames and equally trembling, also prepared to leave her presence.","\"Don’t,\" she whispered, \"Please don’t.\"","But Noah could not stay. The risk was too great. The contagion too dangerous.","He left without responding.","Seconds break the strongest minds","Minutes shatter souls","But time keeps passing, relentless","As the burning takes its toll","In yet another isolated domain, this one filled with gently falling snow that never seemed to accumulate, Adelaide stood in a flowing blue dress. The snowflakes caught in her hair like diamonds, but her eyes held only sorrow as she looked toward Noah’s burning form.","\"Let me...\" she started. \"Let me feel what you feel. Let me feel the same pain.\"","Noah shook his head with agonizing slowness, each movement sending fresh waves of torture through his frame. For the sake of his loved ones, he could not even be near them at this moment!","He wasn’t afraid of them accidentally coming in contact with him and being branded with the same curse. What he couldn’t bear was being around when one of them inevitably came close or felt like they wanted to share that burden.","It was causing him this many issues already. He would not be able to watch his own people suffer THE Immolation of the Sacrilegious Savage as they eventually collapsed their own existence just to escape the pain!","So he simply shook his head lightly, and even from Adelaide, he left.","The symphony continued to play from Existence itself, solemn and heavy.","What is pain but a teacher?","What is agony but proof?","That something still exists to feel","That there’s still a will to move","The scene shifted again to show something unprecedented.","All of Noah’s bodies throughout The Infiniverse, every single iteration that had been spread across countless domains and separated to prevent the spread of the Brand, began to gather in a single isolated area.","This space was filled with sandy golden dream authority that swirled like desert winds frozen in time.","And then, with excruciating slowness, they began fusing into each other.","He compressed himself back into singularity, consolidating his existence despite the torture it caused.","Until finally, only a single Noah floated in that golden space, trembling but whole.","The humanoid form of The Infiniverse appeared before her Master with silent grace. She looked at his trembling form with eyes that held infinite sorrow and infinite determination.","\"Can Master follow me?\" she asked quietly.","Noah looked at her briefly and nodded once.","The two of them warped through space with The Infiniverse guiding them, and they appeared above a radiant blue world that pulsed with concentrated authority.","The moment Noah saw it, his eyes buzzed.","This was the Cultivation Citadel!","The feature The Infiniverse had designed where one would be imposed with the weight of existence many times over, where if they adapted they would gain an explosive increase in Complexity and Purity.","But even moving for Noah was painful at this moment. If he added an elevated weight of existence on top of what he was already bearing...","...!","Here the answer to pain manifests","In trembling, burning form","Pain becomes a currency","And endurance, the new norm","The Infiniverse looked at her Master with an expression that mixed love and necessity and terrible resolve.","\"I’ve been elevating it as we increase in power,\" she said softly. \"The Cultivation Citadel is even grander and harder than before. I know it will be excruciating for Master. I know it seems like you cannot adapt to this pain.\"","She paused.","\"But... I need you to go in, Master.\"","...!","Noah’s body shook with a solemn tyranny.","He looked at the Cultivation Citadel that would make his pain hundreds of times worse, and he truly did not want to enter it.","But this was a calamity as much as an opportunity. He needed to make use of it. He needed to do something to adapt to it even if adaptation seemed impossible.","So even though he did not want to, even though every fiber of his being screamed in protest...","Noah flew toward the Cultivation Citadel.","His body, wreathed in the curse of THE Living Elemental, descended like a falling star wrapped in chains of agony.","Lesser beings would have long since perished from what he faced!","But he persevered!","In the space above, The Infiniverse watched silently as her Master descended. Beside her, RUIN/EDEN materialized with an expression that was pained and heavy.","\"We could have waited,\" RUIN/EDEN said quietly. \"For him to adapt a bit more, to see if the pain gets any less...\"","And yet, The Infiniverse shook her head decisively.","\"It will not get less. It will not get any less .\"","The surrounding existence continued the solemn symphony as another chorus swelled across reality.","This is the Brand of sacred violation","The mark that even Sovereigns cannot erase","Crimson-gold immolation","Burns across time and space","RUIN/EDEN listened silently, and then her expression shifted to something enraged and terrible.","\" THE Living Elemental. ..\" she started.","But The Infiniverse’s focus was entirely on the scene below. Her eyes reflected her Master’s burning figure as he reached the earth of the Cultivation Citadel and tried to stand with excruciating effort.","His knees buckled as his hands pressed against the ground. Every muscle trembled.","But he stood.","As she watched this impossible display of will, golden lines of terrifying wonder began to leak from The Infiniverse’s infinite eyes as she had never seen her Master like this!","They fell like molten stars, each one carrying the weight of her fury and her pride and her absolute devotion.","\"I am going to rip THE Living Elemental apart,\" she whispered, but her voice carried across dimensions. \"Atom by atom. Particle of authority by particle of authority. I will dissect every weaving of its existence. I will make it experience pain beyond what it inflicted. I will make it beg for the mercy of non-existence. I will make it wish it had never experienced existence at all. And then, when it has suffered for eons... I will grant it oblivion and erase even that mercy from the memory of reality.\"","...!","The symphony and chorus resounded even heavier now, the voices of existence itself acknowledging the vow.","Let THE Ancients tremble","At what their curse became","Not a weapon of destruction","But a forge for his ascension’s flame","HUUM!","On this day, The Infiniverse shed a tear.","On this day, the entirety of The Infiniverse, the countless Frequencies of Existence, the Wheels of Existence, the Omniverses, the Domains of Existence, all of it trembled in resonance with her emotion.","And oh, for the entity that caused The Infiniverse to shed a tear... bless their poor souls.","The Infiniverse turned to RUIN/EDEN, and when she spoke her voice was cold and tyrannical and absolute.","\"Mobilize the Primus Inevitabilities into all Elemental Folds immediately,\" she commanded with the force of inevitability itself. \"Convert every single Elemental into The Way of Mana, whether by choice or by force. I do not care which. Erase every single signature of The Primordial Civilization of Elementals outside THE Loom. Convert every single iota into The Derivative Primordial Civilization of Elemental under the banner of Mana.\"","Her eyes blazed brighter.","\"Afterwards we will begin devouring and incorporating all Transcendent and Minor Elemental Folds without exception . After that... I shall begin devouring every single remnant of the Shattered First Folds , all the Transcendent Folds and Minor Folds across Observable Existence. I shall take it all. Every piece. Every fragment.\"","Her voice dropped to something even more dangerous.","\" They want to play? Let us fucking play.\"","...!","The command was heavy and absolute. RUIN/EDEN nodded silently, her own expression grim with determination, and then she disappeared to carry out the orders.","The flames don’t cease their hunger","The pain knows no reprieve","But standing in the inferno","Is the choice that sets him free","The final chorus and symphony swelled across existence as The Infiniverse stood alone above the Cultivation Citadel.","She overlooked Noah, her Master, at seemingly his most pained state. She would watch over him. She would guard him. She would feel everything he felt.","After all, they were connected in a Quintessential and irreversible manner.","If she wanted to, she could feel what he felt through their bond.","And this whole time, from the moment THE Living Elemental had branded him, she had subjected herself to feel the inescapable pain her Master endured!","She trembled alongside him and she suffered alongside him.","And she would have her vengeance for it.","Below, Noah took his first step into the deeper gravity of the Cultivation Citadel, and the weight increased tenfold.","And The Infiniverse watched with golden lines still falling from her eyes, each one a declaration of war against those who had dared to harm what was hers like this!"]},{"number":4499,"title":"Chapter 4499: Chapter 4498: At The Darkest Hour III","paragraphs":["In the Cultivation Citadel, Noah’s thoughts burned brightly.","The weight of existence pressed down on him like the gravity of a collapsing star. The crimson-gold flames continued their endless feast on his being.","But in the midst of all of this excruciating pain, his mind remained unbearably clear.","And currently a single thought was burning through the haze of agony. A single idea crystallizing with perfect clarity.","The idea and reality that THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage would have no answer, no counter, no solution... unless you possessed the distinction of THE .","And he knew someone with the distinction of THE !","THE Dead Order!","He closed his eyes with agonizing slowness. In the next moment, he focused his weavings of existence toward that unique space that held The Veil which divided him and Sigrid from THE Dead Order on the other side.","The domain that didn’t really exist anywhere in physical Observable Existence, but in a unique conceptual space where Sigrid was siphoning The Civilizational Authority of Order.","At this moment, the scene shifted to that ethereal realm.","In that space between spaces, Noah had already made distance and moved away from Sigrid who was looking at him with pained eyes.","Even here, even in this conceptual domain, his figure was burning with crimson-gold fire that refused to be extinguished.","...!","On the other side of The Veil, THE Dead Order sat upon her throne of white marble and looked at him with a particularly unfavorable expression.","In the last few hours, with Sigrid becoming more and more powerful naturally, her rate of siphoning Order had become even more immense. The flow of Civilizational Authority being drained through The Veil had increased to torrential levels.","So THE Dead Order was not their biggest fan at this moment.","But even she tilted her head with curiosity and looked at those flames burning around his figure with something like astonishment in her ancient eyes.","\" What did you do ?\" she asked.","Noah looked at her through The Veil with eyes that burned despite the pain, his voice steady despite the cost of speaking.","\"Are you familiar with the curses of entities with THE distinction?\"","She replied with incredulity that he could even ask such a question. \" You can say that.\"","He nodded slowly and continued with that same terrible calmness. \"I seem to have pissed off THE Living Elemental , and that pathetic excuse for a fire has proceeded to brand me with THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage . A constant excruciating burning that cares not for Complexity or Purity. An indefinite burning until I collapse my own existence.\"","...!","As he said this with such casual matter-of-factness, THE Dead Order looked at him with sheer incredulity written across her features.","\" How are you not dead? \" she demanded. \" How have you not collapsed your existence already?\"","...!","Noah looked at her calmly through the excruciating pain, his gaze unwavering.","\"The two of us are some of the few powers that exist outside of THE Loom . We both wish to survive The Fallout and come through on the other side stronger than before.\" His voice carried the weight of inevitability. \"An answer to The Fallout lies with existences that have the distinction of THE . You have such a distinction, even if you do not have the full power of THE currently.\"","He paused, letting his words sink in.","\"If you and I were able to come to an understanding... maybe The Fallout would be something that we can easily get past. This is what I have always thought. Right now, faced with this ordeal, would you happen to have an answer or solution or knowledge regarding how such a curse could be taken care of?\"","His eyes gleamed with something dangerous.","\"And to show my goodwill...\"","Noah nodded toward Sigrid, and in the next moment the massive river of white Order that was flowing from the other side of The Veil to Sigrid stopped abruptly. It rapidly reduced and became a barely imperceptible line as barely any Civilizational Authority of Order was being siphoned anymore.","...!","THE Dead Order looked at such a scene with somber eyes, looking at Noah as if he were a dead man walking as she asked with genuine curiosity, \" What exactly did you do to make THE Living Elemental so enraged that he would exert his authority outside of THE Loom? With the suppression of Existence itself laid down by THE Creature, any entity with THE distinction would pay a heavy cost to unleash even a semblance of their power like this outside THE Loom. Just what did you do?\"","Noah did not answer such a question.","He simply floated closer to The Veil with deliberate movements, appearing inches away from it, close enough that the flames around him cast dancing shadows across her throne.","He asked again with calm tyranny amidst all the burning, \"Do you have a solution?\"","At such a direct question, THE Dead Order became utterly still as if she were thinking carefully about her options.","Noah looked at her with eyes that seemed to pierce through layers of existence, and as if he could seemingly see inside of her being and what decision she was about to make, he said with quiet certainty, \"In your head right now, you are debating two choices. I do advise for you to lean towards the better choice for your sake and mine.\"","...!","At such presumptuous words, THE Dead Order smiled with a sense of brutality and calculation. She leaned back on her throne and laughed with genuine amusement.","\" Since you already seem to know then I will choose the other choice ,\" she said with cruel delight. \" Why would I help you? You are an antagonist against what I wish to achieve. And now that you have been struck with such an affliction, your existence will likely collapse itself soon enough, even though it should have done so some time ago.\"","Her smile widened.","\" After you are collapsed... this little vile Young Order you have been defiling, who is so emotionally connected to you that she is holding back tears right now as you burn... she would lose her protector. Any semblance of Civilization that you are building will crumble. And once the one protecting her has crumbled, I can send my Guides of Order to the other side of The Veil without worry and claim that vile Young Order beside you. I will erase her existence completely and fuse with what she has.\"","HUUM!","She spread her hands as if presenting an obvious truth.","\" All of this just works out perfectly for me. Why would I not choose this path? No, Osmont. There will be no help from me to you. You have been an interesting little character in this grand play of Existence. But it is now time for you to make an exit. Like many other insignificant beings since The Earliest Folds, you will be forgotten very, very quickly.\"","Her eyes glittered with malicious satisfaction.","\" Even though I do admire the fact that you are able to stand here and even talk... while experiencing an attack of a Civilizational Authority from an entire scale of Existence above you. Now that is something worthy of note. You are akin to a little chicken that has been thrown into burning boiling oil and yet somehow you are refusing to be burnt and cooked.\"","She laughed again, the sound echoing across the domain.","\" That burning oil will only increase in temperature, Osmont. And as soon as you collapse... I will make my move.\"","...!","Her eyes shone with a sadistic brutality as she threw her head back on her throne and laughed at his misfortune with genuine glee!","She continued with utterly ugly words dripping with schadenfreude. \" Haha, I never expected to feel thankful for that shitty Living Elemental. I will give him your regards when I come across him after The Fallout. When I have my revenge against him and all the others. I will...!\"","She was so deeply entrenched in her words and laughing at his misfortune that she only realized what had happened in the next moment.","She looked down with sudden alarm to see the figure of Noah... floating right beside her throne, his burning hand reaching out and touching her leg.","In the next instant, crimson-gold flames began to spread and ravage across her form like wildfire!","...!","THE Dead Order opened her eyes with absolute incredulity and shock, her mind unable to process what had just occurred.","Noah used that instant moment of shock to rapidly shoot back across to the other side of The Veil with desperate speed!","THE Dead Order then howled out in rage as the flames climbed higher up her body!","Immense waves of Order erupted from her like a tsunami, blanketing down on the flames that had already covered half of her lower body!","\" YOU CAN CROSS THE VEIL?!\" she roared with disbelief and fury mixing together. \" You sycophantic fuck!\"","Noah looked at her from the safety of the other side with an utterly cold and tyrannical gaze that held no sympathy whatsoever.","\" Watch your language, O pristine and righteous Order,\" he said with quiet venom. \"I told you to make a different choice. You did not. So now... we share the same affliction.\"","His eyes blazed with satisfaction despite the pain.","\"I sincerely hope that you have a solution for it.\"","...!","BOOM !","Rageful waves of Order erupted like volcanic fury as shockingly, Noah observed seas of white authority trying desperately to press down on the flames that were rising to cover the massive body of THE Dead Order .","They were shockingly slowing the advance of the flames from covering her entirely, the Civilizational Authority of Order combating the curse with desperate intensity.","Noah could feel the eyes of THE Dead Order vibrating with immense pain and incredulity mixing with absolute rage, and her domineering voice bellowed out in the next moment with a single word that shook the entire domain.","\" OSMONT!!!\"","The roar was primal and furious and filled with a pain she had not experienced in eons.","Noah simply watched with cold satisfaction as THE Dead Order experienced the same burning he had been enduring, and he waited to see what choice she would make now!"]},{"number":4500,"title":"Chapter 4500: Chapter 4499: At The Darkest Hour IV","paragraphs":["As the rage of THE Dead Order became apparent and built to a crescendo, she seemed like she was about to unleash even more words filled with venom and malice... and yet the rising flames of THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage caused her to be unable to even do this as she had to focus entirely on survival.","She glared towards Noah with eyes that promised retribution as seas of her authority continued to crash down on the flames with desperate intensity.","Noah looked towards Sigrid to confirm something important, and he saw that she had already completely stopped siphoning off the Civilizational Authority of Order. Just in case this would transfer the curse of THE Living Elemental to her as well.","Noah looked at THE Dead Order once more through The Veil with calm tyranny.","\"So, I ask you again,\" he said with measured words. \"Do you have a solution to such a curse? You should be able to feel it intimately now.\"","...!","As he said this, he also saw the prompts that flashed before his eyes with brilliant light.","|You have carried out a bold action of unsurpassable effort and audacity.|","|Your choices currently cause an existence much more complex than you to feel unbearable pain.|","|By spreading THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage to THE Dead Order, you have created a situation of unprecedented consequence.|","|Depending on the result of your actions, you can potentially harvest unfathomable wonders.|","He simply watched these prompts come and go like waves as he looked at THE Dead Order who gazed at him with eyes of utter malice and suffering combined.","She struggled against the flames for a long moment before speaking through gritted teeth, her voice dripping with hatred.","\" Only THE Civilizational Authority can go against THE Civilizational Authority ,\" she said with cruel finality. \" You are not at that level. You are far from that level, and as of now, you will never reach that level. You could go past Septillions, Octillions, Nonillions, and even Decillions in Complexity and Purity, and you, Osmont...would not reach THE.\"","Her expression twisted with spiteful satisfaction despite her pain.","\" All the efforts you have made, the grand Civilization you have been trying to build... all of it will crumble even before The Fallout happens. And I will be waiting for that patiently, Osmont. I will be waiting for your complete cession and collapse that you will carry out with your own hands when the pain you feel becomes unbearable.\"","Her voice rose to something like triumph through the agony.","\" Rejoice, Osmont! Rejoice, for your death is coming!\"","Her expression turned utterly spiteful and hateful towards the end, and after she finished these words she waved her hands with tremendous effort. A white veil emerged to surround her completely, blocking off any view of her brilliance and figure as if she did not even wish to look at him while she fought against the encroaching THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage.","...!","Noah looked at the scene in silence as behind him the figure of Sigrid asked with desperation in her voice, \"What can I do?\"","And the answer to this as Noah continued to burn was a calm and simple, \"Nothing. It’s okay.\"","His eyes burned brightly as he thought of her answer echoing in his mind. Only THE Civilizational Authority can go against THE Civilizational Authority.","He closed his eyes and the scene of this ethereal domain, of the space between spaces, faded away as his focus came once more to his body that was within the Cultivation Citadel.","He strained as his legs and arms trembled with effort, and he only managed to stand upright while bearing the flames through sheer tyrannical will.","In the next moment, the figure of The Infiniverse made her descent, and she actually came bearing gifts in her hands.","She voiced out with shining eyes, \"Elyndra provided these gifts from The First Farmer. As the first course of action for his Civilization, he planted seeds of effort that bore The Fruits of Effort. \"","She held them forward reverently.","\"Consuming such a fruit will grant one the harvest of effort that they have been putting in across existence from the day they were born. The screaming the moment you arrived into the world in that hospital. As your mother cried in happiness and clutched you and held you. As your heart beat furiously and as your lungs sought air. As your teeth formed and grew, as your body and organs continued to develop. As you went through schools in the effort of communicating with others. As your first love turned you down because you were not enough. As you went through an apocalypse and lost your mother. As you awakened and made the effort to cast your very first fireball. All the effort since the day you were born...\"","As she said this with a sense of hope, she threw these Fruits of Effort to him.","Noah managed to grab them with trembling hands, his steady gaze filled with tyranny looking at them as he nodded with understanding.","\"Give my thanks to The First Farmer,\" Noah said with genuine gratitude despite the pain.","Thereafter, he opened his mouth unnaturally wide and swallowed the entirety of the first Fruit of Effort in a single gulp before he proceeded to do the same with the others in rapid succession.","Effort .","It took a great deal of effort to be who he was since the day that he was born.","Noah felt the vibrant Fruits of Effort bloom across his existence as everything began to shake and tremble with accumulated power.","His existence was currently surrounded by an array of harvests all around him, with the harvests of encroaching upon The Primordial Civilization of Elemental being immense and still being gathered. His Architect’s Bulwarks would undoubtedly advance and reach a glorious stage of achievement from all of this harvest.","And right now, as he sensed the Fruits of Effort dissolving into his existence, his eyes began to flicker with memories as he sensed the very first breath that he took the day that he was born.","As he began to feel all that effort accumulating, he spoke with commanding authority.","\"All the effort of my existence from the day that I was born, from when I was even in my mother’s womb... let all of that effort flow into persevering and surviving and coming up with a solution for THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage.\"","...!","All the effort of his existence even before he was born!","His existence began to buzz with accumulated power as even while scorching flames tore apart every single cell in every atom... even as his existence continued to be battered by a pain that other existences could not handle for a second...","HUUUM!","His existence began to vibrate and resonate as verdant-gold light permeated all around him in waves of increasing intensity.","| All your Principles surge with unprecedented brilliance.|","| Retroactive Harvesting of Perpetual Harvest has been activated.|","| Harvest of Intent has been activated.|","| The Laborer’s Paradise multiplies all efforts at this moment by 1,000 times.|","| Primus Singularity has been activated.|","| Hardship Dissolution of The Principle of Arcana Infinitum has been activated.|","|The Cheating Architect has called upon The Developmental Console of your existence.|","|The ultimate feature of Existential Mod Support has been triggered.|","| Existential Mod Support can manifest concepts or weavings not currently present in Observable Existence.|","|You are attempting to birth something new.|","...!","Noah read through all of these prompts as they all burned with an unfathomable amount of effort and utter pristine glory.","He felt all of his five Principles burn with a light that almost exceeded the crimson-gold flames that were excruciatingly burning him","Almost .","And as all of this effort gathered and concentrated, as every ounce of effort from even before he was born burned for this singular moment in time...","The one thing that remained constant within him burned furiously the most.","His blue-gold Mana. His Primus Mana.","How infinitely grand they were was its own infinite effort.","| Mana is behind countless weavings of existence itself.|","|Mana is behind pain.|","|Mana is behind change.|","|Mana is behind mutations.|","|Mana is behind evolution.|","|Mana is behind adaptation.|","|Fundamental Truth: Mana dictates that if an answer does not exist in Observable Existence, Mana can simply be the source that brings a new answer to fruition.|","|Existential Mod Support agrees with this assessment.|","|A Glorious Mutation is underway.|","|A Glorious Evolution is underway.|","|THE Civilizational Authority Resistance has begun to bloom within your existence. THE Organ of Civilization seeks to bloom within your existence.|","...!","BOOOM!"]}]);
